1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
*A while back, there was this anime called Mobius Ring, the Cycle of Reincarnation.*

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:13,000
*The town I live in, Shiromitsugawa, helped sponsor it, as a way of promoting tourism to the area.*

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:28,000
*The show had some convoluted plot based off of local folklore. It left a big impression on a small group of dedicated fans, but most people regarded it as one of those oddball shows that doesn't make a whole lot of sense.*

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:41,000
*Though it went down in anime history as a complete failure, it's unclear whether the bigwigs behind the regional sponsorship deal are clueless to that fact or simply aren't willing to admit it.*

5
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:44,000
*It's been two years since the anime aired.*

6
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:59,000
*And here we are at the second annual Mobius Festival, a hamfisted attempt to get some mileage out of the anime despite the local residents' overwhelming opposition to going through the cringeworthy event a second time.*

7
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:05,000
*Though as it turns out, the festivities end up being the furthest thing from anyone's mind.*

8
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Cosplayer: "Everyone, please don't panic. Follow the staff's instructions!"

9
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
*A rather scantily-clad cosplayer shouts to the smattering of festival-goers.*

10
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:24,000
*The majority do as they're told, while the more die-hard enthusiasts continue their quest for the ideal camera angle and snap away.*

11
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:31,000
*Pretty impressive dedication, considering the rather substantial earthquake we went through a minute ago.*

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:34,000
Sora: "Hey, Kakeru! I'm back with the goods."

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:38,000
*I blink and turn around to find Sora, my younger sister.*

14
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,000
Sora: "Here's the bandage."

15
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:41,000
Kakeru: "Oh, thanks."

16
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:46,000
*I take the bandage and wrap it around my bloody right index finger.*

17
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Sora: "You really sliced your finger up good, huh? Man, that looks like it smarts."

18
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Kakeru: "I really should've been more careful picking that thing up. Guess it's ruined, huh?"

19
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Sora: "Yeah, and the shrine workers looked pretty upset about it. Oh, hey, here comes the boss. If you're worried about it, best ask her."

20
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:12,000
*I look over to where Sora is pointing to find a woman slowly walking towards us.*

21
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:28,000
*She's one of the family that runs the shrine, and she works as a shrine maiden here, but she's just walking around in casual clothes rather than wearing the traditional shrine maiden outfit. It just ruins the whole festival atmosphere.*

22
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:40,000
*Incidentally, she's also a teacher at our school, Hakusen Academy, and while I call her Ms. Naruse like any good student would, she's always saying she prefers Satsuki-chan.*

23
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:47,000
*A shrine maiden and a teacher. I guess you could say both of those jobs are something of a higher calling.*

24
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Kakeru: "Afternoon. Rough day, huh?"

25
00:02:49,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Satsuki: "Sure is. All these weirdos showed up for the anime stuff, and now I have to work hard. Serves them all right that their little festival got put on hold, don't you think?"

26
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Kakeru: "..."

27
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:05,000
*As you can see, she has a lovely personality.*

28
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:08,000
Satsuki: "They even vandalized the place."

29
00:03:08,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I saw."

30
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Satsuki: "I brought some disinfectant for you, but it looks like you already bandaged it up?"

31
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Kakeru: "Oh, thanks, but I'm fine. I made sure to wash it off a little."

32
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:28,000
Satsuki: "Well, considering how old that thing is, I sure hope you don't catch any bacteria from God-knows-where."

33
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:31,000
Kakeru: "On second thought, disinfectant please?"

34
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:33,000
Sora: "Wow, cracked like an egg."

35
00:03:33,000 --> 00:03:34,000
Kakeru: "Oh, shut up."

36
00:03:34,000 --> 00:03:42,000
*I accept the disinfectant and continue the conversation while pouring the liquid on my cut through the bandage.*

37
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Kakeru: "So, about this sacred relic thing. Do you think it can be fixed up?"

38
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:57,000
Satsuki: "Not a chance. That's thing busted up good. Guess we can just make a replica out of papier-mache or something and stick it up there instead."

39
00:03:57,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Sora: "For real? Wasn't it important or something?"

40
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:01,000
Satsuki: "Beats me."

41
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:09,000
*This should be a disaster, but Ms. Naruse seems oddly optimistic about it. Or maybe apathetic is more the word.*

42
00:04:09,000 --> 00:04:10,000
*The sacred relic...*

43
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:17,000
*According to local mythology, it was a treasure bequeathed by a god, and it also featured in that anime.*

44
00:04:17,000 --> 00:04:26,000
*And it was no prop. Legend says it's a relic from ancient times and has been safeguarded in this very shrine since the days of old.*

45
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:39,000
*The sacred relic is an oval-shaped sphere no bigger than a fist. At first glance it looks like a rusted hunk of metal, but it certainly does exude the aura of something rich with history.*

46
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:48,000
*The shrine was keeping it out on display for the festival, but during that earthquake a minute ago, it got smashed, much to our surprise.*

47
00:04:48,000 --> 00:04:54,000
*It rolled right off its pedestal and fell to the ground, where it shattered into pieces.*

48
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:59,000
*Though it looked like metal, it was apparently as fragile as glass.*

49
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:08,000
*The resulting mess having been deemed a safety hazard, I was ordered to clean it up, which is how I ended up stupidly cutting my finger.*

50
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:14,000
*Had I known this was in store for me, I wouldn't have taken this side job to begin with.*

51
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Satsuki: "Now then, Niimi siblings."

52
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:17,000
Kakeru: "Yes?"

53
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Sora: "What's up?"

54
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:23,000
Satsuki: "You can both go home for today. Don't worry about the festival."

55
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Are you sure?"

56
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Satsuki: "Sure I'm sure. Not like I care about it."

57
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:38,000
Sora: "Boy, talk about irresponsible. Welp, I was just here to enjoy myself, not to work, so I guess it's okay. C'mon, broski, let's head back."

58
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:41,000
Kakeru: "I'd like to go back too, but..."

59
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,000
*I take a glance.*

60
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:51,000
Cosplayer: "Um, I'm sorry. Please, if you would all just refrain from photography. There may be an aftershock, so we need to evacuate."

61
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:58,000
*A few guys with cameras are still crowded around that cosplayer, putting her in quite the awkward predicament.*

62
00:05:58,000 --> 00:06:02,000
Satsuki: "Kujo-san is too diligent for her own good."

63
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,000
*The cosplayer is Miyako Kujo.*

64
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:16,000
*She's working the festival just like me, and not only does she go to the same school that I do, she's also in the same class. We've had a little interaction outside of that too.*

65
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
*Well, sort of. Truth is, we've hardly ever talked.*

66
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:30,000
*We're not what I'd call close, not by a long shot, but when I see her working so hard, it gives me second thoughts about taking Ms. Naruse's advice and bailing.*

67
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:37,000
Sora: "Oh man, that cosplayer sure is cute! Did they rope in one of the voice actresses or something?"

68
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:41,000
Satsuki: "Not a voice actress, no, but rather a sponsor."

69
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,000
Sora: "Wait, what?"

70
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:46,000
Satsuki: "She's the daughter of the president of the Corona Group."

71
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Sora: "What's the Corona Group?"

72
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:51,000
Kakeru: "You've heard of Corona Beverages, right?"

73
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:54,000
Sora: "Huh? THAT Corona? As in Corona Cola?"

74
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Satsuki: "You got it."

75
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:56,000
Sora: "No way!"

76
00:06:56,000 --> 00:07:01,000
Kakeru: "Yep. I thought everyone knew the Corona heiress went to our school."

77
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:06,000
Sora: "What's a company president's daughter doing stuff like that for?!"

78
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Satsuki: "She said she couldn't stand idly by after that flop of an anime made so much trouble for all the residents, so she offered to take on the hardest job at the festival."

79
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:22,000
Sora: "Uh. Are you saying she personally sponsored this event?"

80
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:31,000
Satsuki: "Oh, don't be silly. The corporation is funding the festival. No way would she be paying for this out of her own pocket."

81
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:36,000
Sora: "So you're saying she feels responsible for her family's actions?"

82
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Kakeru: "I guess so."

83
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:39,000
Sora: "She seems nice."

84
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:43,000
Satsuki: "She really is, you know. Her grades are also top-notch."

85
00:07:43,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Sora: "What is she, Miss Congeniality? That kinda bugs me. I'mma snap some photos."

86
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:50,000
Kakeru: "Why?"

87
00:07:50,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Sora: "I might want to blackmail her someday!"

88
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:55,000
Kakeru: "You're the worst."

89
00:07:55,000 --> 00:08:09,000
Sora: "Shows you how much influence parents have. You can blame my personality on being raised by the kind of people who'd give their kids cheesy names like Sora and Kakeru. 'Soar through the skies,' blech."

90
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, and people sometimes call you 'Ten' since the character for your name is a little unusual."

91
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Sora: "If they were gonna name me 'Sora', they could at least have stuck to the regular way of writing it, darn it. I'll change my name sooner or later, mark my words. Or I'll change the writing, at the very least."

92
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:41,000
Satsuki: "I bet them thinking your name is 'Ten' makes you the butt of a lot of jokes. You know, like, they could quote that movie title. Ten, things I hate about you..."

93
00:08:41,000 --> 00:08:44,000
Sora: "Huh? Where the heck is that from?"

94
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:45,000
Kakeru: "No clue."

95
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
Satsuki: "Okay, you're making me feel old. Go on, leave."

96
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:50,000
Sora: "Aww."

97
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Kakeru: "Well, I don't have anything else to do, so I guess I will head home."

98
00:08:55,000 --> 00:09:00,000
*I stand up and glance over at Kujo before getting ready to head back.*

99
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:06,000
Miyako: "I-I'm sorry. I really shouldn't pose for you. I'm only here as a venue guide, you see."

100
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:12,000
*She's having a hard time handling the few remaining guys who insist on taking pictures of her.*

101
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
*She really looks like she's in a bind.*

102
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:18,000
*My super-duper fun Sunday has come and gone.*

103
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:29,000
*Monday has arrived, and my No Desire To Go To School-itis and Don't Wanna Get Out Of Bed-osis are both acting up, but I muster up my willpower and get dressed.*

104
00:09:29,000 --> 00:09:40,000
*I pull out a pouch of jelly drink from the fridge and gulp it down, resupplying my energy reserves for the day ahead. Ahh, the little bits of gelatin really hit the spot.*

105
00:09:40,000 --> 00:09:43,000
*After a quick bedhead check, I exit my apartment.*

106
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,000
*April...*

107
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:50,000
*I heard the average temperature is lower this year, which explains the oddly cool breeze.*

108
00:09:50,000 --> 00:09:55,000
*The brisk snap of a gust of wind helps me shake off my drowsiness.*

109
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Sora: "Jeez, about time you got here!"

110
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:01,000
*Someone shouts at me in a really aggravating tone.*

111
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:08,000
*Going against the flow of students heading towards school, the owner of said aggravating voice shows herself.*

112
00:10:08,000 --> 00:10:13,000
*I keep my feet moving, walking along while reluctantly engaging in conversation.*

113
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Sora: "Boy, you're a slowpoke. Try getting here faster. What, did you stop at the convenience store?"

114
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:22,000
Kakeru: "Well, I gotta buy my lunch."

115
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:31,000
Sora: "You're breaking my heart. Here I am with Mom's homemade lunch, and my dear brother is stuck with a cheap sandwich off a store shelf."

116
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Kakeru: "You're sadly mistaken. Today I got onigiri."

117
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:42,000
Sora: "Is that little thing going to be enough for you? Want me to start asking Mom to make lunch for you too?"

118
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Kakeru: "Wait, you'll seriously ask?"

119
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:50,000
Sora: "Oh, on second thought, never mind. Lugging lunch for two would be heavy, so scratch that."

120
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Kakeru: "..."

121
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:59,000
Sora: "Wow, talk about stink eye. A proper older brother only gazes at his little sister with utter love and adoration."

122
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Kakeru: "Hey, Sora?"

123
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:01,000
Sora: "Hm? What?"

124
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Kakeru: "Do you not have any friends?"

125
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:09,000
Sora: "Huh? What are you implying? Of course I've got friends. Tons of them."

126
00:11:09,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Kakeru: "Then how about you go to school with your friends and leave me alone."

127
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Sora: "This is the thanks I get for keeping my dear older brother company so he doesn't have to walk to school all by his lonesome every morning."

128
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:26,000
Kakeru: "Mind your own business."

129
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Sora: "What the heck? Now see here, Mr. Rude. I think you could stand to treat me with a little more courtesy. How come you've always got such a stick up your butt?"

130
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:42,000
Kakeru: "I'm talking with you now, aren't I? Seems plenty courteous to me."

131
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:47,000
Sora: "Like hell it is. Check THAT out. Now that's what I'm talkin' about!"

132
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:49,000
*She points ahead of us.*

133
00:11:49,000 --> 00:11:52,000
*There's a gathering of male students there.*

134
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:58,000
*No, wait, not exactly. It's actually a meek-looking girl surrounded by a bunch of boys.*

135
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:02,000
???: "U-Um, no, I... I apologize... Please, would you mind...?"

136
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:08,000
*She's acting awfully timid, but it doesn't seem like they're bullying her or anything.*

137
00:12:08,000 --> 00:12:14,000
*They all seem to be trying to charm her by chatting her up or offering to carry her bag.*

138
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Sora: "Damn. A regular boy magnet. They're treating her like she's royalty."

139
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:23,000
Kakeru: "True, but she doesn't seem all that happy about it."

140
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Sora: "That's the kind of treatment I expect from my brother dearest."

141
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:29,000
Kakeru: "..."

142
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:33,000
Sora: "Hey, hey. Could we not, with the drawn-out sighs?"

143
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
Kakeru: "Dealing with you this early in the morning is exhausting."

144
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Sora: "Could we not with those remarks as well?!"

145
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:47,000
*I pick up the pace, trying to get past this crowd that's undoubtedly having a negative influence on Sora.*

146
00:12:47,000 --> 00:12:49,000
???: "R-Really, um, please...!"

147
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:53,000
*As we pass them, I check the girl out from the corner of my eye.*

148
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:57,000
*I don't think she's in my grade. A freshmen? A senior?*

149
00:12:57,000 --> 00:13:00,000
*She really looks like she's in a bind.*

150
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:08,000
Sora: "Oh, wait, I recognize her. I've seen her on the train a couple times. She's always sitting alone, reading a book."

151
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:12,000
Kakeru: "Maybe she's an idol on the side or something."

152
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Sora: "Seriously? What, you think she's straight out of a porn game?"

153
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,000
Kakeru: "Don't tell me you got into those too."

154
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:27,000
Sora: "Just by chance. There was this game that kinda tickled my fancy, which just so happened to be R-18."

155
00:13:27,000 --> 00:13:29,000
Kakeru: "Welp, time to tell Mom."

156
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:31,000
Sora: "Don't you dare!"

157
00:13:31,000 --> 00:13:34,000
*I suffer Sora's antics all the way to school.*

158
00:13:34,000 --> 00:13:47,000
*Well, I shouldn't complain. Sora did just enroll here, and despite the way she acts around me, she's pretty shy. She's probably dealing with a bit of stress from the unfamiliar environment.*

159
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
*That said...*

160
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:57,000
*The way she tries to follow me all the way to class is just plain silly, so I ditch her and make a break for the second year room.*

161
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:00,000
*I ignore everybody and head to my seat.*

162
00:14:00,000 --> 00:14:07,000
*The school year just started, so most of the people I knew got shuffled around to different classes from mine.*

163
00:14:07,000 --> 00:14:11,000
*Kujo is already here, but we haven't made eye contact yet.*

164
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:18,000
*Well, that's the way it goes. I'm sure I'll get more familiar with my new classmates soon enough.*

165
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:22,000
Yoichi: "Morning! And morning! And morning to you, too!"

166
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:31,000
*As I'm trying not to make a scene, a youthful guy comes in with exactly the opposite plan in mind, greeting everyone around him.*

167
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
*That would be Yoichi Fukazawa.*

168
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:38,000
*The only friend of mine from last year who ended up in the same class as me.*

169
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:46,000
*His androgynous looks and charming personality have won over a handful of girls, who I've heard call him a "prince".*

170
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Yoichi: "Good morning t'ya, Kakeru."

171
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:53,000
*He heads my way and perches on the edge of the seat of a nearby vacant desk.*

172
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:57,000
*My unenthusiastic response of "Sup" is, well, the norm.*

173
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Yoichi: "How'd things go yesterday?"

174
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Kakeru: "With the festival, you mean?"

175
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:05,000
Yoichi: "Yeah, that. You did go, right?"

176
00:15:05,000 --> 00:15:09,000
Kakeru: "Technically, but I was really just helping out."

177
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:11,000
Yoichi: "Did it go well?"

178
00:15:11,000 --> 00:15:15,000
Kakeru: "Not particularly. Remember that earthquake?"

179
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Yoichi: "Oh, yeah. That was a big one."

180
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:28,000
Kakeru: "After that, they shut a bunch of stuff down, so there just wasn't anything to do. All in all, it kind of sucked, even worse than last year."

181
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Yoichi: "Man oh man. And after all that merch they made for it, too."

182
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Kakeru: "I'm not sure if they realize how long it's been since that anime aired. Though the character Kujo dressed up as was kind of a big deal."

183
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Yoichi: "Kujo did what as who now?"

184
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:47,000
Kakeru: "Kujo was in cosplay."

185
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,000
Yoichi: "Huh? You mean our Kujo-san?"

186
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:50,000
Kakeru: "Yup."

187
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:53,000
*Inevitably, we both turn to look at Kujo.*

188
00:15:53,000 --> 00:16:01,000
*She's sitting at her desk, her spine straight as a ruler, looking distressed as she stares at something in her hand.*

189
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:07,000
*Looks like the hair clip from yesterday. It seems she hasn't found the owner yet.*

190
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Yoichi: "What character did she cosplay as?"

191
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Kakeru: "Uh, I dunno her name, but the heroine or whatever, I guess? There were other cosplayers there too, but I feel like she was the one showing the most skin."

192
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,000
Yoichi: "Iris!"

193
00:16:22,000 --> 00:16:23,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

194
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Yoichi: "If she was about to pop out of her outfit, then it has to be Iris the Evil Eye!"

195
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:32,000
Kakeru: "Like I said, I didn't catch the name."

196
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:41,000
Yoichi: "Shucks, I should have gone too. Can't believe I missed my chance to see Kujo-san in cosplay. I could've even gotten some photos."

197
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Kakeru: "Wait, you're into that stuff? Since when?"

198
00:16:44,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Yoichi: "Cosplaying itself is whatever, but I'm all about sexy costumes."

199
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,000
Kakeru: "Ugh."

200
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:57,000
Yoichi: "Kujo-san's got a killer body, so she definitely would have made for some 'usable' pics. Shit."

201
00:16:57,000 --> 00:17:06,000
*I find myself glaring through hooded eyes at my friend as he seriously bemoans not taking compromising photos of our classmate.*

202
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:10,000
*He may look like a pure and charming prince on the outside...*

203
00:17:10,000 --> 00:17:13,000
*...but on the inside, he's a skeevy horndog.*

204
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:24,000
*"With my baby face, I can probably pull off sneaking into the ladies' bath, don'tcha think?" Yes, he seriously said that to me once. He's actually that bad.*

205
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:31,000
*The gulf between his appearance and reality is bound to make any poor, starry-eyed girl's head spin.*

206
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:38,000
*Then again, if he was as innocent as he looks, I probably wouldn't be friends with him in the first place.*

207
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:41,000
Yoichi: "You didn't take any pictures?"

208
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:47,000
Kakeru: "No, but people were all over her with the cameras. Try searching the net."

209
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:53,000
Yoichi: "Good call, I'm gonna get right on that! Time to dig up some dirty images of Kujo-san!"

210
00:17:53,000 --> 00:18:01,000
Kakeru: "Okay, you need to at least be a little quieter when you say stuff like that. She'll end up hearing you."

211
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:03,000
Yoichi: "I'll take that risk!"

212
00:18:03,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Kakeru: "Not on my watch. Anyway, there's the bell, so scram."

213
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Yoichi: "Yes, sir. Right away, sir."

214
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:15,000
*Yoichi returns to his desk, blatantly getting out his smartphone to start on his new quest.*

215
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:19,000
Satsuki: "Okay, everyone to your seats. Homeroom is starting."

216
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:26,000
*Ms. Naruse enters the classroom right as the bell goes silent, prompting my classmates to rush to their seats.*

217
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:32,000
Satsuki: "Everyone's here, right? Well, I don't really have any announcements to make, but..."

218
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:35,000
*I half-listen to her, and my eyes start to wander.*

219
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,000
Miyako: "..."

220
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:39,000
*Kujo is still staring at that hair clip.*

221
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:44,000
*It's a little weird how preoccupied she is with some lost hair clip.*

222
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
*...*

223
00:18:45,000 --> 00:18:50,000
*Thank goodness, she doesn't seem to have overheard our raunchy conversation.*

224
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:52,000
*I breathe a little easier.*

225
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:57,000
*I'm not sure if it's because I just moved up a grade, but class is a drag.*

226
00:18:57,000 --> 00:19:04,000
*I inevitably find myself mechanically writing notes, my mind drifting, as I try to stifle the occasional yawn.*

227
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:17,000
*Fifty minutes taking notes, rinse, and repeat. Perform this cycle umpteen times, each one feeling longer than the last, as my boredom grows, and I finally reach the promised land: after school.*

228
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:22,000
Yoichi: "I really wish they had janitors to do the cleanup duty instead."

229
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Kakeru: "I hear you, man."

230
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:29,000
*Yoichi's complaints go in one ear and out the other as I sweep the hallway.*

231
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:35,000
*Fortunately, cleaning the hallway is easy work. I want to get this done and go home.*

232
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Yoichi: "By the way, I totally found some."

233
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Kakeru: "Found what?"

234
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Yoichi: "Cosplay pictures of Kujo."

235
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah?"

236
00:19:42,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Yoichi: "It's such a minor anime that it took me longer than I expected. I just found them a second ago, though. Wanna see?"

237
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Kakeru: "I saw it in real life, so I'm good."

238
00:19:53,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Yoichi: "In real life, huh? You lucky dog. Man, Kujo-san sure is something, isn't she? No touch-ups and she's still super cute. Sexy as hell, to boot."

239
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:04,000
Kakeru: "Touch-ups?"

240
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:11,000
Yoichi: "Usually you, y'know, tinker with photos. Enlarge the eyes here, smooth the skin out there."

241
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:16,000
Kakeru: "Huh. I had no idea. And you can tell if something's been touched up?"

242
00:20:16,000 --> 00:20:24,000
Yoichi: "Sure can. Their skin will look unnaturally smooth and shiny, kinda doll-like. But Kujo-san? Man oh man."

243
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:27,000
*He moves a little towards the classroom door.*

244
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:33,000
*And then he sticks out his phone so the camera lens is pointed into the classroom.*

245
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:36,000
Kakeru: "Quit trying to sneak a photo."

246
00:20:36,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Yoichi: "I'm not. I'm comparing. Here, check it out."

247
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
Kakeru: "Hmm?"

248
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:42,000
*I peer at his phone.*

249
00:20:42,000 --> 00:20:46,000
*There on the screen is the picture of Kujo blushing her head off.*

250
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:49,000
*And meanwhile, in the classroom, is the real Kujo.*

251
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:53,000
*She's talking with Ms. Naruse, a serious look on her face.*

252
00:20:53,000 --> 00:20:56,000
Yoichi: "See? Just like the picture, right?"

253
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:59,000
Kakeru: "No clue. I'm the wrong guy to ask."

254
00:20:59,000 --> 00:21:07,000
Yoichi: "Oh come on, seriously? Check out those slender legs, that tight waist. This photo wasn't shopped, that's for sure."

255
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:15,000
Yoichi: "As you can see, they also didn't touch up her curves in this photo. You do know what that means, right, Kakeru?"

256
00:21:15,000 --> 00:21:16,000
Kakeru: "Nope."

257
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:23,000
Yoichi: "If you've got a perfect model of her figure, then you can imagine exactly what she'd look like naked!"

258
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Kakeru: "Right, sure, whatever. Mind keeping it down a little?"

259
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:31,000
Yoichi: "Can't you just picture Kujo-san's bangin' body?!"

260
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:36,000
Kakeru: "Are you doing this shit on purpose?! Quit freaking yelling!"

261
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:39,000
*Flustered, I glance at the classroom.*

262
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:40,000
*...*

263
00:21:40,000 --> 00:21:45,000
*Crap, Ms. Naruse is looking our way, and Kujo is hanging her head.*

264
00:21:45,000 --> 00:21:49,000
*Figures. They overheard, right? Of course they did.*

265
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:52,000
Satsuki: "Niimi-kun, care to step inside?"

266
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:53,000
Kakeru: "'Ulp?"

267
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:55,000
*My eyes pop. Why me?!*

268
00:21:55,000 --> 00:21:57,000
*Are you serious? Why JUST me?!*

269
00:21:57,000 --> 00:21:59,000
Yoichi: "Good luck, champ!"

270
00:21:59,000 --> 00:22:01,000
Kakeru: "You're coming with me."

271
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,000
Yoichi: "Like hell. She didn't even ask for me. Like I wanna stand there and get yelled at."

272
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,000
Kakeru: "Dammit."

273
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:15,000
*This is how it always goes. Whenever Yoichi's in the picture, I'm the one who ends up holding the bag.*

274
00:22:15,000 --> 00:22:19,000
*I prop the broom against the wall and trudge into the classroom.*

275
00:22:19,000 --> 00:22:21,000
Kakeru: "Wh-What is it?"

276
00:22:21,000 --> 00:22:26,000
Satsuki: "Niimi-kun, have you noticed anything out of the ordinary?"

277
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,000
Kakeru: "Pardon?"

278
00:22:27,000 --> 00:22:28,000
Miyako: "N-No, um...!"

279
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,000
Kakeru: "...?"

280
00:22:29,000 --> 00:22:35,000
*I was absolutely certain she was going to yell at me for our dumbass conversation.*

281
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:42,000
*Instead, I just get asked some random question, and for no apparent reason, Kujo is freaking out.*

282
00:22:42,000 --> 00:22:44,000
*What the heck is going on?*

283
00:22:44,000 --> 00:22:48,000
Satsuki: "You showed that thing to Niimi-kun, right?"

284
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:50,000
Miyako: "W-Well, yes, I did."

285
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:51,000
Kakeru: "What thing?"

286
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,000
Satsuki: "Kujo-san asked me to exorcise it."

287
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
Kakeru: "Wait, what?"

288
00:22:55,000 --> 00:22:56,000
Miyako: "..."

289
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:58,000
*Kujo blushes and looks away.*

290
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:03,000
*Oh, I see. It must be something private she doesn't want to talk about.*

291
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Kakeru: "Why are you telling me this?"

292
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:10,000
Satsuki: "Well, she said if she's cursed, then you might be too."

293
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Kujo, why do you think we're both cursed?"

294
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Miyako: "L-Let me explain. It's just that, ever since yesterday, some peculiar things have been happening."

295
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
Kakeru: "Such as?"

296
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
Miyako: "..."

297
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:28,000
*She sticks out her hand and shows me what she's been hiding in it.*

298
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:29,000
*The lost hair clip?*

299
00:23:29,000 --> 00:23:31,000
Kakeru: "What about it?"

300
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:34,000
Miyako: "I blink and it's next to me."

301
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:35,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

302
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:42,000
Miyako: "Y-Yeah, I figured you'd react that way. Even I thought maybe I was just fatigued, at first."

303
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:45,000
Kakeru: "Hold on. I'm not following here."

304
00:23:45,000 --> 00:23:56,000
Satsuki: "She told me that even if she puts it in a drawer or something, before she knows it, it's always back in her pocket or somewhere within arm's reach."

305
00:23:56,000 --> 00:23:59,000
Kakeru: "Huh. You mean it's moving on its own?"

306
00:23:59,000 --> 00:24:00,000
Satsuki: "Yep."

307
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:01,000
Miyako: "..."

308
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,000
*Kujo nods.*

309
00:24:02,000 --> 00:24:03,000
*No way.*

310
00:24:03,000 --> 00:24:05,000
Kakeru: "Wow, that's freaky."

311
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:10,000
Satsuki: "I know, right? Legit scary stuff. An actual paranormal phenomenon."

312
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:14,000
Miyako: "Even I think it's ludicrous, but I'm terrified by it."

313
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:18,000
Kakeru: "Which is where the whole exorcism thing comes in?"

314
00:24:18,000 --> 00:24:25,000
Miyako: "Yes. I heard that the shrine's sacred relic shattered yesterday. I thought maybe that was related."

315
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:28,000
Kakeru: "Aha, now I get why you called me in."

316
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:39,000
Satsuki: "If breaking the sacred relic put a curse on people, then you'd probably take the brunt of it, seeing as how you were the one who broke the relic, right?"

317
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:43,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, good point... Wait, no, I didn't break it!"

318
00:24:43,000 --> 00:24:47,000
Satsuki: "Oh, that reminds me about your pay for yesterday."

319
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,000
Kakeru: "Uh, okay?"

320
00:24:48,000 --> 00:24:55,000
Satsuki: "Dad and Granddad are both so mortified by what you did that they've decided not to pay you."

321
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:57,000
Kakeru: "Gimme a break."

322
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:59,000
Miyako: "E-Excuse me, Ms. Naruse?"

323
00:24:59,000 --> 00:25:08,000
Satsuki: "Oh, right, we were talking the exorcism. What do you say we wait a bit longer and see how things play out, before we try that?"

324
00:25:08,000 --> 00:25:11,000
Miyako: "Are you sure that's a good idea?"

325
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:18,000
Satsuki: "Fantastic idea, if I do say so myself. I mean, even if I did exorcise it, it wouldn't do anything."

326
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,000
Miyako: "Huh? R-Really?"

327
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:23,000
Satsuki: "I mean, exorcism is all a sham anyway."

328
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:24,000
Miyako: "..."

329
00:25:24,000 --> 00:25:28,000
Kakeru: "Is it really okay for YOU of all people to say that?"

330
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:39,000
Satsuki: "You know the same thing's true of paranormal phenomena, right? It's all in your head. The only thing exorcism does is put gullible people's minds at ease."

331
00:25:39,000 --> 00:25:44,000
Satsuki: "It's gotta be that, you know, uh, tip of my tongue... gazebo effect."

332
00:25:44,000 --> 00:25:46,000
Miyako: "Placebo effect?"

333
00:25:46,000 --> 00:25:48,000
Satsuki: "Oh, yeah, that."

334
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:50,000
Kakeru: "Some teacher you are."

335
00:25:50,000 --> 00:26:01,000
Satsuki: "Oh, I was just testing you two. So, anyway, even if this turns out to be a real paranormal phenomenon, you don't know for sure that it's a bad thing yet, right?"

336
00:26:01,000 --> 00:26:03,000
Miyako: "I'm pretty sure."

337
00:26:03,000 --> 00:26:08,000
Satsuki: "Did something bad already happen? Like, is it giving you nightmares?"

338
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:10,000
Miyako: "Well, not exactly."

339
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:15,000
Satsuki: "If the answer is no, then what's the harm in just ignoring it?"

340
00:26:15,000 --> 00:26:18,000
Kakeru: "That's such irresponsible advice."

341
00:26:18,000 --> 00:26:25,000
Satsuki: "Mind over matter, especially with the paranormal. The best thing you can do is not worry about it."

342
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:36,000
Satsuki: "I give you my word, as the revered and honorable maiden of the Shrine of the White Serpent's Relic, that you've got a relic on your hands. Probably."

343
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:40,000
Kakeru: "Wait, you mean something similar to the sacred relic?"

344
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Satsuki: "Yup. Legend says the sacred relic you broke was an artifact spirit housed in a jewel bequeathed by the Great White Serpent, I'll have you know."

345
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Kakeru: "It's that important, and you have no problem suggesting replacing it with a papier-mache replica? Are you for real?"

346
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Satsuki: "Of course. It's not like I believe any of that bull."

347
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,000
Kakeru: "..."

348
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,000
*This woman is hopeless.*

349
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:14,000
Satsuki: "Aaaanyhoo, that hair clip is probably also an artifact spirit housed in a relic. Given how the stories go, I doubt it's malicious."

350
00:27:14,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Miyako: "..."

351
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:21,000
Miyako: "Very well, I see your point. Thank you very much, Ms. Naruse. I will wait a bit longer."

352
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:25,000
Satsuki: "All righty! Thanks for the help, Niimi-kun."

353
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:28,000
Kakeru: "Oh, can I get back to cleaning?"

354
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
Satsuki: "I expect you to walk Kujo-san home."

355
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:32,000
Kakeru: "Pardon?"

356
00:27:32,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Satsuki: "You'd have a sweet, worried girl walk home by herself? Heartless, simply heartless."

357
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:40,000
Kakeru: "Huh? I mean, she's fine."

358
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Miyako: "Um, I-I will manage. I rode here on my bike, anyway."

359
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Satsuki: "I don't want to hear about your bike. Come on, you two are young. Nurture that budding romance in your hearts, and whatnot."

360
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:55,000
Kakeru: "Budding romance? What?"

361
00:27:55,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Satsuki: "Come on, I need some fodder for office gossip. 'Looks like they're going steady! How scandalous!'"

362
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:08,000
Kakeru: "You've got a screw loose somewhere. We're not your playthings, I'll have you know."

363
00:28:08,000 --> 00:28:10,000
Miyako: "Erm... Aha, ahaha..."

364
00:28:10,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Satsuki: "Look, you, just take her home. Kujo-san, grab your bike and wait at the gate."

365
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:17,000
Miyako: "Oh, o-okay."

366
00:28:17,000 --> 00:28:22,000
Satsuki: "Niimi-kun, once you're finished cleaning, head straight to the gate."

367
00:28:22,000 --> 00:28:23,000
Kakeru: "Fine."

368
00:28:23,000 --> 00:28:31,000
Satsuki: "Then, ride double on the bike like you're on a date, take a spill, and enjoy the lovely hospital stay!"

369
00:28:31,000 --> 00:28:36,000
Kakeru: "Wait, what?! What are you trying to do to us, Ms. Naruse?!"

370
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:38,000
Satsuki: "I wish I were still young."

371
00:28:38,000 --> 00:28:39,000
Kakeru: "Seriously?"

372
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Satsuki: "All right, I'm off. I have things to do myself. See ya tomorrow."

373
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:52,000
*She raps a stack of printouts on the table to align them, picks up her attendance book, and exits the classroom.*

374
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:58,000
*Admittedly this is par for the course, but I still marvel at how incomprehensible she can be.*

375
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,000
Miyako: "Erm..."

376
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:06,000
*Kujo is completely at a loss, unsure what to do after Ms. Naruse's injunction that we go home together.*

377
00:29:06,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Kakeru: "Sorry, she's always like that."

378
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:15,000
Miyako: "Oh, don't worry. Niimi-kun, you and Ms. Naruse sure are close, aren't you?"

379
00:29:15,000 --> 00:29:17,000
Kakeru: "We go way back, yeah."

380
00:29:17,000 --> 00:29:21,000
Miyako: "Oh, that must be why you were there yesterday."

381
00:29:21,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Kakeru: "Yup, I was helping out her family."

382
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,000
Miyako: "I see."

383
00:29:25,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Yoichi: "Have you heard the rumor going around?"

384
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,000
Kakeru: "Hm?"

385
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,000
*Lunchtime.*

386
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:37,000
*I take a bite of my mediocre sandwich from the cafeteria and engage in mediocre small talk with Yoichi.*

387
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Yoichi: "On a bench..."

388
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Kakeru: "Yeah?"

389
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Yoichi: "...in the park..."

390
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:43,000
Kakeru: "Mm-hmm?"

391
00:29:43,000 --> 00:29:45,000
Yoichi: "...there's a stone statue."

392
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:46,000
Kakeru: "Of what?"

393
00:29:46,000 --> 00:29:47,000
Yoichi: "A girl!"

394
00:29:47,000 --> 00:29:51,000
Kakeru: "That really is the only thing you talk about, isn't it?"

395
00:29:51,000 --> 00:29:57,000
Yoichi: "I mean, it's not like I was interested in the rumor just because it's about a girl."

396
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:58,000
Kakeru: "Liar."

397
00:29:58,000 --> 00:29:59,000
Yoichi: "You got me."

398
00:29:59,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Kakeru: "See?"

399
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Yoichi: "It's supposed to be super lifelike! They say it looks like it'll move at any second."

400
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:12,000
Kakeru: "Man, there goes the city again, wasting more money on dumb promotional crap."

401
00:30:12,000 --> 00:30:15,000
Yoichi: "Wait, why are you blaming the city?"

402
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:26,000
Kakeru: "The city manages the park, don't they? Can't you just see them making a statue of a girl from the anime, trying to milk a little more out of the investment?"

403
00:30:26,000 --> 00:30:33,000
Yoichi: "It doesn't seem like they're behind it. You know the fancy-pants school next to the park?"

404
00:30:33,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Kakeru: "Oh, yeah. Kuho?"

405
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:40,000
Yoichi: "That's the one, Kuho Girls Academy. I heard it's wearing their uniform."

406
00:30:40,000 --> 00:30:41,000
Kakeru: "Huh."

407
00:30:41,000 --> 00:30:51,000
Yoichi: "The statue wasn't there yesterday, but then this morning someone found it sitting there when they went to walk their dog in the park."

408
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:54,000
Kakeru: "Are people actually talking about this?"

409
00:30:54,000 --> 00:30:55,000
Yoichi: "Hm?"

410
00:30:55,000 --> 00:30:59,000
Kakeru: "The only one who even cares about is you, isn't it?"

411
00:30:59,000 --> 00:31:07,000
Yoichi: "Pretty much. I heard some girl mention it to her friends, and I butted in asking for more details, basically."

412
00:31:07,000 --> 00:31:12,000
Kakeru: "And so? Why'd you bring up this statue that nobody cares about?"

413
00:31:12,000 --> 00:31:15,000
Yoichi: "Don't you wanna check the goods?"

414
00:31:15,000 --> 00:31:17,000
Kakeru: "Check what goods?"

415
00:31:17,000 --> 00:31:22,000
Yoichi: "Check whether they made it with panties like a real girl, duh."

416
00:31:22,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Kakeru: "..."

417
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Yoichi: "Kakeru, I think I've seen that look before. That's your look of utter disappointment."

418
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:36,000
Kakeru: "I should hope you've seen it before, seeing as I give you this look several times a day."

419
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Yoichi: "There's something wrong with you, Kakeru! Don't you have a sex drive? Wait, are you gay?!"

420
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:48,000
Kakeru: "What the... You dumbass! Don't just shout stuff like that!"

421
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:58,000
Yoichi: "Well, if you're not gay, then how come you won't come check it out? It's supposed to be cool! Like a real-life human got turned into stone!"

422
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Yoichi: "Let's go appreciate some art! The glory of the human figure! C'mon!"

423
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:09,000
Kakeru: "Why are you so hellbent on this? You can say all you want about art appreciation, I..."

424
00:32:09,000 --> 00:32:13,000
Miyako: "Excuse me. Um. Do you mind if I come along?"

425
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:14,000
Kakeru: "Wha?"

426
00:32:14,000 --> 00:32:15,000
Yoichi: "Huh?"

427
00:32:15,000 --> 00:32:21,000
*We're both so shocked to see her cut into our conversation that our eyes go wide.*

428
00:32:21,000 --> 00:32:27,000
*Even all the girls who were eating with Kujo until a moment ago are looking on in shock.*

429
00:32:27,000 --> 00:32:31,000
Yoichi: "Kujo, are you interested in her panties too?"

430
00:32:31,000 --> 00:32:32,000
Miyako: "P-P...?!"

431
00:32:32,000 --> 00:32:34,000
Kakeru: "Knock it off."

432
00:32:34,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Yoichi: "Sorry, just a joke. You want to see the statue at the park, too?"

433
00:32:39,000 --> 00:32:43,000
Miyako: "Yes. It only appeared there yesterday, right?"

434
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:45,000
Yoichi: "Yeah, seems like."

435
00:32:45,000 --> 00:32:53,000
Miyako: "In that case, they would have had to bring it over early in the morning or late at night, wouldn't they?"

436
00:32:53,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Yoichi: "Oh, yeah. Good point."

437
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:09,000
Miyako: "I can't stop thinking about how strange that is. I would assume that, even if the city had commissioned a park monument, they would install it in the middle of the day. You know, some time more convenient."

438
00:33:09,000 --> 00:33:14,000
Kakeru: "Huh, interesting. Now that you mention it, it is kind of weird."

439
00:33:14,000 --> 00:33:16,000
Miyako: "Right? It's odd."

440
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, no question about it."

441
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Yoichi: "So, are you more interested now, Kakeru?"

442
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Kakeru: "Pains me to admit it, but yeah, I am. Basically, someone else must have put it there for their own reasons."

443
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Yoichi: "I'm telling you man, it's art. Anti-establishment stuff. Like tagging an underpass."

444
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:36,000
Kakeru: "Art, huh."

445
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:43,000
Miyako: "There's just something about it that seems really mysterious to me. Do you mind if I come along?"

446
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:47,000
Yoichi: "Cool with me. You don't mind, do you, Kakeru?"

447
00:33:47,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Kakeru: "That's a fine question considering I haven't agreed on going yet."

448
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:57,000
Yoichi: "Be that way. Kujo-san and I will just have to go together."

449
00:33:57,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Kakeru: "Good point, you can't be trusted. I'll have to come along. It'll be the three of us."

450
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:05,000
Yoichi: "What about you two?"

451
00:34:05,000 --> 00:34:08,000
*Yoichi invites Kujo's friends along as well.*

452
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:12,000
*They glance his way and shake their heads, looking dubious.*

453
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:14,000
Yoichi: "Ah man, shot down."

454
00:34:14,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Kakeru: "Well then, I guess it'll be the three of us going to inspect this so-called work of art."

455
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:25,000
Miyako: "Thank you. I shall see you both after school."

456
00:34:25,000 --> 00:34:28,000
*With a quick bow, Kujo returns to her seat.*

457
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,000
*...*

458
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,000
*Hmm.*

459
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:42,000
Yoichi: "Man, what a shock. That might be the first time I've actually talked with Kujo-san. I guess she's the type who can really jump into a conversation when she wants to."

460
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:49,000
Kakeru: "Apparently we've been reading her all wrong; she might actually be surprisingly sociable."

461
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:53,000
Yoichi: "I feel like she and I might get along well."

462
00:34:53,000 --> 00:35:00,000
Kakeru: "Don't do anything stupid. If you do anything to Kujo, you can kiss your life in this town goodbye."

463
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:02,000
Yoichi: "Oh, you're exaggerating."

464
00:35:02,000 --> 00:35:03,000
Yoichi: "..."

465
00:35:03,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Yoichi: "Oh, wait. Her dad runs the Corona Group."

466
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:09,000
Kakeru: "If she gets hurt, heads are gonna roll."

467
00:35:09,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Yoichi: "If things get bad, maybe I could lick her shoes or something?"

468
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:17,000
Kakeru: "You're the only one who'd enjoy that."

469
00:35:17,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Yoichi: "Heck yeah. I want to lick them till they're nice and wet. God, I hope they taste nasty..."

470
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:26,000
Kakeru: "Are you for real?"

471
00:35:26,000 --> 00:35:29,000
*I sigh and bite into my yakisoba sandwich.*

472
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:30,000
*That was strange...*

473
00:35:30,000 --> 00:35:31,000
*...*

474
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:33,000
*She was oddly serious.*

475
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:40,000
*While I could always chalk it up to that overwhelming sense of responsibility of hers, something's bugging me.*

476
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:42,000
*Well, it's probably no big deal.*

477
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:43,000
Yoichi: "Say, Kakeru."

478
00:35:43,000 --> 00:35:44,000
Kakeru: "Yeah?"

479
00:35:44,000 --> 00:35:49,000
Yoichi: "If I screw things up, you'll lick Kujo-san's shoes with me, right?"

480
00:35:49,000 --> 00:35:51,000
Kakeru: "I ain't licking shit!"

481
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:53,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry it took so long."

482
00:35:53,000 --> 00:35:55,000
*Kujo arrives leading her bike.*

483
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:58,000
*Me, Yoichi and Kujo—what an odd combination.*

484
00:35:58,000 --> 00:36:00,000
Yoichi: "All right, let's get going!"

485
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:02,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, whatever."

486
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:05,000
Miyako: "It's the park over that way, right?"

487
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:08,000
Yoichi: "Yup. It's not even ten minutes away."

488
00:36:08,000 --> 00:36:13,000
Miyako: "Oh, you can put your bag in my bike basket, if you'd like."

489
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:15,000
Yoichi: "Really? Thanks."

490
00:36:15,000 --> 00:36:17,000
Miyako: "You too, Niimi-kun."

491
00:36:17,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Kakeru: "I'll be fine. Looks pretty full already."

492
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Miyako: "Then do you want to handle it?"

493
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Yoichi: "No, I don't think he can handle it."

494
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,000
Kakeru: "Ha ha, very funny."

495
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:34,000
Miyako: "Oh, I just meant to ask if he wanted to hang it off the handlebars. I-I'm sorry."

496
00:36:34,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Kakeru: "No need to apologize."

497
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:40,000
Yoichi: "Boy, Kujo-san, I can't even handle how serious you are."

498
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Miyako: "R-Really? Me?"

499
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:49,000
Kakeru: "Don't take him seriously. This dimwit talks out of his butt about ninety percent of the time."

500
00:36:49,000 --> 00:36:53,000
Yoichi: "Well that's rude! More like one hundred percent!"

501
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Kakeru: "Case in point."

502
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Miyako: "Oh."

503
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Yoichi: "We're losing Kujo-san since she can't keep up with all of our nonsense!"

504
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:04,000
Kakeru: "Just you and your nonsense, actually."

505
00:37:04,000 --> 00:37:08,000
*Things are a little strange the whole way to the park.*

506
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:11,000
*Yoichi natters on, and I respond halfheartedly.*

507
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:14,000
*Kujo, in contrast, doesn't really speak.*

508
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:18,000
*I don't think Yoichi is right about why she's gone quiet, though.*

509
00:37:18,000 --> 00:37:23,000
*She's not having trouble keeping up; rather, she's deep in thought.*

510
00:37:23,000 --> 00:37:25,000
*Something has her on edge.*

511
00:37:25,000 --> 00:37:29,000
*Could it be that paranormal phenomenon we talked about yesterday?*

512
00:37:29,000 --> 00:37:32,000
*Or maybe she has a clue about the statue?*

513
00:37:32,000 --> 00:37:35,000
*Well, either way, we'll know soon enough.*

514
00:37:35,000 --> 00:37:37,000
Yoichi: "Oh, is that it?"

515
00:37:37,000 --> 00:37:39,000
*Yoichi points as we reach the park.*

516
00:37:39,000 --> 00:37:41,000
Kakeru: "Yikes. Not what I expected."

517
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:44,000
*A realistic statue is sitting on the bench.*

518
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:46,000
*A statue of a female student.*

519
00:37:46,000 --> 00:37:50,000
*And it is indeed wearing a familiar school uniform.*

520
00:37:50,000 --> 00:37:54,000
*The statue makes her look like a rather charming girl.*

521
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
Miyako: "She looks like she's in pain."

522
00:37:57,000 --> 00:37:59,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, definitely."

523
00:37:59,000 --> 00:38:13,000
*It's shockingly detailed, enough that even someone like me, who knows nothing about art, can tell. But in spite of that, there's no one else checking it out, presumably because of how damn spooky it is.*

524
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:17,000
*The girl is seated on the bench with a smartphone in her hand.*

525
00:38:17,000 --> 00:38:23,000
*The pose makes it look like she's just here to take a quick a break, but her face is anguished.*

526
00:38:23,000 --> 00:38:32,000
*The sight of a sweet-looking girl in apparent agony has probably been scaring off anybody curious enough to come check it out.*

527
00:38:32,000 --> 00:38:36,000
*I can almost feel the incredible terror she's experiencing.*

528
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:42,000
Yoichi: "If that famous statue is The Thinker... would you call this The Sufferer?"

529
00:38:42,000 --> 00:38:53,000
Kakeru: "Why would they put something like this in the park? Shouldn't they keep stuff like this in... Uh, what do sculptors call their workplace? An atelier?"

530
00:38:53,000 --> 00:38:58,000
Miyako: "Maybe they had some reason why they didn't want to keep it there."

531
00:38:58,000 --> 00:39:05,000
Yoichi: "You mean like, 'My master won't acknowledge my masterpiece, so I'll have to show it to the world!'"

532
00:39:05,000 --> 00:39:15,000
Kakeru: "Even if their goal was to make some waves, this is an outrageous amount of effort. Imagine how long this statue must've taken to make."

533
00:39:15,000 --> 00:39:22,000
Yoichi: "You said it. Heck, how did they even carry it here? Think it walked all the way here on its own?"

534
00:39:22,000 --> 00:39:27,000
Kakeru: "Well, it does look like it could start moving at any moment."

535
00:39:27,000 --> 00:39:35,000
Yoichi: "Man, I bet she smells nice. And her chest is probably soft too... and a few other places I'd like to inspect."

536
00:39:35,000 --> 00:39:36,000
Kakeru: "No touching."

537
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:45,000
Yoichi: "Aww, but we came all this way! We can't leave without pushing a few sexual harassment boundaries, like...! Wait, what?"

538
00:39:45,000 --> 00:39:47,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

539
00:39:47,000 --> 00:39:50,000
Yoichi: "Does this spot seem weird to you?"

540
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:52,000
Kakeru: "Hey, I said no touching!"

541
00:39:52,000 --> 00:39:56,000
*Ignoring my warning, Yoichi fusses with the statue.*

542
00:39:56,000 --> 00:40:02,000
*I can't believe he's going to cop a feel from a statue. What is this dude's deal?*

543
00:40:02,000 --> 00:40:04,000
Yoichi: "Look here. See?"

544
00:40:04,000 --> 00:40:06,000
Miyako: "Oh. Her fingernails?"

545
00:40:06,000 --> 00:40:09,000
Yoichi: "Yeah. This part isn't stone."

546
00:40:09,000 --> 00:40:11,000
Miyako: "Could they be real?"

547
00:40:11,000 --> 00:40:14,000
Kakeru: "Hey, cut it out with the spooky stuff."

548
00:40:14,000 --> 00:40:20,000
Yoichi: "No, don't you think so too? It's like someone pasted on real fingernails."

549
00:40:20,000 --> 00:40:26,000
Kakeru: "Putting real fingernails on such a lifelike statue... That's just messed up."

550
00:40:26,000 --> 00:40:33,000
Yoichi: "They were obviously trying to send a message. Why else use real nails here, when they...? Uh-oh."

551
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:34,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

552
00:40:34,000 --> 00:40:35,000
Kakeru: "Whoa."

553
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:37,000
*Yoichi brushes the nail, and...*

554
00:40:37,000 --> 00:40:39,000
*...it falls right off.*

555
00:40:39,000 --> 00:40:42,000
*The statue's fingernail just fell off.*

556
00:40:42,000 --> 00:40:43,000
Yoichi: "..."

557
00:40:43,000 --> 00:40:44,000
Miyako: "..."

558
00:40:44,000 --> 00:40:45,000
Kakeru: "..."

559
00:40:45,000 --> 00:40:46,000
Yoichi: "Oh shit."

560
00:40:46,000 --> 00:40:49,000
*Yoichi whispers after several seconds of silence.*

561
00:40:49,000 --> 00:40:50,000
*For crying out loud.*

562
00:40:50,000 --> 00:40:53,000
Kakeru: "That's why I told you, no touching!"

563
00:40:53,000 --> 00:41:05,000
Yoichi: "Oh shit, wha'do I do, wha'do I do, wha'do I do?! How screwed am I? Oh my God, I am SO screwed. Are they gonna yell at me? Arrest me? Lock me up and throw away the key?!"

564
00:41:05,000 --> 00:41:10,000
Kakeru: "How would I know, dude? Ah, man, you sure screwed up this time."

565
00:41:10,000 --> 00:41:21,000
Yoichi: "No way. No way! There's gotta be a way outta this, right?! Glue! All I gotta do is glue it back on, right?! It'll be like nothing ever happened, see?!"

566
00:41:21,000 --> 00:41:22,000
Miyako: "Hold it."

567
00:41:22,000 --> 00:41:30,000
Yoichi: "Huh? You don't think it'll work? But I'll just glue it back on there! You really don't think it'll work?!"

568
00:41:30,000 --> 00:41:32,000
Miyako: "Look at her finger."

569
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:33,000
Yoichi: "Huh?"

570
00:41:33,000 --> 00:41:35,000
Miyako: "It's bleeding."

571
00:41:35,000 --> 00:41:36,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

572
00:41:36,000 --> 00:41:38,000
*I look at the statue's finger.*

573
00:41:38,000 --> 00:41:39,000
*...*

574
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:41,000
*Are you freaking kidding me?*

575
00:41:41,000 --> 00:41:42,000
Yoichi: "..."

576
00:41:42,000 --> 00:41:47,000
Yoichi: "Hey, that's for real! It's seriously bleeding! How is this possible?!"

577
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:50,000
Miyako: "It's a statue that bleeds..."

578
00:41:50,000 --> 00:41:54,000
Kakeru: "Hey, hold on. Just calm down. Isn't it just ink?"

579
00:41:54,000 --> 00:41:58,000
Yoichi: "But it looks like blood! It totally looks like blood!"

580
00:41:58,000 --> 00:42:08,000
Kakeru: "Maybe they just made something that looks like blood? Seriously, everybody needs to chill out. There's just no way that statues can bleed."

581
00:42:08,000 --> 00:42:15,000
*I try to calm the others down while I pick up the fingernail that fell to the ground near the statue's feet.*

582
00:42:15,000 --> 00:42:16,000
*...*

583
00:42:16,000 --> 00:42:19,000
*The underside is awfully raw-looking.*

584
00:42:19,000 --> 00:42:25,000
*Almost like there's a portion of skin attached. The red drops on it look like dried blood, too.*

585
00:42:25,000 --> 00:42:27,000
*Is it the sculptor's fingernail?*

586
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:32,000
*And the blood too... Maybe they drew some of their own and put it in the statue?*

587
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:34,000
*But that'd be insane.*

588
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:35,000
Miyako: "An Artifact."

589
00:42:35,000 --> 00:42:36,000
Kakeru: "...?"

590
00:42:36,000 --> 00:42:39,000
*My thoughts stop upon hearing Kujo's murmur.*

591
00:42:39,000 --> 00:42:41,000
Kakeru: "What was that?"

592
00:42:41,000 --> 00:42:44,000
Miyako: "O-Oh, it's nothing. I'm sorry."

593
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:50,000
*All I get in response is an apology. She doesn't even try answering the question.*

594
00:42:50,000 --> 00:42:57,000
*I hope her imagination isn't running wild, connecting this with the paranormal phenomenon from before.*

595
00:42:57,000 --> 00:43:01,000
Yoichi: "Hey, what do we do now? Do we high-tail it?"

596
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:07,000
Kakeru: "This is a vicious prank. We can't just leave something like this here in the park."

597
00:43:07,000 --> 00:43:10,000
Miyako: "We should contact the authorities."

598
00:43:10,000 --> 00:43:14,000
Kakeru: "Oh, yeah, maybe... Actually, yeah. Let's do that."

599
00:43:14,000 --> 00:43:19,000
Yoichi: "Huh? No way. No cops. They'll want to take me in, for sure!"

600
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:23,000
Kakeru: "You're being paranoid. Kujo, do you have work today?"

601
00:43:23,000 --> 00:43:25,000
Miyako: "Huh? Um, yes, I do."

602
00:43:25,000 --> 00:43:28,000
Kakeru: "Yoichi, you know Nine Ball, right?"

603
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:30,000
Yoichi: "Oh, yeah, sure."

604
00:43:30,000 --> 00:43:34,000
Kakeru: "Walk Kujo over there for me. I'll talk to the police."

605
00:43:34,000 --> 00:43:35,000
Yoichi: "Roger that!"

606
00:43:35,000 --> 00:43:36,000
Miyako: "Huh? But..."

607
00:43:36,000 --> 00:43:42,000
Kakeru: "You shouldn't let this nonsense make you late for work. It's fine; just leave it to me."

608
00:43:42,000 --> 00:43:43,000
Miyako: "..."

609
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:50,000
Yoichi: "C'mon now, Kujo-san. Let's head out. Manly Man Kakeru here has got our backs on this one."

610
00:43:50,000 --> 00:43:53,000
Miyako: "Oh, um, okay. See you later."

611
00:43:53,000 --> 00:43:58,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, and when I'm done, I'll stop by the cafe and report."

612
00:43:58,000 --> 00:44:06,000
Yoichi: "Sounds like a plan! I'll be sipping on some tea, awaiting your return, good sir! Let's mosey, Kujo-san."

613
00:44:06,000 --> 00:44:07,000
Miyako: "O-Okay."

614
00:44:07,000 --> 00:44:13,000
*The two of them depart, Yoichi with a spring in his step and Kujo looking unconvinced.*

615
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:14,000
Kakeru: "..."

616
00:44:14,000 --> 00:44:15,000
Kakeru: "Haahh..."

617
00:44:15,000 --> 00:44:16,000
*I let out a sigh.*

618
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:25,000
*A combination of simple annoyance at the situation and first-time jitters about making a police report has got me nervous all around.*

619
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:30,000
*I backed myself into a corner here by trying to show off in front of Kujo.*

620
00:44:30,000 --> 00:44:31,000
*...*

621
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:32,000
*A bloody fingernail.*

622
00:44:32,000 --> 00:44:34,000
*A statue that bleeds.*

623
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:38,000
*Well, I can't just walk away from this whole thing.*

624
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:42,000
*I set the fingernail on the statue and pull out my phone.*

625
00:44:42,000 --> 00:44:48,000
*My heart is pounding like mad as I slowly dial "110" on my phone and call the police.*

626
00:44:48,000 --> 00:45:04,000
*They let me off the hook sooner than I was dreading. Honestly, they looked totally put out, like they were just going through the motions and trying to get out of there. Eventually, I made my way to the cafe, arriving as the sun was setting.*

627
00:45:04,000 --> 00:45:07,000
*Slightly exhausted, I open the door and enter.*

628
00:45:07,000 --> 00:45:08,000
Miyako: "Welcome."

629
00:45:08,000 --> 00:45:11,000
*Kujo calls out instantly, a practiced reaction.*

630
00:45:11,000 --> 00:45:17,000
*Once she realizes it's me, however, a hint of concern touches her business-like expression.*

631
00:45:17,000 --> 00:45:19,000
Miyako: "Did everything work out?"

632
00:45:19,000 --> 00:45:24,000
Kakeru: "All they did was ask for my school and contact info. Where's Yoichi?"

633
00:45:24,000 --> 00:45:27,000
Miyako: "Over there, at the seat near the window."

634
00:45:27,000 --> 00:45:31,000
*I track Kujo's eyes to discover Yoichi waving me down.*

635
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:35,000
*I resettle my bag on my shoulder and head over to the table.*

636
00:45:35,000 --> 00:45:37,000
Yoichi: "That sure was quick."

637
00:45:37,000 --> 00:45:38,000
Kakeru: "Yeah."

638
00:45:38,000 --> 00:45:43,000
*Once I set down my bag and take a seat, Kujo comes over with a glass of water.*

639
00:45:43,000 --> 00:45:45,000
Miyako: "Are you ready to order?"

640
00:45:45,000 --> 00:45:48,000
Kakeru: "Uh, sure, let me get a cola, please."

641
00:45:48,000 --> 00:45:50,000
Miyako: "Very good. Coming right up."

642
00:45:50,000 --> 00:45:53,000
*She gives a bow before going to the kitchen.*

643
00:45:53,000 --> 00:45:59,000
*We've talked a lot more now, but the distance between us hasn't really changed, I guess.*

644
00:45:59,000 --> 00:46:09,000
Yoichi: "Man, Kujo-san in her waitress outfit is a sight for sore eyes. She's super cute, but in a different way from her cosplay, know what I mean?"

645
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:15,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. She's got a different vibe from when she's at school, that's for sure."

646
00:46:15,000 --> 00:46:19,000
Yoichi: "So, what happened? Am I going to the slammer?"

647
00:46:19,000 --> 00:46:24,000
Kakeru: "I told them that I was the one who ripped the fingernail off."

648
00:46:24,000 --> 00:46:28,000
Yoichi: "Kakeru, you're the best guy in the world! Marry me!"

649
00:46:28,000 --> 00:46:32,000
Kakeru: "Hell no. Anyway, explaining was a pain in the ass."

650
00:46:32,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Yoichi: "You didn't tell them that we were there with you?"

651
00:46:36,000 --> 00:46:44,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I told them that part. Said that I was with my friends, but one had to go to work, so only I stuck around."

652
00:46:44,000 --> 00:46:51,000
Yoichi: "They didn't dig any further? You know, like, 'Jig's up! Who did it?!" Something like that?"

653
00:46:51,000 --> 00:47:00,000
Kakeru: "Nope. The cops came, but they looked like they didn't care. From their uniforms, I guess they were both neighborhood beat cops."

654
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:03,000
Yoichi: "So was it all just a prank, or what?"

655
00:47:03,000 --> 00:47:10,000
Kakeru: "Dunno. I will say, once they saw the fingernail and the blood, they looked a lot more serious."

656
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:19,000
Kakeru: "They asked for my name and a bunch of other stuff, and then they told me to scram. I spent longer waiting than talking to them."

657
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:25,000
Yoichi: "Huh. Try and do the right thing by reporting it, and they treat you like dirt, huh?"

658
00:47:25,000 --> 00:47:37,000
Kakeru: "I mean, being all friendly wouldn't have helped me either. Though I will say that something about the way they treated me like it was all my fault didn't sit right with me."

659
00:47:37,000 --> 00:47:44,000
Yoichi: "Hey, you remember the statue's uniform? Isn't that girl over there wearing the same one?"

660
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:45,000
Kakeru: "Over where?"

661
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:46,000
Yoichi: "There."

662
00:47:46,000 --> 00:47:50,000
*He jerks his chin a little, urging me to look behind me.*

663
00:47:50,000 --> 00:47:51,000
???: "..."

664
00:47:51,000 --> 00:47:59,000
*Sitting at a table near the entrance is a short-haired girl wearing a Kuho Girls Academy uniform, just like the statue.*

665
00:47:59,000 --> 00:48:04,000
*I watch as she calmly digs her spoon into her dessert and takes a bite.*

666
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:07,000
Kakeru: "Oh, you mean the Parfait Queen."

667
00:48:07,000 --> 00:48:08,000
Yoichi: "'Scuse me?"

668
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:16,000
Kakeru: "She's a regular, so I see her pretty often, and whenever I do, she's always having a parfait. Hence the nickname."

669
00:48:16,000 --> 00:48:20,000
Yoichi: "Wow. She sure is a cutie. Maybe I should go say hi."

670
00:48:20,000 --> 00:48:22,000
Kakeru: "Uh-huh. Knock 'er dead."

671
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:26,000
Yoichi: "Yeah right, like I've got the guts for that."

672
00:48:26,000 --> 00:48:28,000
Kakeru: "Figured as much."

673
00:48:28,000 --> 00:48:30,000
Miyako: "Thank you for waiting."

674
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:34,000
*She silently places the soda and a straw on the table.*

675
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:44,000
*Normally this would be where Kujo would offer a bow and walk away, but instead she holds the tray to her chest and stands there for a moment.*

676
00:48:44,000 --> 00:48:46,000
Miyako: "Um, Niimi-kun?"

677
00:48:46,000 --> 00:48:47,000
Kakeru: "Yeah?"

678
00:48:47,000 --> 00:48:49,000
Miyako: "Do you use LING?"

679
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:52,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I have it on my phone."

680
00:48:52,000 --> 00:48:55,000
Miyako: "Here, I wanted to give you my ID."

681
00:48:55,000 --> 00:48:58,000
*She sets a scrap of paper next to my glass.*

682
00:48:58,000 --> 00:49:06,000
Miyako: "Can you and I chat a little after I'm off work? I'd like to know how your conversation with the authorities went."

683
00:49:06,000 --> 00:49:10,000
Kakeru: "Of course, though there isn't much to talk about."

684
00:49:10,000 --> 00:49:14,000
Miyako: "That's okay. Just for a bit, if you can; I'm curious."

685
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:16,000
Kakeru: "When does your shift end?"

686
00:49:16,000 --> 00:49:19,000
Miyako: "Let's see. Today, I work until eight."

687
00:49:19,000 --> 00:49:22,000
Kakeru: "Okay then, I'll message you around nine."

688
00:49:22,000 --> 00:49:25,000
Miyako: "Thank you. I really appreciate it."

689
00:49:25,000 --> 00:49:31,000
*She gives me a deep bow by way of thanks and goes off to greet a customer who entered the cafe.*

690
00:49:31,000 --> 00:49:32,000
*...*

691
00:49:32,000 --> 00:49:35,000
*Oh shit. I just got a girl's number.*

692
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:37,000
Yoichi: "Hey, lemme see that."

693
00:49:37,000 --> 00:49:39,000
Kakeru: "Not a chance."

694
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:40,000
Yoichi: "Show me."

695
00:49:40,000 --> 00:49:41,000
Kakeru: "Nope."

696
00:49:41,000 --> 00:49:43,000
Yoichi: "Show me, dammit!"

697
00:49:43,000 --> 00:49:45,000
Kakeru: "Hell no, dude!"

698
00:49:45,000 --> 00:49:51,000
*I carefully tuck the note away in my pocket so that Yoichi doesn't steal it from me.*

699
00:49:51,000 --> 00:49:56,000
Yoichi: "Dammit, just let me see it! I wanna chat with Kujo-san on LING, too!"

700
00:49:56,000 --> 00:50:02,000
Kakeru: "Man, there's nothing like a tasty beverage after getting a girl's digits."

701
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:04,000
Yoichi: "Dammit! Why, God, why?!"

702
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:09,000
*Ignoring Yoichi's bitter tears, I wet my whistle with some sweet, sweet cola.*

703
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:12,000
*A hair clip that follows you around.*

704
00:50:12,000 --> 00:50:14,000
*A statue that bleeds.*

705
00:50:14,000 --> 00:50:23,000
*All this occult stuff is kind of freaky, but it's also helping Kujo and me grow closer, so I've got mixed feelings about the whole thing.*

706
00:50:23,000 --> 00:50:30,000
*Honestly, it's enough to make me have the idiotic thought, "Gee, I sure do hope something else happens."*

707
00:50:30,000 --> 00:50:32,000
Yoichi: "All right, Kakeru."

708
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:33,000
Kakeru: "Hmm?"

709
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:36,000
Yoichi: "Just tell me the first and second digit."

710
00:50:36,000 --> 00:50:37,000
Kakeru: "..."

711
00:50:37,000 --> 00:50:39,000
Yoichi: "Okay, just the first!"

712
00:50:39,000 --> 00:50:42,000
Kakeru: "Man, this is one tasty beverage."

713
00:50:42,000 --> 00:50:44,000
Yoichi: "Dammiiiiiiiiiit!"

714
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:45,000
???: "..."

715
00:50:45,000 --> 00:50:46,000
Yoichi: "Oh."

716
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:48,000
Kakeru: "Huh? What's up?"

717
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:50,000
Yoichi: "The Queen glared at me."

718
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:53,000
Kakeru: "No surprise, with the way you're shouting."

719
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:58,000
Yoichi: "No surprise, with the way you won't tell me Kujo-san's ID."

720
00:50:58,000 --> 00:51:03,000
Kakeru: "You know, this beverage is so tasty, I should get another."

721
00:51:03,000 --> 00:51:04,000
Yoichi: "Gah!"

722
00:51:04,000 --> 00:51:10,000
*I kill some time with Yoichi, eat dinner while I'm at it, and, when I'm done, I head back home.*

723
00:51:10,000 --> 00:51:14,000
*I boot up my computer, waiting for the familiar startup sound.*

724
00:51:14,000 --> 00:51:20,000
Sora: "Took you long enough! How dare you take a detour on the way home, you dipshit!"

725
00:51:20,000 --> 00:51:27,000
*...but am instead greeted to by a delightful new recording. I immediately go into the settings and revert it.*

726
00:51:27,000 --> 00:51:34,000
*This virus I've picked up seems awfully persistent. Might be a good idea to change the locks on my place.*

727
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:38,000
*I'm actually not joking. I begin looking up locksmiths online.*

728
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:43,000
*One thing leads to another and I end up surfing the web for a while.*

729
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:44,000
*It's five till nine.*

730
00:51:44,000 --> 00:51:48,000
*I step away from my computer and fidget with my phone.*

731
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:59,000
*Sending a message at exactly nine would probably be coming on too strong, or at least be a little off-putting. Ugh, fretting about this is stressing me out.*

732
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:02,000
*I end up sending the message at 9:03.*

733
00:52:02,000 --> 00:52:07,000
*Maybe Kujo has been waiting this whole time, since I get a reply right away.*

734
00:52:07,000 --> 00:52:11,000
*'Thank you very much for the message. It's me, Kujo.'*

735
00:52:11,000 --> 00:52:15,000
*It's a modest, reserved, and somewhat formal message.*

736
00:52:15,000 --> 00:52:20,000
*However, I'm antisocial and hardly have any friends who are girls.*

737
00:52:20,000 --> 00:52:24,000
*Nah, who am I trying to fool? I don't have a single one.*

738
00:52:24,000 --> 00:52:29,000
*At any rate, even a tepid conversation with a girl is a thing of joy to me.*

739
00:52:29,000 --> 00:52:30,000
Kakeru: "..."

740
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:32,000
*I'm grinning like an idiot.*

741
00:52:32,000 --> 00:52:36,000
*...I must never let Sora or Yoichi see me like this.*

742
00:52:36,000 --> 00:52:42,000
*Trying to keep my enthusiasm in check, I do my level best to prepare a cool and composed reply.*

743
00:52:42,000 --> 00:52:45,000
*"What did you want to talk about?" I reply.*

744
00:52:45,000 --> 00:52:48,000
*Not even a minute later, Kujo zips back a reply.*

745
00:52:48,000 --> 00:52:50,000
*'How did the authorities react?'*

746
00:52:50,000 --> 00:52:58,000
*"The authorities"? Yikes, talk about stuffy. It's one thing to be a little uptight in person, but even on a chat app?*

747
00:52:58,000 --> 00:53:04,000
*I try not to pay it any mind, refocusing myself, and tell her the same thing I told Yoichi.*

748
00:53:04,000 --> 00:53:10,000
*'I detoured by the park on the way back home, but the statue was no longer there.'*

749
00:53:10,000 --> 00:53:12,000
Kakeru: "Did they collect it?"

750
00:53:12,000 --> 00:53:15,000
*I type what I muttered as-is and reply.*

751
00:53:15,000 --> 00:53:20,000
*'It would appear so. Perhaps the police investigation will shed some light?'*

752
00:53:20,000 --> 00:53:31,000
Kakeru: "I'm not so sure. I mean, don't get me wrong. This is the kind of mischief that would terrify little kids, so I'm hoping they find the culprit. But..."

753
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:37,000
*'This is just a hypothesis, but it's possible that statue was actually once a human being.'*

754
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:38,000
Kakeru: "...?"

755
00:53:38,000 --> 00:53:43,000
*She says it's just a hypothesis, but the message seems strangely confident.*

756
00:53:43,000 --> 00:53:49,000
*Slightly at a loss as to how I should answer her, my fingers hover over the screen.*

757
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,000
*If that girl had once been an actual person...*

758
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:53,000
*...*

759
00:53:53,000 --> 00:53:56,000
*How could a person be turned into a stone statue?*

760
00:53:56,000 --> 00:53:58,000
*Like, encasing them in cement?*

761
00:53:58,000 --> 00:54:01,000
*That'd make this some bizarro murder case.*

762
00:54:01,000 --> 00:54:05,000
*If that's what's going on, there'll be a huge uproar.*

763
00:54:05,000 --> 00:54:13,000
*It also means Shiromitsugawa's name will get dragged through the mud yet again. That'd be kind of a bummer, to say the least.*

764
00:54:13,000 --> 00:54:18,000
*But that's not the kind of tongue-in-cheek response Kujo is likely after.*

765
00:54:18,000 --> 00:54:25,000
*I guess she really is into all that occult stuff, huh? I've never really bought into it much myself.*

766
00:54:25,000 --> 00:54:27,000
*'I'm sorry. I was only joking.'*

767
00:54:27,000 --> 00:54:33,000
*Perhaps sensing the bewilderment behind my hesitance to respond, Kujo follows up with that.*

768
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:42,000
*A little flustered by her apology, I try to give a noncommittal reply: "Y'know, a lot of strange things have been going down lately."*

769
00:54:42,000 --> 00:54:45,000
*I try turning the conversation to the hair clip.*

770
00:54:45,000 --> 00:54:56,000
*But maybe she's realized that talking about the occult isn't going to help the conversation along, since she gives me yet another curt reply: "I'm fine. Thank you."*

771
00:54:56,000 --> 00:55:02,000
*We exchange some idle chit-chat until Kujo wishes me goodnight, signaling an end to our talk.*

772
00:55:02,000 --> 00:55:10,000
*I put my phone on sleep mode, set it next to my computer, and sprawl out on my bed, when something catches my eye.*

773
00:55:10,000 --> 00:55:11,000
Kakeru: "..."

774
00:55:11,000 --> 00:55:13,000
*That mysterious plushie.*

775
00:55:13,000 --> 00:55:18,000
*That reminds me, I never did check with Sora whether this was hers.*

776
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:24,000
*I reach out and grab it by its... uh, torso? Head? Anyway, I grab it and pull it over.*

777
00:55:24,000 --> 00:55:27,000
*It's oddly heavy. Unsettlingly warm, too.*

778
00:55:27,000 --> 00:55:32,000
*Maybe, like the stone statue, this thing's insides are also alive.*

779
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:40,000
*I try fiddling with the zipper running down the length of its face, but it doesn't budge. Just for decoration, huh?*

780
00:55:40,000 --> 00:55:41,000
*...*

781
00:55:41,000 --> 00:55:43,000
Kakeru: "This is dumb."

782
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:48,000
*I mutter to myself, setting down the plushie and getting to my feet.*

783
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:50,000
*We've had a huge earthquake.*

784
00:55:50,000 --> 00:55:52,000
*A broken sacred relic.*

785
00:55:52,000 --> 00:55:53,000
*A cursed hair clip.*

786
00:55:53,000 --> 00:55:55,000
*And now a human petrification.*

787
00:55:55,000 --> 00:55:58,000
*I'm afraid to see what happens next.*

788
00:55:58,000 --> 00:56:00,000
Kakeru: "Time for a bath, I think."

789
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:04,000
*Scratching the back of my head, I make my way to the bath.*

790
00:56:04,000 --> 00:56:05,000
Kakeru: "..."

791
00:56:05,000 --> 00:56:10,000
*I wake up a few seconds before my alarm and stop it as soon as it rings.*

792
00:56:10,000 --> 00:56:12,000
*I kick off my comforter and get up.*

793
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:16,000
*Rubbing the sleep from my eyes, I stumble to the bathroom.*

794
00:56:16,000 --> 00:56:20,000
*After heeding nature's call, I brush my teeth and wash my face.*

795
00:56:20,000 --> 00:56:24,000
*I grab a jelly drink from the fridge and walk over to my PC.*

796
00:56:24,000 --> 00:56:30,000
*After it boots up, I begin checking the daily news sites while changing into my uniform.*

797
00:56:30,000 --> 00:56:31,000
Kakeru: "..."

798
00:56:31,000 --> 00:56:32,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

799
00:56:32,000 --> 00:56:34,000
*I grunt absentmindedly.*

800
00:56:34,000 --> 00:56:37,000
*"Missing Girl Discovered as Statue."*

801
00:56:37,000 --> 00:56:40,000
*This headline doesn't make any sense.*

802
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:42,000
*I continue reading the article.*

803
00:56:42,000 --> 00:56:47,000
*She was last seen on the night of the 18th, at the cram school she attended.*

804
00:56:47,000 --> 00:56:55,000
*She never returned home, and late at night, as her parents grew increasingly concerned, they contacted the authorities.*

805
00:56:55,000 --> 00:57:07,000
*A citizen subsequently reported encountering an unusual statue in a local park, and police investigation uncovered that the object in question was not in fact a statue at all.*

806
00:57:07,000 --> 00:57:15,000
*The girl's belongings were found inside the petrified bag, and data was recovered from her petrified cellphone's memory.*

807
00:57:15,000 --> 00:57:25,000
*Several other pivotal factors further confirmed the identity of the statue as the girl herself. How her skin was turned to stone is still unknown.*

808
00:57:25,000 --> 00:57:26,000
*...*

809
00:57:26,000 --> 00:57:33,000
*I go through several news sites, checking the facts at each one, but they're all completely consistent.*

810
00:57:33,000 --> 00:57:35,000
Kakeru: "You can't be serious."

811
00:57:35,000 --> 00:57:41,000
*'This is just a hypothesis, but it's possible that statue was actually once a human being.'*

812
00:57:41,000 --> 00:57:45,000
*Kujo's message from the night before pops into my mind.*

813
00:57:45,000 --> 00:57:49,000
*It can't be... what she was afraid of turned out to be true?*

814
00:57:49,000 --> 00:57:54,000
*No, the truth is undeniable now. That was no statue; it was a person.*

815
00:57:54,000 --> 00:58:02,000
*The fingernail wasn't some prop set up by the sculptor for an elaborate prank. It was the girl's actual fingernail.*

816
00:58:02,000 --> 00:58:03,000
*The blood was real.*

817
00:58:03,000 --> 00:58:05,000
*And her skin was turned to stone...*

818
00:58:05,000 --> 00:58:09,000
*Which means... under the stone was once flesh and warm blood.*

819
00:58:09,000 --> 00:58:10,000
Kakeru: "..."

820
00:58:10,000 --> 00:58:12,000
*I check my timeline on Titter.*

821
00:58:12,000 --> 00:58:13,000
*...*

822
00:58:13,000 --> 00:58:16,000
*A strange disease is turning people to stone.*

823
00:58:16,000 --> 00:58:23,000
*You can smell a whiff of perverse delight running through the posts, among the fear and consternation.*

824
00:58:23,000 --> 00:58:31,000
*One theory claims it's a virus from outer space, and it's crazy how many people are actually standing up for that view.*

825
00:58:31,000 --> 00:58:39,000
*A handful of locals, or just people who know more about the town, are even drawing connections to that lousy anime.*

826
00:58:39,000 --> 00:58:43,000
*Apparently, there's a monster in it that turns people into stone.*

827
00:58:43,000 --> 00:58:52,000
*That faction is claiming that the earthquake awakened the monster, and that it's what's responsible for turning the girl to stone.*

828
00:58:52,000 --> 00:58:58,000
*Until someone deals with the monster, this mystery disease isn't going away, or so they say.*

829
00:58:58,000 --> 00:58:59,000
*This is nuts.*

830
00:58:59,000 --> 00:59:05,000
*But I can't say with complete confidence that they're wrong, and that's frustrating.*

831
00:59:05,000 --> 00:59:11,000
*Someone was turned to stone. That's crazy in and of itself, and yet I saw it with my own eyes.*

832
00:59:11,000 --> 00:59:18,000
*The virus from outer space? The mysterious monster? Bizarre as they sound, one of them might even be right.*

833
00:59:18,000 --> 00:59:20,000
Kakeru: "This is getting weird."

834
00:59:20,000 --> 00:59:26,000
*With a mutter, I dismiss the whole situation as someone else's problem and close my laptop.*

835
00:59:26,000 --> 00:59:29,000
*First, Kujo's paranormal phenomenon.*

836
00:59:29,000 --> 00:59:32,000
*Now, a disease turning people to stone.*

837
00:59:32,000 --> 00:59:38,000
*And from the way Kujo's been acting, I'm starting to think there's some link between the two.*

838
00:59:38,000 --> 00:59:42,000
*What was it Kujo said again? Something about a curse?*

839
00:59:42,000 --> 00:59:50,000
Kakeru: "She said that when the sacred relic broke, it brought down disaster upon Shiromitsugawa. There's no way, right?"

840
00:59:50,000 --> 00:59:54,000
???: "In fact, yes, that is exactly what has transpired."

841
00:59:54,000 --> 00:59:55,000
Kakeru: "..."

842
00:59:55,000 --> 00:59:56,000
Kakeru: "...?!"

843
00:59:56,000 --> 01:00:03,000
*I hear an unfamiliar girl's voice, prompting to me to turn around so fast you can practically hear the whoosh.*

844
01:00:03,000 --> 01:00:04,000
Kakeru: "..."

845
01:00:04,000 --> 01:00:06,000
*Nothing. No one is there.*

846
01:00:06,000 --> 01:00:12,000
*Of course no one's there. This is my apartment. I'm the only one who should be here.*

847
01:00:12,000 --> 01:00:16,000
Kakeru: "Was that you, Sora? Is this some kind of trick? Hey!"

848
01:00:16,000 --> 01:00:17,000
*...*

849
01:00:17,000 --> 01:00:18,000
*......*

850
01:00:18,000 --> 01:00:19,000
*.........*

851
01:00:19,000 --> 01:00:20,000
*No response.*

852
01:00:20,000 --> 01:00:23,000
*Am I imagining things? Hearing things?*

853
01:00:23,000 --> 01:00:27,000
*Or maybe I'm a victim of a paranormal phenomenon of my own?*

854
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:28,000
*...*

855
01:00:28,000 --> 01:00:29,000
*......*

856
01:00:29,000 --> 01:00:30,000
*.........*

857
01:00:30,000 --> 01:00:33,000
Kakeru: "Dammit, this is dumb. How stupid am I?"

858
01:00:33,000 --> 01:00:38,000
*I try to shame myself into acting tougher, after getting spooked by the voice.*

859
01:00:38,000 --> 01:00:42,000
*I gulp down my jelly drink while roughly scratching my head.*

860
01:00:42,000 --> 01:00:51,000
*Unable to completely shake off the feeling of dread, I quickly finish getting ready for the day, while constantly checking over my shoulder.*

861
01:00:51,000 --> 01:00:54,000
*I then make my way to school, earlier than usual.*

862
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:55,000
???: "..."

863
01:00:55,000 --> 01:00:58,000
???: "And here I thought it was about time."

864
01:00:58,000 --> 01:00:59,000
???: "..."

865
01:00:59,000 --> 01:01:03,000
???: "Seems I should see how things play out a little more."

866
01:01:03,000 --> 01:01:04,000
Kakeru: "..."

867
01:01:04,000 --> 01:01:08,000
*Nothing from class is sticking, even more so than usual.*

868
01:01:08,000 --> 01:01:13,000
*Yoichi started chattering away at me the moment I walked in the classroom.*

869
01:01:13,000 --> 01:01:23,000
*And Sora, not knowing that I left early, waited for me until she was almost late for school, so you can add guilt over that to my list of concerns.*

870
01:01:23,000 --> 01:01:29,000
*During lunch, the case of the petrified girl ends up being the talk of the school.*

871
01:01:29,000 --> 01:01:32,000
*Kujo looks more tense than usual, too.*

872
01:01:32,000 --> 01:01:33,000
*...*

873
01:01:33,000 --> 01:01:41,000
*Also, the more I remember it, the less confident I feel that the voice I heard was just my ears playing tricks on me.*

874
01:01:41,000 --> 01:01:46,000
*No way am I crazy enough to hear a voice so crystal clear like that.*

875
01:01:46,000 --> 01:01:48,000
*So then, what did I hear?*

876
01:01:48,000 --> 01:01:54,000
*And for that matter, what's the deal with that plushie that just appeared in my room one day?*

877
01:01:54,000 --> 01:01:55,000
*...*

878
01:01:55,000 --> 01:02:00,000
*Is it some cursed toy? Or maybe an artifact spirit that brings good luck?*

879
01:02:00,000 --> 01:02:01,000
Kakeru: "..."

880
01:02:01,000 --> 01:02:04,000
*I heave a brief sigh and collapse on my desk.*

881
01:02:04,000 --> 01:02:07,000
*Maybe I should try talking to Ms. Naruse about it.*

882
01:02:07,000 --> 01:02:15,000
*Or maybe I could bring it up with Kujo? Like, "You know, I'm having a run-in with the paranormal, too!" Or something?*

883
01:02:15,000 --> 01:02:18,000
*I bet it'd make a great conversation starter.*

884
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:25,000
*That kind of wishful thinking is the only thing keeping me from being totally down in the dumps.*

885
01:02:25,000 --> 01:02:27,000
*God, I'm so pathetic.*

886
01:02:27,000 --> 01:02:30,000
*At the sound of the bell, we stand and bow.*

887
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:32,000
*That's the last morning class.*

888
01:02:32,000 --> 01:02:37,000
*Maybe my mood will improve a little after I eat some lunch and fill my belly.*

889
01:02:37,000 --> 01:02:38,000
*...*

890
01:02:38,000 --> 01:02:39,000
*Oh, crap.*

891
01:02:39,000 --> 01:02:42,000
Yoichi: "Kakeru my man, let's get our grub on!"

892
01:02:42,000 --> 01:02:47,000
*Yoichi comes over to my desk with a convenience store bag in hand.*

893
01:02:47,000 --> 01:02:50,000
Yoichi: "What's the matter? Not hungry?"

894
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:54,000
Kakeru: "I am indeed hungry. Problem is, I don't have a lunch."

895
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:57,000
Yoichi: "Huh? You didn't buy anything?"

896
01:02:57,000 --> 01:03:03,000
Kakeru: "I forgot to pick something up this morning. I'll have to stop by the cafe."

897
01:03:03,000 --> 01:03:05,000
Yoichi: "No sweat, I'll tag along."

898
01:03:05,000 --> 01:03:08,000
Kakeru: "You can start eating without me, you know?"

899
01:03:08,000 --> 01:03:15,000
Yoichi: "I don't want to eat alone. Besides, I'm going to buy a drink, so coming along's no big..."

900
01:03:15,000 --> 01:03:18,000
Yoichi: "Whoa, what the heck? What's going on?!"

901
01:03:18,000 --> 01:03:22,000
*Out of nowhere, the fire alarm goes off, a shrill, blaring sound.*

902
01:03:22,000 --> 01:03:25,000
Yoichi: "Huh? What is this? A fire drill?"

903
01:03:25,000 --> 01:03:29,000
Kakeru: "Normally they'd have said announced it beforehand, if so."

904
01:03:29,000 --> 01:03:35,000
Yoichi: "Huh? Why are you so calm? Though I have to admit, it's so manly I'm about to swoon."

905
01:03:35,000 --> 01:03:41,000
Kakeru: "I'm totally freaking out, dude. You're the one acting like it's no big deal."

906
01:03:41,000 --> 01:03:49,000
Yoichi: "Anyway, what do we do? Should we evacuate? This happened last year too, when someone pulled the alarm as a prank."

907
01:03:49,000 --> 01:03:56,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah... Anyway, we should probably just sit tight until Ms. Naruse or someone comes to..."

908
01:03:56,000 --> 01:03:57,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

909
01:03:57,000 --> 01:04:01,000
*My phone vibrates, so I pull it out of my pocket and check it.*

910
01:04:01,000 --> 01:04:02,000
*Sora's calling me?*

911
01:04:02,000 --> 01:04:06,000
*She texts me constantly, but she hardly ever calls.*

912
01:04:06,000 --> 01:04:07,000
Yoichi: "'Sup?"

913
01:04:07,000 --> 01:04:09,000
Kakeru: "My sister's calling me."

914
01:04:09,000 --> 01:04:11,000
Yoichi: "Introduce me!"

915
01:04:11,000 --> 01:04:12,000
Kakeru: "Get bent."

916
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:16,000
*I cut Yoichi down to size before answering the call.*

917
01:04:16,000 --> 01:04:17,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, hel..."

918
01:04:17,000 --> 01:04:19,000
Sora: "Onii-chan, it's terrible!"

919
01:04:19,000 --> 01:04:23,000
*Sora's shriek pierces my ear and cuts me off mid-hello.*

920
01:04:23,000 --> 01:04:25,000
*I blink, suddenly serious.*

921
01:04:25,000 --> 01:04:29,000
*Sora only calls me "Onii-chan" when she really needs my help.*

922
01:04:29,000 --> 01:04:31,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

923
01:04:31,000 --> 01:04:34,000
Sora: "Someone in my class set the room on fire!"

924
01:04:34,000 --> 01:04:38,000
Kakeru: "They what?! They set it on fire, on purpose?!"

925
01:04:38,000 --> 01:04:41,000
*I find myself yelling that question.*

926
01:04:41,000 --> 01:04:49,000
*All eyes turn to me, and the classroom works itself up into a frenzy, but I can't be bothered to worry about that.*

927
01:04:49,000 --> 01:04:52,000
Kakeru: "H-How the hell did that happen?"

928
01:04:52,000 --> 01:04:57,000
Sora: "I really don't know! They just started shouting, and then...!"

929
01:04:57,000 --> 01:04:59,000
Kakeru: "Can you get out?!"

930
01:04:59,000 --> 01:05:02,000
Sora: "No! There's flames everywhere!"

931
01:05:02,000 --> 01:05:04,000
Kakeru: "What about the window?!"

932
01:05:04,000 --> 01:05:06,000
Sora: "No, they're everywhere!"

933
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:07,000
Kakeru: "Dammit!"

934
01:05:07,000 --> 01:05:09,000
*Every exit is sealed off?*

935
01:05:09,000 --> 01:05:14,000
*It's not a drill, so the fire engines should be coming any moment now.*

936
01:05:14,000 --> 01:05:15,000
*...!*

937
01:05:15,000 --> 01:05:18,000
Kakeru: "Don't hang up! Stay on the line!"

938
01:05:18,000 --> 01:05:19,000
Sora: "O-Okay."

939
01:05:19,000 --> 01:05:21,000
Kakeru: "Which class is yours?!"

940
01:05:21,000 --> 01:05:23,000
Sora: "Um... C-Class D!"

941
01:05:23,000 --> 01:05:25,000
Kakeru: "Hang on, I'm coming!"

942
01:05:25,000 --> 01:05:29,000
*I slip my phone in my pocket, leaving the call live.*

943
01:05:29,000 --> 01:05:32,000
Yoichi: "S-Something tells me it's bad news."

944
01:05:32,000 --> 01:05:36,000
Kakeru: "It's a real fire! The first floor is on fire!"

945
01:05:36,000 --> 01:05:38,000
Yoichi: "No way! What do we do?!"

946
01:05:38,000 --> 01:05:44,000
*I can't afford to stand around and deal with Yoichi's panicking. I dash out into the hall.*

947
01:05:44,000 --> 01:05:49,000
*What am I going to do?! Even if I go to the first floor, what can I even do?!*

948
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:52,000
*Gotta fill a bucket with water... No!*

949
01:05:52,000 --> 01:05:53,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun!"

950
01:05:53,000 --> 01:05:56,000
*Kujo seems to have followed me for some reason.*

951
01:05:56,000 --> 01:05:59,000
*I really can't spare the time to talk to her.*

952
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:01,000
Miyako: "I overheard there's a fire."

953
01:06:01,000 --> 01:06:05,000
Kakeru: "My sister told me her classmate started it!"

954
01:06:05,000 --> 01:06:08,000
Miyako: "They started a fire? But how?"

955
01:06:08,000 --> 01:06:11,000
Kakeru: "I have no clue! Sorry, we can talk later!"

956
01:06:11,000 --> 01:06:17,000
*I pull a fire extinguisher from its storage container and rush toward the stairs.*

957
01:06:17,000 --> 01:06:18,000
*Kujo follows.*

958
01:06:18,000 --> 01:06:21,000
Kakeru: "It's dangerous! Wait in the classroom!"

959
01:06:21,000 --> 01:06:23,000
Miyako: "Same to you, Niimi-kun!"

960
01:06:23,000 --> 01:06:26,000
Kakeru: "My sister couldn't get away in time!"

961
01:06:26,000 --> 01:06:28,000
Miyako: "I can probably help!"

962
01:06:28,000 --> 01:06:29,000
Kakeru: "...!"

963
01:06:29,000 --> 01:06:33,000
*It's useless arguing with her, so we rush down the stairs.*

964
01:06:33,000 --> 01:06:35,000
Kakeru: "What the hell?"

965
01:06:35,000 --> 01:06:37,000
Miyako: "What is this...?"

966
01:06:37,000 --> 01:06:39,000
*The first floor is a sea of flames.*

967
01:06:39,000 --> 01:06:42,000
*But there's something strange about them.*

968
01:06:42,000 --> 01:06:47,000
*The windows, walls, and floors are burning up, yet I don't feel any heat.*

969
01:06:47,000 --> 01:06:50,000
*There's no smoke coming from the flames, either.*

970
01:06:50,000 --> 01:06:54,000
*I can only tell they're hot by moving right up next to them.*

971
01:06:54,000 --> 01:06:59,000
*There's something peculiar about the way the fire is burning, too.*

972
01:06:59,000 --> 01:07:06,000
*I don't know how to describe it, but it's like they're not burning any material. They're just... there.*

973
01:07:06,000 --> 01:07:08,000
*In any case, it's a bizarre sight.*

974
01:07:08,000 --> 01:07:13,000
*A bunch of students are crowded together, watching it from a distance.*

975
01:07:13,000 --> 01:07:16,000
Kakeru: "This is no time to stand around gawking!"

976
01:07:16,000 --> 01:07:21,000
*I'm chastising myself as well as the others. I'm no better than them right now.*

977
01:07:21,000 --> 01:07:28,000
*I pull out the pin on the extinguisher, point the nozzle at the blaze, and squeeze down the lever.*

978
01:07:28,000 --> 01:07:31,000
*A white mist engulfs the area ten feet in front.*

979
01:07:31,000 --> 01:07:38,000
*The can runs dry in a mere ten or fifteen seconds, and I reel at how pathetically short it lasted.*

980
01:07:38,000 --> 01:07:42,000
*However, what makes my blood run colder than that is...*

981
01:07:42,000 --> 01:07:45,000
Kakeru: "No way... It didn't do anything?!"

982
01:07:45,000 --> 01:07:48,000
*The flames are still burning, unaffected.*

983
01:07:48,000 --> 01:07:54,000
*I finally understand why the students and teachers nearby are just standing there in confusion.*

984
01:07:54,000 --> 01:07:57,000
*The flames don't just look abnormal!*

985
01:07:57,000 --> 01:08:00,000
*Did someone spill some kind of chemical?*

986
01:08:00,000 --> 01:08:01,000
Kakeru: "...!"

987
01:08:01,000 --> 01:08:05,000
*I'm not going to resolve this by thinking about it.*

988
01:08:05,000 --> 01:08:07,000
*I'll try another extinguisher.*

989
01:08:07,000 --> 01:08:12,000
*If one full extinguisher isn't enough, then I'll use up as many as it takes!*

990
01:08:12,000 --> 01:08:13,000
Miyako: "Wait."

991
01:08:13,000 --> 01:08:17,000
*I walk toward the storage box, but Kujo grabs my arm.*

992
01:08:17,000 --> 01:08:18,000
Kakeru: "Now what?!"

993
01:08:18,000 --> 01:08:23,000
Miyako: "I don't think it's going to work. We need a different approach."

994
01:08:23,000 --> 01:08:24,000
Kakeru: "Like what?!"

995
01:08:24,000 --> 01:08:27,000
*I'm panicking so much that I snap at her.*

996
01:08:27,000 --> 01:08:33,000
*Kujo, on the other hand, is trying her best to be composed as she reasons with me.*

997
01:08:33,000 --> 01:08:35,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, are you a User?"

998
01:08:35,000 --> 01:08:36,000
Kakeru: "Huh? A what?"

999
01:08:36,000 --> 01:08:42,000
Miyako: "Very well then. I'll have to explain later. For now, just leave this to me."

1000
01:08:42,000 --> 01:08:48,000
Kakeru: "Whoa, hold on. What do you mean, leave this to you? What do you plan on doing?!"

1001
01:08:48,000 --> 01:08:52,000
Miyako: "I'm going to find the person who started the fire."

1002
01:08:52,000 --> 01:08:54,000
Kakeru: "And then what?"

1003
01:08:54,000 --> 01:08:58,000
Miyako: "If I can find him, I believe I can put the fire out."

1004
01:08:58,000 --> 01:09:01,000
*I don't understand what she could possibly mean.*

1005
01:09:01,000 --> 01:09:03,000
*But her firm gaze is reassuring.*

1006
01:09:03,000 --> 01:09:07,000
*There's something in it that makes me want to believe her.*

1007
01:09:07,000 --> 01:09:09,000
Kakeru: "Do you really mean it?"

1008
01:09:09,000 --> 01:09:13,000
Miyako: "I can't promise you, but I'll give it a shot."

1009
01:09:13,000 --> 01:09:14,000
Kakeru: "...! Sora!"

1010
01:09:14,000 --> 01:09:17,000
*I take out my phone and shout her name.*

1011
01:09:17,000 --> 01:09:20,000
Kakeru: "Is the arsonist still nearby?!"

1012
01:09:20,000 --> 01:09:25,000
Sora: "Y-Yeah! They're groaning and shouting! I'm so scared, and I can't get out!"

1013
01:09:25,000 --> 01:09:27,000
Kakeru: "Okay, just hold tight!"

1014
01:09:27,000 --> 01:09:32,000
Kakeru: "Kujo, they're in Class D! They'll be the one groaning and shouting!"

1015
01:09:32,000 --> 01:09:34,000
Miyako: "Class D, got it!"

1016
01:09:34,000 --> 01:09:37,000
Kakeru: "I'll go first! Kujo, you're behind me!"

1017
01:09:37,000 --> 01:09:38,000
Miyako: "Huh? But...!"

1018
01:09:38,000 --> 01:09:40,000
Kakeru: "No time to argue!"

1019
01:09:40,000 --> 01:09:43,000
*I take off my blazer and fan away the flames.*

1020
01:09:43,000 --> 01:09:48,000
*Maybe I can't put them out, but they at least flicker to the side a moment.*

1021
01:09:48,000 --> 01:09:53,000
*Still no smoke. And despite the sea of flames, there are a lot of safe areas.*

1022
01:09:53,000 --> 01:09:55,000
*We can make it through.*

1023
01:09:55,000 --> 01:09:56,000
Kakeru: "Let's go!"

1024
01:09:56,000 --> 01:09:57,000
Miyako: "R-Right!"

1025
01:09:57,000 --> 01:10:06,000
*Keeping an eye out for patches of hallway that aren't ablaze, I dash through, carving a path by brushing the flames aside with my blazer.*

1026
01:10:06,000 --> 01:10:13,000
*Completely avoiding the flames proves difficult, and they occasionally lick at my arms and legs.*

1027
01:10:13,000 --> 01:10:22,000
*I'm getting flashbacks to when I used to cook for myself. The pain is about as bad as when I accidentally touched a hot frying pan.*

1028
01:10:22,000 --> 01:10:28,000
*However, neither my blazer nor any part of me that the flames touch actually catches fire.*

1029
01:10:28,000 --> 01:10:37,000
*Admittedly, I've never seen a real fire on this scale, so I don't know exactly what it acts like, but this is definitely strange.*

1030
01:10:37,000 --> 01:10:39,000
Crazed Male Student: "Nooooo! Stop!"

1031
01:10:39,000 --> 01:10:44,000
*The onlookers go silent as an unsettling scream echoes through the hall.*

1032
01:10:44,000 --> 01:10:48,000
*There, in the center of a cylindrical wall of flames.*

1033
01:10:48,000 --> 01:10:53,000
*A boy is thrashing around, head and arms arms flailing unnaturally as he rages.*

1034
01:10:53,000 --> 01:10:55,000
Miyako: "That must be him."

1035
01:10:55,000 --> 01:10:57,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, definitely. What now?"

1036
01:10:57,000 --> 01:11:00,000
Miyako: "I need to get within thirty feet of him."

1037
01:11:00,000 --> 01:11:03,000
Kakeru: "Thirty feet? That's way too close!"

1038
01:11:03,000 --> 01:11:07,000
Miyako: "I know, but I think that was my limit, last time I tried."

1039
01:11:07,000 --> 01:11:13,000
Kakeru: "You're not making any sense. You better tell me why we're doing this all later!"

1040
01:11:13,000 --> 01:11:18,000
*I brush more flames aside with my blazer as we close the distance.*

1041
01:11:18,000 --> 01:11:21,000
Crazed Male Student: "Gaaaah! I can't control it!"

1042
01:11:21,000 --> 01:11:22,000
*Another scream.*

1043
01:11:22,000 --> 01:11:25,000
*A pillar of fire erupts from the ceiling.*

1044
01:11:25,000 --> 01:11:29,000
*The flames wreathe around the student and grow as he cries out.*

1045
01:11:29,000 --> 01:11:31,000
*I can't get any closer!*

1046
01:11:31,000 --> 01:11:36,000
*Damn, the front of Class D's room looks like the gates of hell itself!*

1047
01:11:36,000 --> 01:11:41,000
Crazed Male Student: "My powers are out of control! They're going berserk!"

1048
01:11:41,000 --> 01:11:46,000
Kakeru: "Shit, it's too hot! Dammit, what the hell's up with this guy?!"

1049
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:48,000
Miyako: "I knew it. He's a User."

1050
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:50,000
Kakeru: "What the hell's a User?!"

1051
01:11:50,000 --> 01:11:54,000
Miyako: "We'll talk later. Thank you! I'm finally in range!"

1052
01:11:54,000 --> 01:11:58,000
Kakeru: "What, going to unleash your superpowers or something?"

1053
01:11:58,000 --> 01:11:59,000
Miyako: "Precisely!"

1054
01:11:59,000 --> 01:12:00,000
Kakeru: "Wait, what?"

1055
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:01,000
Miyako: "...!"

1056
01:12:01,000 --> 01:12:03,000
*Kujo extends her left hand.*

1057
01:12:03,000 --> 01:12:08,000
Miyako: "Cowardly Power of the Thief, defend the world and the people in it..."

1058
01:12:08,000 --> 01:12:11,000
*She's muttering something under her breath.*

1059
01:12:11,000 --> 01:12:14,000
*Don't tell me it's some sort of incantation?*

1060
01:12:14,000 --> 01:12:17,000
*But maybe that's exactly what it is.*

1061
01:12:17,000 --> 01:12:23,000
*A pattern... No, an emblem appears on the back of her hand. What the hell is that?*

1062
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:24,000
*I don't know.*

1063
01:12:24,000 --> 01:12:29,000
*A mysterious glowing blue symbol appears on the back of Kujo's hand.*

1064
01:12:29,000 --> 01:12:31,000
Kakeru: "Kujo, what IS that?"

1065
01:12:31,000 --> 01:12:33,000
Miyako: "Not right now!"

1066
01:12:33,000 --> 01:12:34,000
Miyako: "...!"

1067
01:12:34,000 --> 01:12:39,000
Miyako: "Where is it? I need to find the thing that's driving him insane."

1068
01:12:39,000 --> 01:12:45,000
*Kujo hesitates, her glowing left hand still outstretched toward the male student.*

1069
01:12:45,000 --> 01:12:48,000
*I don't have the foggiest idea what she's doing.*

1070
01:12:48,000 --> 01:12:54,000
*I'm fully occupied waving my blazer around, pushing the flames aside so they don't engulf Kujo.*

1071
01:12:54,000 --> 01:13:05,000
*Of course, between me wildly waving around my jacket and Kujo's light show, we're bound to draw attention no matter how crazy this guy is, and he turns our way.*

1072
01:13:05,000 --> 01:13:09,000
Crazed Male Student: "What?! Don't come near me! Go away!"

1073
01:13:09,000 --> 01:13:10,000
Miyako: "...!"

1074
01:13:10,000 --> 01:13:11,000
Kakeru: "Kujo!"

1075
01:13:11,000 --> 01:13:16,000
*The flames rush at us like a tsunami, and I instinctively shield Kujo from it.*

1076
01:13:16,000 --> 01:13:20,000
*The flames pass over us and scatter to the floor and walls.*

1077
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:21,000
Kakeru: "Agh...!"

1078
01:13:21,000 --> 01:13:23,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, are you okay?!"

1079
01:13:23,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Kakeru: "I'm fine! Are you okay, Kujo?"

1080
01:13:26,000 --> 01:13:29,000
Miyako: "I-I'm sorry, thank you! I'm fine!"

1081
01:13:29,000 --> 01:13:36,000
Kakeru: "When he waved his arm, the flames came at us! It's like he's controlling the flames himself!"

1082
01:13:36,000 --> 01:13:39,000
Miyako: "Yes, I think that's exactly right."

1083
01:13:39,000 --> 01:13:42,000
Kakeru: "You're saying he has superpowers too?!"

1084
01:13:42,000 --> 01:13:45,000
Miyako: "That's the long and short of it!"

1085
01:13:45,000 --> 01:13:49,000
Kakeru: "Boy, I was hoping you'd say I had the wrong idea."

1086
01:13:49,000 --> 01:13:52,000
Miyako: "Oh, he moved. He's outside my range!"

1087
01:13:52,000 --> 01:13:57,000
*I look over my shoulder to see the guy stepping back, still screaming.*

1088
01:13:57,000 --> 01:14:00,000
*From the look in his eyes, he's totally lost it.*

1089
01:14:00,000 --> 01:14:03,000
*And... there's a glowing symbol on his face.*

1090
01:14:03,000 --> 01:14:05,000
*Just like the one on Kujo's hand.*

1091
01:14:05,000 --> 01:14:07,000
Kakeru: "So. Superpowers."

1092
01:14:07,000 --> 01:14:08,000
Kakeru: "...!"

1093
01:14:08,000 --> 01:14:11,000
Kakeru: "You said thirty feet, right?"

1094
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:12,000
Miyako: "Uh, right!"

1095
01:14:12,000 --> 01:14:15,000
Kakeru: "I'll hold him down. The rest is up to you!"

1096
01:14:15,000 --> 01:14:17,000
Miyako: "Huh? Wait a... Niimi-kun!"

1097
01:14:17,000 --> 01:14:20,000
*I ignore her and charge headlong at him.*

1098
01:14:20,000 --> 01:14:33,000
*If this were a manga, I'd be shouting courageously while I do it, but instead, let's just say that if I weren't grinding my teeth together right now, I'd be crying like a little bitch from the pain.*

1099
01:14:33,000 --> 01:14:37,000
*So I shout out my warcry in my head, "Yaaaaaaaaahhhh!"*

1100
01:14:37,000 --> 01:14:40,000
*The unnatural flames burn me everywhere.*

1101
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:44,000
*Intense pain assaults me, the sensation of being seared alive.*

1102
01:14:44,000 --> 01:14:47,000
*And yet my clothes don't catch fire.*

1103
01:14:47,000 --> 01:14:50,000
*Therefore, these flames have to be fakes.*

1104
01:14:50,000 --> 01:14:53,000
*Meaning the pain is an illusion too!*

1105
01:14:53,000 --> 01:14:55,000
Crazed Male Student: "Stay baaack!"

1106
01:14:55,000 --> 01:14:57,000
*A gout of flame flies at me.*

1107
01:14:57,000 --> 01:15:01,000
*I plunge straight through it, grabbing on to the student.*

1108
01:15:01,000 --> 01:15:03,000
Crazed Male Student: "Aagh!"

1109
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:05,000
*I pin him to the ground.*

1110
01:15:05,000 --> 01:15:11,000
*My phone falls from my pocket and hits the floor, and I hear Sora's voice coming from it.*

1111
01:15:11,000 --> 01:15:14,000
*She can probably see me from the classroom.*

1112
01:15:14,000 --> 01:15:16,000
*Hang on, Sora! Leave it to me!*

1113
01:15:16,000 --> 01:15:18,000
*Or rather, leave it to her!*

1114
01:15:18,000 --> 01:15:19,000
Kakeru: "Kujo!"

1115
01:15:19,000 --> 01:15:22,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, you're incredible!"

1116
01:15:22,000 --> 01:15:29,000
*With a line that would make me blush under ordinary circumstances, Kujo extends her left hand once more.*

1117
01:15:29,000 --> 01:15:32,000
*The symbol on her hand is the same as this guy's.*

1118
01:15:32,000 --> 01:15:35,000
*Wait, actually, the design is different.*

1119
01:15:35,000 --> 01:15:39,000
*Is it some sort of counter to his power to control flame?*

1120
01:15:39,000 --> 01:15:41,000
*Speaking of which...!*

1121
01:15:41,000 --> 01:15:44,000
Crazed Male Student: "Let go of meeeee!"

1122
01:15:44,000 --> 01:15:48,000
Kakeru: "Yeowch! Hold still, you! Kujo, what's the holdup?!"

1123
01:15:48,000 --> 01:15:53,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry! I need to find it first! It should be something he's wearing!"

1124
01:15:53,000 --> 01:15:57,000
Kakeru: "What is it you need to find?! And then what?!"

1125
01:15:57,000 --> 01:16:04,000
Miyako: "It'll be something he's wearing. Probably jewelry! Like a hair clip! I have to be able to see it!"

1126
01:16:04,000 --> 01:16:08,000
Kakeru: "I still don't get what the hell's goin' on, but...!"

1127
01:16:08,000 --> 01:16:11,000
Crazed Male Student: "Gaaah, stoooooop!"

1128
01:16:11,000 --> 01:16:15,000
Kakeru: "Shit! Stop thrashing! Shaddup and hold still!"

1129
01:16:15,000 --> 01:16:18,000
*Giving in to my anger, I slug the guy in the face.*

1130
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:25,000
*His head hits the floor and bounces off with a dull thud, and after a groan, he stops flailing around.*

1131
01:16:25,000 --> 01:16:32,000
*Oh, shit, did I kill him? I panic for an instant, before the burning pain brings me back to what I need to do.*

1132
01:16:32,000 --> 01:16:34,000
*Gotta find the jewelry!*

1133
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:38,000
*She said a hair clip? But a dude wouldn't be wearing that!*

1134
01:16:38,000 --> 01:16:40,000
*Where could it be, dammit?!*

1135
01:16:40,000 --> 01:16:43,000
???: "It's the silver cross dangling from his neck."

1136
01:16:43,000 --> 01:16:44,000
Kakeru: "...!"

1137
01:16:44,000 --> 01:16:45,000
*That voice again!*

1138
01:16:45,000 --> 01:16:48,000
*Now's not the time to worry about who it is!*

1139
01:16:48,000 --> 01:16:50,000
Kakeru: "Gotta trust 'em!"

1140
01:16:50,000 --> 01:16:53,000
*I flip the unconscious guy over onto his back.*

1141
01:16:53,000 --> 01:16:55,000
*There it is! A silver cross!*

1142
01:16:55,000 --> 01:17:00,000
*I grab it and yank at the thin chain with all my might, hoisting it up.*

1143
01:17:00,000 --> 01:17:02,000
Kakeru: "Kujo! This is it!"

1144
01:17:02,000 --> 01:17:05,000
Miyako: "Thank you! Please, this has to work!"

1145
01:17:05,000 --> 01:17:08,000
*She closes her glowing left hand into a fist.*

1146
01:17:08,000 --> 01:17:11,000
*I feel an odd discomfort for a split second.*

1147
01:17:11,000 --> 01:17:13,000
*In the palm of my hand...*

1148
01:17:13,000 --> 01:17:18,000
*It's like the thing that should be clenched in my fist disappeared.*

1149
01:17:18,000 --> 01:17:19,000
Miyako: "I did it!"

1150
01:17:19,000 --> 01:17:23,000
*The cross that was in my hand has appeared in Kujo's.*

1151
01:17:23,000 --> 01:17:24,000
*Wh-What on Earth?*

1152
01:17:24,000 --> 01:17:26,000
???: "Get away from him, quickly!"

1153
01:17:26,000 --> 01:17:27,000
Kakeru: "...!"

1154
01:17:27,000 --> 01:17:28,000
*That voice again?*

1155
01:17:28,000 --> 01:17:35,000
*I instinctively follow its advice, jumping back and putting some distance between myself and the boy.*

1156
01:17:35,000 --> 01:17:36,000
*And then it happens.*

1157
01:17:36,000 --> 01:17:39,000
Crazed Male Student: "AaaaaAAAAAAAHHHHHH!"

1158
01:17:39,000 --> 01:17:47,000
*He should still be unconscious, but the student's eyes pop open, and he screams as he scratches at the symbol on his face.*

1159
01:17:47,000 --> 01:17:57,000
*The flames near him... No, every flame throughout the hallway suddenly quivers and goes flying straight at him, a hail of arrows and spears of fire.*

1160
01:17:57,000 --> 01:17:58,000
*A tempest of flame.*

1161
01:17:58,000 --> 01:18:00,000
*It's been about a week since then.*

1162
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:03,000
*The incidents have only become more frequent.*

1163
01:18:03,000 --> 01:18:07,000
*Both the Evil Eye's User and new Artifact Users have been active.*

1164
01:18:07,000 --> 01:18:13,000
*The opening of the gate plunged Shiromitsugawa into chaos, just like in the anime.*

1165
01:18:13,000 --> 01:18:15,000
*...Or so you would think.*

1166
01:18:15,000 --> 01:18:18,000
*In reality, it's been a total snoozefest.*

1167
01:18:18,000 --> 01:18:21,000
*We had the human petrification case.*

1168
01:18:21,000 --> 01:18:23,000
*And then the illusory fire.*

1169
01:18:23,000 --> 01:18:26,000
*But since then, nothing to speak of has happened.*

1170
01:18:26,000 --> 01:18:39,000
*This is just conjecture, but I suspect that after those two incidents caused such a huge stir, the various Users, including the culprit behind the petrification incident, are probably lying low.*

1171
01:18:39,000 --> 01:18:47,000
*As for that guy who turned the school into a sea of flames, the only thing I know is that he's stopped coming to school.*

1172
01:18:47,000 --> 01:18:52,000
*There's only so much that a normal student can investigate on their own.*

1173
01:18:52,000 --> 01:18:59,000
*Still, I can say with confidence that there's been no sign of the chaos Sophie predicted, at the very least.*

1174
01:18:59,000 --> 01:19:06,000
*As a result, both finding the culprit and finding allies have turned out to be difficult objectives.*

1175
01:19:06,000 --> 01:19:19,000
*The ever-responsible Kujo has been fretting over it, saying, "We need to resolve this as soon as possible." But, though I feel a little guilty admitting it, I've been hoping that things stay peaceful.*

1176
01:19:19,000 --> 01:19:22,000
*My reason should be readily apparent.*

1177
01:19:22,000 --> 01:19:23,000
Miyako: "♪"

1178
01:19:23,000 --> 01:19:26,000
*I can hear Kujo humming to herself in the kitchen.*

1179
01:19:26,000 --> 01:19:33,000
*I don't know why, but Kujo has started to come over and make me dinner on days she doesn't have work.*

1180
01:19:33,000 --> 01:19:34,000
*According to Kujo:*

1181
01:19:34,000 --> 01:19:41,000
Miyako: "All those convenience store lunches and eating out all the time aren't providing a balanced diet."

1182
01:19:41,000 --> 01:19:43,000
*Who am I to disagree?*

1183
01:19:43,000 --> 01:19:47,000
*Apparently, she finds my unhealthy eating habits unacceptable.*

1184
01:19:47,000 --> 01:19:53,000
*Also, she says cooking for me is her way of thanking me for always looking out for her.*

1185
01:19:53,000 --> 01:20:00,000
*I don't have the foggiest memory of always looking out for her, which makes me feel a little guilty, but...*

1186
01:20:00,000 --> 01:20:13,000
*Not only do I have a girl coming over to cook for me, but it's not just any girl. It's the most popular, smart and beautiful girl in class... no, in my grade... no, in the whole damn school!*

1187
01:20:13,000 --> 01:20:18,000
*No way could I let an event straight out of my dreams slip through my fingers.*

1188
01:20:18,000 --> 01:20:28,000
*When Kujo offered to cook for me, I played it cool and said she didn't need to bother, but in my mind, I was flexing like I'd won a title match.*

1189
01:20:28,000 --> 01:20:31,000
Miyako: "Let's see, where's the olive oil?"

1190
01:20:31,000 --> 01:20:35,000
*Though quick, Kujo never makes a false step in the kitchen.*

1191
01:20:35,000 --> 01:20:40,000
*Today, she's making Salisbury steak. Its savory aroma wafts through the air.*

1192
01:20:40,000 --> 01:20:45,000
*Aah, this must be what it feels like to live with your girlfriend. What bliss.*

1193
01:20:45,000 --> 01:20:49,000
*Each day Kujo comes over is a real treat... or, it would be.*

1194
01:20:49,000 --> 01:20:52,000
Sora: "Salisbury steak♪ Yay! Salisbury steak♪ Yay!"

1195
01:20:52,000 --> 01:20:53,000
Kakeru: "..."

1196
01:20:53,000 --> 01:20:56,000
*If only SHE were out of the picture.*

1197
01:20:56,000 --> 01:21:00,000
*Whyyy can't my clever little sister take a freaking hint?*

1198
01:21:00,000 --> 01:21:02,000
Sora: "So, hey, Bromeo."

1199
01:21:02,000 --> 01:21:03,000
Kakeru: "What?"

1200
01:21:03,000 --> 01:21:10,000
Sora: "It'd sure be nice if you'd quit glaring at me like I'm cockblocking you every time I visit."

1201
01:21:10,000 --> 01:21:12,000
Kakeru: "Oh, you caught on?"

1202
01:21:12,000 --> 01:21:20,000
Sora: "It doesn't take a genius when you're being so obvious about it. I'll have you know, I'm the one paying for dinner here."

1203
01:21:20,000 --> 01:21:22,000
Kakeru: "You're not; Dad is."

1204
01:21:22,000 --> 01:21:25,000
Sora: "I milked him for a little extra this week."

1205
01:21:25,000 --> 01:21:27,000
Kakeru: "You're incorrigible."

1206
01:21:27,000 --> 01:21:31,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry for having you pay for my portion as well."

1207
01:21:31,000 --> 01:21:33,000
*Kujo sets out a serving platter.*

1208
01:21:33,000 --> 01:21:37,000
*On the platter sits a beautifully plated, multicolored salad.*

1209
01:21:37,000 --> 01:21:42,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry, here I went and made enough for myself without asking."

1210
01:21:42,000 --> 01:21:54,000
Kakeru: "Nah, I told you, you don't need to worry about that. It's more fun if we all eat together, and it'd just be a pain to try to figure out how much you should pay us back."

1211
01:21:54,000 --> 01:21:59,000
Sora: "Yeah, what he said. Just consider it your pay for preparing the meal!"

1212
01:21:59,000 --> 01:22:05,000
Miyako: "Haha, thank you. Whenever I cook, I'll try to be as cost-effective as possible."

1213
01:22:05,000 --> 01:22:10,000
Sora: "Nah, don't sweat it. Dear old Dad's paying all my food bills anyway."

1214
01:22:10,000 --> 01:22:15,000
Miyako: "That attitude won't do at all. You should value your money!"

1215
01:22:15,000 --> 01:22:18,000
*Kujo emphasizes her point, clenching her fist.*

1216
01:22:18,000 --> 01:22:27,000
Miyako: "Grandfather always told me, 'If you're frivolous with money, you'll run out in no time, so you should make a habit of saving up.'"

1217
01:22:27,000 --> 01:22:37,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, you're either racking up close to a thousand yen at the convenience store, or around five hundred if you come to our cafe."

1218
01:22:37,000 --> 01:22:48,000
Miyako: "Plus, you usually buy a sandwich or onigiri at the convenience store for lunch, too, right? The amount you spend on food each day must be substantial."

1219
01:22:48,000 --> 01:23:06,000
Miyako: "However, if you were just to cook your dinner, you'd slash your costs dramatically. Lettuce was cheap today, and ground beef was half off! If you made a habit of selecting inexpensive ingredients, you could cut your food expenses even further! Not to mention..."

1220
01:23:06,000 --> 01:23:07,000
Kakeru: "R-Right."

1221
01:23:07,000 --> 01:23:09,000
Sora: "Is this her housewife mode?"

1222
01:23:09,000 --> 01:23:16,000
*Kujo waxes eloquent over the subject while I stand there listening, half in horror and half in awe.*

1223
01:23:16,000 --> 01:23:17,000
*Miyako Kujo.*

1224
01:23:17,000 --> 01:23:21,000
*The heiress of the Corona Group, a titanic corporation.*

1225
01:23:21,000 --> 01:23:24,000
*Her hobbies: coupon clipping and bargain hunting.*

1226
01:23:24,000 --> 01:23:35,000
*She's so prudent with how she spends money that she'd cringe to see a guy like me buy three sweet rolls at once without a thought and say, "What conspicuous consumption!"*

1227
01:23:35,000 --> 01:23:43,000
*Kujo is the antithesis of what you'd expect from a wealthy person. If anything, she comes off as a model proletarian.*

1228
01:23:43,000 --> 01:23:47,000
*This is a side of her I've only come to know in this past week.*

1229
01:23:47,000 --> 01:23:52,000
*What's more, that stiff attitude towards me has started to soften up.*

1230
01:23:52,000 --> 01:23:56,000
*I'm pretty excited about how fast we're growing closer.*

1231
01:23:56,000 --> 01:24:03,000
Miyako: "So, for the celery, I like to... Oh! I put celery in this. Are you both okay with eating it?"

1232
01:24:03,000 --> 01:24:05,000
Kakeru: "No problems here."

1233
01:24:05,000 --> 01:24:06,000
Sora: "Same for me!"

1234
01:24:06,000 --> 01:24:11,000
Miyako: "Haha, what a relief. Oh! Oh no, the Salisbury steaks are going to burn!"

1235
01:24:11,000 --> 01:24:14,000
*She gasps and rushes off to the kitchen.*

1236
01:24:14,000 --> 01:24:21,000
Miyako: "Oh, thank goodness, they still need a little more time. Go ahead and start on the salad!"

1237
01:24:21,000 --> 01:24:22,000
Kakeru: "Can do."

1238
01:24:22,000 --> 01:24:23,000
Sora: "Okie dokie!"

1239
01:24:23,000 --> 01:24:27,000
*Or so we say, but neither of us makes a move for the salad.*

1240
01:24:27,000 --> 01:24:33,000
*We're not about to start eating without Kujo, while she's slaving over a hot stove for us.*

1241
01:24:33,000 --> 01:24:36,000
Sora: "I'm tellin' ya, she'd make a great wife."

1242
01:24:36,000 --> 01:24:38,000
Kakeru: "Heh heh, oh, quit it, you."

1243
01:24:38,000 --> 01:24:44,000
Sora: "Are you for real? Already playing the lovesick husband? God, you're disgusting."

1244
01:24:44,000 --> 01:24:47,000
Kakeru: "Shut your mouth and take your ass home."

1245
01:24:47,000 --> 01:24:48,000
Sora: "No, you."

1246
01:24:48,000 --> 01:24:50,000
Kakeru: "This IS my home, brat."

1247
01:24:50,000 --> 01:24:52,000
Sora: "It'll be mine soon enough."

1248
01:24:52,000 --> 01:24:54,000
Kakeru: "Are you an idiot?"

1249
01:24:54,000 --> 01:24:56,000
Sora: "Takes one to know one!"

1250
01:24:56,000 --> 01:24:59,000
Miyako: "Either of you want cheese on top?"

1251
01:24:59,000 --> 01:25:01,000
Kakeru: "Oh, for sure!"

1252
01:25:01,000 --> 01:25:02,000
Sora: "Heck yeah!"

1253
01:25:02,000 --> 01:25:06,000
*Kujo's charming voice brings our pointless scuffle to a close.*

1254
01:25:06,000 --> 01:25:10,000
*With a practiced hand, she puts on the finishing touches.*

1255
01:25:10,000 --> 01:25:15,000
*And five minutes later, a delicious-looking dinner adorns the table.*

1256
01:25:15,000 --> 01:25:17,000
Miyako: "I hope you all enjoy it."

1257
01:25:17,000 --> 01:25:18,000
Sora: "Looks awesome!"

1258
01:25:18,000 --> 01:25:21,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I bet it's gonna be great."

1259
01:25:21,000 --> 01:25:26,000
*I put my hands together and offer a prayer, and then I pick up my chopsticks.*

1260
01:25:26,000 --> 01:25:29,000
Sora: "Did you even make the sauce, Miya?"

1261
01:25:29,000 --> 01:25:35,000
Miyako: "Yes. I just mixed some ketchup and Worcestershire sauce together, though."

1262
01:25:35,000 --> 01:25:37,000
Kakeru: "It's fantastic."

1263
01:25:37,000 --> 01:25:40,000
Miyako: "I'm so glad you like it, haha."

1264
01:25:40,000 --> 01:25:45,000
Sora: "It's so tender! Our mom's Salisbury steak always comes out hard as a rock."

1265
01:25:45,000 --> 01:25:46,000
*I get out of bed.*

1266
01:25:46,000 --> 01:25:48,000
*Wash my face and brush my teeth.*

1267
01:25:48,000 --> 01:25:50,000
*Have a simple breakfast.*

1268
01:25:50,000 --> 01:25:52,000
*Finally, I change into my uniform.*

1269
01:25:52,000 --> 01:25:59,000
*Just as I'm slinging my bag over my shoulder, ready to head out, the space in front of me distorts.*

1270
01:25:59,000 --> 01:26:02,000
Sophitia: "Oh my, already on your way?"

1271
01:26:02,000 --> 01:26:06,000
*A hole in the fabric of space tears open, and Sophie emerges.*

1272
01:26:06,000 --> 01:26:09,000
*Always with the needlessly flashy entrance.*

1273
01:26:09,000 --> 01:26:11,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, just heading out."

1274
01:26:11,000 --> 01:26:16,000
Sophitia: "Incidentally, I finished looking into the first girl you mentioned."

1275
01:26:16,000 --> 01:26:18,000
Kakeru: "Whoa, that was quick."

1276
01:26:18,000 --> 01:26:21,000
Sophitia: "Like I said, I'm not useless like you."

1277
01:26:21,000 --> 01:26:22,000
Kakeru: "Mhmm."

1278
01:26:22,000 --> 01:26:28,000
*I casually brush off her comment, causing Sophie to knit her brows in dissatisfaction.*

1279
01:26:28,000 --> 01:26:32,000
*After letting out a sigh, she continues in a bored voice.*

1280
01:26:32,000 --> 01:26:44,000
Sophitia: "It was quite a simple feat. I deduced everything I needed from your past actions and found an individual who matched the parameters you specified almost immediately."

1281
01:26:44,000 --> 01:26:49,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah? You really have been keeping me under observation."

1282
01:26:49,000 --> 01:26:57,000
Sophitia: "But of course. A User unaware of their powers is absolutely hilariou... I mean, is no laughing matter."

1283
01:26:57,000 --> 01:26:59,000
Kakeru: "I heard that."

1284
01:26:59,000 --> 01:27:02,000
Sophitia: "Just shut up and listen, okay?"

1285
01:27:02,000 --> 01:27:04,000
Kakeru: "Alright, alright."

1286
01:27:04,000 --> 01:27:16,000
Sophitia: "I decided to investigate the long-haired girl first. Her name is Haruka Kosaka. I don't know how you'd write it, only how it's pronounced. She's a year older than you."

1287
01:27:16,000 --> 01:27:19,000
Kakeru: "Ah, so she really is a third-year."

1288
01:27:19,000 --> 01:27:25,000
Sophitia: "Judging by how she acts, your prediction was correct. She is quite suspicious."

1289
01:27:25,000 --> 01:27:26,000
Kakeru: "Interesting."

1290
01:27:26,000 --> 01:27:27,000
Sophitia: "..."

1291
01:27:27,000 --> 01:27:28,000
Kakeru: "..."

1292
01:27:28,000 --> 01:27:29,000
Kakeru: "And?"

1293
01:27:29,000 --> 01:27:30,000
Sophitia: "And what?"

1294
01:27:30,000 --> 01:27:33,000
Kakeru: "You don't have anything else?"

1295
01:27:33,000 --> 01:27:35,000
Sophitia: "Not a thing."

1296
01:27:35,000 --> 01:27:37,000
Kakeru: "Are you serious?"

1297
01:27:37,000 --> 01:27:42,000
Sophitia: "You're busy, aren't you? I gave you the abridged version."

1298
01:27:42,000 --> 01:27:50,000
Kakeru: "Why, thank you so much for your kind consideration. I hope you can handle investigating the other girl."

1299
01:27:50,000 --> 01:27:52,000
Sophitia: "That goes without saying."

1300
01:27:52,000 --> 01:28:00,000
*Perhaps due to her not taking too kindly to how I phrased my remark, Sophie looks a bit miffed as she vanishes.*

1301
01:28:00,000 --> 01:28:09,000
*Her appearance is rather disarming, so I tend to be pretty casual with her, but she sure is a moody one. What a pain in the ass.*

1302
01:28:09,000 --> 01:28:10,000
Kakeru: "Now then."

1303
01:28:10,000 --> 01:28:13,000
*At least we have a name to work wtih.*

1304
01:28:13,000 --> 01:28:17,000
*I suppose it's my responsibility to check out her class, now.*

1305
01:28:17,000 --> 01:28:20,000
Sora: "Finally. Took you long enough, slowpoke!"

1306
01:28:20,000 --> 01:28:22,000
Miyako: "Morning, Niimi-kun!"

1307
01:28:22,000 --> 01:28:24,000
*Sora is waiting by the station.*

1308
01:28:24,000 --> 01:28:31,000
*Kujo, who lives in the opposite direction, is also here for some reason, which throws me for a loop.*

1309
01:28:31,000 --> 01:28:33,000
Kakeru: "Why are you here, Kujo?"

1310
01:28:33,000 --> 01:28:37,000
Sora: "She said she wants to get a look at the super popular girl."

1311
01:28:37,000 --> 01:28:41,000
Miyako: "I just really wanted to see what she's like."

1312
01:28:41,000 --> 01:28:48,000
Kakeru: "Sophie looked into her a bit. Says her name is Haruka Kosaka, and that she's a year ahead of us."

1313
01:28:48,000 --> 01:28:50,000
Miyako: "Kosaka-senpai, huh?"

1314
01:28:50,000 --> 01:28:52,000
Kakeru: "You know the name?"

1315
01:28:52,000 --> 01:28:53,000
Miyako: "No, sorry."

1316
01:28:53,000 --> 01:28:59,000
Sora: "Anyhow, we should get going. She and her gaggle of guys have a head-start on us!"

1317
01:28:59,000 --> 01:29:02,000
Kakeru: "Oh shoot, sorry. Let's catch up to them."

1318
01:29:02,000 --> 01:29:06,000
Miyako: "Oh! Feel free to put your bags in the basket."

1319
01:29:06,000 --> 01:29:08,000
Sora: "Thank y'kindly!"

1320
01:29:08,000 --> 01:29:11,000
Kakeru: "Did you see her when she passed by, Kujo?"

1321
01:29:11,000 --> 01:29:20,000
Miyako: "You could say that, I suppose, but honestly, she was completely surrounded by boys, so I couldn't actually get a look at her."

1322
01:29:20,000 --> 01:29:28,000
Sora: "She's kind of a big deal, huh? I think we'll be able to catch up to them quick since they only passed by a moment ago."

1323
01:29:28,000 --> 01:29:30,000
*We jog for ten seconds or so.*

1324
01:29:30,000 --> 01:29:35,000
*As Sora predicted, we catch up with the obvious commotion in no time.*

1325
01:29:35,000 --> 01:29:42,000
Haruka: "Could I ask you to be a little more gentle with my things? You've let my lunch box sit at an angle."

1326
01:29:42,000 --> 01:29:52,000
Haruka: "Now now, I'd rather you not come any closer than that. And under no circumstances are you to touch me. I am not some woman of loose morals."

1327
01:29:52,000 --> 01:30:00,000
*A flock of boys surrounding a princess. Or, to be more accurate, I suppose it's a flock of boys and the Queen of Eden.*

1328
01:30:00,000 --> 01:30:07,000
*One of her entourage is carrying her bag, while she struts about with an overacted air of refinement.*

1329
01:30:07,000 --> 01:30:14,000
Kakeru: "The first time I saw her, she was acting so troubled about everything and timid, but now..."

1330
01:30:14,000 --> 01:30:24,000
Sora: "She's not wrong, calling herself a queen. She's even got her uniform undone a good ways down, with her chest just, BAM, right out there."

1331
01:30:24,000 --> 01:30:29,000
Miyako: "This might come across as rude, but I can't help feeling like..."

1332
01:30:29,000 --> 01:30:33,000
Sora: "You can tell she's totally forcing it, right?"

1333
01:30:33,000 --> 01:30:39,000
Miyako: "Oh, yes, exactly. The way she's speaking doesn't seem to come naturally to her."

1334
01:30:39,000 --> 01:30:50,000
Kakeru: "Y'know, maybe she really did just become popular all of a sudden, and she's just trying to make the most out of it. No Artifacts or anything, just coincidences."

1335
01:30:50,000 --> 01:30:54,000
Sora: "But then what explains her sudden popularity?"

1336
01:30:54,000 --> 01:30:58,000
Miyako: "Maybe people finally noticed how attractive she is?"

1337
01:30:58,000 --> 01:31:01,000
Kakeru: "Or like, maybe she won the lottery."

1338
01:31:01,000 --> 01:31:05,000
Sora: "You're too sweet, Miya. And my big brother's too jaded."

1339
01:31:05,000 --> 01:31:11,000
Kakeru: "How can you say that? I'm not ashamed to admit I'd lick her shoes for a million yen!"

1340
01:31:11,000 --> 01:31:12,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

1341
01:31:12,000 --> 01:31:15,000
Sora: "Damn, you're right. So would I."

1342
01:31:15,000 --> 01:31:16,000
Miyako: "Huh?!"

1343
01:31:16,000 --> 01:31:27,000
Kakeru: "Well, all joking aside... It doesn't feel like it's my place to say, but there definitely is something abnormal about her sudden surge in popularity."

1344
01:31:27,000 --> 01:31:38,000
Miyako: "I admit, I never saw what she was like before, but if she's really changed that much, then I would suspect something in her environment has caused that change."

1345
01:31:38,000 --> 01:31:40,000
Kakeru: "Something like an Artifact?"

1346
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:50,000
Sora: "Is it an Artifact that makes you a guy magnet? I can't decide if I'm super jealous or if I don't give a shit. Shall we check things out?"

1347
01:31:50,000 --> 01:31:53,000
Miyako: "And how do you propose we do that?"

1348
01:31:53,000 --> 01:32:00,000
Sora: "Just leave that to me. I've got something in mind that should do the trick, now that I know her name."

1349
01:32:00,000 --> 01:32:04,000
Sora: "Brother dearest, may I borrow your back for a moment?"

1350
01:32:04,000 --> 01:32:06,000
Kakeru: "...? Uh, okay."

1351
01:32:06,000 --> 01:32:14,000
*Sora pulls out a pen and a notebook, carefully tears out a piece of paper, braces it against my back, and begins writing.*

1352
01:32:14,000 --> 01:32:21,000
Sora: "Crap, writing like this is a pain in the ass. I should have ripped it out after I wrote it."

1353
01:32:21,000 --> 01:32:24,000
Miyako: "You're using him as a writing surface?"

1354
01:32:24,000 --> 01:32:27,000
Sora: "Oh, don't worry, he doesn't mind."

1355
01:32:27,000 --> 01:32:29,000
Kakeru: "You're writing a letter?"

1356
01:32:29,000 --> 01:32:35,000
Sora: "Yup. Hmmmm... Okay, that should do it. I'm gonna go hand this to her, okay?"

1357
01:32:35,000 --> 01:32:38,000
Miyako: "Really? Are you sure that's a good idea?"

1358
01:32:38,000 --> 01:32:41,000
Sora: "Have you forgotten about my power?"

1359
01:32:41,000 --> 01:32:45,000
*Sora starts folding up the letter and jogs over to the group.*

1360
01:32:45,000 --> 01:32:55,000
*Without so much as being noticed by any of them, she slips the letter into Kosaka-senpai's pocket and returns to us with a triumphant look on her face.*

1361
01:32:55,000 --> 01:32:57,000
Sora: "Heh. Piece of cake."

1362
01:32:57,000 --> 01:33:01,000
Miyako: "Oh, I see. You used your Perceptual Control on yourself."

1363
01:33:01,000 --> 01:33:14,000
Sora: Yup. It may not work if they're already staring right at me, but to anybody who hasn't yet noticed me, I'm practically invisible. I'm a modern-day ninja! This sure is one handy power, heheh."

1364
01:33:14,000 --> 01:33:20,000
Kakeru: "Here I was thinking it was pretty lame, but it's more useful than I gave it credit for."

1365
01:33:20,000 --> 01:33:30,000
Sora: "I do believe you just said something insulting. If you apologize immediately, I'll be merciful and let you off the hook with a mere slap to the face."

1366
01:33:30,000 --> 01:33:33,000
Kakeru: "What did you write in the letter?"

1367
01:33:33,000 --> 01:33:43,000
Sora: "Wow, cold. I said, 'You're the Queen of Eden, correct? I'm on your side, so I'd appreciate if you'd get in contact with me.' And then the LING ID."

1368
01:33:43,000 --> 01:33:45,000
Miyako: "Wow, that's pretty bold."

1369
01:33:45,000 --> 01:33:46,000
Sora: "Oh. Bad idea?"

1370
01:33:46,000 --> 01:33:58,000
Kakeru: "If we're wrong, she'll just ignore it, but even if we're right, it might just make her more cautious. Still, she might reply, and that would certainly be good for us."

1371
01:33:58,000 --> 01:34:00,000
Kakeru: "You did good, kid."

1372
01:34:00,000 --> 01:34:08,000
Sora: "Ehehe, yes, good, sing my praises to the sky. Hey, wait, stop patting my head! You're gonna ruin my beautiful hair!"

1373
01:34:08,000 --> 01:34:11,000
*I try stroking her hair, but she shakes me off.*

1374
01:34:11,000 --> 01:34:12,000
*How cruel.*

1375
01:34:12,000 --> 01:34:20,000
Kakeru: "For now, all we can do is wait. If nothing happens by the time school ends, we'll rethink our strategy."

1376
01:34:20,000 --> 01:34:23,000
Miyako: "You said you gave her your ID, Sora-chan?"

1377
01:34:23,000 --> 01:34:25,000
Sora: "Hm? Oh, uh... of course."

1378
01:34:25,000 --> 01:34:28,000
Kakeru: "Hold it right there. What was that?"

1379
01:34:28,000 --> 01:34:29,000
Sora: "What was what?"

1380
01:34:29,000 --> 01:34:33,000
Kakeru: "You hesitated. Whose ID did you REALLY write down?"

1381
01:34:33,000 --> 01:34:34,000
Sora: "..."

1382
01:34:34,000 --> 01:34:37,000
Kakeru: "Christ, don't even bother answering."

1383
01:34:37,000 --> 01:34:39,000
Sora: "Please, forgive me!"

1384
01:34:39,000 --> 01:34:50,000
Kakeru: "Nah, honestly, it's fine. If anything, it was a good idea. I'm just another guy, so it's not like it'll be a big deal even if she leaks my ID to her followers."

1385
01:34:50,000 --> 01:34:54,000
Sora: "Wait, what the heck?! Get angry! You're ruining the joke!"

1386
01:34:54,000 --> 01:34:58,000
Kakeru: "What's with you? God, you're a pain in the ass."

1387
01:34:58,000 --> 01:35:05,000
Miyako: "Haha. Niimi-kun, you're so blunt with her, but you really dote on your little sister, don't you?"

1388
01:35:05,000 --> 01:35:08,000
Kakeru: "Uh, no, you're way off-base."

1389
01:35:08,000 --> 01:35:12,000
Sora: "C'mon, tell her the truth. You're just crazy about me!"

1390
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:14,000
Kakeru: "In your dreams."

1391
01:35:14,000 --> 01:35:20,000
Miyako: "I find it hard to believe you'd jump into a sea of fire for her unless you loved her."

1392
01:35:20,000 --> 01:35:23,000
Sora: "Preach it, sister! You adore me, don't you?"

1393
01:35:23,000 --> 01:35:25,000
Kakeru: "God, put a cork in it."

1394
01:35:25,000 --> 01:35:27,000
Sora: "We won't judge you for it!"

1395
01:35:27,000 --> 01:35:28,000
Kakeru: "Drop dead."

1396
01:35:28,000 --> 01:35:30,000
Sora: "You're terrible!"

1397
01:35:30,000 --> 01:35:34,000
Miyako: "Haha. I wish I had someone I was so close to."

1398
01:35:34,000 --> 01:35:36,000
Kakeru: "Wait, what do you mean?"

1399
01:35:36,000 --> 01:35:41,000
Sora: "Yeah, for realsies, what part of that looked like we're close?"

1400
01:35:41,000 --> 01:35:53,000
Miyako: "Well, the fact that he can even say something like 'drop dead' proves that he knows you won't take it the wrong way. Niimi-kun would never say that to me, for instance."

1401
01:35:53,000 --> 01:35:56,000
Kakeru: "You know, I can't deny that."

1402
01:35:56,000 --> 01:35:59,000
Miyako: "Haha. I'm a little envious of you two."

1403
01:35:59,000 --> 01:36:05,000
Sora: "Huh. So you want someone to tell you to drop dead. Are you some kind of masochist?"

1404
01:36:05,000 --> 01:36:15,000
Miyako: "No, that's not what I meant. I'm an only child, so I was just thinking how nice it'd be to have a dependable older brother like Niimi-kun."

1405
01:36:15,000 --> 01:36:16,000
Kakeru: "..."

1406
01:36:16,000 --> 01:36:20,000
Sora: "Yo, that's one hell of a shit-eating grin you're wearing."

1407
01:36:20,000 --> 01:36:23,000
Kakeru: "Who asked for your opinion, stupid?!"

1408
01:36:23,000 --> 01:36:26,000
Sora: "You're the stupid one, stupid!"

1409
01:36:26,000 --> 01:36:29,000
Miyako: "Hahaha. What a happy famiwwy."

1410
01:36:29,000 --> 01:36:32,000
Sora: "Uh, did you just lisp the heck out of that?"

1411
01:36:32,000 --> 01:36:33,000
Miyako: "..."

1412
01:36:33,000 --> 01:36:35,000
Sora: "You totally lisped."

1413
01:36:35,000 --> 01:36:37,000
Miyako: "What a... happy family."

1414
01:36:37,000 --> 01:36:38,000
Sora: "Happy famiwwy?"

1415
01:36:38,000 --> 01:36:41,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry. Please just let it go."

1416
01:36:41,000 --> 01:36:47,000
Sora: "Oh my god, look at that blush! Senpai, you're so cute I'm taking you home with me!"

1417
01:36:47,000 --> 01:36:49,000
Kakeru: "You're merciless."

1418
01:36:49,000 --> 01:36:56,000
Sora: "If all you're going to do is sigh at my jokes, I'm left with no recourse but to tease Miya instead."

1419
01:36:56,000 --> 01:37:00,000
Miyako: "Please, I'm begging you, don't. I'm sorry..."

1420
01:37:00,000 --> 01:37:02,000
*Still blushing, she hangs her head.*

1421
01:37:02,000 --> 01:37:12,000
*You may be wondering why I'm not telling off Sora for bullying Kujo. The reason should be obvious, however. Kujo is freaking adorable like this!*

1422
01:37:12,000 --> 01:37:18,000
*I'm sorry, Kujo! I couldn't live up your lofty ideals for me as a caring older brother figure!*

1423
01:37:18,000 --> 01:37:22,000
Miyako: "I-I sure hope she gets in contact with you!"

1424
01:37:22,000 --> 01:37:29,000
Sora: "Try and change the subject all you want, Senpai, but the teasing will continue until morale improves."

1425
01:37:29,000 --> 01:37:33,000
Miyako: "Ugh. I bet even you lisp things now and then, Sora-chan."

1426
01:37:33,000 --> 01:37:37,000
Sora: "You know, can't say I do! I've got perfect pwonuncia..."

1427
01:37:37,000 --> 01:37:39,000
Miyako: "Hey, you just lisped!"

1428
01:37:39,000 --> 01:37:41,000
Sora: "No, no, you must be mistaken."

1429
01:37:41,000 --> 01:37:45,000
Miyako: "Yes you did! You were about to say 'pwonunciation!'"

1430
01:37:45,000 --> 01:37:50,000
Sora: "Nah, nothing like that happened. Senpai, you should get your ears checked."

1431
01:37:50,000 --> 01:37:53,000
Miyako: "Sheesh, you're being a meanie, Sora-chan."

1432
01:37:53,000 --> 01:37:59,000
*I'm keeping out of the conversation, enjoying the sight of the two of them bantering.*

1433
01:37:59,000 --> 01:38:05,000
*It's only thanks to Sora that Kujo feels comfortable enough to show us this side of herself.*

1434
01:38:05,000 --> 01:38:13,000
*As I mentally offer her my thanks, we make our way to school, the two girls still continuing their back-and-forth.*

1435
01:38:13,000 --> 01:38:19,000
Yoichi: "Y'know, Kakeru, I kinda feel like our relationship has gotten a bit strained lately."

1436
01:38:19,000 --> 01:38:25,000
*Lunchtime. Yoichi is staring at me with dissatisfaction while gnawing on his sandwich.*

1437
01:38:25,000 --> 01:38:26,000
Kakeru: "That so?"

1438
01:38:26,000 --> 01:38:32,000
Yoichi: "I'll say. I keep inviting you to hang out, but you just go straight home, dude."

1439
01:38:32,000 --> 01:38:41,000
Kakeru: "You wanted me to go to karaoke with some girls or something dumb like that, right? I've told you before, that's not my scene."

1440
01:38:41,000 --> 01:38:44,000
Yoichi: "I knew it. Kakeru, you really are..."

1441
01:38:44,000 --> 01:38:45,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

1442
01:38:45,000 --> 01:38:47,000
Yoichi: "You really ARE gay."

1443
01:38:47,000 --> 01:38:48,000
Kakeru: "Moron."

1444
01:38:48,000 --> 01:38:53,000
Yoichi: "I'm sorry. I can't do this with you, Kakeru. It's just not me."

1445
01:38:53,000 --> 01:38:55,000
Kakeru: "It ain't me either, dammit."

1446
01:38:55,000 --> 01:38:59,000
*My yakisoba sandwich finished, I go to unwrap the tuna salad...*

1447
01:38:59,000 --> 01:39:04,000
*...and my phone vibrates, displaying a new message notification for LING.*

1448
01:39:04,000 --> 01:39:07,000
Yoichi: "Must be nice being you, Kakeru."

1449
01:39:07,000 --> 01:39:10,000
Kakeru: "What're you even talking about?"

1450
01:39:10,000 --> 01:39:14,000
Yoichi: "The way you and Kujo-san are hitting it off."

1451
01:39:14,000 --> 01:39:17,000
Kakeru: "Uhh, fine, but why bring it up now?"

1452
01:39:17,000 --> 01:39:20,000
Yoichi: "The message is from Kujo-san, right?"

1453
01:39:20,000 --> 01:39:24,000
Kakeru: "Uh, no. She doesn't even have her phone out, genius."

1454
01:39:24,000 --> 01:39:26,000
Yoichi: "Oh, you're right."

1455
01:39:26,000 --> 01:39:30,000
*Yoichi turns to look at her, chewing all the while.*

1456
01:39:30,000 --> 01:39:35,000
*Kujo's in a circle of her friends, all chatting while eating their meals.*

1457
01:39:35,000 --> 01:39:38,000
*Probably either Sora or Mom, but it could be...*

1458
01:39:38,000 --> 01:39:39,000
Kakeru: "..."

1459
01:39:39,000 --> 01:39:41,000
*Holy shit, it actually worked.*

1460
01:39:41,000 --> 01:39:44,000
*"Who are you? Are you a User like myself?"*

1461
01:39:44,000 --> 01:39:47,000
*Looks like Sora's idea was right on the money.*

1462
01:39:47,000 --> 01:39:49,000
*So she's got an Artifact, too.*

1463
01:39:49,000 --> 01:39:52,000
*And she just came right out and told us.*

1464
01:39:52,000 --> 01:39:57,000
*Apparently she's just as careless as us, blabbing our secrets in a busy cafe.*

1465
01:39:57,000 --> 01:40:00,000
*While I could reply to her right away...*

1466
01:40:00,000 --> 01:40:01,000
Yoichi: "Sup?"

1467
01:40:01,000 --> 01:40:05,000
Kakeru: "Just a little surprised; never got a spam message before."

1468
01:40:05,000 --> 01:40:12,000
Yoichi: "Aah, one of those 'C'mon, honey, buy a prepaid card from the store and tell me the number' scams?"

1469
01:40:12,000 --> 01:40:14,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, one of those."

1470
01:40:14,000 --> 01:40:19,000
Yoichi: "Those are still around, huh? Wonder if they'll ever go after me."

1471
01:40:19,000 --> 01:40:26,000
Kakeru: "I was thinking about jerking around the spammer, but I just can't bring myself to do it."

1472
01:40:26,000 --> 01:40:31,000
*With a pang of guilt for lying to Yoichi, I put away my phone and peek at Kujo.*

1473
01:40:31,000 --> 01:40:38,000
*I should talk this over with her before I do anything. I'll shoot her a message when she's finished eating.*

1474
01:40:38,000 --> 01:40:39,000
Yoichi: "Hey, Kakeru?"

1475
01:40:39,000 --> 01:40:40,000
Kakeru: "What?"

1476
01:40:40,000 --> 01:40:43,000
Yoichi: "Can I come over to your place?"

1477
01:40:43,000 --> 01:40:45,000
Kakeru: "Hm? Sure, but when?"

1478
01:40:45,000 --> 01:40:46,000
Yoichi: "Today."

1479
01:40:46,000 --> 01:40:51,000
Kakeru: "Today? Well, my sister is coming over after I get back home."

1480
01:40:51,000 --> 01:40:53,000
Yoichi: "Okay, tomorrow!"

1481
01:40:53,000 --> 01:40:57,000
Kakeru: "Sorry, I really treasure my time relaxing on the weekend."

1482
01:40:57,000 --> 01:41:01,000
Yoichi: "Then when CAN I come over? I wanna hang out!"

1483
01:41:01,000 --> 01:41:03,000
Kakeru: "Someday soon, I'm sure."

1484
01:41:03,000 --> 01:41:11,000
Yoichi: "Ughh. You're so cruel to me nowadays, even though we used to hang out every day when we were first-years."

1485
01:41:11,000 --> 01:41:16,000
Kakeru: "That was because you always came over to my house uninvited."

1486
01:41:16,000 --> 01:41:21,000
Yoichi: "I remember the time you snapped at me for overstaying my welcome."

1487
01:41:21,000 --> 01:41:25,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, you mean that time you infected my PC with a virus?"

1488
01:41:25,000 --> 01:41:29,000
Yoichi: "I just couldn't keep my youthful impulses in check."

1489
01:41:29,000 --> 01:41:32,000
Kakeru: "Man, do it in your OWN room."

1490
01:41:32,000 --> 01:41:37,000
Yoichi: "No can do. My parents believe I'm still an innocent little angel."

1491
01:41:37,000 --> 01:41:44,000
Kakeru: "If you acted like an angel at school too, you'd probably have a girlfriend or two by now."

1492
01:41:44,000 --> 01:41:49,000
Yoichi: "That'd be way too much effort. Besides, I don't need a girlfriend."

1493
01:41:49,000 --> 01:41:54,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Isn't that exactly what you've been complaining about lately?"

1494
01:41:54,000 --> 01:41:59,000
Yoichi: "No. What I want is a companion who will cater to my every need."

1495
01:41:59,000 --> 01:42:04,000
Kakeru: "Hot takes like that are what keep anyone from wanting to date you, dude."

1496
01:42:04,000 --> 01:42:13,000
Yoichi: "To tell the truth, I'd settle for anyone with a pair of tits at this point. How about it. Hook me up with your sister?"

1497
01:42:13,000 --> 01:42:19,000
Kakeru: "You are now absolutely forbidden from coming to my place whenever my sister is around."

1498
01:42:19,000 --> 01:42:25,000
Yoichi: "Dammit! That's it, I'm going to go out of my way to cockblock you and Kujo-san."

1499
01:42:25,000 --> 01:42:27,000
Kakeru: "Hah! Go ahead, make my day."

1500
01:42:27,000 --> 01:42:34,000
Yoichi: "I'm gonna tell her that you've got loose bowels and you're always making skid marks in your drawers!"

1501
01:42:34,000 --> 01:42:39,000
Kakeru: "You sonofa...! Shut up, dude, someone might actually believe that!"

1502
01:42:39,000 --> 01:42:44,000
*Kosaka-senpai fades from my mind as I get into arguing over nothing with Yoichi.*

1503
01:42:44,000 --> 01:42:47,000
*Guess she'll have to wait until after school.*

1504
01:42:47,000 --> 01:42:50,000
*In the meantime, I'll have to come up with a plan.*

1505
01:42:50,000 --> 01:42:59,000
Miyako: "I suppose, if Kosaka-senpai's ability is the power to charm and attract others, then she must not be the Evil Eye's User."

1506
01:42:59,000 --> 01:43:04,000
Kakeru: "We can't be certain. It might be possible to possess multiple Artifacts."

1507
01:43:04,000 --> 01:43:05,000
Miyako: "Oh, really?"

1508
01:43:05,000 --> 01:43:09,000
Kakeru: "Sophie said she has several in her possession."

1509
01:43:09,000 --> 01:43:13,000
Miyako: "Oh, I see. Not everything is the same as the anime."

1510
01:43:13,000 --> 01:43:17,000
*After school, Kujo and I head to Nine Ball together.*

1511
01:43:17,000 --> 01:43:22,000
*I messaged Kosaka-senpai for a little bit after lunch and set up a meeting.*

1512
01:43:22,000 --> 01:43:28,000
*Admittedly, from the way she talked to me, it seems like she doesn't completely trust me.*

1513
01:43:28,000 --> 01:43:32,000
Kakeru: "She didn't come across as being a bad person."

1514
01:43:32,000 --> 01:43:39,000
Miyako: "But I think we need to be on our guard. We might be coming into contact with a murderer here."

1515
01:43:39,000 --> 01:43:41,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, you're right."

1516
01:43:41,000 --> 01:43:46,000
*It makes me feel pathetic, but that idea Kujo planted scares the shit out of me.*

1517
01:43:46,000 --> 01:43:48,000
*I am seriously not ready for this.*

1518
01:43:48,000 --> 01:43:52,000
*Still, I can't afford to look bad in front of Kujo.*

1519
01:43:52,000 --> 01:43:55,000
Miyako: "I wonder if Senpai is already on her way."

1520
01:43:55,000 --> 01:44:03,000
Kakeru: "We should get there early. I'll make the approach alone. You just keep working and pretend like you don't know me."

1521
01:44:03,000 --> 01:44:07,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry for always making you do the dangerous work."

1522
01:44:07,000 --> 01:44:17,000
Kakeru: "Naw, we're just using the right people for the right jobs. If she tries anything funny, use your power to do something about it, okay?"

1523
01:44:17,000 --> 01:44:19,000
Miyako: "Yeah, will do."

1524
01:44:19,000 --> 01:44:21,000
*Kujo nods reassuringly.*

1525
01:44:21,000 --> 01:44:29,000
*If we had Sora along with us, I'd ask her to back us up as well, but instead I asked her to wait back at my apartment.*

1526
01:44:29,000 --> 01:44:40,000
*She wasn't too keen on the idea, but it's only been a week since that fire. I didn't want to put her in danger, on the off-chance that something bad does happen.*

1527
01:44:40,000 --> 01:44:43,000
Miyako: "Okay. I'll see you in there."

1528
01:44:43,000 --> 01:44:45,000
Kakeru: "Right, see ya."

1529
01:44:45,000 --> 01:44:46,000
Miyako: "Mm-hmm."

1530
01:44:46,000 --> 01:44:51,000
*I part ways with Kujo in front of the cafe, entering the cafe before her.*

1531
01:44:51,000 --> 01:44:53,000
*The place looks pretty unoccupied.*

1532
01:44:53,000 --> 01:44:54,000
*...*

1533
01:44:54,000 --> 01:44:59,000
*There, at the table near the wall, as far as possible from the entrance.*

1534
01:44:59,000 --> 01:45:00,000
*It's Kosaka-senpai.*

1535
01:45:00,000 --> 01:45:07,000
*The waitress comes up to me and offers to show me to a seat, but I decline and make my way to the far table.*

1536
01:45:07,000 --> 01:45:11,000
*I pull out the chair across from Senpai and take my seat.*

1537
01:45:11,000 --> 01:45:12,000
Haruka: "Huh? Oh...?"

1538
01:45:12,000 --> 01:45:15,000
Kakeru: "Pleased to meet you, Kosaka-senpai."

1539
01:45:15,000 --> 01:45:17,000
Haruka: "I-It was you?"

1540
01:45:17,000 --> 01:45:21,000
Kakeru: "Yes. I'm the one who sent you those messages."

1541
01:45:21,000 --> 01:45:22,000
Haruka: "..."

1542
01:45:22,000 --> 01:45:25,000
*She's looking down, timid and fidgety.*

1543
01:45:25,000 --> 01:45:28,000
*She murmurs to herself, just barely audible.*

1544
01:45:28,000 --> 01:45:31,000
Haruka: "I... I thought you'd be a girl."

1545
01:45:31,000 --> 01:45:36,000
*Oh. The letter was in Sora's handwriting, so it's no surprise she got confused.*

1546
01:45:36,000 --> 01:45:38,000
*But that's neither here nor there.*

1547
01:45:38,000 --> 01:45:39,000
Haruka: "..."

1548
01:45:39,000 --> 01:45:43,000
*She keeps staring at the table, not so much as glancing at me.*

1549
01:45:43,000 --> 01:45:50,000
*She's nothing like she was this morning. Perhaps this is what she's really like? I couldn't say.*

1550
01:45:50,000 --> 01:45:54,000
*That first time I saw her, she acted all timid like this.*

1551
01:45:54,000 --> 01:45:55,000
Miyako: "Welcome."

1552
01:45:55,000 --> 01:45:58,000
*Kujo brings a glass of water for me.*

1553
01:45:58,000 --> 01:46:06,000
*She must have changed in a hurry. She's usually immaculate in her waitress uniform, but this time it's obviously wrinkled.*

1554
01:46:06,000 --> 01:46:10,000
Miyako: "Please let me know once you are ready to order."

1555
01:46:10,000 --> 01:46:12,000
Kakeru: "Oh, can we order now?"

1556
01:46:12,000 --> 01:46:13,000
Miyako: "Of course."

1557
01:46:13,000 --> 01:46:17,000
Kakeru: "Are you going to order something, too, Senpai?"

1558
01:46:17,000 --> 01:46:19,000
Haruka: "Huh? Um, I..."

1559
01:46:19,000 --> 01:46:26,000
*She snaps her head up and reaches for the menu, but then she freezes and pulls away from it for some reason.*

1560
01:46:26,000 --> 01:46:29,000
*She's so nervous that I feel sorry for her.*

1561
01:46:29,000 --> 01:46:35,000
*I can't imagine she's our murderer, but even so, I mustn't let my guard down just yet.*

1562
01:46:35,000 --> 01:46:40,000
Kakeru: "Uh, we'll take two iced teas. Is that okay with you, Senpai?"

1563
01:46:40,000 --> 01:46:41,000
Haruka: "..."

1564
01:46:41,000 --> 01:46:45,000
*She timidly nods in reply, shivering like a chihuahua.*

1565
01:46:45,000 --> 01:46:50,000
*Man, I feel so guilty. She's acting like I'm here to threaten her.*

1566
01:46:50,000 --> 01:46:52,000
Kakeru: "Two iced teas, then."

1567
01:46:52,000 --> 01:46:55,000
Miyako: "Understood. I will be right back."

1568
01:46:55,000 --> 01:46:58,000
*Kujo bows and briefly catches my eye.*

1569
01:46:58,000 --> 01:47:02,000
*I nod ever so slightly, trying to avoid Senpai noticing.*

1570
01:47:02,000 --> 01:47:05,000
*I wait for Kujo to leave before opening my mouth.*

1571
01:47:05,000 --> 01:47:11,000
Kakeru: "I'm sorry for the impromptu meeting today. That letter must have surprised you."

1572
01:47:11,000 --> 01:47:12,000
Haruka: "..."

1573
01:47:12,000 --> 01:47:18,000
Kakeru: "Thing is, I'm on that Leaves of Agastya forum. You're familiar with it, I take it?"

1574
01:47:18,000 --> 01:47:19,000
Haruka: "..."

1575
01:47:19,000 --> 01:47:28,000
Kakeru: "I saw you on the way to school every morning, and I thought, maybe... So, I used my power to deliver that letter to you."

1576
01:47:28,000 --> 01:47:30,000
Haruka: "Your power...?"

1577
01:47:30,000 --> 01:47:36,000
Kakeru: "It ended up in your pocket without you noticing, right? I did that with my power."

1578
01:47:36,000 --> 01:47:37,000
Haruka: "..."

1579
01:47:37,000 --> 01:47:38,000
Kakeru: "..."

1580
01:47:38,000 --> 01:47:40,000
*This is going nowhere.*

1581
01:47:40,000 --> 01:47:46,000
*Damn, this is extra tough on me considering how terrible I am at keeping a conversation going.*

1582
01:47:46,000 --> 01:47:49,000
*Guess I should have had Sora tag along after all.*

1583
01:47:49,000 --> 01:47:54,000
Kakeru: "Oh, right, I haven't introduced myself yet. My name is Kakeru Niimi."

1584
01:47:54,000 --> 01:47:55,000
Haruka: "..."

1585
01:47:55,000 --> 01:47:56,000
Haruka: "......"

1586
01:47:56,000 --> 01:47:58,000
Haruka: "M-My name is..."

1587
01:47:58,000 --> 01:47:59,000
Haruka: "..."

1588
01:47:59,000 --> 01:48:00,000
Haruka: "..."

1589
01:48:00,000 --> 01:48:01,000
Haruka: "Ko..."

1590
01:48:01,000 --> 01:48:02,000
Haruka: "..."

1591
01:48:02,000 --> 01:48:03,000
Haruka: "K-K-Ko..."

1592
01:48:03,000 --> 01:48:04,000
Haruka: "......"

1593
01:48:04,000 --> 01:48:08,000
*Stammering like mad, she takes a deep sigh and hangs her head.*

1594
01:48:08,000 --> 01:48:10,000
*Is she afraid of strangers?*

1595
01:48:10,000 --> 01:48:14,000
*Maybe she gets all domineering once she's gotten used to you.*

1596
01:48:14,000 --> 01:48:18,000
*Boy... this looks like it's gonna be a long, drawn-out struggle.*

1597
01:48:18,000 --> 01:48:19,000
Haruka: "..."

1598
01:48:19,000 --> 01:48:20,000
Kakeru: "...?"

1599
01:48:20,000 --> 01:48:22,000
*Something's off here.*

1600
01:48:22,000 --> 01:48:29,000
*I can't quite describe what happened, but I'm suddenly getting a completely different vibe off of Senpai.*

1601
01:48:29,000 --> 01:48:31,000
*There's no way I'm imagining it.*

1602
01:48:31,000 --> 01:48:32,000
Haruka: "..."

1603
01:48:32,000 --> 01:48:38,000
*Senpai raises her head, and every trace of nervousness has vanished from her features.*

1604
01:48:38,000 --> 01:48:43,000
Haruka: "You may call me Haruka Kosaka. Pleased to make your acquaintance."

1605
01:48:43,000 --> 01:48:44,000
Kakeru: "Oh, r-right."

1606
01:48:44,000 --> 01:48:46,000
*What's with the fancy talk?*

1607
01:48:46,000 --> 01:48:53,000
*Hold on, no, the way she talks is the least of my concerns. What's the deal with this sudden transformation?*

1608
01:48:53,000 --> 01:48:56,000
*It's like she's a different person altogether.*

1609
01:48:56,000 --> 01:49:02,000
*A different person, or perhaps just a different personality. Is this a part of her power, too?*

1610
01:49:02,000 --> 01:49:07,000
*Charm, and a split personality. Maybe she really does have multiple powers.*

1611
01:49:07,000 --> 01:49:14,000
*I've been staying wary, but somewhere in my mind, I was certain she wouldn't have more than one.*

1612
01:49:14,000 --> 01:49:15,000
*How careless of me.*

1613
01:49:15,000 --> 01:49:17,000
Miyako: "Thank you for waiting."

1614
01:49:17,000 --> 01:49:27,000
*She arranges a glass of iced tea, a straw, and two little containers, one with simple syrup and one with milk, in front of both Senpai and me.*

1615
01:49:27,000 --> 01:49:30,000
Miyako: "Is there anything else I can get for you?"

1616
01:49:30,000 --> 01:49:32,000
Haruka: "This will be all."

1617
01:49:32,000 --> 01:49:34,000
Miyako: "...Please, enjoy."

1618
01:49:34,000 --> 01:49:44,000
*Kujo hesitates a moment at Senpai's haughty tone, but regains her composure quickly, leaving the check on the table with a bow before walking away.*

1619
01:49:44,000 --> 01:49:54,000
*She turns back halfway and casts a worried look at me, but since I'm unable to give her any kind of obvious reaction, I simply put my straw into the glass.*

1620
01:49:54,000 --> 01:50:02,000
*With some ceremony, she picks up the syrup and pours a little into her drink, before daintily stirring it with her straw.*

1621
01:50:02,000 --> 01:50:07,000
Haruka: "Now, I believe you were saying that you had seen my posts on that forum."

1622
01:50:07,000 --> 01:50:09,000
Kakeru: "Oh, uh, right."

1623
01:50:09,000 --> 01:50:14,000
Haruka: "In that case, you are already well informed regarding my troubles."

1624
01:50:14,000 --> 01:50:18,000
Kakeru: "Yes. Your powers are getting the better of yo..."

1625
01:50:18,000 --> 01:50:19,000
Haruka: "..."

1626
01:50:19,000 --> 01:50:23,000
*With a delicate flourish, Senpai lifts her hand, palm facing me.*

1627
01:50:23,000 --> 01:50:33,000
Haruka: "While I did indeed post something of that sort to that message board, I fear these matters are not a suitable topic for a place such as this."

1628
01:50:33,000 --> 01:50:36,000
Kakeru: "Oh. Right, sorry about that."

1629
01:50:36,000 --> 01:50:43,000
Haruka: "No, no need for apologies. Thank you ever so much for reaching out to me in the first place."

1630
01:50:43,000 --> 01:50:52,000
Haruka: "You are most unlike those other men who only approach me in an effort to win my affection. You have been terribly kind."

1631
01:50:52,000 --> 01:50:53,000
Kakeru: "R-Right..."

1632
01:50:53,000 --> 01:50:55,000
*Great, now I'M the one stammering.*

1633
01:50:55,000 --> 01:51:03,000
*She's just oozing confidence head to toe. She couldn't say a word earlier, but suddenly she's hot and she knows it.*

1634
01:51:03,000 --> 01:51:09,000
*Her personality has taken a complete one-eighty. She really is a different person.*

1635
01:51:09,000 --> 01:51:12,000
Haruka: "Will you allow me a question?"

1636
01:51:12,000 --> 01:51:13,000
Kakeru: "Uh, sure."

1637
01:51:13,000 --> 01:51:19,000
Haruka: "I am curious why you went through so much effort to get in contact with me."

1638
01:51:19,000 --> 01:51:21,000
Kakeru: "Oh, yes, well..."

1639
01:51:21,000 --> 01:51:26,000
*Do I just come right out and tell her that I'm looking for the Evil Eye's User?*

1640
01:51:26,000 --> 01:51:31,000
*No, bad idea. There's still the possibility that she's the culprit.*

1641
01:51:31,000 --> 01:51:32,000
*In that case...*

1642
01:51:32,000 --> 01:51:35,000
Kakeru: "I've been searching for allies."

1643
01:51:35,000 --> 01:51:36,000
Haruka: "Oh? Do tell."

1644
01:51:36,000 --> 01:51:47,000
Kakeru: "Well, maybe this will sound silly, but like, I think we are The Leaves of Agastya. It's like we're all lost in the world of Mobius. You know what I mean?"

1645
01:51:47,000 --> 01:51:51,000
Haruka: "Yes, I do. I have at times felt lost myself."

1646
01:51:51,000 --> 01:52:01,000
Kakeru: "Right! So I figured, I should find companions in the same situation. And, as I was thinking that, I came across a certain genuine-looking post."

1647
01:52:01,000 --> 01:52:03,000
Haruka: "By which you mean mine."

1648
01:52:03,000 --> 01:52:05,000
Kakeru: "Yes, exactly."

1649
01:52:05,000 --> 01:52:06,000
Haruka: "..."

1650
01:52:06,000 --> 01:52:09,000
Haruka: "I can feel the hand of fate upon us."

1651
01:52:09,000 --> 01:52:10,000
Kakeru: "Pardon?"

1652
01:52:10,000 --> 01:52:11,000
Haruka: "..."

1653
01:52:11,000 --> 01:52:12,000
Kakeru: "Uh. What?"

1654
01:52:12,000 --> 01:52:19,000
*She unravels the ribbon on her uniform, pops open the buttons on her blouse, and spreads open the collar.*

1655
01:52:19,000 --> 01:52:21,000
*What on earth is she thinking?!*

1656
01:52:21,000 --> 01:52:25,000
Haruka: "I don't suppose you'd like to... retire somewhere else?"

1657
01:52:25,000 --> 01:52:27,000
Kakeru: "Uh. Like where?"

1658
01:52:27,000 --> 01:52:30,000
Haruka: "Preferably, somewhere we can be alone."

1659
01:52:30,000 --> 01:52:31,000
Kakeru: "Wait, what?!"

1660
01:52:31,000 --> 01:52:35,000
*I reach for my glass, and Senpai places her hand over mine.*

1661
01:52:35,000 --> 01:52:42,000
*Am I going crazy here? Why is this happening?! Flustered, I start fretting that Kujo might see us like this.*

1662
01:52:42,000 --> 01:52:44,000
*Seriously, what the hell?!*

1663
01:52:44,000 --> 01:52:48,000
Haruka: "You shall be my white knight, the one to lead me to Eden."

1664
01:52:48,000 --> 01:52:51,000
Kakeru: "Wh-What do you mean by that?"

1665
01:52:51,000 --> 01:52:56,000
Haruka: "We shall become Adam and Eve, and birth a paradise on Earth."

1666
01:52:56,000 --> 01:53:00,000
Kakeru: "No, see, I think I'm missing something here."

1667
01:53:00,000 --> 01:53:02,000
Haruka: "Look into my eyes."

1668
01:53:02,000 --> 01:53:04,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Oh, okay."

1669
01:53:04,000 --> 01:53:07,000
*This is odd. I'm getting lightheaded.*

1670
01:53:07,000 --> 01:53:12,000
*Lazing around with my computer playing music on shuffle, I mull things over.*

1671
01:53:12,000 --> 01:53:15,000
*There are two newly emerged Artifact Users.*

1672
01:53:15,000 --> 01:53:17,000
*Haruka Kosaka and Noa Yuuki.*

1673
01:53:17,000 --> 01:53:31,000
*I think I can consider Kosaka-senpai to be on our side, but I have to be careful with her. She said she'll explain her powers the next time we meet, but to be frank, I don't really want to see her again.*

1674
01:53:31,000 --> 01:53:42,000
*Yuuki, on the other hand, clearly has no intention of getting along with us. If anything, she's straight-up hostile. However, at least our objectives are similar.*

1675
01:53:42,000 --> 01:53:44,000
*Well, in that case...*

1676
01:53:44,000 --> 01:53:48,000
*Why do Miyako, Sora, and I even need to be involved?*

1677
01:53:48,000 --> 01:53:54,000
*If we get Yuuki and Sophie to join forces, we can put an end to our part in this.*

1678
01:53:54,000 --> 01:53:58,000
*There will be no need for Kujo to put herself in harm's way.*

1679
01:53:58,000 --> 01:54:00,000
*It makes perfect sense.*

1680
01:54:00,000 --> 01:54:01,000
*Still...*

1681
01:54:01,000 --> 01:54:04,000
Kakeru: "Convincing Kujo isn't going to be easy."

1682
01:54:04,000 --> 01:54:06,000
*I grimace, scratching my stomach.*

1683
01:54:06,000 --> 01:54:17,000
*Wanting to see justice done is certainly a factor in why Kujo is after the Evil Eye's User, but I have a feeling she's also seeking some sort of validation.*

1684
01:54:17,000 --> 01:54:27,000
*Kujo is uncomfortable with the mere existence of this power to steal from others, and much more so with the fact that she was chosen to wield that power.*

1685
01:54:27,000 --> 01:54:33,000
*And so now she's trying to prove that it's a positive thing, by using it to uphold justice.*

1686
01:54:33,000 --> 01:54:37,000
*Or at least, that's the impression I get from watching her.*

1687
01:54:37,000 --> 01:54:40,000
*Today, I'm a bit late to my noon meal.*

1688
01:54:40,000 --> 01:54:42,000
*I'm having ginger pork.*

1689
01:54:42,000 --> 01:54:49,000
*I was holding out hope that Kujo might be around the cafe, but unfortunately, she's nowhere to be seen.*

1690
01:54:49,000 --> 01:54:53,000
*If she did have a shift today, it'd probably be in the evening.*

1691
01:54:53,000 --> 01:54:54,000
*...*

1692
01:54:54,000 --> 01:54:59,000
*If I really did come here hoping to see Kujo, does that make me a stalker?*

1693
01:54:59,000 --> 01:55:05,000
*Alas, gone are the days when I came to this cafe just looking forward to the grub.*

1694
01:55:05,000 --> 01:55:08,000
*I hunch down in my seat and focus on eating.*

1695
01:55:08,000 --> 01:55:13,000
Miyako: "Wow, what a rare sight. You're never here for lunch, Niimi-kun."

1696
01:55:13,000 --> 01:55:14,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Oh!"

1697
01:55:14,000 --> 01:55:16,000
*That was Kujo's voice!*

1698
01:55:16,000 --> 01:55:21,000
*I look up to see her set down a plate across from me and take a seat.*

1699
01:55:21,000 --> 01:55:23,000
Miyako: "Mind if I eat with you?"

1700
01:55:23,000 --> 01:55:27,000
Kakeru: "O-Oh, of course not. You came here for lunch too, Kujo?"

1701
01:55:27,000 --> 01:55:34,000
Miyako: "Nah, I just got off work. Grandfather told me to have lunch before I left and made me something."

1702
01:55:34,000 --> 01:55:38,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah? Hahah, how about that. You sure surprised me."

1703
01:55:38,000 --> 01:55:41,000
Miyako: "I was surprised to see you too! Haha."

1704
01:55:41,000 --> 01:55:45,000
*She puts her hands together in prayer before picking up her fork.*

1705
01:55:45,000 --> 01:55:47,000
*Spaghetti Napoletana, huh?*

1706
01:55:47,000 --> 01:55:51,000
Kakeru: "Looks great. I should try ordering that next time."

1707
01:55:51,000 --> 01:55:58,000
Miyako: "Oh. You should know, when we're properly serving it, we actually bring it out on a small griddle."

1708
01:55:58,000 --> 01:55:59,000
Kakeru: "A what?"

1709
01:55:59,000 --> 01:56:11,000
Miyako: "You know! The sizzling-hot iron cookware you sometimes see restaurants serve steaks on. We crack an egg on the griddle, too, before we plate the pasta on it. It's great."

1710
01:56:11,000 --> 01:56:14,000
Kakeru: "Cool. I'll give it a try next time I come."

1711
01:56:14,000 --> 01:56:19,000
Miyako: "Haha, I'm looking forward to it. Were you out on an errand, Niimi-kun?"

1712
01:56:19,000 --> 01:56:23,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Naw, I was just kicking around the apartment."

1713
01:56:23,000 --> 01:56:32,000
Miyako: "Oh, I see. You're in for such a late lunch that I thought you maybe stopped by the cafe on your way back home from something."

1714
01:56:32,000 --> 01:56:37,000
Kakeru: "I was waiting out the lunch rush, since I figured it'd be crowded."

1715
01:56:37,000 --> 01:56:47,000
Miyako: "Well, you were right about that. We get a lot of families in here on the weekends around lunchtime, though it does calm down by nighttime."

1716
01:56:47,000 --> 01:56:51,000
Kakeru: "You're a hard worker, coming in on the weekends too."

1717
01:56:51,000 --> 01:56:58,000
Miyako: "Why thank you. But I'm doing it because I enjoy it. Haha. It's good real-world experience, too."

1718
01:56:58,000 --> 01:57:06,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I've been thinking about working a serious part-time job myself. Pretty hard to take that first step, though."

1719
01:57:06,000 --> 01:57:14,000
Miyako: "Having a job is great. As tough as it may be, it really changes how you view the world. Not to mention, you get paid."

1720
01:57:14,000 --> 01:57:18,000
Kakeru: "I bet you're the type to save all your pay?"

1721
01:57:18,000 --> 01:57:22,000
Miyako: "Yep! Though... I do spoil myself once a month."

1722
01:57:22,000 --> 01:57:24,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah? Like how?"

1723
01:57:24,000 --> 01:57:30,000
Miyako: "Like going to Nockoff Ichibanya for curry, or getting a burger from MockDonald's!"

1724
01:57:30,000 --> 01:57:33,000
Kakeru: "Ah, I see. You're really splurging there."

1725
01:57:33,000 --> 01:57:44,000
Miyako: "Right? It always ends up costing well over five hundred yen, and, sometimes it can be close to a thousand! That's why I only spoil myself once a month."

1726
01:57:44,000 --> 01:57:49,000
Kakeru: "Y'know, Kujo, it's kind of surprising to hear you eat out."

1727
01:57:49,000 --> 01:57:56,000
Miyako: "'Money must not only be saved, and when spent, must be spent without a moment's hesitation!'"

1728
01:57:56,000 --> 01:57:58,000
Kakeru: "Another family motto?"

1729
01:57:58,000 --> 01:58:09,000
Miyako: "Yes. If you simply horde all your money, then the economy will stagnate, which is why spending is just as important. According to Grandfather, at least."

1730
01:58:09,000 --> 01:58:19,000
Kakeru: "That makes sense. So you're just doing your part to keep the economy buzzing with your extravagant thousand yen purchases, huh, Kujo?"

1731
01:58:19,000 --> 01:58:25,000
Miyako: "Hey! It's not like I don't know I'm a cheapskate. You don't have to be rude about it."

1732
01:58:25,000 --> 01:58:34,000
Kakeru: "Hahah, my bad. I'm still just sponging off of my parents, so I want you to know, I think it's pretty cool what you do."

1733
01:58:34,000 --> 01:58:37,000
Miyako: "You could've said that sooner."

1734
01:58:37,000 --> 01:58:38,000
Kakeru: "Aw, come on."

1735
01:58:38,000 --> 01:58:41,000
Miyako: "Haha. Oh, feel free to have seconds."

1736
01:58:41,000 --> 01:58:44,000
Kakeru: "Oh, nah, I'll be fine. Thanks though."

1737
01:58:44,000 --> 01:58:47,000
*We chat through the rest of our meal.*

1738
01:58:47,000 --> 01:58:56,000
*We've avoided talking about the Artifact stuff, but right when we're about done with our food, Kujo speaks to me in a muted tone.*

1739
01:58:56,000 --> 01:58:59,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, do you have plans after this?"

1740
01:58:59,000 --> 01:59:01,000
Kakeru: "No, not really."

1741
01:59:01,000 --> 01:59:05,000
Miyako: "Um, then, would you mind accompanying me for a bit?"

1742
01:59:05,000 --> 01:59:10,000
Kakeru: "This about the experiment? I know we couldn't do it yesterday."

1743
01:59:10,000 --> 01:59:18,000
Miyako: "Well, there is that, but I wanted to try going to the park one more time today. There, and one more place."

1744
01:59:18,000 --> 01:59:19,000
Kakeru: "Ah. Right."

1745
01:59:19,000 --> 01:59:24,000
*So she wants to visit the scene of the second petrification incident.*

1746
01:59:24,000 --> 01:59:30,000
Miyako: "I figure we might find out something about our culprit. Every little bit helps."

1747
01:59:30,000 --> 01:59:32,000
Kakeru: "Looking for clues, huh?"

1748
01:59:32,000 --> 01:59:36,000
Miyako: "Though I'm doubtful there are any still left to be found."

1749
01:59:36,000 --> 01:59:44,000
Kakeru: "Well, it won't hurt to go take a look. There might be something there that nobody but us would recognize."

1750
01:59:44,000 --> 01:59:46,000
Miyako: "Okay. Thank you."

1751
01:59:46,000 --> 01:59:49,000
Kakeru: "Alright, let's finish eating and mosey."

1752
01:59:49,000 --> 01:59:52,000
Miyako: "As always, thank you for your your help."

1753
01:59:52,000 --> 01:59:54,000
Kakeru: "You're most welcome."

1754
01:59:54,000 --> 02:00:02,000
*For some reason, we courteously bow our heads to one another, before quickly finishing off the rest of our meals.*

1755
02:00:02,000 --> 02:00:07,000
*In a surprise twist, I find myself together with Kujo yet again today.*

1756
02:00:07,000 --> 02:00:17,000
*A part of me is ecstatic, thinking about what a lucky break this is, but the rest of me is all too aware that we're heading to the scene of a murder.*

1757
02:00:17,000 --> 02:00:18,000
*I've got to focus.*

1758
02:00:18,000 --> 02:00:23,000
*We exit Nine Ball, first stopping by the convenience store near the station.*

1759
02:00:23,000 --> 02:00:29,000
*Seems like we're in for a long day, so we're going to buy something to drink first.*

1760
02:00:29,000 --> 02:00:37,000
Miyako: "Haha... There I go spoiling myself again. It's been so long since I've bought tea at a convenience store."

1761
02:00:37,000 --> 02:00:38,000
Kakeru: "Hmm..."

1762
02:00:38,000 --> 02:00:40,000
Miyako: "...? What's the matter?"

1763
02:00:40,000 --> 02:00:43,000
Kakeru: "Okay, this has been bugging me."

1764
02:00:43,000 --> 02:00:44,000
Miyako: "...?"

1765
02:00:44,000 --> 02:00:49,000
Kakeru: "So this bottle of water cost me a hundred and eight yen. Fine, whatever."

1766
02:00:49,000 --> 02:00:50,000
Miyako: "Okay?"

1767
02:00:50,000 --> 02:00:57,000
Kakeru: "But you know the ones bigger than these? The two-liter ones? They're just a hundred yen."

1768
02:00:57,000 --> 02:01:02,000
Miyako: "Oh yeah, you're right! The smaller ones are more expensive."

1769
02:01:02,000 --> 02:01:06,000
Kakeru: "Right, exactly. That kinda rubs me the wrong way."

1770
02:01:06,000 --> 02:01:15,000
Miyako: "I wonder if there's some reason for it. It's not just this one; even at other convenience stores, the two-liter bottle is cheaper."

1771
02:01:15,000 --> 02:01:22,000
Kakeru: "Really feels like you're getting a bad deal, doesn't it? Oh well, forget about it. Let's hit the road."

1772
02:01:22,000 --> 02:01:26,000
Miyako: "Sure. Oh, you can put your bottle in the basket."

1773
02:01:26,000 --> 02:01:33,000
Kakeru: "Cool, thanks. Alright, let's get going. The second victim was found right next to the park, right?"

1774
02:01:33,000 --> 02:01:39,000
Miyako: "Yes, that's right. Past the park and more toward the shopping district... Ah!"

1775
02:01:39,000 --> 02:01:45,000
*Just as Kujo kicks up her bike stand and starts to walk with it, she lets out a little gasp.*

1776
02:01:45,000 --> 02:01:47,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, Niimi-kun."

1777
02:01:47,000 --> 02:01:49,000
*She tugs at my shirt sleeve.*

1778
02:01:49,000 --> 02:01:52,000
*There, maybe thirty feet in front of us.*

1779
02:01:52,000 --> 02:01:55,000
*Kosaka-senpai is walking timidly, her head hung.*

1780
02:01:55,000 --> 02:02:00,000
Miyako: "Given how she looks, that's the normal Kosaka-senpai, I assume?"

1781
02:02:00,000 --> 02:02:05,000
Kakeru: "Probably, yeah. We don't want her finding us, so let's... Well, crap."

1782
02:02:05,000 --> 02:02:11,000
*I figure we should get while the getting's good, but unfortunately, she notices us.*

1783
02:02:11,000 --> 02:02:20,000
*Her eyes bug out, and she starts fidgeting, shaking her head and putting her hand to her mouth like she's coming down with a case of nausea.*

1784
02:02:20,000 --> 02:02:26,000
*But a moment later, she lifts her head again and, like a different person, smiles softly.*

1785
02:02:26,000 --> 02:02:30,000
Kakeru: "Guess we get to find out what's behind door number two."

1786
02:02:30,000 --> 02:02:33,000
Miyako: "Just what kind of power does she have?"

1787
02:02:33,000 --> 02:02:41,000
Kakeru: "She said she'd tell me about it next time we met. Anyway, she's seen us already, so we might as well talk to her."

1788
02:02:41,000 --> 02:02:50,000
*Kosaka-senpai holds the hem of her skirt and curtsies to us like a faux aristocrat. I give her a wave in return and walk up to her.*

1789
02:02:50,000 --> 02:02:54,000
Haruka: "To think I should see you again in such an unusual place."

1790
02:02:54,000 --> 02:03:01,000
Kakeru: "I had something to pick up at the convenience store over here. Were you at the bookstore, Senpai?"

1791
02:03:01,000 --> 02:03:06,000
Haruka: "Oh yes, just picking up a few reference materials and what have you."

1792
02:03:06,000 --> 02:03:14,000
*She puts her free hand to her cheek and smiles, lifting her shopping bag up to her chest by way of demonstration.*

1793
02:03:14,000 --> 02:03:20,000
*Yeah, I can make out a couple of the covers. She totally just bought a bunch of manga.*

1794
02:03:20,000 --> 02:03:22,000
*I really don't get this girl.*

1795
02:03:22,000 --> 02:03:28,000
Haruka: "Ahh, and let's see. You're the girl from the cafe, if I recall correctly."

1796
02:03:28,000 --> 02:03:33,000
Miyako: "My name is Miyako Kujo. Pleased to make your acquaintance."

1797
02:03:33,000 --> 02:03:34,000
Haruka: "Indeed."

1798
02:03:34,000 --> 02:03:35,000
Miyako: "..."

1799
02:03:35,000 --> 02:03:41,000
*The unbelievably cold reception is enough to make even Kujo's expression tighten.*

1800
02:03:41,000 --> 02:03:50,000
*Kosaka-senpai flashes a narrow-eyed, provocative smile at Kujo, who is still frowning, before quickly turning to face me once again.*

1801
02:03:50,000 --> 02:03:56,000
*I don't know what's going through her head, but the next thing I know, she's grabbed my hand.*

1802
02:03:56,000 --> 02:04:03,000
Haruka: "I'm certain now that you must be my knight, after destiny has seen fit to bring us together here."

1803
02:04:03,000 --> 02:04:05,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Oh, uh, uh-huh."

1804
02:04:05,000 --> 02:04:11,000
Haruka: "I don't suppose I could entice you to join me for a spot of tea? Just the two of us?"

1805
02:04:11,000 --> 02:04:14,000
Kakeru: "Uh, no, see, I've got plans."

1806
02:04:14,000 --> 02:04:19,000
Haruka: "Did you not want to be privy to the secrets of my abilities?"

1807
02:04:19,000 --> 02:04:24,000
Kakeru: "Uh, I mean, when you put it that way, yeah, I do want to know, but..."

1808
02:04:24,000 --> 02:04:35,000
Haruka: "I don't mind revealing myself to you. Come along now. Let us find somewhere more private where we can converse. I assure you, my bed is quite comfortable."

1809
02:04:35,000 --> 02:04:37,000
*Senpai's eyes shimmer alluringly.*

1810
02:04:37,000 --> 02:04:40,000
*Shit, this is bad. It's just like last time...*

1811
02:04:40,000 --> 02:04:41,000
Miyako: "..."

1812
02:04:41,000 --> 02:04:42,000
Haruka: "Oh my."

1813
02:04:42,000 --> 02:04:50,000
*Kujo thankfully steps between us, breaking senpai's gaze as well as her grip on my hand, and I slip out of my trance.*

1814
02:04:50,000 --> 02:04:54,000
*Yikes, close call. She used her power on me again, huh?*

1815
02:04:54,000 --> 02:04:58,000
Miyako: "My apologies, but Niimi-kun and I have plans together."

1816
02:04:58,000 --> 02:05:00,000
Haruka: "I'm certain they can wait."

1817
02:05:00,000 --> 02:05:02,000
Miyako: "No, they can't."

1818
02:05:02,000 --> 02:05:04,000
*Kujo gets a little snippy.*

1819
02:05:04,000 --> 02:05:08,000
*And Kosaka-senpai looks like she's ready for a fight too.*

1820
02:05:08,000 --> 02:05:15,000
*In a pathetic display, I'm too intimidated to do anything and simply watch the two of them duke it out.*

1821
02:05:15,000 --> 02:05:18,000
Haruka: "Kakeru-sama wishes to be with me, not you."

1822
02:05:18,000 --> 02:05:19,000
Kakeru: "..."

1823
02:05:19,000 --> 02:05:22,000
*I sit in class, listening with half an ear.*

1824
02:05:22,000 --> 02:05:27,000
*After... After we split up in the park, I tried sending a message to Kujo.*

1825
02:05:27,000 --> 02:05:29,000
*"I'm fine. And, I'm sorry."*

1826
02:05:29,000 --> 02:05:31,000
*That was all she sent back.*

1827
02:05:31,000 --> 02:05:35,000
*She wouldn't elaborate on why she was so shaken up.*

1828
02:05:35,000 --> 02:05:37,000
*Am I seriously the culprit?*

1829
02:05:37,000 --> 02:05:43,000
*That couldn't possibly be true. Although... there are strange cases like Kosaka-senpai.*

1830
02:05:43,000 --> 02:05:49,000
*What if I've got a second personality, and I've been doing this without even knowing it?*

1831
02:05:49,000 --> 02:05:56,000
*What if I've been completely ignorant about it this entire time, while I went out and killed people?*

1832
02:05:56,000 --> 02:05:58,000
*It's only too believable.*

1833
02:05:58,000 --> 02:06:02,000
*It would explain why Kujo is acting the way she is.*

1834
02:06:02,000 --> 02:06:08,000
*We said hi today, but we haven't had anything like an actual conversation since then.*

1835
02:06:08,000 --> 02:06:12,000
*I let out a little sigh and look up, peeking over at Kujo.*

1836
02:06:12,000 --> 02:06:13,000
Miyako: "..."

1837
02:06:13,000 --> 02:06:20,000
*Her expression is grim—even more so than that time she was fretting over her hair clip's paranormal activity.*

1838
02:06:20,000 --> 02:06:23,000
*It looks like she's also not focusing on class.*

1839
02:06:23,000 --> 02:06:28,000
*It also looks like she's trying to figure out a way to tell me the truth.*

1840
02:06:28,000 --> 02:06:41,000
*Ah, man... And we were hitting it off so well, too. Actually, y'know, it's thoughts like that, where I get all mopey at totally inappropriate times, that make me kind of question myself.*

1841
02:06:41,000 --> 02:06:42,000
Miyako: "..."

1842
02:06:42,000 --> 02:06:43,000
Kakeru: "...?"

1843
02:06:43,000 --> 02:06:48,000
*That was Kujo's Stigma, flashing for a split second on her left hand.*

1844
02:06:48,000 --> 02:06:49,000
*Am I seeing things?*

1845
02:06:49,000 --> 02:06:50,000
*No.*

1846
02:06:50,000 --> 02:06:51,000
Miyako: "..."

1847
02:06:51,000 --> 02:06:54,000
*There it is again. A momentary blue light.*

1848
02:06:54,000 --> 02:07:00,000
*I pull out my phone and type a message under my desk so that Ms. Naruse doesn't notice.*

1849
02:07:00,000 --> 02:07:02,000
*"Did you just use your power?"*

1850
02:07:02,000 --> 02:07:03,000
Miyako: "..."

1851
02:07:03,000 --> 02:07:06,000
*Kujo pulls out her phone and checks the screen.*

1852
02:07:06,000 --> 02:07:09,000
*She then quickly puts it away without replying.*

1853
02:07:09,000 --> 02:07:17,000
*I know that Kujo is a diligent person, so she'd be reluctant to have a text chat in the middle of class, but...*

1854
02:07:17,000 --> 02:07:21,000
*It just isn't like her to go using her powers on a whim.*

1855
02:07:21,000 --> 02:07:27,000
*I wonder if... No, I'm positive this has something to do with what happened yesterday.*

1856
02:07:27,000 --> 02:07:28,000
Miyako: "..."

1857
02:07:28,000 --> 02:07:32,000
*Kujo conceals her left hand in an unnatural manner.*

1858
02:07:32,000 --> 02:07:37,000
*It seems that she's been using her power over and over during class.*

1859
02:07:37,000 --> 02:07:38,000
Kakeru: "Kujo!"

1860
02:07:38,000 --> 02:07:39,000
Miyako: "...?"

1861
02:07:39,000 --> 02:07:44,000
*When Kujo leaves the room after class, I run after her and call out to her.*

1862
02:07:44,000 --> 02:07:46,000
Miyako: "What's the matter?"

1863
02:07:46,000 --> 02:07:50,000
Kakeru: "Don't give me that. You read my message, didn't you?"

1864
02:07:50,000 --> 02:07:51,000
Miyako: "Oh, yeah."

1865
02:07:51,000 --> 02:07:53,000
Kakeru: "Are you alright?"

1866
02:07:53,000 --> 02:07:55,000
Miyako: "Why do you ask?"

1867
02:07:55,000 --> 02:08:01,000
Kakeru: "You've been acting weird. I can't believe you used your power repeatedly in class."

1868
02:08:01,000 --> 02:08:03,000
Miyako: "It was necessary."

1869
02:08:03,000 --> 02:08:05,000
Kakeru: "Necessary? Why?"

1870
02:08:05,000 --> 02:08:14,000
Miyako: "When targeting things without form, it becomes difficult to steal the target I'm after. Therefore, I need to practice."

1871
02:08:14,000 --> 02:08:17,000
Kakeru: "Hold on, Kujo, you don't mean..."

1872
02:08:17,000 --> 02:08:20,000
Kakeru: "You've been stealing everyone's memories?"

1873
02:08:20,000 --> 02:08:21,000
Miyako: "..."

1874
02:08:21,000 --> 02:08:23,000
*Kujo doesn't answer my question.*

1875
02:08:23,000 --> 02:08:26,000
*But her silence is all the answer I need.*

1876
02:08:26,000 --> 02:08:28,000
Kakeru: "Why are you doing this?"

1877
02:08:28,000 --> 02:08:31,000
Miyako: "I hoped you would understand, Niimi-kun."

1878
02:08:31,000 --> 02:08:35,000
Kakeru: "You plan on just randomly searching everyone?"

1879
02:08:35,000 --> 02:08:37,000
Miyako: "Yes, precisely."

1880
02:08:37,000 --> 02:08:38,000
*Kujo readily admits.*

1881
02:08:38,000 --> 02:08:45,000
*Despite being so hesitant back when she used it on me? Despite the tremble in her hands when she did it?*

1882
02:08:45,000 --> 02:08:51,000
*That was just yesterday! How has she changed this much in the span of a single day?*

1883
02:08:51,000 --> 02:08:56,000
Miyako: "I'll be fine. Don't worry. I'll find the culprit, mark my words."

1884
02:08:56,000 --> 02:08:59,000
Kakeru: "...Is there anything I can do?"

1885
02:08:59,000 --> 02:09:00,000
Miyako: "..."

1886
02:09:00,000 --> 02:09:05,000
Miyako: "This is something I have to do. And I want to do it alone."

1887
02:09:05,000 --> 02:09:07,000
Miyako: "I feel it's my obligation."

1888
02:09:07,000 --> 02:09:08,000
Kakeru: "What?"

1889
02:09:08,000 --> 02:09:12,000
Miyako: "Thank you for everything you've done for me."

1890
02:09:12,000 --> 02:09:15,000
Miyako: "I won't trouble you any more."

1891
02:09:15,000 --> 02:09:16,000
Kakeru: "Huh? H-Hey!"

1892
02:09:16,000 --> 02:09:17,000
Miyako: "..."

1893
02:09:17,000 --> 02:09:20,000
*I reach out my hand, but it falls short.*

1894
02:09:20,000 --> 02:09:24,000
*Kujo walks down the hallway and disappears into the bathroom.*

1895
02:09:24,000 --> 02:09:25,000
*...*

1896
02:09:25,000 --> 02:09:27,000
Yoichi: "What's up? You alright?"

1897
02:09:27,000 --> 02:09:29,000
Kakeru: "Huh? O-Oh, yeah."

1898
02:09:29,000 --> 02:09:33,000
Yoichi: "Did you have a fight with Kujo-san or something?"

1899
02:09:33,000 --> 02:09:35,000
Kakeru: "No. Not exactly."

1900
02:09:35,000 --> 02:09:40,000
Yoichi: "Oh yeah? You two have been acting strange since this morning."

1901
02:09:40,000 --> 02:09:41,000
Kakeru: "..."

1902
02:09:41,000 --> 02:09:44,000
Yoichi: "You're fighting, aren't you?"

1903
02:09:44,000 --> 02:09:50,000
Kakeru: "I might have been keeping something from her. Something bad enough to spark a fight."

1904
02:09:50,000 --> 02:09:58,000
Yoichi: "Whoa, really? Kinda shocking, since you guys always give me a more-than-friends-but-less-than-lovers kinda vibe."

1905
02:09:58,000 --> 02:10:01,000
Kakeru: "Let's get back to the classroom."

1906
02:10:01,000 --> 02:10:03,000
Yoichi: "Hm? Oh, sure."

1907
02:10:03,000 --> 02:10:06,000
*We turn around and head back to the classroom.*

1908
02:10:06,000 --> 02:10:07,000
*...*

1909
02:10:07,000 --> 02:10:09,000
*She "won't trouble me anymore"?*

1910
02:10:09,000 --> 02:10:21,000
*That single comment brings me back to the same feeling of unfamiliarity I had back when I'd only just started talking to Kujo, when I was just another regular customer at Nine Ball.*

1911
02:10:21,000 --> 02:10:23,000
*That's the sense I got, at least.*

1912
02:10:23,000 --> 02:10:25,000
*The frustration is overwhelming.*

1913
02:10:25,000 --> 02:10:27,000
*I can't help but feel like...*

1914
02:10:27,000 --> 02:10:30,000
*Kujo and I have begun to drift apart.*

1915
02:10:30,000 --> 02:10:34,000
*For the past few days, Kujo and I have hardly spoken.*

1916
02:10:34,000 --> 02:10:43,000
*The only communication we've had has been me constantly sending her messages like some kind of stalker, and her replying curtly.*

1917
02:10:43,000 --> 02:10:48,000
*She doesn't come over to cook me dinner, nor does she ask me for advice.*

1918
02:10:48,000 --> 02:10:56,000
*For what it's worth, I did go back to my folks' place for Golden Week, and Kujo was busy with something or another.*

1919
02:10:56,000 --> 02:11:03,000
*But even considering that, Kujo is clearly avoiding me. It's as though she no longer deems me necessary.*

1920
02:11:03,000 --> 02:11:09,000
*Maybe it'd be an exaggeration to say I'm heartbroken, but I'm certainly pretty down.*

1921
02:11:09,000 --> 02:11:11,000
*I felt awful for the whole break.*

1922
02:11:11,000 --> 02:11:14,000
*Even when we got back, Kujo remained the same.*

1923
02:11:14,000 --> 02:11:25,000
*She hasn't been using her powers in class, but now I'm not the only one she's avoiding talking to. Even her usual group of friends are getting the cold shoulder.*

1924
02:11:25,000 --> 02:11:28,000
*Being pathetic, I actually feel relieved by that.*

1925
02:11:28,000 --> 02:11:29,000
Satsuki: "Niimi-kun!"

1926
02:11:29,000 --> 02:11:30,000
Kakeru: "...? Yes?"

1927
02:11:30,000 --> 02:11:36,000
*At the end of class, as I'm getting ready to head home, Ms. Naruse calls me over.*

1928
02:11:36,000 --> 02:11:42,000
*Wonder what she wants with me. I stuff my pencil case in my bag and head to the podium.*

1929
02:11:42,000 --> 02:11:43,000
Kakeru: "Yes, ma'am?"

1930
02:11:43,000 --> 02:11:47,000
Satsuki: "What happened?! You two were thick as thieves."

1931
02:11:47,000 --> 02:11:48,000
Kakeru: "Pardon?"

1932
02:11:48,000 --> 02:11:51,000
Satsuki: "Did you break up with Kujo-san?"

1933
02:11:51,000 --> 02:11:52,000
Kakeru: "..."

1934
02:11:52,000 --> 02:11:55,000
*Is this seriously what she wanted to talk about?*

1935
02:11:55,000 --> 02:11:57,000
Kakeru: "No. We were never dating."

1936
02:11:57,000 --> 02:12:00,000
Satsuki: "Wait, what? But everybody said you were!"

1937
02:12:00,000 --> 02:12:01,000
Kakeru: "Like who?"

1938
02:12:01,000 --> 02:12:04,000
Satsuki: "Everybody in the Kujo Fan Club."

1939
02:12:04,000 --> 02:12:07,000
Kakeru: "Mhmm. Kujo's friends, I take it?"

1940
02:12:07,000 --> 02:12:12,000
Satsuki: "If you didn't break up, then you're just having a little tiff?"

1941
02:12:12,000 --> 02:12:13,000
Kakeru: "Not exactly."

1942
02:12:13,000 --> 02:12:17,000
Satsuki: "Why don't you stop being stubborn and apologize?"

1943
02:12:17,000 --> 02:12:22,000
Kakeru: "Look, we're not fighting. Even I don't know what's going on between us."

1944
02:12:22,000 --> 02:12:29,000
Satsuki: "People keep coming to talk to me about it. I've had Murase-san, and then Miyano-san, and..."

1945
02:12:29,000 --> 02:12:31,000
Kakeru: "Who are they?"

1946
02:12:31,000 --> 02:12:35,000
Satsuki: "Would it kill you to learn your classmates' names?"

1947
02:12:35,000 --> 02:12:36,000
Kakeru: "My bad."

1948
02:12:36,000 --> 02:12:38,000
*So it's just her usual friends?*

1949
02:12:38,000 --> 02:12:47,000
Satsuki: "It's honestly a pain in the ass talking to all these people, so I'd appreciate it if you would hurry and patch things up."

1950
02:12:47,000 --> 02:12:50,000
Kakeru: "I mean, that's easier said than done..."

1951
02:12:50,000 --> 02:12:52,000
*I randomly look over my shoulder.*

1952
02:12:52,000 --> 02:12:54,000
*Kujo is already gone.*

1953
02:12:54,000 --> 02:13:02,000
Satsuki: "Or maybe something happened at home? Like, maybe the Corona Group's business is going through a downturn?"

1954
02:13:02,000 --> 02:13:04,000
Kakeru: "I don't think that's it."

1955
02:13:04,000 --> 02:13:07,000
Satsuki: "Okay then, have you heard anything?"

1956
02:13:07,000 --> 02:13:08,000
Kakeru: "Uh..."

1957
02:13:08,000 --> 02:13:10,000
Satsuki: "You're holding out on me!"

1958
02:13:10,000 --> 02:13:11,000
Kakeru: "..."

1959
02:13:11,000 --> 02:13:19,000
*"You see, ma'am, she's been acting strange ever since she read my memories." Yeah... Can't exactly go saying that, can I?*

1960
02:13:19,000 --> 02:13:21,000
Kakeru: "Nah, I don't know anything."

1961
02:13:21,000 --> 02:13:24,000
Satsuki: "You sure you're not holding out on me?"

1962
02:13:24,000 --> 02:13:26,000
Kakeru: "Definitely not."

1963
02:13:26,000 --> 02:13:35,000
Satsuki: "Hmm, all right. I'm getting worried about her. She's even been coming by the shrine at night and spacing out, lately."

1964
02:13:35,000 --> 02:13:38,000
Kakeru: "Really? What's she been doing there?"

1965
02:13:38,000 --> 02:13:49,000
Satsuki: "Oh, well I only heard this secondhand from my dad, but apparently Kujo-san has been hanging around. I'm kinda curious what she's doing there myself."

1966
02:13:49,000 --> 02:13:50,000
Kakeru: "..."

1967
02:13:50,000 --> 02:13:57,000
Satsuki: "At any rate, I'd appreciate it if you patched things up quickly so we can all stop fetting over her."

1968
02:13:57,000 --> 02:13:59,000
Kakeru: "This is my fault?"

1969
02:13:59,000 --> 02:14:08,000
Satsuki: "Incidentally, we've all seen you two out together on the weekends, so when you say you're not dating, nobody's buying it."

1970
02:14:08,000 --> 02:14:11,000
Kakeru: "I'm telling you, we really aren't."

1971
02:14:11,000 --> 02:14:16,000
Satsuki: "And yet you two always look so happy together. Go get her, tiger!"

1972
02:14:16,000 --> 02:14:21,000
*Ms. Naruse gives me a pat on the shoulder and leaves the classroom.*

1973
02:14:21,000 --> 02:14:26,000
*Seeing how Kujo is actively avoiding me, I can't do much of anything.*

1974
02:14:26,000 --> 02:14:29,000
*I breathe a sigh and return to my desk.*

1975
02:14:29,000 --> 02:14:31,000
Yoichi: "Was that about Kujo-san?"

1976
02:14:31,000 --> 02:14:33,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, pretty much."

1977
02:14:33,000 --> 02:14:43,000
Yoichi: "You need to make up with her quick, dude. There's a rumor going around that you used Kujo-san for her money and tossed her away when you were done."

1978
02:14:43,000 --> 02:14:46,000
Kakeru: "Huh? What kind of crap is that?"

1979
02:14:46,000 --> 02:14:54,000
Yoichi: "The girls are having a ball talking about it. I think they're half-joking, but they're also half-serious."

1980
02:14:54,000 --> 02:14:58,000
Kakeru: "Well, they can say what they want. Sticks and stones."

1981
02:14:58,000 --> 02:15:01,000
*I sling my bag over my shoulder and walk away.*

1982
02:15:01,000 --> 02:15:05,000
Yoichi: "Hey, wait up, Kakeru! Let's go home together!"

1983
02:15:05,000 --> 02:15:06,000
Kakeru: "..."

1984
02:15:06,000 --> 02:15:08,000
*There's nothing I can do...*

1985
02:15:08,000 --> 02:15:11,000
*Still, I can't just let things stay like this.*

1986
02:15:11,000 --> 02:15:16,000
*I wonder if the reason Sophie hasn't been showing up is because she's with Kujo.*

1987
02:15:16,000 --> 02:15:17,000
*...*

1988
02:15:17,000 --> 02:15:24,000
*Man, I give. Kujo rejecting me was such a shock that I haven't been able to make any rational decisions since.*

1989
02:15:24,000 --> 02:15:26,000
*Man, I'm such a wimp.*

1990
02:15:26,000 --> 02:15:28,000
Sora: "Yo, welcome home."

1991
02:15:28,000 --> 02:15:35,000
*Upon returning to my apartment, I find Sora already there, lazing around and munching on chocolates.*

1992
02:15:35,000 --> 02:15:36,000
Sora: "Want some?"

1993
02:15:36,000 --> 02:15:40,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, sure. Hey, this thing is empty, you jerk!"

1994
02:15:40,000 --> 02:15:41,000
Sora: "Mwahaha!"

1995
02:15:41,000 --> 02:15:46,000
*She belts out an unnatural chortle, chucking the empty box into the garbage can.*

1996
02:15:46,000 --> 02:15:48,000
Sora: "Is Miya coming today?"

1997
02:15:48,000 --> 02:15:50,000
Kakeru: "Probably not."

1998
02:15:50,000 --> 02:15:53,000
Sora: "Aww, man. I was looking forward to dinner."

1999
02:15:53,000 --> 02:15:56,000
Kakeru: "She probably won't be coming anymore."

2000
02:15:56,000 --> 02:16:00,000
Sora: "What?! What about our search for the culprit?"

2001
02:16:00,000 --> 02:16:03,000
Kakeru: "She said she wants to go it alone."

2002
02:16:03,000 --> 02:16:11,000
Sora: "Jeez, I could tell you were out of it lately, but now I know why. You two had a fight, didn't you, Bromeo?"

2003
02:16:11,000 --> 02:16:14,000
Kakeru: "No! But... I dunno, maybe we kinda did?"

2004
02:16:14,000 --> 02:16:18,000
Sora: "That's it, we're going to Nine Ball for dinner later."

2005
02:16:18,000 --> 02:16:19,000
Kakeru: "Say what?"

2006
02:16:19,000 --> 02:16:24,000
Sora: "I'll mediate for you two, so you can patch things up pronto."

2007
02:16:24,000 --> 02:16:28,000
Kakeru: "That's all anyone says to me: patch things up."

2008
02:16:28,000 --> 02:16:30,000
Sora: "Want me to butt out?"

2009
02:16:30,000 --> 02:16:34,000
Kakeru: "No. Thank you, Sora. I'd appreciate the help."

2010
02:16:34,000 --> 02:16:39,000
Sora: "Whoa, you even thanked me. You must be in a truly awful spot right now."

2011
02:16:39,000 --> 02:16:40,000
Kakeru: "Guess I am."

2012
02:16:40,000 --> 02:16:41,000
Sora: "Broken heart?"

2013
02:16:41,000 --> 02:16:43,000
Kakeru: "Shut your hole."

2014
02:16:43,000 --> 02:16:47,000
Sora: "Whoops, slip of the tongue. Anyway, mind if I play a game?"

2015
02:16:47,000 --> 02:16:51,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, knock yourself out. Just don't overwrite my save."

2016
02:16:51,000 --> 02:16:53,000
Sora: "Yeah, yeah, whatever."

2017
02:16:53,000 --> 02:17:04,000
*She licks her fingers, presumably because she has some chocolate still stuck to them, before she turns on my portable game console and starts playing with it.*

2018
02:17:04,000 --> 02:17:07,000
*I quickly get changed and lie down on the floor.*

2019
02:17:07,000 --> 02:17:14,000
Sora: "What day was it again, when the second person got turned to stone? Saturday, right? Or maybe Sunday?"

2020
02:17:14,000 --> 02:17:19,000
Kakeru: "It was in the news on Saturday, so I'd guess it was Friday night."

2021
02:17:19,000 --> 02:17:21,000
Sora: "When was the first?"

2022
02:17:21,000 --> 02:17:28,000
Kakeru: "I heard about it and reported it on Tuesday, so it was probably already there by Monday."

2023
02:17:28,000 --> 02:17:31,000
Sora: "So the crime probably happened on Sunday."

2024
02:17:31,000 --> 02:17:33,000
Kakeru: "Likely, yeah."

2025
02:17:33,000 --> 02:17:37,000
Sora: "I wonder if the culprit will strike this weekend, too."

2026
02:17:37,000 --> 02:17:38,000
Kakeru: "Who knows."

2027
02:17:38,000 --> 02:17:40,000
*I find myself whispering.*

2028
02:17:40,000 --> 02:17:42,000
*I'm... not the culprit, right?*

2029
02:17:42,000 --> 02:17:49,000
*Sophie's been monitoring me. If it were me, she wouldn't be telling me to "find the Evil Eye's User."*

2030
02:17:49,000 --> 02:17:55,000
*Besides, if I were the culprit, I'm sure Kujo would have taken some sort of action by now.*

2031
02:17:55,000 --> 02:18:01,000
*Or maybe, she's worrying so much precisely because she can't bring herself to come after me?*

2032
02:18:01,000 --> 02:18:07,000
*She can't come to grips with admitting I'm the real culprit, and it's stressing her out?*

2033
02:18:07,000 --> 02:18:13,000
*Though I doubt she has all that much regard for me, that she'd struggle like that.*

2034
02:18:13,000 --> 02:18:21,000
*She could be working with Sophie to form a plan to steal my still-unknown Artifact. That's a possibility still on the table.*

2035
02:18:21,000 --> 02:18:27,000
*Earlier, Kujo was trying to enhance her ability to snatch the specific memories she was after.*

2036
02:18:27,000 --> 02:18:33,000
*Maybe I have memories linked to the culprit, and she's trying to delve deeper into the facts?*

2037
02:18:33,000 --> 02:18:34,000
*I have no clue.*

2038
02:18:34,000 --> 02:18:36,000
*I don't know what to believe, now.*

2039
02:18:36,000 --> 02:18:38,000
*I can't even believe in myself.*

2040
02:18:38,000 --> 02:18:39,000
*...*

2041
02:18:39,000 --> 02:18:43,000
*I don't want to be alone. I don't know what I might do.*

2042
02:18:43,000 --> 02:18:44,000
Kakeru: "Hey, Sora?"

2043
02:18:44,000 --> 02:18:45,000
Sora: "Hmm?"

2044
02:18:45,000 --> 02:18:47,000
Kakeru: "Want to stay over?"

2045
02:18:47,000 --> 02:18:48,000
Sora: "Oh, sure."

2046
02:18:48,000 --> 02:18:49,000
Sora: "..."

2047
02:18:49,000 --> 02:18:50,000
Sora: "Huh?!"

2048
02:18:50,000 --> 02:18:52,000
Kakeru: "Either today or tomorrow."

2049
02:18:52,000 --> 02:18:54,000
Sora: "A-Are you sure?"

2050
02:18:54,000 --> 02:18:57,000
Kakeru: "Every now and then's no big deal."

2051
02:18:57,000 --> 02:19:01,000
Sora: "The heck? This is freaky. You gonna prank me or something?"

2052
02:19:01,000 --> 02:19:03,000
Kakeru: "Don't be stupid."

2053
02:19:03,000 --> 02:19:07,000
Sora: "You're really cool with me staying the night?"

2054
02:19:07,000 --> 02:19:08,000
Kakeru: "Yeah."

2055
02:19:08,000 --> 02:19:13,000
Sora: "Yippie! Okay, tomorrow, then. I'll have to grab a change of clothes!"

2056
02:19:13,000 --> 02:19:14,000
Kakeru: "Got it."

2057
02:19:14,000 --> 02:19:17,000
Sora: "Alrighty, this is my gateway to moving in."

2058
02:19:17,000 --> 02:19:19,000
Kakeru: "Like hell it is."

2059
02:19:19,000 --> 02:19:20,000
Sora: "Aww..."

2060
02:19:20,000 --> 02:19:24,000
Kakeru: "We'll go to Nine Ball around six o' clock, okay?"

2061
02:19:24,000 --> 02:19:25,000
Sora: "Mmm, sure."

2062
02:19:25,000 --> 02:19:29,000
*She replies with a big smile, still mashing on the buttons.*

2063
02:19:29,000 --> 02:19:33,000
*I zone out, listening to the digital sound of the game.*

2064
02:19:33,000 --> 02:19:36,000
*Catchy, upbeat music, and flashy sound effects...*

2065
02:19:36,000 --> 02:19:41,000
Sora: "Bronii-chan, give me a bite of that. I'll trade you a carrot."

2066
02:19:41,000 --> 02:19:44,000
Kakeru: "Quit being picky and eat your food."

2067
02:19:44,000 --> 02:19:49,000
Sora: "I'm not really being picky, I just like meat more than veggies!"

2068
02:19:49,000 --> 02:19:51,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, well, same here."

2069
02:19:51,000 --> 02:19:54,000
*Sora and I are having dinner at Nine Ball.*

2070
02:19:54,000 --> 02:20:01,000
*Thanks to a bunch of students having just finished up their after-school clubs, it's somewhat crowded.*

2071
02:20:01,000 --> 02:20:06,000
*Kujo is nowhere to be found. Seems like she's not scheduled for today.*

2072
02:20:06,000 --> 02:20:08,000
Sora: "Shame Miya's not here."

2073
02:20:08,000 --> 02:20:14,000
Kakeru: "Oh well. I'll try talking to her again at the start of the week or something."

2074
02:20:14,000 --> 02:20:25,000
Sora: "All you gotta do is invite her over to your apartment again. Just give her a line like, 'You always cook for me, so now it's my turn to cook for you as thanks.'"

2075
02:20:25,000 --> 02:20:30,000
Kakeru: "Boil some pasta, mix in some packaged sauce, and call it a meal, huh?"

2076
02:20:30,000 --> 02:20:35,000
Sora: "Shit, that'd be awesome. Me, I'd have just made her some instant ramen."

2077
02:20:35,000 --> 02:20:40,000
Kakeru: "Touche. It was a hard-fought battle, but you win the lazy chef award."

2078
02:20:40,000 --> 02:20:41,000
Sora: "Heck yeah."

2079
02:20:41,000 --> 02:20:46,000
*We natter on over our dinner, and before too long, we're done eating.*

2080
02:20:46,000 --> 02:20:48,000
Kakeru: "A great meal as always."

2081
02:20:48,000 --> 02:20:50,000
Sora: "Can I order dessert?"

2082
02:20:50,000 --> 02:20:53,000
Kakeru: "If you pay for it yourself, go ahead."

2083
02:20:53,000 --> 02:20:54,000
Sora: "That's a nope."

2084
02:20:54,000 --> 02:20:59,000
Kakeru: "Alright, then you can wait for me outside. I'm going to pay the bill."

2085
02:20:59,000 --> 02:21:02,000
Sora: "Aye aye, sir. Thanks for the treat."

2086
02:21:02,000 --> 02:21:09,000
*I get up and walk over to the register while taking out my wallet. Sora keeps walking, leaving the cafe.*

2087
02:21:09,000 --> 02:21:13,000
*Usually, one of the waitresses would come over, but...*

2088
02:21:13,000 --> 02:21:15,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "..."

2089
02:21:15,000 --> 02:21:16,000
Kakeru: "Oh."

2090
02:21:16,000 --> 02:21:21,000
*I gasp as Kujo's grandfather, who rarely leaves the kitchen, walks up to me.*

2091
02:21:21,000 --> 02:21:24,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "That will be 1,100 yen."

2092
02:21:24,000 --> 02:21:25,000
Kakeru: "Oh, r-right."

2093
02:21:25,000 --> 02:21:29,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "Miyako has been coming home late recently."

2094
02:21:29,000 --> 02:21:30,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

2095
02:21:30,000 --> 02:21:36,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "I've heard she's been going to your house to cook, Niimi-kun."

2096
02:21:36,000 --> 02:21:40,000
Kakeru: "Oh, yes. Up until last week, sir. But not this past week."

2097
02:21:40,000 --> 02:21:48,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "Ah, I see. I was worried that she might be imposing upon you by staying late at your home."

2098
02:21:48,000 --> 02:21:53,000
Kakeru: "O-Oh, no, never! I am greatly indebted to you both, Kujo-san."

2099
02:21:53,000 --> 02:21:57,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "Here is your change, 900 yen."

2100
02:21:57,000 --> 02:21:59,000
Kakeru: "Th-Thank you."

2101
02:21:59,000 --> 02:22:02,000
Miyako's Grandfather: "Please come again."

2102
02:22:02,000 --> 02:22:06,000
Kakeru: "I will. Thank you for the excellent dinner."

2103
02:22:06,000 --> 02:22:10,000
*I take my change, bow respectfully, and leave the cafe.*

2104
02:22:10,000 --> 02:22:12,000
Sora: "Yo, thanks for dinner."

2105
02:22:12,000 --> 02:22:13,000
Kakeru: "..."

2106
02:22:13,000 --> 02:22:15,000
Sora: "...? What's wrong?"

2107
02:22:15,000 --> 02:22:17,000
Kakeru: "I'm in shock."

2108
02:22:17,000 --> 02:22:18,000
Sora: "Over?"

2109
02:22:18,000 --> 02:22:22,000
Kakeru: "I talked to Kujo's grandfather for the first time."

2110
02:22:22,000 --> 02:22:26,000
Sora: "You can have my granddaughter over my dead body!"

2111
02:22:26,000 --> 02:22:35,000
Kakeru: "You know, that might have been where things were going for a bit. He thought she was hanging around my apartment late at night."

2112
02:22:35,000 --> 02:22:38,000
Sora: "...? Miya hasn't been going home?"

2113
02:22:38,000 --> 02:22:40,000
Kakeru: "Seems that way."

2114
02:22:40,000 --> 02:22:44,000
Sora: "Something must be wrong with her, don't you think?"

2115
02:22:44,000 --> 02:22:46,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I think you're right."

2116
02:22:46,000 --> 02:22:54,000
Sora: "Where could she be? You think she's so short with everyone now because she got herself a boyfriend or something?"

2117
02:22:54,000 --> 02:22:55,000
Kakeru: "..."

2118
02:22:55,000 --> 02:23:00,000
Sora: "Hey, I was kidding! C'mon, don't actually get all sad over it."

2119
02:23:00,000 --> 02:23:03,000
Kakeru: "I ain't sad! Come on, we're leaving."

2120
02:23:03,000 --> 02:23:04,000
Sora: "Yessir."

2121
02:23:04,000 --> 02:23:06,000
Sora: "Alright, see you tomorrow!"

2122
02:23:06,000 --> 02:23:09,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. Take care on the way home."

2123
02:23:09,000 --> 02:23:15,000
Sora: "I'm bringing a change of clothes tomorrow. Don't you dare change your mind, okay?!"

2124
02:23:15,000 --> 02:23:17,000
Kakeru: "Relax, I won't."

2125
02:23:17,000 --> 02:23:19,000
Sora: "Good. Okay, see ya!"

2126
02:23:19,000 --> 02:23:22,000
*I see Sora off and turn to head back home.*

2127
02:23:22,000 --> 02:23:30,000
*But I'm not quite in the mood to do that yet, so I wait until Sora is out of sight and make my way to the convenience store.*

2128
02:23:30,000 --> 02:23:33,000
*I flip through a few magazines to kill some time.*

2129
02:23:33,000 --> 02:23:37,000
*Even after I exit the store, I wander around near the station.*

2130
02:23:37,000 --> 02:23:42,000
*I watch some adults coming home from work and a few students milling around.*

2131
02:23:42,000 --> 02:23:46,000
*But after a couple hours, that crowd too has thinned out.*

2132
02:23:46,000 --> 02:23:50,000
*With the students gone, it's like the town has gone to sleep.*

2133
02:23:50,000 --> 02:23:57,000
*The later it grows, the more I feel as though I'm the last person on the planet, so silent is it.*

2134
02:23:57,000 --> 02:24:03,000
*I expect this is why the Evil Eye's User can run amok without fear of consequences.*

2135
02:24:03,000 --> 02:24:04,000
*...*

2136
02:24:04,000 --> 02:24:07,000
*Kujo is wandering the town at night.*

2137
02:24:07,000 --> 02:24:10,000
*Most likely, searching for the Evil Eye's User.*

2138
02:24:10,000 --> 02:24:17,000
*So that should mean I'm not the culprit, because if I were, she'd have no need to wander around.*

2139
02:24:17,000 --> 02:24:20,000
*Okay, then why is she avoiding me to begin with?*

2140
02:24:20,000 --> 02:24:21,000
Kakeru: "..."

2141
02:24:21,000 --> 02:24:23,000
*I walk aimlessly, still thinking.*

2142
02:24:23,000 --> 02:24:27,000
*Looking around, I realize that I'm near the shrine.*

2143
02:24:27,000 --> 02:24:33,000
*That reminds me, Ms. Naruse mentioned that Kujo has been showing up here at night.*

2144
02:24:33,000 --> 02:24:36,000
*I've been subconsciously looking for Kujo.*

2145
02:24:36,000 --> 02:24:41,000
*I feel a little hope well up in me. There's a chance I can find her here.*

2146
02:24:41,000 --> 02:24:43,000
*I hurry through the imposing gate.*

2147
02:24:43,000 --> 02:24:44,000
Kakeru: "..."

2148
02:24:44,000 --> 02:24:45,000
Kakeru: "Not here."

2149
02:24:45,000 --> 02:24:46,000
*I look around.*

2150
02:24:46,000 --> 02:24:50,000
*With a sigh, I sit down in a random spot to rest my feet.*

2151
02:24:50,000 --> 02:24:51,000
*...*

2152
02:24:51,000 --> 02:24:57,000
*Would she really be randomly roaming the city at night to search for the culprit?*

2153
02:24:57,000 --> 02:25:00,000
*It's an extremely inefficient process.*

2154
02:25:00,000 --> 02:25:04,000
*Could it be that Kujo has gotten hold of some sort of clue?*

2155
02:25:04,000 --> 02:25:09,000
*I mean, if she had just told me, I probably could have helped to her.*

2156
02:25:09,000 --> 02:25:14,000
*Nah. I don't even know my own ability. How could I expect her to rely on me?*

2157
02:25:14,000 --> 02:25:17,000
Sophitia: "Slacking on the job, I see."

2158
02:25:17,000 --> 02:25:23,000
*The space in front of me distorts, cleaving a path for my very least favorite living plushie.*

2159
02:25:23,000 --> 02:25:27,000
Kakeru: "You sure you should be appearing in public like this?"

2160
02:25:27,000 --> 02:25:32,000
Sophitia: "You have a bad memory. You lower life forms are unable to see me."

2161
02:25:32,000 --> 02:25:34,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, fine. I forgot."

2162
02:25:34,000 --> 02:25:37,000
Sophitia: "What are you doing here anyway?"

2163
02:25:37,000 --> 02:25:39,000
Kakeru: "Taking a break."

2164
02:25:39,000 --> 02:25:45,000
Sophitia: "Who gave you permission to take a break? You've been slacking off lately."

2165
02:25:45,000 --> 02:25:50,000
Kakeru: "You vanish for weeks, and then you show up just to pick a fight?"

2166
02:25:50,000 --> 02:25:54,000
Sophitia: "What happened with your search for the Artifacts."

2167
02:25:54,000 --> 02:25:55,000
Kakeru: "..."

2168
02:25:55,000 --> 02:26:00,000
Sophitia: "It doesn't seem as though Miyako is working with you anymore either."

2169
02:26:00,000 --> 02:26:03,000
Kakeru: "She said she could do it alone."

2170
02:26:03,000 --> 02:26:06,000
Sophitia: "Oh noooo. Did she get fed up with you?"

2171
02:26:06,000 --> 02:26:09,000
Kakeru: "Right after she read my memories, yeah."

2172
02:26:09,000 --> 02:26:11,000
Sophitia: "I beg your pardon?"

2173
02:26:11,000 --> 02:26:15,000
Kakeru: "Kujo also has the ability to steal others' memories."

2174
02:26:15,000 --> 02:26:19,000
Sophitia: "Oh-ho. Her power is more useful than I realized."

2175
02:26:19,000 --> 02:26:26,000
Kakeru: "She suddenly got really distant. I thought maybe she suspected me of being the Evil Eye's User."

2176
02:26:26,000 --> 02:26:28,000
Sophitia: "Oh. You aren't."

2177
02:26:28,000 --> 02:26:32,000
Kakeru: "Sure would've been nice to hear that a couple weeks ago."

2178
02:26:32,000 --> 02:26:43,000
Sophitia: "I've told you that dozens of times. At any rate, the reason she's fed up with you is that she saw through to your real motivation, don't you think?"

2179
02:26:43,000 --> 02:26:45,000
Kakeru: "My... what now?"

2180
02:26:45,000 --> 02:26:49,000
Sophitia: "The pouty look on your face makes it painfully obvious."

2181
02:26:49,000 --> 02:26:50,000
Kakeru: "..."

2182
02:26:50,000 --> 02:26:54,000
*The plushie's got a point. I've considered that as well.*

2183
02:26:54,000 --> 02:26:58,000
*My motive for helping out Kujo in the first place was selfish.*

2184
02:26:58,000 --> 02:27:01,000
*After finding that out, she lost faith in me.*

2185
02:27:01,000 --> 02:27:05,000
*After finding out something she shouldn't... my feelings for her.*

2186
02:27:05,000 --> 02:27:06,000
*...*

2187
02:27:06,000 --> 02:27:07,000
Kakeru: "...!"

2188
02:27:07,000 --> 02:27:08,000
*It hits me.*

2189
02:27:08,000 --> 02:27:11,000
*Finally, after so long in the dark, it all clicks.*

2190
02:27:11,000 --> 02:27:14,000
*God, what a freaking idiot I've been!*

2191
02:27:14,000 --> 02:27:22,000
*I've been so damn self-absorbed in how Kujo thought about me that I forgot the most important piece of this equation.*

2192
02:27:22,000 --> 02:27:26,000
*I had a memory that I absolutely had to keep a secret from her!*

2193
02:27:26,000 --> 02:27:28,000
Kakeru: "She found out..."

2194
02:27:28,000 --> 02:27:30,000
Sophitia: "About what?"

2195
02:27:30,000 --> 02:27:35,000
Kakeru: "She read my memories. She knows she indirectly killed that guy."

2196
02:27:35,000 --> 02:27:38,000
Sophitia: "Oh, yeah. The one from the fire."

2197
02:27:38,000 --> 02:27:47,000
Kakeru: "Dammit! That's what she meant, talking about her 'obligation'. That's why she's feeling guilty and won't stop using her powers!"

2198
02:27:47,000 --> 02:27:51,000
Sophitia: "Wait, what was that? Is Miyako overusing her powers?"

2199
02:27:51,000 --> 02:27:57,000
Kakeru: "Yes! She's been stealing the memories of all our classmates, in the middle of class."

2200
02:27:57,000 --> 02:28:01,000
Sophitia: "Hmm. The power has overwhelmed her, then."

2201
02:28:01,000 --> 02:28:03,000
Kakeru: "What does that mean?"

2202
02:28:03,000 --> 02:28:08,000
Sophitia: "Just like that boy who made the school into a sea of flames."

2203
02:28:08,000 --> 02:28:11,000
Kakeru: "Don't you group Kujo with that jerk!"

2204
02:28:11,000 --> 02:28:21,000
Sophitia: "You didn't realize? Even in my world, where the Artifacts originated, particularly strong powers can change the people who possess them."

2205
02:28:21,000 --> 02:28:29,000
Sophitia: "They want to use it, to flaunt it. A wondrous power that's theirs and theirs alone... How could they not?"

2206
02:28:29,000 --> 02:28:39,000
Sophitia: "Hence why we of Sephirot exist. We monitor the Artifacts, so that people like you inferior beings don't get too big for your britches."

2207
02:28:39,000 --> 02:28:43,000
Kakeru: "Are you saying Kujo is going to end up like that guy?"

2208
02:28:43,000 --> 02:28:55,000
Sophitia: "Hard to tell. I doubt that she would cause quite as much of a scene. That said, if Miyako is not limiting her use of her powers, then she has probably already succumbed."

2209
02:28:55,000 --> 02:29:05,000
Kakeru: "But Kujo is using her powers to bring justice! Even now, she's most likely running around this whole town searching for the Evil Eye's User!"

2210
02:29:05,000 --> 02:29:07,000
Sophitia: "Is that truly her goal?"

2211
02:29:07,000 --> 02:29:09,000
Kakeru: "What are you trying to say?"

2212
02:29:09,000 --> 02:29:16,000
Sophitia: "She is capable of stealing even other people's memories. Other people's experiences become her own."

2213
02:29:16,000 --> 02:29:22,000
Sophitia: "She might be out hunting for prey: anyone with particularly savory memories."

2214
02:29:22,000 --> 02:29:23,000
Kakeru: "..."

2215
02:29:23,000 --> 02:29:29,000
Sophitia: "If you have time to glare at me, wouldn't it be better spent looking for her?"

2216
02:29:29,000 --> 02:29:32,000
Kakeru: "I don't need you to tell me!"

2217
02:29:32,000 --> 02:29:35,000
*I whip out my phone and send Kujo a message.*

2218
02:29:35,000 --> 02:29:38,000
*I tell her about how her grandfather is worried.*

2219
02:29:38,000 --> 02:29:40,000
*Ask her where she is now.*

2220
02:29:40,000 --> 02:29:45,000
*Tell her that I'm sorry for keeping what happened to that man a secret.*

2221
02:29:45,000 --> 02:29:49,000
*That she doesn't need to shoulder the burden by herself.*

2222
02:29:49,000 --> 02:29:53,000
*And last, I plead that she let me lend her a helping hand.*

2223
02:29:53,000 --> 02:29:55,000
*I send her message after message.*

2224
02:29:55,000 --> 02:29:56,000
*No reply.*

2225
02:29:56,000 --> 02:29:58,000
*Not even a read notification.*

2226
02:29:58,000 --> 02:29:59,000
Kakeru: "Dammit!"

2227
02:29:59,000 --> 02:30:07,000
Sophitia: "The technology of this world is amazing! You're able to contact faraway friends without use of an Artifact."

2228
02:30:07,000 --> 02:30:13,000
Sophitia: "Though I suppose if the other person never replies, it's utterly useless."

2229
02:30:13,000 --> 02:30:17,000
Kakeru: "...! Do you have any idea where Kujo could be?"

2230
02:30:17,000 --> 02:30:22,000
Sophitia: "Of course not. You should know that. Your desperation is pathetic."

2231
02:30:22,000 --> 02:30:25,000
Kakeru: "You're damn right I'm desperate!"

2232
02:30:25,000 --> 02:30:34,000
Sophitia: "Quit shouting, you savage. It's hard to believe Miyako is the one causing all this trouble. Oh well. I'll help you out this once."

2233
02:30:34,000 --> 02:30:36,000
Kakeru: "Oh thank god!"

2234
02:30:36,000 --> 02:30:40,000
Sophitia: "I'm not familiar with the area, so don't expect much."

2235
02:30:40,000 --> 02:30:42,000
Kakeru: "Anything helps!"

2236
02:30:42,000 --> 02:30:44,000
*I grip my phone and start running.*

2237
02:30:44,000 --> 02:30:46,000
*Where would Kujo likely be?*

2238
02:30:46,000 --> 02:30:47,000
*No. Wrong question.*

2239
02:30:47,000 --> 02:30:50,000
*Where would the Evil Eye's User likely be?*

2240
02:30:50,000 --> 02:30:57,000
*Kujo hasn't been overcome by her powers. I'm sure she's just trying to make sure justice is served!*

2241
02:30:57,000 --> 02:30:59,000
*Where? Somewhere unpopulated...*

2242
02:30:59,000 --> 02:31:02,000
*But also someplace where they could find a victim.*

2243
02:31:02,000 --> 02:31:04,000
Kakeru: "How should I know?!"

2244
02:31:04,000 --> 02:31:05,000
*I spit out, running.*

2245
02:31:05,000 --> 02:31:07,000
*I have a bad feeling.*

2246
02:31:07,000 --> 02:31:09,000
*Kujo is diligent and strait-laced.*

2247
02:31:09,000 --> 02:31:12,000
*However, she can be easily swayed emotionally.*

2248
02:31:12,000 --> 02:31:15,000
*That is exactly why you have to be careful of her.*

2249
02:31:15,000 --> 02:31:18,000
*I can't leave Kujo alone, in the state she's in.*

2250
02:31:18,000 --> 02:31:20,000
*That's what my hunch is telling me.*

2251
02:31:20,000 --> 02:31:26,000
*It's not like Kujo to just go using her powers on her classmates without a moment's hesitation.*

2252
02:31:26,000 --> 02:31:30,000
*I should have realized something was wrong when I saw that!*

2253
02:31:30,000 --> 02:31:35,000
*Why haven't I tried to consider Kujo's feelings, even just a little?!*

2254
02:31:35,000 --> 02:31:37,000
*It's all been about me, me, me!*

2255
02:31:37,000 --> 02:31:39,000
Kakeru: "I'm sorry, Kujo!"

2256
02:31:39,000 --> 02:31:42,000
*I start messaging her, not breaking my stride.*

2257
02:31:42,000 --> 02:31:44,000
*Message after message.*

2258
02:31:44,000 --> 02:31:45,000
*But no reply comes.*

2259
02:31:45,000 --> 02:31:48,000
*Would it really be better to leave her alone?*

2260
02:31:48,000 --> 02:31:51,000
*Even if Kujo does find the culprit, what can I do?*

2261
02:31:51,000 --> 02:31:54,000
*But then, why do I feel this sense of foreboding?*

2262
02:31:54,000 --> 02:31:56,000
*I'm practically betraying Kujo.*

2263
02:31:56,000 --> 02:32:01,000
*I'm putting her in the same category as that student who went nuts!*

2264
02:32:01,000 --> 02:32:02,000
Kakeru: "...!"

2265
02:32:02,000 --> 02:32:07,000
*How many hours have I been wandering around with nothing to show for it?*

2266
02:32:07,000 --> 02:32:12,000
*I'm short of breath, I'm physically drained, and I'm fast approaching my limits.*

2267
02:32:12,000 --> 02:32:14,000
*My phone finally vibrates.*

2268
02:32:14,000 --> 02:32:16,000
*It's a message from Kujo.*

2269
02:32:16,000 --> 02:32:21,000
*"I have already found the Evil Eye's User. I will fulfill my obligation."*

2270
02:32:21,000 --> 02:32:23,000
Kakeru: "What does she...?"

2271
02:32:23,000 --> 02:32:24,000
Kakeru: "..."

2272
02:32:24,000 --> 02:32:25,000
Kakeru: "No!"

2273
02:32:25,000 --> 02:32:27,000
*Damn your obligation!*

2274
02:32:27,000 --> 02:32:30,000
*That man died because of an act of God.*

2275
02:32:30,000 --> 02:32:32,000
*None of that was your fault, Kujo.*

2276
02:32:32,000 --> 02:32:34,000
*You already found them?*

2277
02:32:34,000 --> 02:32:38,000
*Does that mean you identified the culprit a long time ago?*

2278
02:32:38,000 --> 02:32:39,000
*But then...*

2279
02:32:39,000 --> 02:32:40,000
*Your obligation...?*

2280
02:32:40,000 --> 02:32:41,000
*Does that mean...?!*

2281
02:32:41,000 --> 02:32:44,000
Kakeru: "Kujo, you can't be planning to...!"

2282
02:32:44,000 --> 02:32:47,000
*She's going to make contact with the culprit? No.*

2283
02:32:47,000 --> 02:32:49,000
*She's already made contact?*

2284
02:32:49,000 --> 02:32:50,000
Kakeru: "Dammit!"

2285
02:32:50,000 --> 02:32:52,000
*I run, and run, and run.*

2286
02:32:52,000 --> 02:32:56,000
*I don't have any powers, so maybe I can't help you.*

2287
02:32:56,000 --> 02:33:01,000
*But that's irrelevant! You can't just confront the culprit on your own!*

2288
02:33:01,000 --> 02:33:03,000
Kakeru: "Where, where, where?!"

2289
02:33:03,000 --> 02:33:05,000
*I search, run, search.*

2290
02:33:05,000 --> 02:33:06,000
*I send a message.*

2291
02:33:06,000 --> 02:33:08,000
*There's no read notification.*

2292
02:33:08,000 --> 02:33:09,000
*No reply either.*

2293
02:33:09,000 --> 02:33:11,000
Kakeru: "Kujo, where are you?!"

2294
02:33:11,000 --> 02:33:12,000
*I shout.*

2295
02:33:12,000 --> 02:33:13,000
*I pray she hears it.*

2296
02:33:13,000 --> 02:33:14,000
*But no response.*

2297
02:33:14,000 --> 02:33:16,000
*I'm filled with a sense of dread.*

2298
02:33:16,000 --> 02:33:18,000
Kakeru: "Haah... Haah... Haah..."

2299
02:33:18,000 --> 02:33:21,000
*I have a wild hunch in the back my mind.*

2300
02:33:21,000 --> 02:33:24,000
*The sudden idea brings me back to here.*

2301
02:33:24,000 --> 02:33:27,000
*This place is far away from where anybody lives.*

2302
02:33:27,000 --> 02:33:32,000
*As long as you don't cause a big scene, no one will ever notice you.*

2303
02:33:32,000 --> 02:33:34,000
*People tend not to come here.*

2304
02:33:34,000 --> 02:33:36,000
*It's out of the public eye.*

2305
02:33:36,000 --> 02:33:37,000
Sophitia: "..."

2306
02:33:37,000 --> 02:33:39,000
*Sophie is here already.*

2307
02:33:39,000 --> 02:33:41,000
*She's looking down at something.*

2308
02:33:41,000 --> 02:33:44,000
Sophitia: "Seems we were a minute too late."

2309
02:33:44,000 --> 02:33:47,000
*I don't understand what she's trying to tell me.*

2310
02:33:47,000 --> 02:33:49,000
*I... don't want to understand.*

2311
02:33:49,000 --> 02:33:50,000
Kakeru: "..."

2312
02:33:50,000 --> 02:33:52,000
Kakeru: "What the hell... is this?"

2313
02:33:52,000 --> 02:33:54,000
*It's a mass of stone.*

2314
02:33:54,000 --> 02:33:57,000
*The legs extending from the skirt are gray.*

2315
02:33:57,000 --> 02:34:01,000
*There is nothing there from the shoulders up, however.*

2316
02:34:01,000 --> 02:34:03,000
Kakeru: "What the hell is this?!"

2317
02:34:03,000 --> 02:34:08,000
*Several feet away, surrounded by a scattering of fine stone shards...*

2318
02:34:08,000 --> 02:34:12,000
*...lies the head that should be attached to this body.*

2319
02:34:12,000 --> 02:34:13,000
*Her expression...*

2320
02:34:13,000 --> 02:34:14,000
Kakeru: "Kujo..."

2321
02:34:14,000 --> 02:34:16,000
*...is frozen in anguish.*

2322
02:34:16,000 --> 02:34:18,000
Kakeru: "Anything but this..."

2323
02:34:18,000 --> 02:34:20,000
*And so it will stay, forever.*

2324
02:34:20,000 --> 02:34:23,000
*Those lips will never call my name again.*

2325
02:34:23,000 --> 02:34:24,000
Kakeru: "How...?"

2326
02:34:24,000 --> 02:34:25,000
*What happened...?*

2327
02:34:25,000 --> 02:34:26,000
*I don't know.*

2328
02:34:26,000 --> 02:34:28,000
*All I know is what came of it.*

2329
02:34:28,000 --> 02:34:29,000
Kakeru: "Why...?"

2330
02:34:29,000 --> 02:34:31,000
*She confronted the culprit...*

2331
02:34:31,000 --> 02:34:32,000
Kakeru: "Kujo...!"

2332
02:34:32,000 --> 02:34:34,000
*...and the culprit murdered her.*

2333
02:34:34,000 --> 02:34:35,000
*...*

2334
02:34:35,000 --> 02:34:36,000
*......*

2335
02:34:36,000 --> 02:34:37,000
*.........*

2336
02:34:37,000 --> 02:34:44,000
Sophitia: "Would you look at that. They left behind her Artifact. I'll just be collecting this now."

2337
02:34:44,000 --> 02:34:46,000
*I hear Sophie's voice.*

2338
02:34:46,000 --> 02:34:49,000
*She detaches something from Kujo's corpse.*

2339
02:34:49,000 --> 02:34:50,000
*Her... corpse?*

2340
02:34:50,000 --> 02:34:52,000
*Where did that word come from?*

2341
02:34:52,000 --> 02:34:53,000
*She's...*

2342
02:34:53,000 --> 02:34:54,000
*She's still...*

2343
02:34:54,000 --> 02:34:58,000
Sophitia: "What a shame. I had such high hopes for her."

2344
02:34:58,000 --> 02:34:59,000
Kakeru: "..."

2345
02:34:59,000 --> 02:35:07,000
Sophitia: "Well, so it goes. She was up against someone talented. Miyako messed up, trying to take them on alone."

2346
02:35:07,000 --> 02:35:08,000
Kakeru: "..."

2347
02:35:08,000 --> 02:35:13,000
Sophitia: "She would have at least stood a chance had she just worked with Sora."

2348
02:35:13,000 --> 02:35:14,000
Kakeru: "......"

2349
02:35:14,000 --> 02:35:15,000
Sophitia: "Bitter?"

2350
02:35:15,000 --> 02:35:16,000
Kakeru: "........."

2351
02:35:16,000 --> 02:35:18,000
Sophitia: "You want revenge?"

2352
02:35:18,000 --> 02:35:19,000
Kakeru: "............"

2353
02:35:19,000 --> 02:35:24,000
Sophitia: "Come now, give your emotions free rein. This is your awakening."

2354
02:35:24,000 --> 02:35:26,000
Kakeru: "..............."

2355
02:35:26,000 --> 02:35:32,000
Sophitia: "Now is the time to awaken those powers, unknown to even me. Do it, Kakeru."

2356
02:35:32,000 --> 02:35:34,000
Kakeru: ".................."

2357
02:35:34,000 --> 02:35:35,000
Sophitia: "..."

2358
02:35:35,000 --> 02:35:38,000
Sophitia: "Worthless. I was wrong about you."

2359
02:35:38,000 --> 02:35:42,000
Sophitia: "Farewell. I'm going to search for the next possibility."

2360
02:35:42,000 --> 02:35:43,000
Kakeru: "..."

2361
02:35:43,000 --> 02:35:45,000
Kakeru: "Let's go back, Kujo..."

2362
02:35:45,000 --> 02:35:47,000
Kakeru: "We should... go back."

2363
02:35:47,000 --> 02:35:49,000
Kakeru: "Let's... go back."

2364
02:35:49,000 --> 02:35:54,000
*It's been a week since Kujo accidentally found out how I feel about her.*

2365
02:35:54,000 --> 02:35:57,000
*Kujo responded in kind, and now we're dating.*

2366
02:35:57,000 --> 02:36:03,000
*Yeah, right. If it'd really turned out like that, I'd be the happiest man on earth.*

2367
02:36:03,000 --> 02:36:04,000
*In reality...*

2368
02:36:04,000 --> 02:36:05,000
Miyako: "Oh!"

2369
02:36:05,000 --> 02:36:09,000
*I step out of the bathroom and nearly run into Kujo.*

2370
02:36:09,000 --> 02:36:13,000
*She quickly looks away and rushes into the girls' bathroom.*

2371
02:36:13,000 --> 02:36:14,000
*...*

2372
02:36:14,000 --> 02:36:16,000
*Yeah, you guessed it.*

2373
02:36:16,000 --> 02:36:20,000
*Ever since that day, she's been avoiding me like the plague.*

2374
02:36:20,000 --> 02:36:22,000
*We haven't so much as spoken.*

2375
02:36:22,000 --> 02:36:28,000
*Needless to say, our search for the Evil Eye's User has been completely abandoned.*

2376
02:36:28,000 --> 02:36:31,000
*It's like she doesn't know what to say to me.*

2377
02:36:31,000 --> 02:36:44,000
*I guess I'm glad that she doesn't seem to think I'm a creep, but this kinda feels like she's already turned me down before I even asked her out, so there's definitely more downside than upside here.*

2378
02:36:44,000 --> 02:36:48,000
*Yesterday was the end of our long-awaited Golden Week holiday.*

2379
02:36:48,000 --> 02:36:52,000
*I went back to my folks' place, where basically nothing happened.*

2380
02:36:52,000 --> 02:36:55,000
*Kujo and I didn't so much as message each other.*

2381
02:36:55,000 --> 02:37:02,000
*I have a horrible feeling that, if things continue like this, we might just keep drifting apart.*

2382
02:37:02,000 --> 02:37:13,000
*I'm really beating myself up for asking her to read my memories, but more than anything, I wish that, if she wanted to turn me down, she would just tell me straight up.*

2383
02:37:13,000 --> 02:37:17,000
*To sum it up, ever since that moment, my days have been...*

2384
02:37:17,000 --> 02:37:18,000
Kakeru: "Haahh..."

2385
02:37:18,000 --> 02:37:20,000
*...filled with lovelorn sighs.*

2386
02:37:20,000 --> 02:37:26,000
Satsuki: "Okay, everyone, that's the end of regular classes. Let's get homeroom out of the way."

2387
02:37:26,000 --> 02:37:30,000
*The bell rings, signifying the start of afternoon homeroom.*

2388
02:37:30,000 --> 02:37:32,000
*Some short announcements are made.*

2389
02:37:32,000 --> 02:37:35,000
*Copies of our math homework are passed out.*

2390
02:37:35,000 --> 02:37:46,000
Satsuki: "If any column has extras or not enough, make sure to get that situated in the back. Okay, that's a wrap for homeroom. Student on duty, take it away."

2391
02:37:46,000 --> 02:37:49,000
*Same as every day, we're told to stand and bow.*

2392
02:37:49,000 --> 02:37:53,000
*I throw my bag over my shoulder without sitting down again.*

2393
02:37:53,000 --> 02:37:55,000
Yoichi: "Hey, hold up!"

2394
02:37:55,000 --> 02:37:59,000
*As I begin preparing to go home, Yoichi calls out to me.*

2395
02:37:59,000 --> 02:38:00,000
Kakeru: "Sup?"

2396
02:38:00,000 --> 02:38:04,000
Yoichi: "Everybody's going to Round Two. Wanna come with?"

2397
02:38:04,000 --> 02:38:06,000
Kakeru: "What, karaoke?"

2398
02:38:06,000 --> 02:38:11,000
Yoichi: "Nah. Maybe shoot some pool or go bowling. You know, whatever."

2399
02:38:11,000 --> 02:38:13,000
Kakeru: "I think I'll pass."

2400
02:38:13,000 --> 02:38:19,000
Yoichi: "Sorry, dude, I really need you to come today. Kujo-san won't come unless you're around."

2401
02:38:19,000 --> 02:38:23,000
Kakeru: "Kujo? More like she's less likely to come WITH me around."

2402
02:38:23,000 --> 02:38:31,000
Yoichi: "I told her you were coming when I invited her, and she said, 'Well, if Niimi-kun will be there, I'll consider it.'"

2403
02:38:31,000 --> 02:38:36,000
Kakeru: "Seriously, man, you can't just volunteer me for... Wait, for real?"

2404
02:38:36,000 --> 02:38:38,000
Yoichi: "For real, what?"

2405
02:38:38,000 --> 02:38:42,000
Kakeru: "She said she'll consider it, because I'm going?"

2406
02:38:42,000 --> 02:38:43,000
Yoichi: "Yup."

2407
02:38:43,000 --> 02:38:45,000
Kakeru: "Sure you're not lying?"

2408
02:38:45,000 --> 02:38:50,000
Yoichi: "Not yet. Though, if you don't come, I'll have lied to Kujo."

2409
02:38:50,000 --> 02:38:51,000
Kakeru: "..."

2410
02:38:51,000 --> 02:38:52,000
Yoichi: "You in?"

2411
02:38:52,000 --> 02:38:53,000
Kakeru: "Okay, fine."

2412
02:38:53,000 --> 02:38:54,000
Yoichi: "Awright!"

2413
02:38:54,000 --> 02:38:56,000
*Yoichi pumps his fist.*

2414
02:38:56,000 --> 02:39:02,000
*He gives me a hearty slap on the back, despite me clearly not being enthusiastic about this.*

2415
02:39:02,000 --> 02:39:07,000
*His lips curl into a suggestive and, might I add, somewhat evil grin.*

2416
02:39:07,000 --> 02:39:09,000
Kakeru: "The hell's wrong with you?"

2417
02:39:09,000 --> 02:39:15,000
Yoichi: "I'm going to set it up so you get some alone time with Kujo-san. Don't blow it."

2418
02:39:15,000 --> 02:39:18,000
Kakeru: "Hey, what's that supposed to mean?"

2419
02:39:18,000 --> 02:39:29,000
Yoichi: "Looking away when you guys make eye contact. The meaningful little pause in your step when you pass by each other. I've had it up to here with that shit!"

2420
02:39:29,000 --> 02:39:38,000
Yoichi: "You still haven't gotten together, have you? You two need to hook up pronto, so I figure it's time for me to play cupid."

2421
02:39:38,000 --> 02:39:44,000
Kakeru: "So that's why you invited her. You're sticking your nose where it doesn't belong."

2422
02:39:44,000 --> 02:39:55,000
Yoichi: "You two are making everyone else uncomfortable. You need to settle things so everyone else can stop feeling like they're walking on eggshells around you two."

2423
02:39:55,000 --> 02:39:57,000
Kakeru: "What do you mean, everyone?"

2424
02:39:57,000 --> 02:40:09,000
Yoichi: "You serious? Literally everyone in class can tell you two are hung up on each other. And I'm not the only one who knows Kujo-san has been going over to your place."

2425
02:40:09,000 --> 02:40:10,000
Kakeru: "..."

2426
02:40:10,000 --> 02:40:17,000
Yoichi: "Holy shit, hahah! I've never seen that look on your face before, Kakeru. You're blushing super hard!"

2427
02:40:17,000 --> 02:40:18,000
Kakeru: "Cram it."

2428
02:40:18,000 --> 02:40:26,000
Yoichi: "Hahah, anyway, just seal the deal today. If you two slip out early together, nobody's gonna bat an eye."

2429
02:40:26,000 --> 02:40:28,000
Kakeru: "Don't get your hopes up."

2430
02:40:28,000 --> 02:40:33,000
Yoichi: "I'm not. In fact, I put some money down, betting that she says no."

2431
02:40:33,000 --> 02:40:38,000
Kakeru: "Why you...! Are all of you are getting a kick out of this?!"

2432
02:40:38,000 --> 02:40:55,000
Yoichi: "Doesn't everybody enjoy watching a relationship try to get itself sorted out? A lot of guys are aiming for Kujo-san, so you should be locking that down while everybody else is content to just watch, or you can kiss your chances with her goodbye."

2433
02:40:55,000 --> 02:40:56,000
Kakeru: "..."

2434
02:40:56,000 --> 02:41:07,000
Yoichi: "Now that's the determination I wanna see. Alright, wait right here. Some of the girls are on cleaning duty, so we'll hit the road once they're done."

2435
02:41:07,000 --> 02:41:08,000
Kakeru: "Fine."

2436
02:41:08,000 --> 02:41:15,000
Yoichi: "There's been a lot of dark stuff going on lately. Give us something fun to talk about, okay?"

2437
02:41:15,000 --> 02:41:19,000
Kakeru: "You're hoping she shoots me down, aren't you?"

2438
02:41:19,000 --> 02:41:22,000
Yoichi: "You know it, dude. That'd be hilarious."

2439
02:41:22,000 --> 02:41:27,000
*He gives me another slap on the back before heading over to the circle of girls.*

2440
02:41:27,000 --> 02:41:35,000
*I've been thinking of doing something about this situation for a while now, but it's tough to get going on my own.*

2441
02:41:35,000 --> 02:41:43,000
*Still, this isn't what I was hoping for. Not only are they pushing us together, they're even wagering on the outcome?*

2442
02:41:43,000 --> 02:41:52,000
*I hate that they're making a spectacle out of me, but I guess, now that I'm in this deep, I don't have any way to go but forward.*

2443
02:41:52,000 --> 02:41:53,000
*...*

2444
02:41:53,000 --> 02:41:55,000
*Fine mess I've ended up in.*

2445
02:41:55,000 --> 02:41:56,000
Kakeru: "..."

2446
02:41:56,000 --> 02:42:00,000
*With a drink in hand, I take a look around the establishment.*

2447
02:42:00,000 --> 02:42:06,000
*Round Two's first floor is less an arcade, and more what we call an amusement corner.*

2448
02:42:06,000 --> 02:42:10,000
*The whole floor is just rhythm games and crane games.*

2449
02:42:10,000 --> 02:42:21,000
*The second floor has more classic arcade games, as well as the games that pay out tickets. Going even further up, there's bowling, darts, billiards, and karaoke.*

2450
02:42:21,000 --> 02:42:24,000
*Everything a student could want is right here.*

2451
02:42:24,000 --> 02:42:28,000
*Which is why the place is jam-packed with students.*

2452
02:42:28,000 --> 02:42:33,000
*To tell the truth, I don't really care for this place. It's too loud for me.*

2453
02:42:33,000 --> 02:42:38,000
*And knowing how frugal Kujo is, my guess is she doesn't come here often either.*

2454
02:42:38,000 --> 02:42:55,000
*Both of us are a bit on the antisocial side, and yet here we are, joining in the "fun". Sure, the plan is to get us some alone time, but the only way I can see this going is that we both just get dragged here, there, and everywhere by our friends.*

2455
02:42:55,000 --> 02:42:56,000
Kakeru: "..."

2456
02:42:56,000 --> 02:42:58,000
*I take another look around.*

2457
02:42:58,000 --> 02:43:00,000
*Nothing but students around us.*

2458
02:43:00,000 --> 02:43:03,000
*However, I've lost track of Yoichi and the others.*

2459
02:43:03,000 --> 02:43:07,000
*Don't tell me they ditched me when I went to buy a drink.*

2460
02:43:07,000 --> 02:43:15,000
*If they seriously are trying to get the two of us alone, then Kujo has probably been stranded on her own, just like me.*

2461
02:43:15,000 --> 02:43:18,000
*I could just go home, if I wanted...*

2462
02:43:18,000 --> 02:43:19,000
*...*

2463
02:43:19,000 --> 02:43:20,000
Kakeru: "Haahh..."

2464
02:43:20,000 --> 02:43:21,000
*I sigh.*

2465
02:43:21,000 --> 02:43:23,000
*I decide to go looking for her.*

2466
02:43:23,000 --> 02:43:29,000
*To be frank, I just want to be able to tell myself later that I at least tried looking.*

2467
02:43:29,000 --> 02:43:36,000
*Right now, the greater part of me wants to just go. No, that's not quite right. I just want to run away.*

2468
02:43:36,000 --> 02:43:40,000
*So, I've concocted a simple rationalization that I can use:*

2469
02:43:40,000 --> 02:43:45,000
*I tried looked for her, but I didn't find her, so I reluctantly went back home.*

2470
02:43:45,000 --> 02:43:48,000
*But things never turn out the way you plan...*

2471
02:43:48,000 --> 02:43:49,000
Miyako: "..."

2472
02:43:49,000 --> 02:43:52,000
*Mere moments later, I catch sight of Kujo.*

2473
02:43:52,000 --> 02:43:55,000
*She's all alone, standing by the wall.*

2474
02:43:55,000 --> 02:43:59,000
*The look on her face says she's waiting to meet someone.*

2475
02:43:59,000 --> 02:44:00,000
*Could it be... me?*

2476
02:44:00,000 --> 02:44:02,000
*I quickly abandon that thought.*

2477
02:44:02,000 --> 02:44:06,000
*Maybe I should pretend I never saw her and go home.*

2478
02:44:06,000 --> 02:44:10,000
*But I still can't shake the idea that just maybe...*

2479
02:44:10,000 --> 02:44:11,000
*It's just...*

2480
02:44:11,000 --> 02:44:12,000
*...*

2481
02:44:12,000 --> 02:44:16,000
*I've been waiting for Kujo to come talk to me this entire time.*

2482
02:44:16,000 --> 02:44:19,000
*It's time to stop being such a wimp.*

2483
02:44:19,000 --> 02:44:20,000
Miyako: "Oh."

2484
02:44:20,000 --> 02:44:21,000
Kakeru: "..."

2485
02:44:21,000 --> 02:44:24,000
*Wordlessly, I lean against the wall next to Kujo.*

2486
02:44:24,000 --> 02:44:29,000
*Kujo sees me and looks down at the floor, but she doesn't walk away.*

2487
02:44:29,000 --> 02:44:31,000
*Relief washes over me.*

2488
02:44:31,000 --> 02:44:32,000
*...*

2489
02:44:32,000 --> 02:44:37,000
*Unfortunately, that's not enough to make a dent in the awkward tension.*

2490
02:44:37,000 --> 02:44:40,000
*I desperately try to start a conversation.*

2491
02:44:40,000 --> 02:44:41,000
Kakeru: "Uh..."

2492
02:44:41,000 --> 02:44:42,000
Kakeru: "..."

2493
02:44:42,000 --> 02:44:44,000
Kakeru: "Where's everyone else?"

2494
02:44:44,000 --> 02:44:47,000
Miyako: "Well, they told me to wait here."

2495
02:44:47,000 --> 02:44:50,000
Kakeru: "They probably aren't coming back."

2496
02:44:50,000 --> 02:44:51,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

2497
02:44:51,000 --> 02:44:55,000
Kakeru: "I heard they're trying to get the two of us alone."

2498
02:44:55,000 --> 02:44:56,000
Miyako: "..."

2499
02:44:56,000 --> 02:44:58,000
Miyako: "I heard that too."

2500
02:44:58,000 --> 02:44:59,000
Kakeru: "..."

2501
02:44:59,000 --> 02:45:02,000
*The words won't come out of my mouth.*

2502
02:45:02,000 --> 02:45:03,000
*I'm too nervous.*

2503
02:45:03,000 --> 02:45:08,000
*Does that mean Kujo knew we'd end up alone together if she waited here?*

2504
02:45:08,000 --> 02:45:10,000
*I'm why she kept waiting?*

2505
02:45:10,000 --> 02:45:12,000
*"Aww, crap," I think to myself.*

2506
02:45:12,000 --> 02:45:14,000
*I really want to run away now.*

2507
02:45:14,000 --> 02:45:19,000
*If Kujo is about to give an answer to my unasked question, right here and now...*

2508
02:45:19,000 --> 02:45:21,000
*...I don't know if I can take it.*

2509
02:45:21,000 --> 02:45:29,000
*She's probably going to say no. I'm not certain of it, but I'm sure as hell not certain she'll say yes, either.*

2510
02:45:29,000 --> 02:45:35,000
*I mean, we've gotten closer recently, right? She's even come to my apartment, right?*

2511
02:45:35,000 --> 02:45:42,000
*But that's probably an indication of just how little she sees me as a potential romantic interest.*

2512
02:45:42,000 --> 02:45:44,000
*Around and around and around.*

2513
02:45:44,000 --> 02:45:48,000
*These self-tormenting, nauseous thoughts flit through my head.*

2514
02:45:48,000 --> 02:45:51,000
*But if I'm going to get shot down anyway...*

2515
02:45:51,000 --> 02:45:56,000
*I should at least give it everything I have and go out in a blaze of glory.*

2516
02:45:56,000 --> 02:45:57,000
Kakeru: "..."

2517
02:45:57,000 --> 02:45:58,000
Kakeru: "Hey, Kujo?"

2518
02:45:58,000 --> 02:45:59,000
Miyako: "Yes?"

2519
02:45:59,000 --> 02:46:02,000
Kakeru: "That time you read my memories?"

2520
02:46:02,000 --> 02:46:03,000
Miyako: "..."

2521
02:46:03,000 --> 02:46:07,000
Kakeru: "You figured out how I feel about you, didn't you?"

2522
02:46:07,000 --> 02:46:08,000
Miyako: "..."

2523
02:46:08,000 --> 02:46:09,000
*Kujo says nothing.*

2524
02:46:09,000 --> 02:46:16,000
*I'm starting to crack, what with her not responding at all, but I manage to hold out and continue speaking.*

2525
02:46:16,000 --> 02:46:21,000
Kakeru: "I've got nothing to hide anymore, so I'll come out and tell you."

2526
02:46:21,000 --> 02:46:23,000
Kakeru: "I like you, Kujo."

2527
02:46:23,000 --> 02:46:24,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

2528
02:46:24,000 --> 02:46:25,000
Miyako: "..."

2529
02:46:25,000 --> 02:46:31,000
*I'm not sure if she's about to say something, or if that was an unintentional gasp.*

2530
02:46:31,000 --> 02:46:39,000
*Kujo keeps her eyes pointed at the floor. Her hair hides her face from me, making it hard to read her expression.*

2531
02:46:39,000 --> 02:46:41,000
*What more should I even say?*

2532
02:46:41,000 --> 02:46:47,000
*My thoughts are a mess, and I have no idea what to say next, but this silence is killing me.*

2533
02:46:47,000 --> 02:46:50,000
*I just keep saying whatever comes to mind.*

2534
02:46:50,000 --> 02:46:56,000
Kakeru: "I... guess you're kind of troubled, the way I'm forcing my feelings on you and all."

2535
02:46:56,000 --> 02:46:58,000
Miyako: "No, that's not..."

2536
02:46:58,000 --> 02:47:01,000
Kakeru: "No, you don't have to be nice. I get it."

2537
02:47:01,000 --> 02:47:06,000
Kakeru: "Heck, I only recently realized that you were the waitress at Nine Ball."

2538
02:47:06,000 --> 02:47:14,000
Kakeru: "I hardly ever spoke a word to you for so long... but then we kind of hit it off, so I got ahead of myself."

2539
02:47:14,000 --> 02:47:21,000
Kakeru: "And, well... You probably know this already, but I just want to get it all off my chest."

2540
02:47:21,000 --> 02:47:22,000
Miyako: "Okay."

2541
02:47:22,000 --> 02:47:30,000
Kakeru: "The reason I've been helping you search for the culprit was that I wanted an excuse to spend time with you, Kujo."

2542
02:47:30,000 --> 02:47:31,000
Miyako: "..."

2543
02:47:31,000 --> 02:47:39,000
Kakeru: "Sorry, you must be disgusted with me. I was afraid of that. That's why I've been hiding it this whole time."

2544
02:47:39,000 --> 02:47:46,000
Kakeru: "You're cute. You're a great cook. I just wanted you to like me, and that's... why I helped you."

2545
02:47:46,000 --> 02:47:47,000
Miyako: "..."

2546
02:47:47,000 --> 02:47:57,000
Kakeru: "And, well... That's how it is. It made me so happy when you said I was guiding you, but now you know, I... I'm not worthy of doing that."

2547
02:47:57,000 --> 02:48:06,000
Kakeru: "I fell for you because you're so cute. Oh, and because you're a good cook... Oh, I said that a second ago, didn't I? Erm, uh, so..."

2548
02:48:06,000 --> 02:48:12,000
Kakeru: "Right! You're kind, and gentle, and you always laugh at the stupid stuff I talk about."

2549
02:48:12,000 --> 02:48:24,000
Kakeru: "So, yeah... that's why I fell for you. That's everything I can think of, honestly. Man, not even a month has passed since we started hanging out. Am I shallow or what?"

2550
02:48:24,000 --> 02:48:29,000
Kakeru: "I'm sorry to just throw this all at you. I know it's unfair of me."

2551
02:48:29,000 --> 02:48:30,000
Miyako: "..."

2552
02:48:30,000 --> 02:48:39,000
Kakeru: "I mean, now you know the real reason I'm with you, searching for the culprit. Unlike you, I don't have a powerful sense of duty."

2553
02:48:39,000 --> 02:48:42,000
Kakeru: "I'm not the honorable guy you think I am."

2554
02:48:42,000 --> 02:48:43,000
Miyako: "..."

2555
02:48:43,000 --> 02:48:46,000
Kakeru: "So, yeah... I guess... That's about it."

2556
02:48:46,000 --> 02:48:52,000
Kakeru: "I'm sorry for making you feel awkward. Feel free to forget everything I just said."

2557
02:48:52,000 --> 02:48:53,000
Miyako: "What?"

2558
02:48:53,000 --> 02:48:55,000
Kakeru: "I'll see you."

2559
02:48:55,000 --> 02:48:56,000
Miyako: "Um..."

2560
02:48:56,000 --> 02:48:59,000
*I walk away, leaving behind poor, flustered Kujo.*

2561
02:48:59,000 --> 02:49:01,000
*So in the end, I still ran away.*

2562
02:49:01,000 --> 02:49:03,000
*Kujo had nothing to say to me.*

2563
02:49:03,000 --> 02:49:07,000
*You didn't have to be a genius to see she was uncomfortable.*

2564
02:49:07,000 --> 02:49:11,000
*It was all too obvious that she was just going to shoot me down.*

2565
02:49:11,000 --> 02:49:16,000
*And so, not wanting to hear her actually say the words, I just ran away.*

2566
02:49:16,000 --> 02:49:18,000
*God, I'm so pathetic.*

2567
02:49:18,000 --> 02:49:20,000
*And that's that. It's over.*

2568
02:49:20,000 --> 02:49:28,000
*We became such good friends, and then my stupid love-struck heart screwed it all up, just like I knew it would.*

2569
02:49:28,000 --> 02:49:32,000
*I can't believe I didn't even have the guts to hear her out.*

2570
02:49:32,000 --> 02:49:37,000
*Man, I need to chill out. Hating on myself isn't gonna do me any good.*

2571
02:49:37,000 --> 02:49:43,000
Yoichi: "Hey, there you are, Kakeru! Did you see Kujo-san? She's right over there."

2572
02:49:43,000 --> 02:49:45,000
Kakeru: "You won the bet."

2573
02:49:45,000 --> 02:49:46,000
Yoichi: "Huh?"

2574
02:49:46,000 --> 02:49:49,000
Kakeru: "Don't make me repeat myself."

2575
02:49:49,000 --> 02:49:54,000
Yoichi: "What? You're kidding, right? We gave you the perfect setup!"

2576
02:49:54,000 --> 02:49:59,000
Kakeru: "We're from two different worlds. It just wasn't meant to be."

2577
02:49:59,000 --> 02:50:05,000
Yoichi: "Aw, c'mon. Did you just royally screw up when it came time to ask her out?"

2578
02:50:05,000 --> 02:50:11,000
Kakeru: "Guess I did. Hey, walk with me a bit. I'm in the mood to shoot some guns."

2579
02:50:11,000 --> 02:50:14,000
Yoichi: "Sure thing. Let's head upstairs."

2580
02:50:14,000 --> 02:50:15,000
Kakeru: "Yeah."

2581
02:50:15,000 --> 02:50:20,000
Yoichi: "Don't cry now, poor little Kakeru. There's always next time!"

2582
02:50:20,000 --> 02:50:23,000
Kakeru: "Shut it. I'm not crying, dude."

2583
02:50:23,000 --> 02:50:27,000
*Yoichi and I head for the escalator while he pokes fun at me.*

2584
02:50:27,000 --> 02:50:35,000
*Still, my guess is that this searing pain in my heart won't go away no matter how many zombies I blast to pieces.*

2585
02:50:35,000 --> 02:50:39,000
*My first love, lost. It stings. It hurts more than I expected.*

2586
02:50:39,000 --> 02:50:43,000
Yoichi: "Thanks for coming, everyone! Take care on the way home!"

2587
02:50:43,000 --> 02:50:48,000
*We play until we're beat, and once people start getting hungry, we head out.*

2588
02:50:48,000 --> 02:50:55,000
*We say our goodbyes at the station, where it seems the only ones not getting on the train are Kujo and I.*

2589
02:50:55,000 --> 02:51:01,000
*Not a soul asks about how it went with me and Kujo. Maybe Yoichi already filled them in.*

2590
02:51:01,000 --> 02:51:11,000
*At any rate, it seems like they're acting considerate of us. As they walk by me, heading into the station, every last one gives me a meaningful look.*

2591
02:51:11,000 --> 02:51:14,000
*And so here we are, just the two of us.*

2592
02:51:14,000 --> 02:51:15,000
Kakeru: "..."

2593
02:51:15,000 --> 02:51:16,000
Miyako: "..."

2594
02:51:16,000 --> 02:51:17,000
*Talk about awkward.*

2595
02:51:17,000 --> 02:51:18,000
*...*

2596
02:51:18,000 --> 02:51:20,000
*Guess we'd better hurry home.*

2597
02:51:20,000 --> 02:51:29,000
*I'm sure in a little while we'll both be over it and able to talk normally, like we used to, but man, I am so not ready for this yet.*

2598
02:51:29,000 --> 02:51:33,000
*God, this is pathetic. I'm about to break down here.*

2599
02:51:33,000 --> 02:51:36,000
Kakeru: "All right, Kujo. Take care of yourself."

2600
02:51:36,000 --> 02:51:39,000
*I turn my back without waiting for her reply.*

2601
02:51:39,000 --> 02:51:40,000
*But then...*

2602
02:51:40,000 --> 02:51:41,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

2603
02:51:41,000 --> 02:51:42,000
Miyako: "..."

2604
02:51:42,000 --> 02:51:43,000
*She yanks at my arm.*

2605
02:51:43,000 --> 02:51:45,000
*Why does she not want me to go?*

2606
02:51:45,000 --> 02:51:52,000
*I don't want to shake off her hand, lightly gripping my wrist, so I can't really turn around to look at her.*

2607
02:51:52,000 --> 02:51:56,000
*What's going through her head? Is she frowning? Smiling?*

2608
02:51:56,000 --> 02:52:02,000
*Kujo remains silent as I wait for her to speak, still suffering that pain in my heart.*

2609
02:52:02,000 --> 02:52:03,000
Miyako: "..."

2610
02:52:03,000 --> 02:52:05,000
Kakeru: "What is it, Kujo?"

2611
02:52:05,000 --> 02:52:07,000
Miyako: "That was unfair."

2612
02:52:07,000 --> 02:52:08,000
Kakeru: "What was?"

2613
02:52:08,000 --> 02:52:11,000
Miyako: "You didn't give me a chance to speak."

2614
02:52:11,000 --> 02:52:12,000
Kakeru: "Oh..."

2615
02:52:12,000 --> 02:52:13,000
Kakeru: "..."

2616
02:52:13,000 --> 02:52:19,000
Kakeru: "You're right. I'm sorry. I ran away, because I was afraid to hear your answer."

2617
02:52:19,000 --> 02:52:28,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, you practically ran off with the conversation. You never asked me. How was I supposed to answer, when you never asked?"

2618
02:52:28,000 --> 02:52:32,000
Kakeru: "I see. You're right. I didn't ask you, did I?"

2619
02:52:32,000 --> 02:52:39,000
Miyako: "I kept waiting for my moment, but you said your piece, and then you walked off. That was very unfair."

2620
02:52:39,000 --> 02:52:40,000
Kakeru: "..."

2621
02:52:40,000 --> 02:52:44,000
Kakeru: "So, is it okay if I pick up where I left off?"

2622
02:52:44,000 --> 02:52:45,000
Miyako: "Okay."

2623
02:52:45,000 --> 02:52:47,000
Kakeru: "Will you go out with me?"

2624
02:52:47,000 --> 02:52:48,000
Miyako: "..."

2625
02:52:48,000 --> 02:52:49,000
*Kujo doesn't answer.*

2626
02:52:49,000 --> 02:52:53,000
*Which is pretty cruel, actually, after making me say all that.*

2627
02:52:53,000 --> 02:52:57,000
*There's a part of me that wants to burst into tears.*

2628
02:52:57,000 --> 02:53:02,000
*But now that I've come this far, I'm past the point of desperation.*

2629
02:53:02,000 --> 02:53:11,000
*I'm hanging on her every word. When she turns me down, it's gonna hit me so hard I'll go flying backwards and right into a trash can.*

2630
02:53:11,000 --> 02:53:13,000
Kakeru: "What's your answer?"

2631
02:53:13,000 --> 02:53:14,000
Miyako: "..."

2632
02:53:14,000 --> 02:53:15,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun..."

2633
02:53:15,000 --> 02:53:16,000
Kakeru: "Yeah?"

2634
02:53:16,000 --> 02:53:21,000
Miyako: "Earlier, you said you're not the honorable guy I think you are."

2635
02:53:21,000 --> 02:53:22,000
Kakeru: "Sure did."

2636
02:53:22,000 --> 02:53:30,000
Miyako: "Well I think you're amazing. Ever since that day you led me through the fire, I've felt nothing but respect for you."

2637
02:53:30,000 --> 02:53:31,000
Kakeru: "..."

2638
02:53:31,000 --> 02:53:32,000
*Respect?*

2639
02:53:32,000 --> 02:53:40,000
*I can see where this is going. She's going to tell me that she respects me but isn't interested in me romantically.*

2640
02:53:40,000 --> 02:53:43,000
*God, now I'm ready to run away again.*

2641
02:53:43,000 --> 02:53:47,000
*But I hold back that urge and stay right where I am.*

2642
02:53:47,000 --> 02:53:55,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun, you have things that I lack. You're smart. You're creative. And, most importantly, you're courageous."

2643
02:53:55,000 --> 02:54:04,000
Miyako: "And because of that, I wanted you by my side. That was why I wanted to look for the culprit together in the first place."

2644
02:54:04,000 --> 02:54:10,000
Miyako: "If you had an ulterior motive for joining in the search, well... maybe I did too."

2645
02:54:10,000 --> 02:54:11,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

2646
02:54:11,000 --> 02:54:15,000
*The topic takes an unexpected turn, leaving me speechless.*

2647
02:54:15,000 --> 02:54:17,000
*It was the same for her?*

2648
02:54:17,000 --> 02:54:23,000
*I'm about to whoop and jump for joy, when I pause. Something still doesn't add up.*

2649
02:54:23,000 --> 02:54:25,000
*And so I have to ask.*

2650
02:54:25,000 --> 02:54:26,000
Kakeru: "'Maybe'?"

2651
02:54:26,000 --> 02:54:31,000
Miyako: "I didn't realize it myself. I only understood it very recently..."

2652
02:54:31,000 --> 02:54:39,000
Miyako: "This has never happened to me before. I didn't know what these feelings I've been holding inside were..."

2653
02:54:39,000 --> 02:54:45,000
Miyako: "When I found out what you felt for me, it all finally started to make sense."

2654
02:54:45,000 --> 02:54:50,000
Miyako: "I even figured out why I hated watching you chat with Kosaka-senpai."

2655
02:54:50,000 --> 02:54:55,000
Miyako: "Even if she was compelling you with her ability, I didn't want to..."

2656
02:54:55,000 --> 02:54:56,000
Miyako: "..."

2657
02:54:56,000 --> 02:54:58,000
Miyako: "...to give you up."

2658
02:54:58,000 --> 02:54:59,000
Kakeru: "..."

2659
02:54:59,000 --> 02:55:00,000
Kakeru: "So, then..."

2660
02:55:00,000 --> 02:55:01,000
*My voice cracks.*

2661
02:55:01,000 --> 02:55:03,000
*Kujo takes a firmer grip on my arm.*

2662
02:55:03,000 --> 02:55:04,000
*She's trembling.*

2663
02:55:04,000 --> 02:55:06,000
*Or maybe that's me trembling.*

2664
02:55:06,000 --> 02:55:09,000
*My body is numb, and my mind is blank.*

2665
02:55:09,000 --> 02:55:11,000
*The silence drags on.*

2666
02:55:11,000 --> 02:55:13,000
*My heart is pounding in my ears.*

2667
02:55:13,000 --> 02:55:17,000
Miyako: "I'm not as honorable as you think I am, either."

2668
02:55:17,000 --> 02:55:21,000
Miyako: "I pried up your feelings without your permission."

2669
02:55:21,000 --> 02:55:29,000
Miyako: "And what I saw scared me, and I ran away. I was so ashamed for running away that I couldn't look you in the face."

2670
02:55:29,000 --> 02:55:35,000
Miyako: "I thought that, after the horrible way I'd treated you, I wasn't worthy of you."

2671
02:55:35,000 --> 02:55:39,000
Miyako: "B-But, even so! Despite all my flaws..." "..."

2672
02:55:39,000 --> 02:55:40,000
Miyako: "..."

2673
02:55:40,000 --> 02:55:42,000
Miyako: "You said all that to me..."

2674
02:55:42,000 --> 02:55:43,000
Miyako: "..."

2675
02:55:43,000 --> 02:55:50,000
Miyako: "I know it hasn't been long since we've gotten to know one another. Since we've become friends."

2676
02:55:50,000 --> 02:55:53,000
Miyako: "But for some things, time doesn't matter."

2677
02:55:53,000 --> 02:55:54,000
Miyako: "..."

2678
02:55:54,000 --> 02:55:55,000
Miyako: "I like you."

2679
02:55:55,000 --> 02:55:58,000
Miyako: "I'm in love with you, Niimi-kun."

2680
02:55:58,000 --> 02:56:00,000
Miyako: "I have my answer for you."

2681
02:56:00,000 --> 02:56:01,000
Miyako: "..."

2682
02:56:01,000 --> 02:56:02,000
Miyako: "Yes."

2683
02:56:02,000 --> 02:56:05,000
Miyako: "I would be honored to be with you."

2684
02:56:05,000 --> 02:56:06,000
Kakeru: "..."

2685
02:56:06,000 --> 02:56:07,000
Miyako: "..."

2686
02:56:07,000 --> 02:56:08,000
Kakeru: "......"

2687
02:56:08,000 --> 02:56:09,000
Miyako: "......"

2688
02:56:09,000 --> 02:56:10,000
Kakeru: "........."

2689
02:56:10,000 --> 02:56:13,000
Miyako: "D-Did you hear me, Niimi-kun?"

2690
02:56:13,000 --> 02:56:14,000
Kakeru: "Oh, y-yes."

2691
02:56:14,000 --> 02:56:16,000
Miyako: "I-I gave you my answer."

2692
02:56:16,000 --> 02:56:23,000
Kakeru: "Oh, r-right, sorry. I sort of blanked out. Or more like, I couldn't believe what I was hearing."

2693
02:56:23,000 --> 02:56:27,000
Kakeru: "So. Uh. H-Hold on. You'll... actually go out with me?"

2694
02:56:27,000 --> 02:56:28,000
Miyako: "..."

2695
02:56:28,000 --> 02:56:30,000
Kakeru: "Wh-Why'd you go all quiet?!"

2696
02:56:30,000 --> 02:56:33,000
Miyako: "I-I didn't! I was... nodding."

2697
02:56:33,000 --> 02:56:35,000
Kakeru: "I-I couldn't see that!"

2698
02:56:35,000 --> 02:56:37,000
Miyako: "Oh. I-I'm sorry."

2699
02:56:37,000 --> 02:56:40,000
Kakeru: "I-Is it okay for me to turn around?"

2700
02:56:40,000 --> 02:56:41,000
Miyako: "N-No, don't!"

2701
02:56:41,000 --> 02:56:43,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Why not?!"

2702
02:56:43,000 --> 02:56:45,000
Miyako: "I'm too embarrassed."

2703
02:56:45,000 --> 02:56:48,000
Kakeru: "Let me look you in the eyes and say it."

2704
02:56:48,000 --> 02:56:51,000
Kakeru: "I'm never running away again."

2705
02:56:51,000 --> 02:56:52,000
Miyako: "..."

2706
02:56:52,000 --> 02:56:54,000
*She loosens her grip on my arm.*

2707
02:56:54,000 --> 02:56:58,000
*I can't feel anything; it's like my whole body is numb.*

2708
02:56:58,000 --> 02:57:05,000
*I can't move my legs properly, so the mere act of turning around is taking an unexpected amount of effort.*

2709
02:57:05,000 --> 02:57:07,000
*At last, I see Kujo's face.*

2710
02:57:07,000 --> 02:57:08,000
Miyako: "..."

2711
02:57:08,000 --> 02:57:16,000
*She's blushing so hard I can't help but smile, but she's also on the verge of tears, which leaves me distraught.*

2712
02:57:16,000 --> 02:57:20,000
*Too embarrassed to meet my gaze, she looks off to the side.*

2713
02:57:20,000 --> 02:57:23,000
*I'm not doing a whole lot better here.*

2714
02:57:23,000 --> 02:57:27,000
*My voice trembles as I try to squeeze out a few more words.*

2715
02:57:27,000 --> 02:57:28,000
Kakeru: "K-Kujo?"

2716
02:57:28,000 --> 02:57:29,000
Miyako: "Y-Yes?"

2717
02:57:29,000 --> 02:57:31,000
Kakeru: "I like you, Kujo."

2718
02:57:31,000 --> 02:57:33,000
Miyako: "...I like you, too."

2719
02:57:33,000 --> 02:57:35,000
Kakeru: "Will you go out with me?"

2720
02:57:35,000 --> 02:57:37,000
Kakeru: "Will you be my girlfriend?"

2721
02:57:37,000 --> 02:57:38,000
Miyako: "..."

2722
02:57:38,000 --> 02:57:39,000
Miyako: "Yes."

2723
02:57:39,000 --> 02:57:41,000
Miyako: "I'll be your..."

2724
02:57:41,000 --> 02:57:42,000
Miyako: "..."

2725
02:57:42,000 --> 02:57:43,000
Miyako: "g-g... g..."

2726
02:57:43,000 --> 02:57:45,000
Kakeru: "H-Hey, settle down."

2727
02:57:45,000 --> 02:57:50,000
Miyako: "I-I-I'm sorry. I'm shaking, and it's making it hard to speak."

2728
02:57:50,000 --> 02:57:51,000
Miyako: "..."

2729
02:57:51,000 --> 02:57:52,000
Miyako: "Phew."

2730
02:57:52,000 --> 02:57:55,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry. Let's try it one more time..."

2731
02:57:55,000 --> 02:57:57,000
Kakeru: "Will you be my girlfriend?"

2732
02:57:57,000 --> 02:57:58,000
Miyako: "Yes."

2733
02:57:58,000 --> 02:57:59,000
Miyako: "Yes!"

2734
02:57:59,000 --> 02:58:02,000
Miyako: "Please, take me as your girlfriend."

2735
02:58:02,000 --> 02:58:04,000
Miyako: "Will you be my boyfriend?"

2736
02:58:04,000 --> 02:58:06,000
Kakeru: "Yes. I'd love to."

2737
02:58:06,000 --> 02:58:08,000
Miyako: "Thank you. I'm so happy."

2738
02:58:08,000 --> 02:58:09,000
Kakeru: "..."

2739
02:58:09,000 --> 02:58:10,000
Miyako: "..."

2740
02:58:10,000 --> 02:58:11,000
Kakeru: "......"

2741
02:58:11,000 --> 02:58:12,000
Miyako: "......"

2742
02:58:12,000 --> 02:58:14,000
Kakeru: "S-So, what do we do now?"

2743
02:58:14,000 --> 02:58:16,000
Miyako: "I-I have no idea."

2744
02:58:16,000 --> 02:58:17,000
Kakeru: "........."

2745
02:58:17,000 --> 02:58:18,000
Miyako: "........."

2746
02:58:18,000 --> 02:58:19,000
Kakeru: "Pfft."

2747
02:58:19,000 --> 02:58:20,000
Miyako: "Haha!"

2748
02:58:20,000 --> 02:58:22,000
Kakeru: "Ahaha, hahaha!"

2749
02:58:22,000 --> 02:58:23,000
Miyako: "Ahaha! Haha."

2750
02:58:23,000 --> 02:58:30,000
*The overwhelming awkwardness pops the tension like a balloon, and the two of us burst out laughing together.*

2751
02:58:30,000 --> 02:58:32,000
*Kujo is my girlfriend.*

2752
02:58:32,000 --> 02:58:34,000
*And I'm her boyfriend.*

2753
02:58:34,000 --> 02:58:37,000
*I can't believe it turned out this way.*

2754
02:58:37,000 --> 02:58:39,000
*I never saw this coming.*

2755
02:58:39,000 --> 02:58:41,000
*None of it feels real.*

2756
02:58:41,000 --> 02:58:51,000
*An immense wave of relief washes over me, along with the thought, "Oh, thank God. I can finally stop being so cripplingly awkward around her."*

2757
02:58:51,000 --> 02:58:54,000
Kakeru: "I was sure you were going to turn me down."

2758
02:58:54,000 --> 02:59:01,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry it was so hard for me to tell you. Contrary to what you may think of me, I'm..."

2759
02:59:01,000 --> 02:59:09,000
Kakeru: "I don't know what you're about to say about yourself, but whatever it is, you won't change what I think of you, Kujo."

2760
02:59:09,000 --> 02:59:10,000
Miyako: "Okay."

2761
02:59:10,000 --> 02:59:16,000
Kakeru: "Me, on the other hand? Contrary to how honorable you may think I am, I'm..."

2762
02:59:16,000 --> 02:59:25,000
Miyako: "I don't know what you're about to say about yourself, but whatever it is, you won't change what I think of you, Niimi-kun."

2763
02:59:25,000 --> 02:59:28,000
Kakeru: "You're sure I'm the one you want?"

2764
02:59:28,000 --> 02:59:31,000
Miyako: "You're the only one for me, Niimi-kun."

2765
02:59:31,000 --> 02:59:35,000
Miyako: "I want to be your girlfriend. Nobody else's."

2766
02:59:35,000 --> 02:59:36,000
Kakeru: "Kujo..."

2767
02:59:36,000 --> 02:59:37,000
Miyako: "Niimi-kun..."

2768
02:59:37,000 --> 02:59:38,000
Kakeru: "..."

2769
02:59:38,000 --> 02:59:39,000
Miyako: "..."

2770
02:59:39,000 --> 02:59:42,000
Kakeru: "W-We should probably go somewhere else."

2771
02:59:42,000 --> 02:59:43,000
Miyako: "Oh, y-yes."

2772
02:59:43,000 --> 02:59:49,000
*We're in everybody's way here, standing around wrapped up in our own little world.*

2773
02:59:49,000 --> 02:59:55,000
*As we calm down, we notice all the people looking at us, so we hightail it out of there.*

2774
02:59:55,000 --> 02:59:56,000
Kakeru: "..."

2775
02:59:56,000 --> 02:59:57,000
Miyako: "..."

2776
02:59:57,000 --> 02:59:59,000
*We walk in silence for a bit.*

2777
02:59:59,000 --> 03:00:07,000
*Part of me wants to shout and jump and sing, I'm so happy. The rest of me still can't believe it's really true.*

2778
03:00:07,000 --> 03:00:13,000
*The only sounds are our footsteps and the slow tread of Kujo's bike tires on the sidewalk.*

2779
03:00:13,000 --> 03:00:15,000
*That's our whole world right now.*

2780
03:00:15,000 --> 03:00:16,000
Miyako: "..."

2781
03:00:16,000 --> 03:00:18,000
Miyako: "I'm this way..."

2782
03:00:18,000 --> 03:00:20,000
Kakeru: "Oh, yeah, uh-huh."

2783
03:00:20,000 --> 03:00:22,000
*Kujo's tone is relucant.*

2784
03:00:22,000 --> 03:00:24,000
*This is where we part.*

2785
03:00:24,000 --> 03:00:26,000
Miyako: "Thanks. It was great."

2786
03:00:26,000 --> 03:00:29,000
Kakeru: "Oh, uh, the pleasure was all mine."

2787
03:00:29,000 --> 03:00:32,000
Miyako: "...What did I just thank you for?"

2788
03:00:32,000 --> 03:00:35,000
Kakeru: "I totally responded like I knew, too..."

2789
03:00:35,000 --> 03:00:38,000
Miyako: "Maybe... for you asking me out?"

2790
03:00:38,000 --> 03:00:41,000
Kakeru: "That'd be sorta... weird, right?"

2791
03:00:41,000 --> 03:00:47,000
Miyako: "I-I know, right? I think I'm still too excited, and it's making my head spin."

2792
03:00:47,000 --> 03:00:48,000
Kakeru: "Same here."

2793
03:00:48,000 --> 03:00:52,000
*Another clumsy exchange puts an awkward smile on our faces.*

2794
03:00:52,000 --> 03:00:57,000
*How are you even supposed to talk to your girlfriend? I have no idea.*

2795
03:00:57,000 --> 03:01:02,000
*I guess it's just something I'll have to figure out as we move forward together.*

2796
03:01:02,000 --> 03:01:03,000
Kakeru: "Hey, Kujo?"

2797
03:01:03,000 --> 03:01:04,000
Miyako: "Yeah?"

2798
03:01:04,000 --> 03:01:06,000
Kakeru: "Do you have work tomorrow?"

2799
03:01:06,000 --> 03:01:08,000
Miyako: "Until 2 PM, I think."

2800
03:01:08,000 --> 03:01:10,000
Kakeru: "Oh, I see. You're busy..."

2801
03:01:10,000 --> 03:01:12,000
Miyako: "But I'm free after 2PM."

2802
03:01:12,000 --> 03:01:14,000
Kakeru: "You won't be tired?"

2803
03:01:14,000 --> 03:01:16,000
Miyako: "I'll be fine."

2804
03:01:16,000 --> 03:01:19,000
Kakeru: "Want to do something together?"

2805
03:01:19,000 --> 03:01:20,000
Miyako: "Sure."

2806
03:01:20,000 --> 03:01:24,000
Kakeru: "I mean... I have no idea what, but, y'know."

2807
03:01:24,000 --> 03:01:28,000
Miyako: "As long as it's with you, anyplace is fine."

2808
03:01:28,000 --> 03:01:30,000
Kakeru: "How about Round Two again?"

2809
03:01:30,000 --> 03:01:36,000
Miyako: "Oh. Actually, I saw something there in the crane game, but... I couldn't get it."

2810
03:01:36,000 --> 03:01:39,000
Kakeru: "I'll get it for you tomorrow!"

2811
03:01:39,000 --> 03:01:42,000
Miyako: "Thank you. I'm looking forward to it."

2812
03:01:42,000 --> 03:01:45,000
Kakeru: "I'll come to pick you up. Um, around 2:30?"

2813
03:01:45,000 --> 03:01:51,000
Miyako: "Okay. Oh, I'll have to change, so it might be good if you come around 2:40."

2814
03:01:51,000 --> 03:01:53,000
Kakeru: "Got it. And lunch?"

2815
03:01:53,000 --> 03:01:56,000
Miyako: "I'll make sure to skip staff lunch."

2816
03:01:56,000 --> 03:01:58,000
Kakeru: "Great, we can eat together."

2817
03:01:58,000 --> 03:01:59,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

2818
03:01:59,000 --> 03:02:01,000
Kakeru: "I'll contact you later."

2819
03:02:01,000 --> 03:02:02,000
Miyako: "Okay."

2820
03:02:02,000 --> 03:02:03,000
Kakeru: "..."

2821
03:02:03,000 --> 03:02:04,000
Miyako: "..."

2822
03:02:04,000 --> 03:02:07,000
Kakeru: "It's still kinda hard to believe."

2823
03:02:07,000 --> 03:02:17,000
Miyako: "Same for me. I feel like once I get back, take a bath, and relax, it's all going to come crashing home and my head is going to explode."

2824
03:02:17,000 --> 03:02:20,000
Kakeru: "Oh man, that's totally gonna be me, too..."

2825
03:02:20,000 --> 03:02:24,000
Miyako: "Yeah, haha. I'll be waiting for your message."

2826
03:02:24,000 --> 03:02:27,000
Kakeru: "Right! Oh, sorry for holding you up."

2827
03:02:27,000 --> 03:02:30,000
Miyako: "No, it's fine. I'll be going."

2828
03:02:30,000 --> 03:02:32,000
Kakeru: "See you tomorrow."

2829
03:02:32,000 --> 03:02:34,000
Miyako: "Okay, see you."

2830
03:02:34,000 --> 03:02:36,000
*Kujo waves and hops on her bike.*

2831
03:02:36,000 --> 03:02:39,000
*After another cheerful wave, she pedals off.*

2832
03:02:39,000 --> 03:02:45,000
*When she's a little ways away, she stops, turns around, and gives me one last big wave.*

2833
03:02:45,000 --> 03:02:47,000
*I turn around as well.*

2834
03:02:47,000 --> 03:02:51,000
*That little exchange alone is enough to make me beam with joy.*

2835
03:02:51,000 --> 03:02:57,000
*Those same quivering emotions that were driving me mad when I was waiting for her reply...*

2836
03:02:57,000 --> 03:03:01,000
*Well, now they feel so damn good I can hardly contain myself.*

2837
03:03:01,000 --> 03:03:03,000
Miyako: "Thank you very much!"

2838
03:03:03,000 --> 03:03:07,000
*Kujo's voice echoes through the cafe as she sees out customers.*

2839
03:03:07,000 --> 03:03:13,000
*It's a big party, all of them with separate checks, so it's slowing down the process a little.*

2840
03:03:13,000 --> 03:03:15,000
*It's currently 2:50 PM.*

2841
03:03:15,000 --> 03:03:25,000
*When I arrived precisely at 2:40, she told me that things might take a while and that I should just wait inside, so I've been hanging around since then.*

2842
03:03:25,000 --> 03:03:35,000
*Just getting a glass of water would have been bad manners, so I ordered a soda and have been sipping on it, waiting for Kujo to get off her shift.*

2843
03:03:35,000 --> 03:03:40,000
Miyako: "Would you like the receipt? Thank you very much! Please come again."

2844
03:03:40,000 --> 03:03:44,000
*She closes out the last person's check with a sigh of relief.*

2845
03:03:44,000 --> 03:03:51,000
*She shoots a glance my way, smiling sweetly. With a a nod to another part-timer, she disappears into the back.*

2846
03:03:51,000 --> 03:03:55,000
*Finally done, I guess? She's probably off to go change.*

2847
03:03:55,000 --> 03:04:02,000
*While vacantly staring at the kitchen area where she disappeared to, I put the straw to my lips.*

2848
03:04:02,000 --> 03:04:03,000
*...*

2849
03:04:03,000 --> 03:04:05,000
*Almost forgot my glass is empty.*

2850
03:04:05,000 --> 03:04:08,000
*My throat is super dry for some reason.*

2851
03:04:08,000 --> 03:04:10,000
*This is bad. I'm nervous as hell.*

2852
03:04:10,000 --> 03:04:11,000
*My first date.*

2853
03:04:11,000 --> 03:04:19,000
*We've walked around town together before, but once you actually call it a date, suddenly it becomes this huge event.*

2854
03:04:19,000 --> 03:04:23,000
*I killed off my soda the instant it was brought over.*

2855
03:04:23,000 --> 03:04:25,000
*Only ice remains in my glass.*

2856
03:04:25,000 --> 03:04:31,000
*Unable to contain my thirst, I slurp up the little bit of water that's melted from the ice.*

2857
03:04:31,000 --> 03:04:37,000
*That, of course, isn't enough, so I pop the ice in my mouth and start crunching down on it.*

2858
03:04:37,000 --> 03:04:44,000
*As soon as I grind the last ice cube into pieces, Kujo returns to the cafe dressed in her casual clothes.*

2859
03:04:44,000 --> 03:04:47,000
*She walks over to me and sits across from me.*

2860
03:04:47,000 --> 03:04:50,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry that took so long."

2861
03:04:50,000 --> 03:04:54,000
Kakeru: "Nah, no worries. Still doing okay? You were awfully busy."

2862
03:04:54,000 --> 03:05:03,000
Miyako: "Things are usually slow on weekends, but today we had a bit of a rush. Still, everything is fine now that the crowd's gone."

2863
03:05:03,000 --> 03:05:05,000
Miyako: "Oh, do you need more water?"

2864
03:05:05,000 --> 03:05:07,000
Kakeru: "Uh, no, I'll be fine."

2865
03:05:07,000 --> 03:05:15,000
Miyako: "Sorry for making you wait so long. You must be hungry. We, um... probably shouldn't eat here, should we? Haha."

2866
03:05:15,000 --> 03:05:20,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, good point. Let's go wherever sounds good to you, Kujo."

2867
03:05:20,000 --> 03:05:22,000
Miyako: "Oh, are you sure?"

2868
03:05:22,000 --> 03:05:25,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. Come on, let's get going."

2869
03:05:25,000 --> 03:05:26,000
Miyako: "Sure."

2870
03:05:26,000 --> 03:05:29,000
*I take the check and stand up from my seat.*

2871
03:05:29,000 --> 03:05:35,000
*Kujo starts to pull out her wallet for some reason, but I obviously stop her and pay alone.*

2872
03:05:35,000 --> 03:05:42,000
*Kujo responds to her coworker's knowing smile with an awkward smile of her own as we leave the cafe.*

2873
03:05:42,000 --> 03:05:48,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry. Not only did I make you wait forever, I made you foot the bill."

2874
03:05:48,000 --> 03:05:56,000
Kakeru: "I ordered that drink on my own, so I couldn't ask you to help pay for it. Besides, I planned on buying us lunch, too."

2875
03:05:56,000 --> 03:05:57,000
Miyako: "You did?"

2876
03:05:57,000 --> 03:06:01,000
Kakeru: "That's right. I asked you out, so I'm paying."

2877
03:06:01,000 --> 03:06:06,000
Miyako: "But you're always the one who pays for the groceries, too."

2878
03:06:06,000 --> 03:06:20,000
Kakeru: "That's from the money for food I get from my folks, so that doesn't count. Though I guess I don't actually work, so it's all my folks' money anyway... Man, not making the best case for myself here."

2879
03:06:20,000 --> 03:06:25,000
Kakeru: "Look, it's our first date, so at least let me pay for the meal."

2880
03:06:25,000 --> 03:06:26,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

2881
03:06:26,000 --> 03:06:27,000
Miyako: "..."

2882
03:06:27,000 --> 03:06:30,000
Miyako: "Fine, then I get to pay for the next one."

2883
03:06:30,000 --> 03:06:31,000
Kakeru: "Sure thing."

2884
03:06:31,000 --> 03:06:32,000
*The next one.*

2885
03:06:32,000 --> 03:06:40,000
*We've only just started our first date, and she's already looking forward to the next one. Man, my heart can't take this.*

2886
03:06:40,000 --> 03:06:43,000
Kakeru: "What are you in the mood for?"

2887
03:06:43,000 --> 03:06:46,000
Miyako: "We're really getting whatever I want?"

2888
03:06:46,000 --> 03:06:47,000
Kakeru: "You bet."

2889
03:06:47,000 --> 03:06:50,000
Miyako: "Alright, then. It's a bit pricey, but..."

2890
03:06:50,000 --> 03:06:52,000
Kakeru: "Whatever you want."

2891
03:06:52,000 --> 03:06:56,000
Miyako: "Could we go to MockDonald's for hamburgers?"

2892
03:06:56,000 --> 03:06:59,000
Kakeru: "That's not pricey, it's cheap!"

2893
03:06:59,000 --> 03:07:05,000
Miyako: "What? I-It is? But a combo meal costs almost eight-hundred yen. That's expensive!"

2894
03:07:05,000 --> 03:07:12,000
Kakeru: "I was ready to spend over a thousand yen. Heck, get a dessert while we're there, if you want."

2895
03:07:12,000 --> 03:07:14,000
Miyako: "Wow. How extravagant."

2896
03:07:14,000 --> 03:07:16,000
Kakeru: "C'mon, let's go."

2897
03:07:16,000 --> 03:07:17,000
Miyako: "Oh, s-sure."

2898
03:07:17,000 --> 03:07:19,000
Kakeru: "Oh, what about your bike?"

2899
03:07:19,000 --> 03:07:22,000
Miyako: "Don't worry. I'll just leave it here."

2900
03:07:22,000 --> 03:07:23,000
Kakeru: "Okay."

2901
03:07:23,000 --> 03:07:26,000
Miyako: "That way, I'll have my hands free."

2902
03:07:26,000 --> 03:07:28,000
Kakeru: "Hm? Oh, sure."

2903
03:07:28,000 --> 03:07:31,000
Miyako: "Oh, um... Ahaha, let's head off."

2904
03:07:31,000 --> 03:07:35,000
*Kujo blushes as she starts walking, though I'm not sure why.*

2905
03:07:35,000 --> 03:07:39,000
*I fall in next to her, tilting my head in confusion.*

2906
03:07:39,000 --> 03:07:40,000
*...*

2907
03:07:40,000 --> 03:07:41,000
*Oh!*

2908
03:07:41,000 --> 03:07:48,000
*She said something about making sure her hands are free... Did she mean, like, she wants to hold hands?*

2909
03:07:48,000 --> 03:07:51,000
*Nah, I'm reading too much into this. Right?*

2910
03:07:51,000 --> 03:08:01,000
*Then again, if I'd been smooth enough to say, "Oh, fancy that. Guess we'll be able to hold hands," or something, we'd actually be holding hands by now.*

2911
03:08:01,000 --> 03:08:03,000
*Did I miss my chance?*

2912
03:08:03,000 --> 03:08:04,000
Kakeru: "Um..."

2913
03:08:04,000 --> 03:08:05,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

2914
03:08:05,000 --> 03:08:07,000
Kakeru: "Oh! No, it's nothing."

2915
03:08:07,000 --> 03:08:11,000
Miyako: "...? Oh, how about the one by the train station?"

2916
03:08:11,000 --> 03:08:13,000
Kakeru: "Y-Yeah, sounds good."

2917
03:08:13,000 --> 03:08:19,000
*I scramble for a response, sweating bullets over how badly I already screwed things up.*

2918
03:08:19,000 --> 03:08:23,000
*I just have to make sure I don't let my next chance get away.*

2919
03:08:23,000 --> 03:08:25,000
Miyako: "This looks good."

2920
03:08:25,000 --> 03:08:26,000
Kakeru: "Yeah!"

2921
03:08:26,000 --> 03:08:28,000
*We both unwrap our burgers.*

2922
03:08:28,000 --> 03:08:33,000
*Kujo has a veggie burger, and I got the the signature item, a Huge Mock.*

2923
03:08:33,000 --> 03:08:41,000
*We both got the combo with onion rings and fries, with Kujo ordering an iced tea for her drink. I settled on oolong tea.*

2924
03:08:41,000 --> 03:08:45,000
*To me, this is an extremely commonplace lunch, but...*

2925
03:08:45,000 --> 03:08:52,000
Miyako: "I get to have my month-end splurge at the beginning of the month... This is the best! Haha!"

2926
03:08:52,000 --> 03:08:57,000
*Kujo's cheeks are pushed up into the biggest smile I've ever seen on her.*

2927
03:08:57,000 --> 03:09:02,000
*The big-shot president's daughter, elated over a fast food burger.*

2928
03:09:02,000 --> 03:09:08,000
*Man, and here I thought this was the sort of thing you only read about in fiction.*

2929
03:09:08,000 --> 03:09:13,000
Kakeru: "Okay, so, I have a question about the stuff you usually eat at home."

2930
03:09:13,000 --> 03:09:14,000
Miyako: "Yeah?"

2931
03:09:14,000 --> 03:09:19,000
Kakeru: "You don't think of your ordinary meals as 'splurging', do you?"

2932
03:09:19,000 --> 03:09:22,000
Miyako: "Nah, they're perfectly normal."

2933
03:09:22,000 --> 03:09:29,000
Kakeru: "I mean, I could understand your reaction if you were, like, eating steak and caviar every day."

2934
03:09:29,000 --> 03:09:38,000
Miyako: "Ohh, haha. Like, if I was having French haute cuisine every night, instant ramen would seem like a treat. That kind of thing?"

2935
03:09:38,000 --> 03:09:40,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, yeah, exactly."

2936
03:09:40,000 --> 03:09:50,000
Miyako: "See, my mom worries about letting me eat stuff that isn't good for me. That's why we never have anything like hamburgers or instant ramen."

2937
03:09:50,000 --> 03:09:54,000
Kakeru: "Ohhh, now I get it. My parents are the same, actually."

2938
03:09:54,000 --> 03:09:56,000
Miyako: "No soft drinks, either."

2939
03:09:56,000 --> 03:09:59,000
Kakeru: "God, yeah, exactly like my folks."

2940
03:09:59,000 --> 03:10:09,000
Miyako: "Haha. We're just an ordinary family. Everybody kind of expects me to act like an upper-crust kind of girl, but I don't really like spending money."

2941
03:10:09,000 --> 03:10:14,000
Kakeru: "If they could see you now, they'd change their opinions in a heartbeat."

2942
03:10:14,000 --> 03:10:15,000
Miyako: "Why's that?"

2943
03:10:15,000 --> 03:10:28,000
Kakeru: "Well, when we'd just started hanging out, you were so uptight, you know? Like how you talked and acted. Gave you this 'prim and proper princess' image, and left me a little on my guard."

2944
03:10:28,000 --> 03:10:36,000
Miyako: "Well, I act that way because I can be rather shy around people. When I get nervous, I tend to fall back on formality."

2945
03:10:36,000 --> 03:10:49,000
Kakeru: "I mean sure, maybe the nervousness explains why you do it, but the way you act is so... How do I put this? You gave me the impression that you're way more cultured than I could ever be."

2946
03:10:49,000 --> 03:10:53,000
Miyako: "Oh, really? I've never considered that before."

2947
03:10:53,000 --> 03:11:03,000
Kakeru: "I can just picture you going to some high-class restaurant and going through the full course dinner without feeling an ounce of discomfort."

2948
03:11:03,000 --> 03:11:16,000
Miyako: "No way, of course it makes me uncomfortable. We do that a few times a year, like at New Years. Whenever we get the whole family together, it seems like we have to go somewhere fancy."

2949
03:11:16,000 --> 03:11:24,000
Kakeru: "Whoa, crazy! That's the first time I've ever heard you mention anything like that. I've never eaten anywhere upscale."

2950
03:11:24,000 --> 03:11:29,000
Miyako: "Ahaha. It's not really all that formal an occasion, though."

2951
03:11:29,000 --> 03:11:32,000
Kakeru: "No hoity-toity French restaurant?"

2952
03:11:32,000 --> 03:11:44,000
Miyako: "Hmm... Well, maybe a while ago, we used to go to places like that, but lately we're pretty much only going to buffets. It helps keep the little kids in the family happy."

2953
03:11:44,000 --> 03:11:51,000
Kakeru: "A top-tier buffet... That's got to be worlds apart from the cheap all-you-can-eat places I've been to."

2954
03:11:51,000 --> 03:11:57,000
Miyako: "Hmm. Well, I don't know the kind of place you mean, so I can't really say either way."

2955
03:11:57,000 --> 03:12:01,000
Kakeru: "I'm suddenly intimately aware of the class divide."

2956
03:12:01,000 --> 03:12:08,000
Miyako: "I-I think you're exaggerating a bit. It's not like the food there is amazingly delicious or anything."

2957
03:12:08,000 --> 03:12:10,000
Kakeru: "Wait, really?"

2958
03:12:10,000 --> 03:12:14,000
Miyako: "Yeah. Plus, I'm always so nervous that I just can't..."

2959
03:12:14,000 --> 03:12:16,000
*She nibbles on her burger.*

2960
03:12:16,000 --> 03:12:20,000
Miyako: "Mmm... It's so good! I think I'd rather have this."

2961
03:12:20,000 --> 03:12:23,000
Kakeru: "Better than haute cuisine, huh?"

2962
03:12:23,000 --> 03:12:27,000
Miyako: "If you ask me, nothing beats these onion rings."

2963
03:12:27,000 --> 03:12:31,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I feel you. They're pretty darn good, aren't they?"

2964
03:12:31,000 --> 03:12:36,000
Miyako: "The craving's so strong, your subconscious orders them for you. Haha."

2965
03:12:36,000 --> 03:12:39,000
*We're having a natural conversation.*

2966
03:12:39,000 --> 03:12:52,000
*We walked the entire way here in silence, and then even at first while we were eating it was the same. I was freaking out, wondering what I was supposed to do. But it all turned out fine.*

2967
03:12:52,000 --> 03:12:56,000
*Now, my only concern is... I can't stop staring at her smile.*

2968
03:12:56,000 --> 03:13:01,000
*As soon as I realize what I'm doing, I blush and take a gulp of my tea.*

2969
03:13:01,000 --> 03:13:04,000
Miyako: "So, how was your Golden Week?"

2970
03:13:04,000 --> 03:13:13,000
Kakeru: "Eh, nothing special. I just went back to my folks'. Granted, it was a bit weird since I don't have a room there anymore."

2971
03:13:13,000 --> 03:13:16,000
Miyako: "What happened to your old room?"

2972
03:13:16,000 --> 03:13:20,000
Kakeru: "I used to share with Sora, but now it's just hers."

2973
03:13:20,000 --> 03:13:28,000
Miyako: "Oh, haha. So the reason you moved out and started living alone was so that Sora-chan could have the room to herself?"

2974
03:13:28,000 --> 03:13:33,000
Kakeru: "No, no. I was KICKED out. I had no choice but to start living on my own."

2975
03:13:33,000 --> 03:13:35,000
Miyako: "Is that true?"

2976
03:13:35,000 --> 03:13:38,000
Kakeru: "C'mon, I'm not that generous."

2977
03:13:38,000 --> 03:13:45,000
Miyako: "I'm not so sure. I get the feeling you're actually quite the kind and generous older brother."

2978
03:13:45,000 --> 03:13:54,000
Kakeru: "Certainly not the look I was aiming for... Oh, that reminds me, I've been wondering how Sora's faring with the investigation."

2979
03:13:54,000 --> 03:13:58,000
Miyako: "Oh... You put it on hold because I ran away, right?"

2980
03:13:58,000 --> 03:14:03,000
Kakeru: "I can't really lay all the blame on you for that. It was my fault too."

2981
03:14:03,000 --> 03:14:12,000
Miyako: "Haha, I suppose. We're lucky—though that may not be the most appropriate word to use—that a third victim hasn't shown up yet."

2982
03:14:12,000 --> 03:14:16,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. But it's bound to happen again sooner or later."

2983
03:14:16,000 --> 03:14:20,000
Miyako: "Yes. We have to get to the bottom of this, and soon."

2984
03:14:20,000 --> 03:14:25,000
Kakeru: "Kujo, your power is going to be a huge help in this, but..."

2985
03:14:25,000 --> 03:14:30,000
Miyako: "But it's not like I can just use it on every person in town."

2986
03:14:30,000 --> 03:14:37,000
Kakeru: "And even if we tried just searching the school, we're still talking about hundreds of people."

2987
03:14:37,000 --> 03:14:39,000
Miyako: "We need a better plan."

2988
03:14:39,000 --> 03:14:52,000
Kakeru: "Sure would be nice if the culprit was making some sort of public declaration before each murder. Or like, if they only struck on the night of a full moon, or something obvious like that."

2989
03:14:52,000 --> 03:14:56,000
Miyako: "It's almost like they're not even planning each one."

2990
03:14:56,000 --> 03:14:58,000
Kakeru: "Sure seems that way."

2991
03:14:58,000 --> 03:15:04,000
Miyako: "So far, all the victims have been girls. And each has occurred late at night."

2992
03:15:04,000 --> 03:15:11,000
Kakeru: "The dates seem to be random. Well, that, or there could be a pattern that we haven't picked up on yet."

2993
03:15:11,000 --> 03:15:12,000
Miyako: "I wonder..."

2994
03:15:12,000 --> 03:15:13,000
Miyako: "..."

2995
03:15:13,000 --> 03:15:16,000
Kakeru: "Sorry, let's drop the topic."

2996
03:15:16,000 --> 03:15:21,000
Miyako: "Oh, y-yes, you're right. This is supposed to be our date, after all."

2997
03:15:21,000 --> 03:15:30,000
Kakeru: "Man, this is the first time I've ever been on a date, so I'm super flustered. Oh... I shouldn't have said that out loud."

2998
03:15:30,000 --> 03:15:39,000
Miyako: "Heh heh, I'm in the same boat. My first-ever relationship. My first-ever boyfriend. My first-ever date. It's all new to me."

2999
03:15:39,000 --> 03:15:41,000
Kakeru: "Kinda redundant there."

3000
03:15:41,000 --> 03:15:42,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

3001
03:15:42,000 --> 03:15:48,000
Kakeru: "If this is your first relationship, then I'm obviously your first boyfriend."

3002
03:15:48,000 --> 03:15:49,000
Miyako: "Huh? Oh..."

3003
03:15:49,000 --> 03:15:53,000
Kakeru: "You have some surprisingly airheaded moments, Kujo."

3004
03:15:53,000 --> 03:15:55,000
Miyako: "I can't deny that."

3005
03:15:55,000 --> 03:16:02,000
*I don't know if she's embarrassed or if she's pouting. She munches on her french fry as she furrows her brow.*

3006
03:16:02,000 --> 03:16:05,000
*I smile, sinking my teeth into my burger.*

3007
03:16:05,000 --> 03:16:06,000
Miyako: "..."

3008
03:16:06,000 --> 03:16:08,000
Miyako: "Hey, Niimi-kun?"

3009
03:16:08,000 --> 03:16:09,000
Kakeru: "Hm?"

3010
03:16:09,000 --> 03:16:12,000
*She's gone very quiet for some reason.*

3011
03:16:12,000 --> 03:16:18,000
*Surprised at the sudden shift in tone, I brace myself for whatever she's going to say.*

3012
03:16:18,000 --> 03:16:20,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

3013
03:16:20,000 --> 03:16:23,000
Miyako: "Sorry to ask this so suddenly, but..."

3014
03:16:23,000 --> 03:16:24,000
Kakeru: "What is it?"

3015
03:16:24,000 --> 03:16:28,000
Miyako: "Um, don't you think 'Niimi-kun' is a bit too formal?"

3016
03:16:28,000 --> 03:16:29,000
Kakeru: "...?"

3017
03:16:29,000 --> 03:16:32,000
Miyako: "Like, the names we use for each other."

3018
03:16:32,000 --> 03:16:35,000
Kakeru: "O-Ohhh, I see. Um, yeah, I guess so."

3019
03:16:35,000 --> 03:16:40,000
Miyako: "So, see, I was thinking, maybe... If you're okay with it..."

3020
03:16:40,000 --> 03:16:42,000
Kakeru: "Can I call you Miyako?"

3021
03:16:42,000 --> 03:16:43,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3022
03:16:43,000 --> 03:16:44,000
Miyako: "...!"

3023
03:16:44,000 --> 03:16:50,000
*Kujo freezes for a second, then her head begins bobbing up and down enthusiastically.*

3024
03:16:50,000 --> 03:16:52,000
*She then goes on, visibly excited.*

3025
03:16:52,000 --> 03:16:55,000
Miyako: "And maybe I can call you Kakeru-kun?"

3026
03:16:55,000 --> 03:16:57,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, definitely."

3027
03:16:57,000 --> 03:17:02,000
Miyako: "Great! In that case, I'll be calling you Niimi-kun from now on."

3028
03:17:02,000 --> 03:17:03,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

3029
03:17:03,000 --> 03:17:04,000
Miyako: "What?"

3030
03:17:04,000 --> 03:17:05,000
Miyako: "...!"

3031
03:17:05,000 --> 03:17:07,000
Miyako: "K-Kakeru-kun, I mean!"

3032
03:17:07,000 --> 03:17:10,000
Kakeru: "You really can be an airhead, Kujo."

3033
03:17:10,000 --> 03:17:12,000
Miyako: "Try it again!"

3034
03:17:12,000 --> 03:17:15,000
Kakeru: "Oh no! Right, not Kujo, Miyako."

3035
03:17:15,000 --> 03:17:19,000
Miyako: "Looks like you can be an airhead too, Nii... Kakeru-kun."

3036
03:17:19,000 --> 03:17:21,000
Kakeru: "You almost called me Niimi."

3037
03:17:21,000 --> 03:17:23,000
Miyako: "This is tough."

3038
03:17:23,000 --> 03:17:26,000
Kakeru: "We'll get used to it over time, I guess."

3039
03:17:26,000 --> 03:17:29,000
Miyako: "Okay, haha. Over time, yeah."

3040
03:17:29,000 --> 03:17:36,000
*Miyako gives me another brilliant smile, and I instinctively grab my tea and hide my embarrassment behind it.*

3041
03:17:36,000 --> 03:17:37,000
*Miyako...*

3042
03:17:37,000 --> 03:17:40,000
*Calling her by her first name feels so intimate.*

3043
03:17:40,000 --> 03:17:46,000
*Am I really going to get used to calling her that, or am I going to be embarrassed every time?*

3044
03:17:46,000 --> 03:17:49,000
*It's almost scary how giddy we both are.*

3045
03:17:49,000 --> 03:17:55,000
*Honestly, this burger could taste like cardboard and I'd never know. I'm that far gone.*

3046
03:17:55,000 --> 03:17:58,000
Kakeru: "What was the thing you wanted?"

3047
03:17:58,000 --> 03:18:01,000
Miyako: "Um, let's see, where was it..."

3048
03:18:01,000 --> 03:18:10,000
*We finish our late lunch and head to Round Two, the very place we went yesterday with our classmates but couldn't enjoy at all.*

3049
03:18:10,000 --> 03:18:20,000
*It seems like Miyako doesn't go to places like this often. Her eyes are darting everywhere, taking in all the sights and sounds, a big grin on her face.*

3050
03:18:20,000 --> 03:18:23,000
Miyako: "Oh, here it is. See, the dome lamp."

3051
03:18:23,000 --> 03:18:32,000
Kakeru: "Wow, didn't know they had dome lamps in the crane games... Huh? Oh, wait, I recognize this thing. Miyako, you play that game?"

3052
03:18:32,000 --> 03:18:33,000
Miyako: "What game?"

3053
03:18:33,000 --> 03:18:42,000
Kakeru: "Oh, guess not. This is a monster from that game Dragon Fantasy. Well, maybe it's more like a mascot? It's called a Tequilar."

3054
03:18:42,000 --> 03:18:45,000
Miyako: "Oh, it's from a game. How cute."

3055
03:18:45,000 --> 03:18:50,000
Kakeru: "Sora used to play that series, but I wonder if she still does."

3056
03:18:50,000 --> 03:18:54,000
Miyako: "Then let's make it a present for Sora-chan."

3057
03:18:54,000 --> 03:18:59,000
Kakeru: "Naw, she can get her own. The one we're getting is for you, Miyako."

3058
03:18:59,000 --> 03:19:02,000
Miyako: "Haha, thank you. Okay, here we go..."

3059
03:19:02,000 --> 03:19:06,000
Kakeru: "Whoa, hold it. Why are you getting your wallet out?"

3060
03:19:06,000 --> 03:19:07,000
Miyako: "Huh? But..."

3061
03:19:07,000 --> 03:19:09,000
Kakeru: "No, I insist."

3062
03:19:09,000 --> 03:19:15,000
*I see how apologetic Miyako looks, but I throw my money in before she has a chance to protest.*

3063
03:19:15,000 --> 03:19:20,000
Miyako: "Y-You just dropped in five-hundred yen like it was nothing!"

3064
03:19:20,000 --> 03:19:25,000
Kakeru: "You get a bonus turn if you put in five-hundred. I'll make it count."

3065
03:19:25,000 --> 03:19:27,000
Miyako: "Are you good at this game?"

3066
03:19:27,000 --> 03:19:29,000
Kakeru: "Stand back and watch."

3067
03:19:29,000 --> 03:19:33,000
*I grin triumphantly, push the button, and control the crane.*

3068
03:19:33,000 --> 03:19:35,000
Kakeru: "Hmm... There."

3069
03:19:35,000 --> 03:19:38,000
Miyako: "Huh? That's where you wanted it?"

3070
03:19:38,000 --> 03:19:41,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. I'm going to push it with the arm."

3071
03:19:41,000 --> 03:19:46,000
Miyako: "Oh, oh, I see! You're going to push it into the hole, huh?"

3072
03:19:46,000 --> 03:19:47,000
Kakeru: "You got it."

3073
03:19:47,000 --> 03:19:52,000
Miyako: "Oh, look, it's leaning...! Oh. You only nudged it a little."

3074
03:19:52,000 --> 03:19:58,000
Kakeru: "Guess I didn't quite nail the positioning. Don't worry, I've got the hang of it now."

3075
03:19:58,000 --> 03:20:00,000
*I begin my second attempt.*

3076
03:20:00,000 --> 03:20:04,000
*This time, I definitely positioned the claw better, but...*

3077
03:20:04,000 --> 03:20:05,000
Miyako: "Oh, oh, oh!"

3078
03:20:05,000 --> 03:20:06,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3079
03:20:06,000 --> 03:20:07,000
Miyako: "Aww..."

3080
03:20:07,000 --> 03:20:08,000
*Another failure.*

3081
03:20:08,000 --> 03:20:12,000
*In fact, the prize isn't even budging when the arm hits it.*

3082
03:20:12,000 --> 03:20:16,000
Kakeru: "Hmm, I see. So the arm isn't strong enough, eh?"

3083
03:20:16,000 --> 03:20:21,000
*I offer a composed and level-headed analysis, while on the inside I freak out.*

3084
03:20:21,000 --> 03:20:23,000
*Shit... I don't think I can get it.*

3085
03:20:23,000 --> 03:20:25,000
Miyako: "It certainly is difficult."

3086
03:20:25,000 --> 03:20:29,000
Kakeru: "I've still got four turns left. Leave it to me."

3087
03:20:29,000 --> 03:20:31,000
*I am clearly on tilt.*

3088
03:20:31,000 --> 03:20:44,000
*I don't have a chance in hell of getting this crane to do what I want. For that matter, I don't even have a strategy to get the damn thing, even if I could put the claw where I wanted it.*

3089
03:20:44,000 --> 03:20:45,000
Kakeru: "..."

3090
03:20:45,000 --> 03:20:46,000
Kakeru: "...?"

3091
03:20:46,000 --> 03:20:47,000
Kakeru: "...!"

3092
03:20:47,000 --> 03:20:48,000
Kakeru: "Mmm."

3093
03:20:48,000 --> 03:20:54,000
*In the blink of an eye, I've effectively flushed five hundred yen down the toilet.*

3094
03:20:54,000 --> 03:20:55,000
*...*

3095
03:20:55,000 --> 03:20:57,000
*You can't be serious.*

3096
03:20:57,000 --> 03:20:59,000
*What am I gonna say to her?!*

3097
03:20:59,000 --> 03:21:05,000
Miyako: "It's just too difficult. Thank you for trying, Kakeru-kun. It was fun to watch."

3098
03:21:05,000 --> 03:21:06,000
Kakeru: "..."

3099
03:21:06,000 --> 03:21:12,000
Miyako: "So, what are we going to do next? I know, why don't we play a game togeth..."

3100
03:21:12,000 --> 03:21:15,000
Kakeru: "No. Stop right there, Miyako."

3101
03:21:15,000 --> 03:21:16,000
Miyako: "Hm?"

3102
03:21:16,000 --> 03:21:20,000
Kakeru: "I have another five-hundred yen coin in my wallet!"

3103
03:21:20,000 --> 03:21:22,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun, you can't!"

3104
03:21:22,000 --> 03:21:23,000
*Miyako grabs my arm.*

3105
03:21:23,000 --> 03:21:30,000
Miyako: "Y-You already used five-hundred! A th-thousand would be too much. I don't want it that badly!"

3106
03:21:30,000 --> 03:21:40,000
Kakeru: "Don't worry. I've got the hang of it now. Besides, it's fully expected that you have to spend at least a thousand yen on games like this!"

3107
03:21:40,000 --> 03:21:43,000
Miyako: "What do you mean 'at least?!'"

3108
03:21:43,000 --> 03:21:56,000
Kakeru: "See, the way these crane games work is, there's a window of time where the arm's grip gets stronger. So if I gave up now, it'd be a total waste of the five-hundred yen I already spent."

3109
03:21:56,000 --> 03:21:57,000
Miyako: "R-Really?"

3110
03:21:57,000 --> 03:22:00,000
Kakeru: "Yeah! I got it this time for sure."

3111
03:22:00,000 --> 03:22:01,000
Miyako: "..."

3112
03:22:01,000 --> 03:22:05,000
*With a worried and dubious look, Miyako releases my arm.*

3113
03:22:05,000 --> 03:22:12,000
*I extend my released arm to the cabinet, the five-hundred yen coin in my fingers, and drop it in the slot.*

3114
03:22:12,000 --> 03:22:13,000
Miyako: "Hwaaah..."

3115
03:22:13,000 --> 03:22:19,000
*The moment the machine swallows up my money, Miyako lets out an indescribable gasp.*

3116
03:22:19,000 --> 03:22:26,000
*A thousand yen must be a lot of money to Miyako. Actually, it's a pretty big hit to my wallet, too...*

3117
03:22:26,000 --> 03:22:29,000
*But I'll do it for my beloved girlfriend!*

3118
03:22:29,000 --> 03:22:32,000
*I swear, that dome lamp will be mine!*

3119
03:22:32,000 --> 03:22:33,000
Kakeru: "Here goes!"

3120
03:22:33,000 --> 03:22:34,000
Miyako: "Y-Yeah!"

3121
03:22:34,000 --> 03:22:37,000
*I psyche myself up, glaring at the dome lamp.*

3122
03:22:37,000 --> 03:22:40,000
*And so begins a battle I can't afford to lose!*

3123
03:22:40,000 --> 03:22:41,000
Kakeru: "..."

3124
03:22:41,000 --> 03:22:42,000
Miyako: "..."

3125
03:22:42,000 --> 03:22:43,000
Kakeru: "......"

3126
03:22:43,000 --> 03:22:44,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun."

3127
03:22:44,000 --> 03:22:45,000
Kakeru: "Okay..."

3128
03:22:45,000 --> 03:22:46,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun?"

3129
03:22:46,000 --> 03:22:48,000
Kakeru: "One more time!"

3130
03:22:48,000 --> 03:22:50,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun, no!"

3131
03:22:50,000 --> 03:22:52,000
Kakeru: "Let go! Let me go!"

3132
03:22:52,000 --> 03:22:59,000
Miyako: "No, no, you can't! You've already spent two-thousand yen! You can't sink any more money into this!"

3133
03:22:59,000 --> 03:23:07,000
Kakeru: "D-Don't try and stop me! My pride is on the line here! You can't make me quit after I've come this far!"

3134
03:23:07,000 --> 03:23:14,000
Miyako: "I-I'm sorry. This only happened because I said I wanted it. You don't have to do this! It's okay!"

3135
03:23:14,000 --> 03:23:19,000
Kakeru: "One-hundred yen more! Just one final hundred yen and I'll stop!"

3136
03:23:19,000 --> 03:23:26,000
Miyako: "You said you were going to stop after the last round, just before you went to the change machine!"

3137
03:23:26,000 --> 03:23:32,000
Kakeru: "I can do it! I finally understand how it works! I can do it on my next try!"

3138
03:23:32,000 --> 03:23:37,000
Miyako: "You said that last time, too! Enough already! You have to stop!"

3139
03:23:37,000 --> 03:23:41,000
Kakeru: "I've got it, seriously! Just you wait and see!"

3140
03:23:41,000 --> 03:23:43,000
Miyako: "Oh no, oh nooooo!"

3141
03:23:43,000 --> 03:23:47,000
*I shake off Miyako's arm and jam in another hundred yen.*

3142
03:23:47,000 --> 03:23:49,000
Miyako: "Ahh... Unbelievable..."

3143
03:23:49,000 --> 03:23:54,000
Kakeru: "This is my last hurrah! The final, ultimate, last one, I swear!"

3144
03:23:54,000 --> 03:24:00,000
*I try not to look at Miyako's disappointed expression, focusing on controlling the crane.*

3145
03:24:00,000 --> 03:24:03,000
*I've shifted it a lot. Just one more push!*

3146
03:24:03,000 --> 03:24:09,000
*Just a tiny bit more, another inch... No! If I can shift it just a fraction of an inch...!*

3147
03:24:09,000 --> 03:24:13,000
Kakeru: "Gah, dammit, I screwed up! Too much to the right!"

3148
03:24:13,000 --> 03:24:15,000
Miyako: "W-Wait, maybe..."

3149
03:24:15,000 --> 03:24:17,000
Kakeru: "Y-Yeah, I think so!"

3150
03:24:17,000 --> 03:24:19,000
Miyako: "Your voice is trembling."

3151
03:24:19,000 --> 03:24:24,000
Kakeru: "No, I mean it! I can do it! This time for sure, I can do this!"

3152
03:24:24,000 --> 03:24:27,000
*I push the button, half in desperation.*

3153
03:24:27,000 --> 03:24:30,000
*The arm position in place, it slowly descends...*

3154
03:24:30,000 --> 03:24:40,000
*My rage wants me to punch through the glass in the machine and tear this weak-ass claw in half, but as though unaware of my ire, the claw opens.*

3155
03:24:40,000 --> 03:24:41,000
Kakeru: "Oh."

3156
03:24:41,000 --> 03:24:42,000
Miyako: "Oh."

3157
03:24:42,000 --> 03:24:51,000
*The box moves to the side just a smidge, tilts precariously, and falls in the hole, accompanied by a clunk from the dispenser slot.*

3158
03:24:51,000 --> 03:24:52,000
Kakeru: "..."

3159
03:24:52,000 --> 03:24:53,000
Miyako: "..."

3160
03:24:53,000 --> 03:24:54,000
Kakeru: "I got it."

3161
03:24:54,000 --> 03:24:55,000
Miyako: "You got it?"

3162
03:24:55,000 --> 03:24:56,000
Kakeru: "I got it!"

3163
03:24:56,000 --> 03:24:57,000
Miyako: "Hooray!"

3164
03:24:57,000 --> 03:25:01,000
Kakeru: "Quick, quick, Miyako! Pull it out of the slot!"

3165
03:25:01,000 --> 03:25:02,000
Miyako: "O-Okay!"

3166
03:25:02,000 --> 03:25:05,000
*We're both bouncing off the walls with excitement.*

3167
03:25:05,000 --> 03:25:09,000
*Miyako kneels down, sticking her hand into the dispenser slot.*

3168
03:25:09,000 --> 03:25:15,000
*She pulls out the little dome lamp-like creature that I spent my life's savings on liberating.*

3169
03:25:15,000 --> 03:25:19,000
Miyako: "Look, it's here! It's really here, Kakeru-kun!"

3170
03:25:19,000 --> 03:25:21,000
Kakeru: "I did it! I got it!"

3171
03:25:21,000 --> 03:25:23,000
Miyako: "This is amazing! Thank you!"

3172
03:25:23,000 --> 03:25:27,000
Kakeru: "Like I said, just leave it to me! All in a day's work!"

3173
03:25:27,000 --> 03:25:32,000
Miyako: "You looked like you were going to break down crying near the end!"

3174
03:25:32,000 --> 03:25:33,000
Kakeru: "..."

3175
03:25:33,000 --> 03:25:37,000
*Miyako's unexpectedly savage take-down shuts me up in a hurry.*

3176
03:25:37,000 --> 03:25:43,000
*Well. She does have a point. If that last try hadn't done it, I would've bawled my eyes out.*

3177
03:25:43,000 --> 03:25:49,000
Kakeru: "I fought the good fight out there. I hope you take care of it... That'd make me happy."

3178
03:25:49,000 --> 03:25:55,000
Miyako: "Haha, I will. Thank you, I'm so happy to have this. I'll put it in my room."

3179
03:25:55,000 --> 03:25:57,000
Kakeru: "Th-That's great."

3180
03:25:57,000 --> 03:25:58,000
Miyako: "That said..."

3181
03:25:58,000 --> 03:26:00,000
*Miyako's sweet smile turns stern.*

3182
03:26:00,000 --> 03:26:08,000
Miyako: "I don't want you to engage in any reckless spending like this going forward, you understand? It gives me the willies."

3183
03:26:08,000 --> 03:26:12,000
Kakeru: "I'm sorry. My enthusiasm got the better of me."

3184
03:26:12,000 --> 03:26:20,000
Miyako: "Haha, I'm sorry I put you through that. Thank you, though. I was so glad to see you working so hard for my sake."

3185
03:26:20,000 --> 03:26:25,000
Miyako: "This lamp is my treasure. I'll care for it for the rest of my life."

3186
03:26:25,000 --> 03:26:28,000
*She smiles, hugging the Tequilar's box tight.*

3187
03:26:28,000 --> 03:26:34,000
*I think about teasing her for exaggerating, but I can't bring myself to do it. She's too cute.*

3188
03:26:34,000 --> 03:26:43,000
*And that thought makes me blush, at which I struggle to hide my embarrassment, as always. I turn away, looking off into space.*

3189
03:26:43,000 --> 03:26:46,000
Miyako: "I wish I could repay the favor."

3190
03:26:46,000 --> 03:26:48,000
Kakeru: "No, don't even think that."

3191
03:26:48,000 --> 03:26:49,000
Miyako: "Huh?"

3192
03:26:49,000 --> 03:26:53,000
Kakeru: "I'm your boyfriend. There's nothing to repay."

3193
03:26:53,000 --> 03:27:00,000
Kakeru: "I like to see you happy, so I wanted to get you something. Seeing you smile is all I need."

3194
03:27:00,000 --> 03:27:02,000
Miyako: "Haha. Okay, thank you."

3195
03:27:02,000 --> 03:27:08,000
Kakeru: "Oh, hey, they have bags to hold these. It won't fit in your purse, right?"

3196
03:27:08,000 --> 03:27:11,000
Miyako: "Oh, no. How much are the bags?"

3197
03:27:11,000 --> 03:27:12,000
Kakeru: "Free."

3198
03:27:12,000 --> 03:27:14,000
Miyako: "Really? Wow, what a deal!"

3199
03:27:14,000 --> 03:27:17,000
Kakeru: "You can only get one, though."

3200
03:27:17,000 --> 03:27:24,000
Miyako: "Hey, don't be rude. Just because I'm frugal doesn't mean I'd get greedy and take a bunch."

3201
03:27:24,000 --> 03:27:26,000
Kakeru: "Yes, ma'am. My apologies."

3202
03:27:26,000 --> 03:27:31,000
Miyako: "Haha. To tell the truth, I was inclined to take a few home."

3203
03:27:31,000 --> 03:27:34,000
Kakeru: "Was there anything else you wanted?"

3204
03:27:34,000 --> 03:27:40,000
Miyako: "No, no. If I had to watch you spend another two-thousand yen, I'd have a heart attack."

3205
03:27:40,000 --> 03:27:41,000
Kakeru: "Good point."

3206
03:27:41,000 --> 03:27:47,000
Miyako: "Plus, if we ARE going to spend that much, we should do something we can enjoy together."

3207
03:27:47,000 --> 03:27:51,000
Kakeru: "Good point, let's go find something we can do together."

3208
03:27:51,000 --> 03:27:52,000
Miyako: "Okay!"

3209
03:27:52,000 --> 03:27:55,000
*We end up spending about two hours at Round Two.*

3210
03:27:55,000 --> 03:28:01,000
*By the time we get out, the sun is setting, the sky above us turning from orange to red.*

3211
03:28:01,000 --> 03:28:07,000
*While I'd like to spend more time here, I decided that was probably enough for today.*

3212
03:28:07,000 --> 03:28:10,000
Miyako: "It's a bit early to get dinner, isn't it?"

3213
03:28:10,000 --> 03:28:12,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, guess so."

3214
03:28:12,000 --> 03:28:15,000
Miyako: "Want to go somewhere to kill some time?"

3215
03:28:15,000 --> 03:28:17,000
Kakeru: "Naw, let's call it a day."

3216
03:28:17,000 --> 03:28:18,000
Miyako: "Oh... Okay."

3217
03:28:18,000 --> 03:28:20,000
*She looks a little sad.*

3218
03:28:20,000 --> 03:28:25,000
*A little stab of pain and a little rush of joy hit me at the same time.*

3219
03:28:25,000 --> 03:28:29,000
*But I have my reasons for wanting to end our date early.*

3220
03:28:29,000 --> 03:28:32,000
Kakeru: "I'd be worried, if it got too late."

3221
03:28:32,000 --> 03:28:34,000
Miyako: "Huh? About what?"

3222
03:28:34,000 --> 03:28:43,000
Kakeru: "I should have said something earlier, but I'm just, well, not sure how I feel about letting you go home alone at night..."

3223
03:28:43,000 --> 03:28:44,000
Miyako: "Ohhh."

3224
03:28:44,000 --> 03:28:46,000
*Miyako gives me a knowing smile.*

3225
03:28:46,000 --> 03:28:52,000
Miyako: "Thank you for worrying about me, haha, but I'm on a bike, so I'll be okay."

3226
03:28:52,000 --> 03:28:59,000
Kakeru: "I mean, I know, but whenever it's possible for you to head home before dark, I'd rather you did that."

3227
03:28:59,000 --> 03:29:02,000
Miyako: "Okay. Alright then, I'll see you."

3228
03:29:02,000 --> 03:29:07,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, see ya... Oh, wait, we have to go pick up your bike."

3229
03:29:07,000 --> 03:29:09,000
Miyako: "Oh, you're right!"

3230
03:29:09,000 --> 03:29:13,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah! Miyako, would you let me carry your lamp?"

3231
03:29:13,000 --> 03:29:15,000
Miyako: "No, I've got it."

3232
03:29:15,000 --> 03:29:17,000
Kakeru: "Don't be modest now."

3233
03:29:17,000 --> 03:29:18,000
Miyako: "Oh."

3234
03:29:18,000 --> 03:29:24,000
*Despite her trying to demur, I somewhat insistently snatch the bag away from her.*

3235
03:29:24,000 --> 03:29:27,000
Miyako: "I really was fine, you know."

3236
03:29:27,000 --> 03:29:34,000
Kakeru: "I know. But, see, you have to carry your own bag. This way, you'll have a hand free, right?"

3237
03:29:34,000 --> 03:29:35,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3238
03:29:35,000 --> 03:29:36,000
Kakeru: "So..."

3239
03:29:36,000 --> 03:29:40,000
*With that stellar explanation, I stick out my right hand.*

3240
03:29:40,000 --> 03:29:42,000
*Miyako timidly takes it.*

3241
03:29:42,000 --> 03:29:45,000
*I wrap my rough fingers around her smooth hand.*

3242
03:29:45,000 --> 03:29:48,000
Kakeru: "I'll walk you back to Nine Ball."

3243
03:29:48,000 --> 03:29:50,000
Miyako: "Yes, thank you."

3244
03:29:50,000 --> 03:29:52,000
*Her voice is small and bashful now.*

3245
03:29:52,000 --> 03:29:57,000
*It may be just the sunset, but Miyako sure looks like she's blushing.*

3246
03:29:57,000 --> 03:29:59,000
*I can't help but worry about her.*

3247
03:29:59,000 --> 03:30:02,000
*There's a murderer on the loose in our city.*

3248
03:30:02,000 --> 03:30:06,000
*But today has undoubtedly been the happiest day in my life.*

3249
03:30:06,000 --> 03:30:14,000
*And I have a feeling that I'll be able to say that again tomorrow, and then again the next day, and the next...*

3250
03:30:14,000 --> 03:30:19,000
*A gentle warmth fills my heart at the thought of our future together.*

3251
03:30:19,000 --> 03:30:21,000
*I fritter away my weekend.*

3252
03:30:21,000 --> 03:30:30,000
*I actually wanted to go on another date today, but I get the feeling that asking her out every day would be pushing it, so I hold back.*

3253
03:30:30,000 --> 03:30:36,000
*Besides, she seems to have a shift starting in the early evening and going until night.*

3254
03:30:36,000 --> 03:30:41,000
*I loaf around my room, still basking in the afterglow of yesterday's date.*

3255
03:30:41,000 --> 03:30:43,000
*I'm Miyako's boyfriend.*

3256
03:30:43,000 --> 03:30:47,000
*Yesterday's date was only the beginning of our relationship.*

3257
03:30:47,000 --> 03:30:50,000
*Because in addition to dates, there's also...*

3258
03:30:50,000 --> 03:30:57,000
*And with that thought, I sink down under the waves of giddiness again. Man, how am I so far gone?*

3259
03:30:57,000 --> 03:31:03,000
*I'm well aware I need to chill out, but I just can't help it. I can't fight my feelings.*

3260
03:31:03,000 --> 03:31:04,000
Kakeru: "Hmm?"

3261
03:31:04,000 --> 03:31:09,000
*As I'm still lying around grinning like a dope, the doorbell rings.*

3262
03:31:09,000 --> 03:31:11,000
*Who could it be at this hour?*

3263
03:31:11,000 --> 03:31:14,000
*Meh, probably just a door-to-door salesman.*

3264
03:31:14,000 --> 03:31:23,000
*I consider ignoring it, but once the thought crosses my mind that it might be Miyako, I'm pulled to the door like a moth to a flame.*

3265
03:31:23,000 --> 03:31:24,000
Kakeru: "Coming!"

3266
03:31:24,000 --> 03:31:28,000
*I respond while getting up and walking to the entrance.*

3267
03:31:28,000 --> 03:31:32,000
*I open the door with the chain still on, and I find...*

3268
03:31:32,000 --> 03:31:33,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

3269
03:31:33,000 --> 03:31:37,000
Miyako: "Good evening. I'm sorry for the late visit."

3270
03:31:37,000 --> 03:31:40,000
*I didn't seriously think it'd be her.*

3271
03:31:40,000 --> 03:31:48,000
*I ask Miyako to wait a moment so I can close the door and undo the chain, then I open the door again to show her inside.*

3272
03:31:48,000 --> 03:31:50,000
Miyako: "Thanks for having me."

3273
03:31:50,000 --> 03:31:54,000
Kakeru: "What's up? I didn't expect to see you here this late."

3274
03:31:54,000 --> 03:31:55,000
Miyako: "Um..."

3275
03:31:55,000 --> 03:31:59,000
*She hesitantly shows me the little box she's carrying.*

3276
03:31:59,000 --> 03:32:03,000
Miyako: "Grandfather told me to bring you our leftover cake."

3277
03:32:03,000 --> 03:32:04,000
Kakeru: "What?"

3278
03:32:04,000 --> 03:32:07,000
Miyako: "Would you like it? It's on the house."

3279
03:32:07,000 --> 03:32:12,000
Kakeru: "Oh, uh, thank you. You went through all the effort to bring this to me?"

3280
03:32:12,000 --> 03:32:16,000
Miyako: "It might not last until tomorrow. Where's Sora-chan?"

3281
03:32:16,000 --> 03:32:18,000
Kakeru: "Oh, she's not here today."

3282
03:32:18,000 --> 03:32:22,000
Miyako: "I see. The thing is, I actually have two slices..."

3283
03:32:22,000 --> 03:32:23,000
Kakeru: "Oh..."

3284
03:32:23,000 --> 03:32:24,000
Kakeru: "..."

3285
03:32:24,000 --> 03:32:27,000
Kakeru: "Did you tell your grandfather about us?"

3286
03:32:27,000 --> 03:32:31,000
Miyako: "No, but... he might have already caught on."

3287
03:32:31,000 --> 03:32:34,000
*She smiles wryly, her cheeks flushed.*

3288
03:32:34,000 --> 03:32:38,000
*He probably caught on from the way Miyako's been acting.*

3289
03:32:38,000 --> 03:32:42,000
*Going to Nine Ball is gonna be tougher from now on...*

3290
03:32:42,000 --> 03:32:46,000
Kakeru: "It's getting late. Are you okay? No curfew?"

3291
03:32:46,000 --> 03:32:48,000
Miyako: "Oh, yes, it's fine."

3292
03:32:48,000 --> 03:32:53,000
Kakeru: "Then, would you like to have a seat and we can eat them together?"

3293
03:32:53,000 --> 03:32:56,000
Miyako: "Haha, I was waiting for you to say that."

3294
03:32:56,000 --> 03:33:01,000
Kakeru: "I figured. I'll get us some plates and something to drink."

3295
03:33:01,000 --> 03:33:03,000
Miyako: "Oh, I can do that."

3296
03:33:03,000 --> 03:33:05,000
Kakeru: "I told you, I've got it."

3297
03:33:05,000 --> 03:33:06,000
Miyako: "Allow me."

3298
03:33:06,000 --> 03:33:11,000
*We start bickering over it, for some reason, as we set out the spread.*

3299
03:33:11,000 --> 03:33:14,000
*I carry the cake box to the table and open it up.*

3300
03:33:14,000 --> 03:33:18,000
*There's a slice of cheesecake and a slice of chocolate cake.*

3301
03:33:18,000 --> 03:33:20,000
Kakeru: "Which do you want?"

3302
03:33:20,000 --> 03:33:22,000
Miyako: "You pick first, Kakeru-kun."

3303
03:33:22,000 --> 03:33:23,000
Kakeru: "Alright..."

3304
03:33:23,000 --> 03:33:27,000
*I pick the cheesecake; Miyako takes the chocolate one.*

3305
03:33:27,000 --> 03:33:31,000
*I put my hands together in thanks, and then I pick up my fork.*

3306
03:33:31,000 --> 03:33:35,000
Miyako: "I'm really sorry for coming out of the blue."

3307
03:33:35,000 --> 03:33:42,000
Kakeru: "I'd never buy a cake on my own, so it's a pleasant surprise. Plus... I didn't get to see you today."

3308
03:33:42,000 --> 03:33:49,000
Miyako: "Haha, thank you. I wanted to see you too. I think Grandfather did this to make an excuse for me."

3309
03:33:49,000 --> 03:33:50,000
Kakeru: "I-I see..."

3310
03:33:50,000 --> 03:33:57,000
Miyako: "Y-Yeah... Oh, d-do you want half?" "Oh, no, I couldn't. Oh, how about we split them both?"

3311
03:33:57,000 --> 03:33:59,000
Kakeru: 「ぁ、いや、ぁ~、じゃあ、半分ずつ食べようか」

3312
03:33:59,000 --> 03:34:01,000
Miyako: "S-Sure, good idea."

3313
03:34:01,000 --> 03:34:04,000
*Unreasonably flustered, we dig in to our cake.*

3314
03:34:04,000 --> 03:34:11,000
*Now that I think of it, this is the first time we've been alone in my apartment since we started dating.*

3315
03:34:11,000 --> 03:34:12,000
*...*

3316
03:34:12,000 --> 03:34:13,000
*Uh-oh.*

3317
03:34:13,000 --> 03:34:16,000
*I can't stop the flood of impure thoughts!*

3318
03:34:16,000 --> 03:34:17,000
Miyako: "..."

3319
03:34:17,000 --> 03:34:21,000
*Miyako's breathing is soft and ordinary, and yet...*

3320
03:34:21,000 --> 03:34:25,000
*I can hear it so vividly that it's making my heart race.*

3321
03:34:25,000 --> 03:34:26,000
Miyako: "..."

3322
03:34:26,000 --> 03:34:27,000
*We make eye contact.*

3323
03:34:27,000 --> 03:34:30,000
*Maybe I'm barking up the wrong tree here...*

3324
03:34:30,000 --> 03:34:35,000
*But I have a feeling Miyako understands what's on my mind right now.*

3325
03:34:35,000 --> 03:34:37,000
*Can I really do this?*

3326
03:34:37,000 --> 03:34:41,000
*Maybe I could gently slip my arm around her shoulders.*

3327
03:34:41,000 --> 03:34:45,000
*Or I could say she's got some frosting on her lips?*

3328
03:34:45,000 --> 03:34:47,000
*I slowly close the distance...*

3329
03:34:47,000 --> 03:34:49,000
*I'm going in for the kiss...*

3330
03:34:49,000 --> 03:34:51,000
Sophitia: "Hello there!"

3331
03:34:51,000 --> 03:34:52,000
Kakeru: "..."

3332
03:34:52,000 --> 03:34:53,000
*You sack of shit.*

3333
03:34:53,000 --> 03:34:56,000
Sophitia: "What are you glaring at me for?"

3334
03:34:56,000 --> 03:34:58,000
Kakeru: "No particular reason."

3335
03:34:58,000 --> 03:35:10,000
*You leave us alone all this time, only to pop up now? Could you have picked a worse time? No, no, I am above such petty thoughts... No, actually, I'm not. Damn this plushie.*

3336
03:35:10,000 --> 03:35:13,000
Miyako: "Sophie-san, i-it's nice to see you again."

3337
03:35:13,000 --> 03:35:20,000
Sophitia: "Yes, nice to see you too. Sorry to interrupt while you were enjoying each other's company."

3338
03:35:20,000 --> 03:35:21,000
Kakeru: "..."

3339
03:35:21,000 --> 03:35:24,000
Sophitia: "Seriously, why are you glaring at me?"

3340
03:35:24,000 --> 03:35:27,000
Kakeru: "Don't know what you're talking about."

3341
03:35:27,000 --> 03:35:30,000
*Sophie gives me a sidelong glance and harrumphs.*

3342
03:35:30,000 --> 03:35:34,000
*Dammit. This punk is definitely interrupting us on purpose.*

3343
03:35:34,000 --> 03:35:39,000
Kakeru: "Get on with it. Why are you here? You haven't showed up in a while."

3344
03:35:39,000 --> 03:35:42,000
Sophitia: "I have been assessing the situation."

3345
03:35:42,000 --> 03:35:46,000
Miyako: "Oh. I'm sorry, we haven't made much progress."

3346
03:35:46,000 --> 03:35:51,000
Sophitia: "Indeed, the thought of scolding you did cross my mind several times."

3347
03:35:51,000 --> 03:35:52,000
Sophitia: "..."

3348
03:35:52,000 --> 03:35:54,000
Miyako: "Hm? What's wrong?"

3349
03:35:54,000 --> 03:35:58,000
Sophitia: "I am glad that the Miyako of this branch is safe."

3350
03:35:58,000 --> 03:36:00,000
Miyako: "Safe? From what?"

3351
03:36:00,000 --> 03:36:03,000
Kakeru: "What are you even talking about?"

3352
03:36:03,000 --> 03:36:07,000
Sophitia: "I am talking about the flow of events in this world."

3353
03:36:07,000 --> 03:36:09,000
Kakeru: "In simpler terms, please?"

3354
03:36:09,000 --> 03:36:12,000
Sophitia: "You really are a primitive."

3355
03:36:12,000 --> 03:36:14,000
*She gives an affected sigh.*

3356
03:36:14,000 --> 03:36:17,000
*After a long pause, Sophie elaborates.*

3357
03:36:17,000 --> 03:36:29,000
Sophitia: "The universe is comprised of many overlapping possible worlds. This moment, where the two of you share a meal, is only taking place along one timeline among a multitude."

3358
03:36:29,000 --> 03:36:35,000
Sophitia: "Worlds split into as many branches as there are possibilities. Understand?"

3359
03:36:35,000 --> 03:36:39,000
Miyako: "Oh... Are you talking about parallel worlds?"

3360
03:36:39,000 --> 03:36:46,000
Sophitia: "Yes. Miyako, you really are quite smart. I refer to the individual worlds as branches."

3361
03:36:46,000 --> 03:36:50,000
Kakeru: "And so what? What are you trying to tell us?"

3362
03:36:50,000 --> 03:36:59,000
Sophitia: "I have the power to investigate the many branching worlds and their possibilities, with the power of the Artifact World's Eye."

3363
03:36:59,000 --> 03:37:04,000
Miyako: "This World's Eye lets you figure out what happens in parallel worlds?"

3364
03:37:04,000 --> 03:37:17,000
Sophitia: "Indeed, although I can only learn what I experience in any given branch. Today, I've come here specifically to tell you two about an incident that's occurred in a different branch."

3365
03:37:17,000 --> 03:37:21,000
Kakeru: "You came here to make sure Miyako is safe, didn't you?"

3366
03:37:21,000 --> 03:37:23,000
Sophitia: "How oddly astute of you."

3367
03:37:23,000 --> 03:37:26,000
Kakeru: "Did something happen to Miyako?"

3368
03:37:26,000 --> 03:37:29,000
Sophitia: "That would be an understatement. Miyako?"

3369
03:37:29,000 --> 03:37:30,000
Miyako: "Y-Yes?"

3370
03:37:30,000 --> 03:37:37,000
Sophitia: "Two days ago—I believe you call it Friday in this world—the Evil Eye's User murdered you."

3371
03:37:37,000 --> 03:37:38,000
Miyako: "...What?"

3372
03:37:38,000 --> 03:37:40,000
*Miyako blinks, speechless.*

3373
03:37:40,000 --> 03:37:43,000
*My thoughts freeze, trying to process the idea.*

3374
03:37:43,000 --> 03:37:45,000
*Miyako... was murdered?*

3375
03:37:45,000 --> 03:37:48,000
Kakeru: "H-Hold up! What do you mean?!"

3376
03:37:48,000 --> 03:37:53,000
Sophitia: "Calm down, you noisy brat. I'll explain it to you from the top."

3377
03:37:53,000 --> 03:37:56,000
*After another sigh, Sophie continues.*

3378
03:37:56,000 --> 03:38:05,000
*She explains that, in another branching world, we didn't end up getting together, and instead we had a massive falling out with one another.*

3379
03:38:05,000 --> 03:38:15,000
*Things got worse, as Miyako started using her powers on random people—probably focusing on students at our school—so she could read their memories.*

3380
03:38:15,000 --> 03:38:24,000
*In the end, she did successfully identify the Evil Eye's User, but after doing so, she rushed off alone to make contact with them.*

3381
03:38:24,000 --> 03:38:26,000
*単独で先走り、魔眼のユーザーと接触したらしいこと。*

3382
03:38:26,000 --> 03:38:27,000
*And when she did...*

3383
03:38:27,000 --> 03:38:35,000
Sophitia: "By the time Kakeru found you, Miyako, he was already too late. You had been murdered by the time he came."

3384
03:38:35,000 --> 03:38:36,000
Kakeru: "..."

3385
03:38:36,000 --> 03:38:37,000
Miyako: "..."

3386
03:38:37,000 --> 03:38:38,000
*We sit speechless.*

3387
03:38:38,000 --> 03:38:40,000
*That's all we can do.*

3388
03:38:40,000 --> 03:38:42,000
*Is this some bad joke?*

3389
03:38:42,000 --> 03:38:46,000
*But Sophie's story is far too detailed to just laugh off.*

3390
03:38:46,000 --> 03:38:52,000
*What's more, she wouldn't have any reason to play a prank like this on us in the first place.*

3391
03:38:52,000 --> 03:38:55,000
*So that means... she's telling the truth.*

3392
03:38:55,000 --> 03:38:56,000
*In another world...*

3393
03:38:56,000 --> 03:38:58,000
*Miyako ended up the third victim.*

3394
03:38:58,000 --> 03:39:04,000
Sophitia: "That is all I have for you. Be careful. The Evil Eye's User is growing."

3395
03:39:04,000 --> 03:39:07,000
Kakeru: "So, their powers are getting stronger..."

3396
03:39:07,000 --> 03:39:19,000
Sophitia: "In the beginning, they could only petrify people's skin, since the first two statues were not petrified all the way through, and even that apparently only piece by piece."

3397
03:39:19,000 --> 03:39:29,000
Sophitia: "However, you were turned completely to stone, from your skin to your guts. The Evil Eye's User is unlocking the full power of their Artifact."

3398
03:39:29,000 --> 03:39:32,000
Miyako: "I was turned completely to stone..."

3399
03:39:32,000 --> 03:39:39,000
Sophitia: "Yes, it was quite a sight. Not only were you turned to stone, but you also fell and shattered."

3400
03:39:39,000 --> 03:39:41,000
Miyako: "I... shattered...?"

3401
03:39:41,000 --> 03:39:43,000
Kakeru: "Cut it out, Sophie!"

3402
03:39:43,000 --> 03:39:54,000
Sophitia: "Cut what out? I'm simply telling her what I saw. I understand it can be shocking to learn the details of your own death, but she needs to hear this..."

3403
03:39:54,000 --> 03:39:58,000
Sophitia: "So that she does not die in this branch as well."

3404
03:39:58,000 --> 03:39:59,000
Miyako: "..."

3405
03:39:59,000 --> 03:40:01,000
*I set down my fork with a clink.*

3406
03:40:01,000 --> 03:40:04,000
*All the life has gone out of her eyes.*

3407
03:40:04,000 --> 03:40:05,000
*She's in a daze.*

3408
03:40:05,000 --> 03:40:10,000
*It's incredibly frustrating that I can't find the words to comfort her.*

3409
03:40:10,000 --> 03:40:19,000
Sophitia: "You're free to take the news I've brought you however you like, but I don't think it's anything to be so depressed over."

3410
03:40:19,000 --> 03:40:22,000
Kakeru: "Easy to say when it doesn't matter to you."

3411
03:40:22,000 --> 03:40:27,000
Sophitia: "Say what you will, but I don't think it was all depressing news."

3412
03:40:27,000 --> 03:40:35,000
Sophitia: "Miyako may have lost to the Evil Eye's User, but only in the other branch. This Miyako is alive and well."

3413
03:40:35,000 --> 03:40:40,000
Sophitia: "Here, she still has the power to identify the Evil Eye's User."

3414
03:40:40,000 --> 03:40:41,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3415
03:40:41,000 --> 03:40:44,000
*A bit of life returns to Miyako's eyes.*

3416
03:40:44,000 --> 03:40:50,000
Miyako: "I see. If I was turned to stone, then I must really have found the Evil Eye's User."

3417
03:40:50,000 --> 03:40:54,000
Sophitia: "Yes. Did you not hear me before? You found them."

3418
03:40:54,000 --> 03:41:00,000
Sophitia: "If you are careful, you may yet have a chance to face the Evil Eye's User and win."

3419
03:41:00,000 --> 03:41:04,000
Miyako: "With my powers, I could put a stop to these murders."

3420
03:41:04,000 --> 03:41:07,000
Sophitia: "That is exactly what I'm hoping for."

3421
03:41:07,000 --> 03:41:09,000
Miyako: "I can do it..."

3422
03:41:09,000 --> 03:41:11,000
*She firmly clenches her fist.*

3423
03:41:11,000 --> 03:41:13,000
*Sophie smiles in satisfaction.*

3424
03:41:13,000 --> 03:41:20,000
Sophitia: "I leave the approach up to you. I have no idea how you came across them in the other branch."

3425
03:41:20,000 --> 03:41:23,000
Miyako: "R-Right, I will figure something out."

3426
03:41:23,000 --> 03:41:31,000
Sophitia: "Kakeru, as incompetent as you may be, make sure you help out Miyako. I'm sure you won't be completely useless."

3427
03:41:31,000 --> 03:41:35,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I don't need you to tell me to help her."

3428
03:41:35,000 --> 03:41:38,000
Sophitia: "Very well. I'll be off, then. Toodle-oo."

3429
03:41:38,000 --> 03:41:43,000
*With those parting words, Sophie disappears into a patch of distorted space.*

3430
03:41:43,000 --> 03:41:44,000
*...*

3431
03:41:44,000 --> 03:41:47,000
*Different branches... Parallel worlds...*

3432
03:41:47,000 --> 03:41:50,000
*And in one of them, Miyako was murdered.*

3433
03:41:50,000 --> 03:41:51,000
*...*

3434
03:41:51,000 --> 03:41:55,000
*No, I can't let this get to me. Gotta stay strong, for her.*

3435
03:41:55,000 --> 03:41:57,000
Kakeru: "S-So, how about that cake?"

3436
03:41:57,000 --> 03:41:58,000
Miyako: "O-Okay."

3437
03:41:58,000 --> 03:42:03,000
*Grasping at straws, I try to lighten the mood by reminding her about the cake.*

3438
03:42:03,000 --> 03:42:10,000
*She went to all that effort to bring it over, and I'm truly grateful. I'd like us to enjoy together.*

3439
03:42:10,000 --> 03:42:11,000
Miyako: "..."

3440
03:42:11,000 --> 03:42:12,000
Miyako: "O-Oh dear..."

3441
03:42:12,000 --> 03:42:15,000
*Her fork falls to the table with a clank.*

3442
03:42:15,000 --> 03:42:17,000
Kakeru: "Miyako, what's wrong?"

3443
03:42:17,000 --> 03:42:18,000
Miyako: "I-I'm sorry."

3444
03:42:18,000 --> 03:42:21,000
*She apologizes and reaches for the fork.*

3445
03:42:21,000 --> 03:42:24,000
*But she fumbles and comes up empty-handed.*

3446
03:42:24,000 --> 03:42:26,000
*Her hands are trembling.*

3447
03:42:26,000 --> 03:42:29,000
Miyako: "Wh-What's come over me? I-I'm sorry."

3448
03:42:29,000 --> 03:42:34,000
*She grabs her wrist with her other hand, trying to stop its shaking.*

3449
03:42:34,000 --> 03:42:39,000
*But her trembling only grows worse, and soon she's shivering all over.*

3450
03:42:39,000 --> 03:42:40,000
Miyako: "..."

3451
03:42:40,000 --> 03:42:46,000
Miyako: "I was trying to be the hero of the story. I never imagined I might end up dead."

3452
03:42:46,000 --> 03:42:51,000
Miyako: "I always have lacked foresight. How did I get this all so wrong?"

3453
03:42:51,000 --> 03:42:59,000
Miyako: "I should have known. I merely stumbled upon these powers. I'm not special. One false move, and I could be killed."

3454
03:42:59,000 --> 03:43:00,000
Kakeru: "Miyako..."

3455
03:43:00,000 --> 03:43:04,000
*I call her name tenderly and take her quivering hand.*

3456
03:43:04,000 --> 03:43:06,000
Miyako: "Thank you. I'm sorry."

3457
03:43:06,000 --> 03:43:08,000
Kakeru: "You don't have to do this."

3458
03:43:08,000 --> 03:43:09,000
Miyako: "..."

3459
03:43:09,000 --> 03:43:16,000
Kakeru: "I know this isn't what you want to hear, but you don't have to put your life on the line, Miyako."

3460
03:43:16,000 --> 03:43:28,000
Kakeru: "I think it's splendid that you want to bring peace to this town. That's the kind of drive I don't have, and that makes me want to be there supporting you in that goal."

3461
03:43:28,000 --> 03:43:34,000
Kakeru: "But much more than that, I don't want you to get hurt. I don't want you to end up dead."

3462
03:43:34,000 --> 03:43:35,000
Miyako: "...Yeah."

3463
03:43:35,000 --> 03:43:38,000
*Her shivering is calming down a bit.*

3464
03:43:38,000 --> 03:43:43,000
*Although I'm trying to console her, my advice is cold and unforgiving.*

3465
03:43:43,000 --> 03:43:50,000
*I even had to tell her it wasn't going to be what she wanted to hear, trying to soften the blow.*

3466
03:43:50,000 --> 03:43:53,000
*But I still believe it's the best option.*

3467
03:43:53,000 --> 03:43:58,000
*I want Miyako to live, even if that means others are going to keep dying.*

3468
03:43:58,000 --> 03:44:00,000
*But of course, I know already...*

3469
03:44:00,000 --> 03:44:01,000
Miyako: "Even so..."

3470
03:44:01,000 --> 03:44:03,000
*I know what Miyako will say.*

3471
03:44:03,000 --> 03:44:05,000
Miyako: "...I don't want to give up."

3472
03:44:05,000 --> 03:44:08,000
*She will press on regardless of what I think.*

3473
03:44:08,000 --> 03:44:16,000
Miyako: "I want to be worthy of you. I want to be the kind of girlfriend who will walk through fire for her beloved."

3474
03:44:16,000 --> 03:44:19,000
Kakeru: "I'm telling you, I'm hardly special."

3475
03:44:19,000 --> 03:44:21,000
Miyako: "You're special to me."

3476
03:44:21,000 --> 03:44:26,000
Kakeru: "See, it's just... I'm giving it all I've got to be worthy of you."

3477
03:44:26,000 --> 03:44:35,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun, you're too good for me. I'm trying to reach you, but I still have a long way to go before I'm that strong."

3478
03:44:35,000 --> 03:44:40,000
*She puts her shivering left hand atop mine, still holding her right hand.*

3479
03:44:40,000 --> 03:44:46,000
Miyako: "I never considered that being told the story of your own death would be this upsetting."

3480
03:44:46,000 --> 03:44:48,000
Kakeru: "It's only a story."

3481
03:44:48,000 --> 03:44:49,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3482
03:44:49,000 --> 03:44:51,000
*She lets go of my hand.*

3483
03:44:51,000 --> 03:44:52,000
*A forlorn sigh.*

3484
03:44:52,000 --> 03:44:56,000
*But I'm sure as hell not going to let her stay like that.*

3485
03:44:56,000 --> 03:44:58,000
*I muster up my courage...*

3486
03:44:58,000 --> 03:45:00,000
*...and put my arms around her.*

3487
03:45:00,000 --> 03:45:11,000
Kakeru: "What Sophie told us about was just a possibility, another way things could have gone. In the here and now, we're both very much alive. We still have each other."

3488
03:45:11,000 --> 03:45:12,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

3489
03:45:12,000 --> 03:45:18,000
Kakeru: "But if you're still worried... If you're afraid you might die in all this..."

3490
03:45:18,000 --> 03:45:20,000
Kakeru: "I swear, I'll protect you."

3491
03:45:20,000 --> 03:45:23,000
Kakeru: "I will not let you die, Miyako."

3492
03:45:23,000 --> 03:45:24,000
Miyako: "..."

3493
03:45:24,000 --> 03:45:25,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

3494
03:45:25,000 --> 03:45:26,000
Miyako: "Thank you."

3495
03:45:26,000 --> 03:45:28,000
*Miyako suddenly relaxes...*

3496
03:45:28,000 --> 03:45:30,000
*...and leans into me.*

3497
03:45:30,000 --> 03:45:34,000
*Is this throbbing I can feel coming from me or from her?*

3498
03:45:34,000 --> 03:45:35,000
*I don't know.*

3499
03:45:35,000 --> 03:45:41,000
*But I do know that Miyako is soft and warm, and that she smells sweet in my arms.*

3500
03:45:41,000 --> 03:45:43,000
*I want to stay like this forever.*

3501
03:45:43,000 --> 03:45:49,000
*But while at first I only feel concern for her, soon enough, my desires rear their ugly head.*

3502
03:45:49,000 --> 03:45:53,000
*Realizing that selfish side of me, I chastise myself internally.*

3503
03:45:53,000 --> 03:45:56,000
*I really am not the man Miyako thinks I am.*

3504
03:45:56,000 --> 03:46:01,000
*I'm worried about what I might do if we stay like this much longer.*

3505
03:46:01,000 --> 03:46:04,000
Kakeru: "Feels like you stopped shivering."

3506
03:46:04,000 --> 03:46:05,000
Miyako: "..."

3507
03:46:05,000 --> 03:46:08,000
Miyako: "Nope... Haven't stopped yet."

3508
03:46:08,000 --> 03:46:10,000
*I'm momentarily at a loss of words.*

3509
03:46:10,000 --> 03:46:14,000
*But it only takes me a moment to read between the lines.*

3510
03:46:14,000 --> 03:46:16,000
*You too, huh, Miyako?*

3511
03:46:16,000 --> 03:46:19,000
*I guess we're more similar than I thought.*

3512
03:46:19,000 --> 03:46:23,000
Kakeru: "Then I guess we'd better stay like this a little longer."

3513
03:46:23,000 --> 03:46:25,000
Miyako: "Not just a little longer."

3514
03:46:25,000 --> 03:46:28,000
Kakeru: "Okay. As long as we feel like."

3515
03:46:28,000 --> 03:46:29,000
Miyako: "Yeah..."

3516
03:46:29,000 --> 03:46:33,000
*Miyako's tension has all bled away, gone without a trace.*

3517
03:46:33,000 --> 03:46:36,000
*She's entrusting all of herself to me.*

3518
03:46:36,000 --> 03:46:40,000
*All her weight, all her existence, in the circle of my arms.*

3519
03:46:40,000 --> 03:46:41,000
Miyako: "..."

3520
03:46:41,000 --> 03:46:44,000
*She tilts her head up, and our eyes meet.*

3521
03:46:44,000 --> 03:46:45,000
*Her face is flushed.*

3522
03:46:45,000 --> 03:46:47,000
*Her eyes are shimmering.*

3523
03:46:47,000 --> 03:46:50,000
*I take a deep breath and drink in her sweet smell.*

3524
03:46:50,000 --> 03:46:52,000
*My head is going blank.*

3525
03:46:52,000 --> 03:46:54,000
*My heart is pounding.*

3526
03:46:54,000 --> 03:46:56,000
*"You're taking advantage of her."*

3527
03:46:56,000 --> 03:46:59,000
*A voice in the back of my head shouts at me.*

3528
03:46:59,000 --> 03:47:00,000
*And maybe I am.*

3529
03:47:00,000 --> 03:47:04,000
*Still, if I can wipe away Miyako's worries, her fears...*

3530
03:47:04,000 --> 03:47:07,000
*Then I'm fine with stooping that low.*

3531
03:47:07,000 --> 03:47:08,000
Miyako: "Mm..."

3532
03:47:08,000 --> 03:47:13,000
*Drawn to each other, our passions inflamed, we gently come together in a kiss.*

3533
03:47:13,000 --> 03:47:16,000
*Her lips are sweet. Maybe the taste of the cake?*

3534
03:47:16,000 --> 03:47:17,000
*Doesn't matter.*

3535
03:47:17,000 --> 03:47:27,000
*The rush of excitement and nervousness paralyze my senses, and my heart hammers in my chest, so hard I can hear the blood pounding in my ears.*

3536
03:47:27,000 --> 03:47:31,000
*With all the blood going to my head, I might just pass out.*

3537
03:47:31,000 --> 03:47:35,000
*I'm so far gone, I don't even know what it feels like.*

3538
03:47:35,000 --> 03:47:37,000
*And so a moment later...*

3539
03:47:37,000 --> 03:47:38,000
Miyako: "..."

3540
03:47:38,000 --> 03:47:39,000
Miyako: "...Another."

3541
03:47:39,000 --> 03:47:42,000
*She pleads as I kiss her slightly parted lips.*

3542
03:47:42,000 --> 03:47:44,000
Miyako: "Mm... Nhh, haah..."

3543
03:47:44,000 --> 03:47:49,000
*When she does, before I realize it, I'm holding her tight in my embrace.*

3544
03:47:49,000 --> 03:47:53,000
*Our first kiss was so good that it overwhelmed my senses.*

3545
03:47:53,000 --> 03:47:56,000
*I'm hoping that Miyako feels the same about it.*

3546
03:47:56,000 --> 03:47:59,000
Miyako: "Nhh... Mmph... Mwah... Mm..."

3547
03:47:59,000 --> 03:48:02,000
*Insatiable, we kiss each other again and again.*

3548
03:48:02,000 --> 03:48:04,000
Miyako: "Mm... Mmh... Mwah...!"

3549
03:48:04,000 --> 03:48:05,000
*Again, and again.*

3550
03:48:05,000 --> 03:48:06,000
Miyako: "..."

3551
03:48:06,000 --> 03:48:07,000
Kakeru: "..."

3552
03:48:07,000 --> 03:48:12,000
*Our lips lock tirelessly, as though all we need in the world is each other.*

3553
03:48:12,000 --> 03:48:14,000
*At last, we separate.*

3554
03:48:14,000 --> 03:48:17,000
*Sweet sighs drift between the two of us.*

3555
03:48:17,000 --> 03:48:30,000
Satsuki: "Yeah, so basically, in episode ten, Shisa says, 'I have seen the depths of calamity!' So she's foretelling the upcoming disaster, which also signals the arrival of the Great White Serpent..."

3556
03:48:30,000 --> 03:48:44,000
*Once a week, the city force-feeds us a shitty lesson that teaches us about the local folklore through details from the anime, and that in no way helps us come test time for things that actually matter.*

3557
03:48:44,000 --> 03:48:50,000
*Needless to say, Ms. Naruse is really phoning it in, and the whole class is ignoring her.*

3558
03:48:50,000 --> 03:48:51,000
*Same goes for me.*

3559
03:48:51,000 --> 03:48:56,000
*I've been completely occupied trying to narrow down our killer's identity.*

3560
03:48:56,000 --> 03:49:01,000
*Sophie gave us some useful information about what occurred in that other branch.*

3561
03:49:01,000 --> 03:49:09,000
*While I'm not sure I should believe everything she said, I'm not going to get anywhere without at least some sort of lead.*

3562
03:49:09,000 --> 03:49:18,000
*I'm going to assume that everything Sophie told us is the truth, organize the information, and then see what conclusions it leads me to.*

3563
03:49:18,000 --> 03:49:23,000
*First of all, Miyako and I had a falling out for one reason or another.*

3564
03:49:23,000 --> 03:49:26,000
*Because of that, Miyako went working on her own.*

3565
03:49:26,000 --> 03:49:30,000
*As a result, Miyako used her ability and identified the culprit.*

3566
03:49:30,000 --> 03:49:33,000
*And finally, she was murdered by them.*

3567
03:49:33,000 --> 03:49:46,000
*The situation is so radically different from what's happening in our world that I decide not to focus on how things would even end up like that. I don't have any idea why it would happen anyway.*

3568
03:49:46,000 --> 03:49:51,000
*Most likely, we've avoided whatever twist of fate caused us to separate.*

3569
03:49:51,000 --> 03:49:54,000
*And thus, Miyako won't go off on her own.*

3570
03:49:54,000 --> 03:50:03,000
*So the way I see it, since she's got me with her, the possibility of Miyako being murdered by the culprit has dropped considerably.*

3571
03:50:03,000 --> 03:50:09,000
*Therefore, I can move on from that and focus on who Miyako used her abilities on.*

3572
03:50:09,000 --> 03:50:15,000
*Going off what Sophie told us, Miyako identified the culprit in less than the span of a week.*

3573
03:50:15,000 --> 03:50:21,000
*Some of that time was the Golden Week holidays, so it might only have taken her a couple days.*

3574
03:50:21,000 --> 03:50:25,000
*How was she able to identify the culprit in such a short time?*

3575
03:50:25,000 --> 03:50:32,000
*I can't help but think they must be a student here, or a teacher. Or maybe a customer at Nine Ball.*

3576
03:50:32,000 --> 03:50:37,000
*But one way or the other, the culprit must be somewhere very close by us.*

3577
03:50:37,000 --> 03:50:40,000
*There's also one more point I should focus on.*

3578
03:50:40,000 --> 03:50:44,000
*That being, why did the culprit smash Miyako's statue?*

3579
03:50:44,000 --> 03:50:49,000
*The culprit had been simply turning girls into statues up until that point.*

3580
03:50:49,000 --> 03:50:56,000
*So why did they go out of their way to break Miyako's statue, and only hers, after the petrification process?*

3581
03:50:56,000 --> 03:51:00,000
*Did they want to check if their abilities were developing?*

3582
03:51:00,000 --> 03:51:04,000
*Or maybe... they had a personal grudge against Miyako?*

3583
03:51:04,000 --> 03:51:14,000
*I can't even imagine why someone would, but if that theory is correct, then the culprit must be someone with an extremely close relationship to Miyako.*

3584
03:51:14,000 --> 03:51:20,000
*Otherwise, there would be no reason they'd have any strong feelings towards her at all.*

3585
03:51:20,000 --> 03:51:27,000
*Now, taking all of that into consideration, we have pretty clear guidelines on which to base our search.*

3586
03:51:27,000 --> 03:51:32,000
*But whatever happens, we mustn't let people learn about her powers.*

3587
03:51:32,000 --> 03:51:44,000
*Even if Miyako's powers rob the target of their memories of the whole event, anybody talking to them would easily detect that they're acting weird. It's a major weakness of her ability.*

3588
03:51:44,000 --> 03:51:54,000
*If the culprit is observant enough and smart enough to figure out what's going on, then using any powers with reckless abandon could be a huge risk.*

3589
03:51:54,000 --> 03:51:55,000
Kakeru: "..."

3590
03:51:55,000 --> 03:51:57,000
*I sigh and take a step back.*

3591
03:51:57,000 --> 03:52:03,000
*At the end of the day, there's no way to eliminate all the risks. All I can do is trust Miyako.*

3592
03:52:03,000 --> 03:52:05,000
*I'm such a pathetic boyfriend.*

3593
03:52:05,000 --> 03:52:10,000
*If I really am a User, I wish I'd unlock my powers already, goddammit.*

3594
03:52:10,000 --> 03:52:23,000
Satsuki: "What I'd like you all to notice here is the sacred relic, the Red Eye of the White Serpent. You see, using this, the Great White Serpent expelled the evil from this land, and..."

3595
03:52:23,000 --> 03:52:25,000
*Ms. Naruse drones on.*

3596
03:52:25,000 --> 03:52:31,000
*Come to think of it, didn't Sophie mention something about the anime being pretty accurate?*

3597
03:52:31,000 --> 03:52:36,000
*The sacred relic... was the Red Eye of the White Serpent? An Artifact...?*

3598
03:52:36,000 --> 03:52:38,000
*The World's Eye... The Evil Eye...*

3599
03:52:38,000 --> 03:52:39,000
*...*

3600
03:52:39,000 --> 03:52:40,000
*Wait a second.*

3601
03:52:40,000 --> 03:52:42,000
*I see... Dammit, Sophie.*

3602
03:52:42,000 --> 03:52:44,000
*You've been holding out on us!*

3603
03:52:44,000 --> 03:52:50,000
*After school, Miyako and I head out of the classroom and make a beeline for the front gates.*

3604
03:52:50,000 --> 03:52:54,000
*There, we plan to meet up with Sora and head to my place.*

3605
03:52:54,000 --> 03:52:56,000
Sora: "Yo, thanks for the wait."

3606
03:52:56,000 --> 03:52:58,000
Kakeru: "Hey, nice hustle."

3607
03:52:58,000 --> 03:53:00,000
Sora: "Huh? Where's Miya?"

3608
03:53:00,000 --> 03:53:02,000
Kakeru: "She's grabbing her bike."

3609
03:53:02,000 --> 03:53:04,000
Sora: "The pushie, eh?"

3610
03:53:04,000 --> 03:53:05,000
Kakeru: "Uh, what?"

3611
03:53:05,000 --> 03:53:09,000
Sora: "It's regional slang for a bike. Short for 'push iron!'"

3612
03:53:09,000 --> 03:53:12,000
Kakeru: "The full name sounds kinda cool."

3613
03:53:12,000 --> 03:53:15,000
Sora: "Both sound pretty raunchy, am I right?"

3614
03:53:15,000 --> 03:53:17,000
Miyako: "Sorry, I'm ready!"

3615
03:53:17,000 --> 03:53:20,000
Sora: "Hey hey, here she is, getting her pushie on."

3616
03:53:20,000 --> 03:53:22,000
Miyako: "Huh? What was that?"

3617
03:53:22,000 --> 03:53:27,000
Kakeru: "She says it's a regional dialect thing. Come on, we're heading out."

3618
03:53:27,000 --> 03:53:30,000
Sora: "Mind if I put my bag in the basket, Miya?"

3619
03:53:30,000 --> 03:53:32,000
Miyako: "Go right ahead."

3620
03:53:32,000 --> 03:53:34,000
*We start walking together.*

3621
03:53:34,000 --> 03:53:43,000
*Miyako says she wants to drop by the supermarket, but since the plan is to split up early today, we head straight to my place.*

3622
03:53:43,000 --> 03:53:51,000
Sora: "What's this?! There's a long hair on the ground! You're cheating, aren't you?! You brought a girl over, didn't you?!"

3623
03:53:51,000 --> 03:53:53,000
Kakeru: "Oh give it a break."

3624
03:53:53,000 --> 03:53:56,000
Miyako: "Oh, sorry, it's probably mine."

3625
03:53:56,000 --> 03:53:59,000
Kakeru: "Miyako, don't take her seriously!"

3626
03:53:59,000 --> 03:54:03,000
*Dropping our bags wherever, the three of us sit around the table.*

3627
03:54:03,000 --> 03:54:07,000
*Now then. Today we have a serious discussion ahead of us.*

3628
03:54:07,000 --> 03:54:10,000
Kakeru: "First order of business is..."

3629
03:54:10,000 --> 03:54:12,000
Sora: "Wait, I've got a question!"

3630
03:54:12,000 --> 03:54:13,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, what?"

3631
03:54:13,000 --> 03:54:17,000
Sora: "It's actually a question for the both of you!"

3632
03:54:17,000 --> 03:54:19,000
Miyako: "Huh? What is it?"

3633
03:54:19,000 --> 03:54:27,000
Sora: "You guys started calling each other 'Kakeru-kun' and 'Miyako', so that means you two are dating now, right?"

3634
03:54:27,000 --> 03:54:28,000
Kakeru: "..."

3635
03:54:28,000 --> 03:54:29,000
Miyako: "..."

3636
03:54:29,000 --> 03:54:32,000
Kakeru: "So, let's see, for starters we..."

3637
03:54:32,000 --> 03:54:39,000
Sora: "Hold the fucking phone! You're actually dating?! No way! Have you been been dating this whole time?!"

3638
03:54:39,000 --> 03:54:42,000
Kakeru: "Look, it's fine, whatever, just let it go."

3639
03:54:42,000 --> 03:54:47,000
Sora: "Like hell it's fine! Why were you trying to hide it, you jerk?!"

3640
03:54:47,000 --> 03:54:55,000
Miyako: "Um, I'll take this opportunity to thank you for all you've done for your brother, and for giving us your blessing..."

3641
03:54:55,000 --> 03:55:00,000
Sora: "Can it with the niceties! I absolutely do not approve of him dating you!"

3642
03:55:00,000 --> 03:55:01,000
Miyako: "Oh!"

3643
03:55:01,000 --> 03:55:09,000
Kakeru: "Alright, settle down, you two. And Miyako, stop taking Sora's stupid jokes seriously. You're just encouraging her."

3644
03:55:09,000 --> 03:55:11,000
Miyako: "Oh, I-I'm sorry."

3645
03:55:11,000 --> 03:55:19,000
Sora: "Dammit. I'll have to plant a bunch of twisted half-truths in Miya's head and drive a wedge between you two."

3646
03:55:19,000 --> 03:55:21,000
Kakeru: "Seriously, don't."

3647
03:55:21,000 --> 03:55:27,000
Sora: "Yeah, whatever. Anyway, you wanted to say something? Get on with it already."

3648
03:55:27,000 --> 03:55:32,000
Kakeru: "Cripes, bad mood much? Anyway, I've got to bring in one more guest."

3649
03:55:32,000 --> 03:55:33,000
Miyako: "Sophie-san?"

3650
03:55:33,000 --> 03:55:36,000
Kakeru: "Yes. You haven't met her yet, right, Sora?"

3651
03:55:36,000 --> 03:55:40,000
Sora: "I've only heard the name. She's a plushie, right?"

3652
03:55:40,000 --> 03:55:46,000
Kakeru: "It's easy to dismiss her as a mascot, but watch out. She can be super rude."

3653
03:55:46,000 --> 03:55:50,000
Kakeru: "Sophie, you're here, aren't you? Come on out, please."

3654
03:55:50,000 --> 03:55:51,000
Miyako: "..."

3655
03:55:51,000 --> 03:55:52,000
Sora: "..."

3656
03:55:52,000 --> 03:55:53,000
Kakeru: "......"

3657
03:55:53,000 --> 03:55:54,000
Miyako: "......"

3658
03:55:54,000 --> 03:55:55,000
Sora: "........."

3659
03:55:55,000 --> 03:55:56,000
Kakeru: "........."

3660
03:55:56,000 --> 03:55:57,000
Miyako: "Um..."

3661
03:55:57,000 --> 03:55:59,000
Sora: "Guess she's not coming."

3662
03:55:59,000 --> 03:56:08,000
Kakeru: "Hey! You're supposed to be monitoring me, right?! I've got something I need to ask you, so please, just come out here!"

3663
03:56:08,000 --> 03:56:09,000
Miyako: "Oh..."

3664
03:56:09,000 --> 03:56:12,000
Sora: "Whoa, the hell? Wow, that's freaky!"

3665
03:56:12,000 --> 03:56:17,000
*A rift in space tears itself open, and Sophie pops half her face through.*

3666
03:56:17,000 --> 03:56:19,000
*About time she showed up.*

3667
03:56:19,000 --> 03:56:23,000
Kakeru: "Sophie, I have something I need to ask you."

3668
03:56:23,000 --> 03:56:24,000
Sophitia: "..."

3669
03:56:24,000 --> 03:56:26,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

3670
03:56:26,000 --> 03:56:30,000
Sophitia: "Is that any way to ask someone for a favor?"

3671
03:56:30,000 --> 03:56:31,000
Kakeru: "..."

3672
03:56:31,000 --> 03:56:39,000
Sophitia: "This has been bugging me for quite some time now. You have absolutely no manners, especially with me."

3673
03:56:39,000 --> 03:56:41,000
Kakeru: "You're one to talk."

3674
03:56:41,000 --> 03:56:45,000
Sophitia: "Is that your way of saying you'd like me to leave?"

3675
03:56:45,000 --> 03:56:46,000
Kakeru: "..."

3676
03:56:46,000 --> 03:56:49,000
Kakeru: "Sophie-san, I have something I need to..."

3677
03:56:49,000 --> 03:56:51,000
Sophitia: "Try again. Politely."

3678
03:56:51,000 --> 03:56:52,000
Kakeru: "..."

3679
03:56:52,000 --> 03:57:02,000
Kakeru: "Sophie-sama, there is something I would very much like to humbly ask you, so might I be so bold as to bother you to listen to my humble question?"

3680
03:57:02,000 --> 03:57:06,000
Sophitia: "Since you asked so nicely, I suppose you may."

3681
03:57:06,000 --> 03:57:11,000
*With a pleased sniff, she passes the rest of the way through the rift in space.*

3682
03:57:11,000 --> 03:57:14,000
*This thing is a real pain in the ass, I swear.*

3683
03:57:14,000 --> 03:57:16,000
Sora: "Wowie, cool! It's so cute!"

3684
03:57:16,000 --> 03:57:24,000
Sophitia: "Thank you, but please do keep your excitement to a minimum. I don't care for obnoxiously loud people like you."

3685
03:57:24,000 --> 03:57:27,000
Sora: "On the first meeting, too... Ouch..."

3686
03:57:27,000 --> 03:57:30,000
Sophitia: "So? What did you need to ask?"

3687
03:57:30,000 --> 03:57:32,000
Kakeru: "It's about the Evil Eye."

3688
03:57:32,000 --> 03:57:36,000
Sophitia: "It grants petrification powers. That's all I've got."

3689
03:57:36,000 --> 03:57:39,000
Kakeru: "No, I'm sure you know more than that."

3690
03:57:39,000 --> 03:57:40,000
Sophitia: "..."

3691
03:57:40,000 --> 03:57:43,000
*Sophie's expression hardens ever so slightly.*

3692
03:57:43,000 --> 03:57:46,000
*It would seem that I guessed correctly.*

3693
03:57:46,000 --> 03:57:52,000
Kakeru: "That thing that lets you experience other branches is called the World's Eye, right?"

3694
03:57:52,000 --> 03:57:53,000
Sophitia: "Correct."

3695
03:57:53,000 --> 03:57:55,000
Kakeru: "Artifacts all have names."

3696
03:57:55,000 --> 03:58:01,000
Sophitia: "But of course. It would prove difficult to monitor them if we don't name them."

3697
03:58:01,000 --> 03:58:05,000
Kakeru: "Then what are the names of Miyako and Sora's Artifacts?"

3698
03:58:05,000 --> 03:58:13,000
Sophitia: "They don't have names. Those Artifacts are not on Sephirot's list. We will name them once they're collected."

3699
03:58:13,000 --> 03:58:14,000
Kakeru: "I knew it."

3700
03:58:14,000 --> 03:58:17,000
Sophitia: "What? What are you getting at?"

3701
03:58:17,000 --> 03:58:25,000
Kakeru: "Earlier, you said that Artifacts that Sephirot wasn't watching over have slipped into our world. Isn't that right?"

3702
03:58:25,000 --> 03:58:28,000
Sophitia: "Yes, exactly. We already went over this."

3703
03:58:28,000 --> 03:58:35,000
Kakeru: "If that's the case, then how come the petrification artifact is already named the Evil Eye?"

3704
03:58:35,000 --> 03:58:40,000
Sophitia: "Tch. I swear, you're perceptive at the worst possible times."

3705
03:58:40,000 --> 03:58:42,000
*She clicks her tongue at me.*

3706
03:58:42,000 --> 03:58:45,000
*I knew this rat had been hiding something.*

3707
03:58:45,000 --> 03:58:49,000
Kakeru: "You knew about the Evil Eye already, didn't you?"

3708
03:58:49,000 --> 03:58:51,000
Sophitia: "Yes, I did."

3709
03:58:51,000 --> 03:58:54,000
Miyako: "Huh? Then, why didn't you...?"

3710
03:58:54,000 --> 03:59:01,000
Sophitia: "Why didn't I tell you everything? It wasn't my choice to make. I have regulations to follow."

3711
03:59:01,000 --> 03:59:03,000
Kakeru: "Sephirot's regulations?"

3712
03:59:03,000 --> 03:59:08,000
Sophitia: "I'm forbidden to divulge any more intel than is strictly necessary."

3713
03:59:08,000 --> 03:59:18,000
Kakeru: "You're telling me it isn't strictly necessary for you to tell us everything you know about this Artifact we're busting our humps to collect?"

3714
03:59:18,000 --> 03:59:21,000
Sophitia: "Look, try to see this from my position."

3715
03:59:21,000 --> 03:59:34,000
Sophitia: "Sure, you're cooperating with me, but the moment I go blabbing classified information to mere humans would also be the moment I'm out of a job, and all the respect that goes with it."

3716
03:59:34,000 --> 03:59:38,000
Miyako: "You couldn't tell us even if you wanted to."

3717
03:59:38,000 --> 03:59:45,000
Sophitia: "Precisely. However... I suppose if you all were to die on me, that would be quite a hassle."

3718
03:59:45,000 --> 03:59:46,000
Sophitia: "..."

3719
03:59:46,000 --> 03:59:52,000
Sophitia: "I will make an exception and tell you one thing. Don't go spreading it around, okay?"

3720
03:59:52,000 --> 03:59:54,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I promise."

3721
03:59:54,000 --> 04:00:01,000
Sophitia: "You won't get anywhere confronting the Evil Eye's User one-on-one. You must operate in numbers."

3722
04:00:01,000 --> 04:00:06,000
Sophitia: "As a duo, defending against the Evil Eye's power is a simple task."

3723
04:00:06,000 --> 04:00:10,000
Kakeru: "That sure would've been nice to know sooner."

3724
04:00:10,000 --> 04:00:17,000
Sophitia: "I wouldn't have given you this tip if it weren't for Miyako dying in the other branch."

3725
04:00:17,000 --> 04:00:18,000
Sora: "D-D...Dying?"

3726
04:00:18,000 --> 04:00:22,000
Miyako: "Oh, d-don't worry about it, I'm fine, Sora-chan."

3727
04:00:22,000 --> 04:00:24,000
Sophitia: "Any other questions?"

3728
04:00:24,000 --> 04:00:30,000
Kakeru: "No, I get it. If you can't talk about it, I'll drop it. Thanks for the help."

3729
04:00:30,000 --> 04:00:40,000
Sophitia: "A 'thank you' is the least I deserve. I can't believe you dragged me here over such a trivial manner in the midst of my busy schedule."

3730
04:00:40,000 --> 04:00:45,000
Kakeru: "Miyako's life is on the line. Don't you dare call it trivial."

3731
04:00:45,000 --> 04:00:48,000
Sophitia: "Wow, you're more clingy than I expected."

3732
04:00:48,000 --> 04:00:53,000
*Sophie offers a snarky parting shot as the space around her begins to distort.*

3733
04:00:53,000 --> 04:01:02,000
Sophitia: "I'll see myself out. If you run into any problems, call me again, though I can't guarantee I'll always be able to advise you."

3734
04:01:02,000 --> 04:01:07,000
*She waves a stubby little hand at us as she disappears into the subspace rift.*

3735
04:01:07,000 --> 04:01:08,000
Sora: "..."

3736
04:01:08,000 --> 04:01:10,000
Sora: "She's insufferable..."

3737
04:01:10,000 --> 04:01:17,000
Kakeru: "It's just her nature to look down on people. Try not to take it too hard when she acts rude."

3738
04:01:17,000 --> 04:01:22,000
Sora: "Still kinda stings. Anyway. Anyway anyway anyway, you gonna explain?"

3739
04:01:22,000 --> 04:01:24,000
Kakeru: "Explain what?"

3740
04:01:24,000 --> 04:01:29,000
Sora: "That stuff about Miya dying, and her life being on the line."

3741
04:01:29,000 --> 04:01:33,000
Miyako: "Ahh... I guess you could call it a premonition?"

3742
04:01:33,000 --> 04:01:36,000
Sora: "Wait, what?! Miya, you're gonna die?!"

3743
04:01:36,000 --> 04:01:41,000
Kakeru: "She most definitely is not. I won't let her. That's what I'm here for."

3744
04:01:41,000 --> 04:01:45,000
Kakeru: "And you're gonna help me protect her, right, Sora?"

3745
04:01:45,000 --> 04:01:47,000
Sora: "Yeah, of course!"

3746
04:01:47,000 --> 04:01:49,000
Miyako: "Thank you, Sora-chan."

3747
04:01:49,000 --> 04:01:56,000
Sora: "So, now that I said I'll help, what do you want me to do? Should I just hang out with Miya all the time?"

3748
04:01:56,000 --> 04:01:58,000
Kakeru: "We need your power."

3749
04:01:58,000 --> 04:02:02,000
Sora: "Huh. You mean the same power you called lame earlier?"

3750
04:02:02,000 --> 04:02:06,000
Kakeru: "You're seriously still holding a grudge over that?"

3751
04:02:06,000 --> 04:02:08,000
Sora: "You better believe it, Slick."

3752
04:02:08,000 --> 04:02:13,000
Kakeru: "Allow me to correct myself: It's the strongest power imaginable."

3753
04:02:13,000 --> 04:02:16,000
Sora: "Kinda feels like you're being sarcastic now."

3754
04:02:16,000 --> 04:02:21,000
Miyako: "You want Sora-chan to diminish my presence so that I can use my power?"

3755
04:02:21,000 --> 04:02:32,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. I think the key problem we have to avoid would be the culprit finding out that Miyako is a User, and moreover, one capable of exposing their identity."

3756
04:02:32,000 --> 04:02:40,000
Kakeru: "But if we can keep Miyako's powers hidden, we should be able to identify the culprit without them catching on to us."

3757
04:02:40,000 --> 04:02:48,000
Kakeru: "And if we can identify the culprit, we've got it made. After all, we have The Great and Powerful Sora on our side."

3758
04:02:48,000 --> 04:02:53,000
Sora: "Heh heh heh. Looks like it's time for me and my spycraft to shine."

3759
04:02:53,000 --> 04:02:54,000
Miyako: "..."

3760
04:02:54,000 --> 04:02:59,000
Sora: "Hey, you're lookin' pretty worried there. Don't you have faith in me?"

3761
04:02:59,000 --> 04:03:01,000
Miyako: "Oh, no, of course I do."

3762
04:03:01,000 --> 04:03:04,000
Kakeru: "Are you worried about something?"

3763
04:03:04,000 --> 04:03:09,000
Miyako: "Yes. You see, I suspect that the culprit may already know who I am."

3764
04:03:09,000 --> 04:03:10,000
Sora: "Huh? How come?"

3765
04:03:10,000 --> 04:03:14,000
Miyako: "Well, I used my powers back during the fire."

3766
04:03:14,000 --> 04:03:15,000
Kakeru: "Oh yeah!"

3767
04:03:15,000 --> 04:03:18,000
*How could I forget about something so important?*

3768
04:03:18,000 --> 04:03:23,000
*So there's a possibility that the culprit is already keeping an eye on us, then.*

3769
04:03:23,000 --> 04:03:30,000
Sora: "If they found you out because they were there during the fire, then maybe the culprit is a first year?"

3770
04:03:30,000 --> 04:03:38,000
Miyako: "Well, anybody there could have told their friends and whatnot, so I don't think we can say that for certain."

3771
04:03:38,000 --> 04:03:42,000
Kakeru: "They might even have figured out your power."

3772
04:03:42,000 --> 04:03:50,000
Miyako: "Yeah. If they're clever like you, Kakeru-kun, and figured out that my powers can be used to steal memories as well..."

3773
04:03:50,000 --> 04:03:54,000
Kakeru: "...then they'd certainly be coming for you."

3774
04:03:54,000 --> 04:03:57,000
Miyako: "Yes. I might already be their next target."

3775
04:03:57,000 --> 04:04:09,000
Sora: "You really think there's someone like that out there? You really think someone else is going to think it through that far and figure out that you can steal memories?"

3776
04:04:09,000 --> 04:04:17,000
Kakeru: "We're talking about a serial killer here. If you believe you know what's going on in their head, think again."

3777
04:04:17,000 --> 04:04:24,000
Sora: "All right, then we need to get cracking on this. We have to nab the perp before they make their move."

3778
04:04:24,000 --> 04:04:32,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, you're right. Our culprit is somewhere very close to us, no doubt. We should be able to catch them."

3779
04:04:32,000 --> 04:04:39,000
Miyako: "Whose memories should I start by reading? I'll trust your judgement on this one, Kakeru-kun."

3780
04:04:39,000 --> 04:04:52,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, 'bout that... We'd be shooting blind, so considering that our culprit might be on the move already, if we can, I'd like to narrow down our choices before we pull the trigger."

3781
04:04:52,000 --> 04:04:58,000
Sora: "Oh, that reminds me. If I may be so bold as to offer my opinion, O elder brother of mine?"

3782
04:04:58,000 --> 04:05:00,000
Kakeru: "But of course."

3783
04:05:00,000 --> 04:05:08,000
Sora: "Very well. As you may or may not remember, I've been checking in on the Leaves of Agastia on a daily basis."

3784
04:05:08,000 --> 04:05:10,000
Miyako: "Oh, that forum..."

3785
04:05:10,000 --> 04:05:16,000
Sora: "Yes, yes, precisely. So, as I was saying, do you remember the Queen of Eden?"

3786
04:05:16,000 --> 04:05:17,000
Miyako: "..."

3787
04:05:17,000 --> 04:05:21,000
Sora: "Whoa, Miya looks super pissed all of a sudden."

3788
04:05:21,000 --> 04:05:26,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I guess you could say there's some bad blood between them."

3789
04:05:26,000 --> 04:05:33,000
Sora: "Well, whatever. Anyway, she seems to have been part of an offline meetup during the break."

3790
04:05:33,000 --> 04:05:34,000
Miyako: "A what?"

3791
04:05:34,000 --> 04:05:39,000
Sora: "A thing where people who know each other online meet up in real life."

3792
04:05:39,000 --> 04:05:41,000
Miyako: "Oh, so that means..."

3793
04:05:41,000 --> 04:05:47,000
Kakeru: "So there's a possibility that Kosaka-senpai is now in contact with other Users, huh?"

3794
04:05:47,000 --> 04:05:55,000
Sora: "Well, she might've just met up with a bunch of wannabes. But what if it really were a meeting of genuine Users?"

3795
04:05:55,000 --> 04:05:59,000
Miyako: "She may very well have had contact with the culprit."

3796
04:05:59,000 --> 04:06:06,000
Sora: "Well, maybe, but I doubt they'd be that stupid. A murderer wouldn't just drop in on an offline meetup."

3797
04:06:06,000 --> 04:06:08,000
Kakeru: "Point taken. But still..."

3798
04:06:08,000 --> 04:06:14,000
Sora: "'If you believe you know what's going on in their head, think again.' Right?"

3799
04:06:14,000 --> 04:06:22,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. If they were the type to worry, they wouldn't have murdered two people, nor would they be gunning for Miyako."

3800
04:06:22,000 --> 04:06:32,000
Kakeru: "I'm positive that our culprit hardly gives a second thought over murdering someone. They're undoubtedly just going on with their normal life."

3801
04:06:32,000 --> 04:06:39,000
Kakeru: "I wouldn't be surprised at all if they just waltzed into an offline meetup and started chatting."

3802
04:06:39,000 --> 04:06:42,000
Miyako: "Where did they hold this meetup?"

3803
04:06:42,000 --> 04:06:46,000
Sora: "It was a pilgrimage to the real-life locales, of course."

3804
04:06:46,000 --> 04:06:51,000
Miyako: "Real-life locales...? Oh, right, it's an anime fansite, after all."

3805
04:06:51,000 --> 04:06:56,000
Sora: "Visiting the places in the anime was the purported purpose of the meetup."

3806
04:06:56,000 --> 04:06:59,000
Kakeru: "So like, exactly where did they go?"

3807
04:06:59,000 --> 04:07:01,000
Sora: "Uh, no clue, actually."

3808
04:07:01,000 --> 04:07:06,000
Kakeru: "Well, crap. Guess we'll have to get it straight from the horse's mouth."

3809
04:07:06,000 --> 04:07:11,000
Miyako: "Meaning I just have to read Kosaka-senpai's memories, right?"

3810
04:07:11,000 --> 04:07:17,000
Kakeru: "Yep. We know someone who went, so reading her memories is our best option."

3811
04:07:17,000 --> 04:07:19,000
Miyako: "Okay, got it."

3812
04:07:19,000 --> 04:07:23,000
Kakeru: "Sora, I'll need you with her when she reads her memories."

3813
04:07:23,000 --> 04:07:29,000
Sora: "Okie dokie. Let's do this in the morning. We're guaranteed to meet her then."

3814
04:07:29,000 --> 04:07:34,000
Miyako: "Yes. Let's not waste any time and do this tomorrow morning."

3815
04:07:34,000 --> 04:07:39,000
Sora: "So, with memories, can you choose and read whichever you like?"

3816
04:07:39,000 --> 04:07:43,000
Miyako: "I'm not certain. I've only tried it once, after all."

3817
04:07:43,000 --> 04:07:54,000
Miyako: "I'm not too sure, but I suspect the strongest memories are the easiest to read. Since you can't see memories, selecting the one you want to take is hard."

3818
04:07:54,000 --> 04:07:57,000
Sora: "So we're just hoping for the best."

3819
04:07:57,000 --> 04:07:58,000
Miyako: "Pretty much."

3820
04:07:58,000 --> 04:08:04,000
Kakeru: "The culprit is someone near us. They may even be a student at our school."

3821
04:08:04,000 --> 04:08:07,000
Kakeru: "We have to pray that this works."

3822
04:08:07,000 --> 04:08:08,000
Miyako: "Yeah!"

3823
04:08:08,000 --> 04:08:11,000
Kakeru: "Alright, then, shall we call it a day?"

3824
04:08:11,000 --> 04:08:22,000
Sora: "Mmm. I haven't had one of Miya's home-cooked meals in forever, so I was kinda hoping for dinner, but if someone is after her life, I'll have to deal with it."

3825
04:08:22,000 --> 04:08:26,000
Kakeru: "I wish you wouldn't be so blase about it..."

3826
04:08:26,000 --> 04:08:27,000
Sora: "Oh, I'm sorry."

3827
04:08:27,000 --> 04:08:32,000
Miyako: "Haha, it's okay. Sora-chan, you be careful going home as well."

3828
04:08:32,000 --> 04:08:41,000
Sora: "I'm just riding the train, and I can sneak around if I need it, so don't worry about me. All right, then, time to head back."

3829
04:08:41,000 --> 04:08:43,000
Miyako: "Okay, see you later."

3830
04:08:43,000 --> 04:08:44,000
Sora: "Huh?"

3831
04:08:44,000 --> 04:08:45,000
Miyako: "What?"

3832
04:08:45,000 --> 04:08:48,000
Sora: "Uh, aren't you leaving along with me?"

3833
04:08:48,000 --> 04:08:49,000
Miyako: "Um..."

3834
04:08:49,000 --> 04:08:50,000
Sora: "Huh?!"

3835
04:08:50,000 --> 04:08:54,000
Miyako: "I still have some... personal matters to attend to."

3836
04:08:54,000 --> 04:08:55,000
Sora: "..."

3837
04:08:55,000 --> 04:08:56,000
Miyako: "..."

3838
04:08:56,000 --> 04:08:59,000
Sora: "You two are going to make out, aren't you?"

3839
04:08:59,000 --> 04:09:01,000
Miyako: "Oh, no, just, um..."

3840
04:09:01,000 --> 04:09:03,000
Sora: "You totally are!"

3841
04:09:03,000 --> 04:09:04,000
Kakeru: "Sora dear!"

3842
04:09:04,000 --> 04:09:05,000
Sora: "Yeah, what?!"

3843
04:09:05,000 --> 04:09:06,000
Kakeru: "..."

3844
04:09:06,000 --> 04:09:11,000
Sora: "Don't just silently slip me a thousand yen! Quit trying to bribe me!"

3845
04:09:11,000 --> 04:09:15,000
Kakeru: "Buy yourself a cake or something and go home."

3846
04:09:15,000 --> 04:09:19,000
Sora: "Aww, this sucks! Can't believe I'm a third wheel!"

3847
04:09:19,000 --> 04:09:21,000
Miyako: "N-No, of course you aren..."

3848
04:09:21,000 --> 04:09:26,000
Sora: "Whatever! Stupid meanie! You're not my brother, you're a bastard!"

3849
04:09:26,000 --> 04:09:32,000
Kakeru: "Th-The hell, how can you say that? That's our mother you're talking about!"

3850
04:09:32,000 --> 04:09:36,000
Sora: "Oh, right. Can I borrow your copy of Ninecraft?"

3851
04:09:36,000 --> 04:09:43,000
Kakeru: "Jeez, you stopped freaking out in a hurry. Whatever, take it and the whole system with you."

3852
04:09:43,000 --> 04:09:47,000
Sora: "Yay! Okay, see ya! Make out and go to hell, you two!"

3853
04:09:47,000 --> 04:09:52,000
*Sora packs the game system on my shelf into her bag and exits my apartment.*

3854
04:09:52,000 --> 04:09:56,000
*The click of the door closing comes from the entryway.*

3855
04:09:56,000 --> 04:10:01,000
*I take a short trip to the entryway, lock the door, and rush back.*

3856
04:10:01,000 --> 04:10:05,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry. I didn't mean to make Sora-chan angry."

3857
04:10:05,000 --> 04:10:10,000
Kakeru: "Oh, don't worry. She's not angry. She always acts like that."

3858
04:10:10,000 --> 04:10:11,000
Miyako: "Really?"

3859
04:10:11,000 --> 04:10:15,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, it's fine. So what did you really want?"

3860
04:10:15,000 --> 04:10:18,000
Miyako: "Um, well... Nothing... in particular..."

3861
04:10:18,000 --> 04:10:19,000
Miyako: "..."

3862
04:10:19,000 --> 04:10:24,000
Miyako: "I was just thinking... we haven't had a moment to ourselves today."

3863
04:10:24,000 --> 04:10:27,000
*She says in a tiny voice, fidgeting.*

3864
04:10:27,000 --> 04:10:30,000
*Her whispered words pierce my heart.*

3865
04:10:30,000 --> 04:10:37,000
Miyako: "I-I'm sorry. I know you wanted to make sure I could get home while it was still light out."

3866
04:10:37,000 --> 04:10:38,000
Kakeru: "No..."

3867
04:10:38,000 --> 04:10:40,000
*I slowly shake my head.*

3868
04:10:40,000 --> 04:10:41,000
*And I take her hand.*

3869
04:10:41,000 --> 04:10:44,000
Kakeru: "I wanted to be alone with you as well."

3870
04:10:44,000 --> 04:10:45,000
Miyako: "Haha. Good."

3871
04:10:45,000 --> 04:10:47,000
*Miyako squeezes my hand.*

3872
04:10:47,000 --> 04:10:51,000
*The dark conversation from a minute ago is only a memory now.*

3873
04:10:51,000 --> 04:10:53,000
*I would love to stay like this.*

3874
04:10:53,000 --> 04:10:55,000
*For a day. For a week.*

3875
04:10:55,000 --> 04:10:59,000
*It even makes me wish we could live together, just the two of us.*

3876
04:10:59,000 --> 04:11:02,000
*"You can stay the night, if you like."*

3877
04:11:02,000 --> 04:11:07,000
*If only I could bring myself to say that. But it's far too embarrassing.*

3878
04:11:07,000 --> 04:11:14,000
*So instead, I put up a brave front, pretending to be an ordinary guy who's worried for his girlfriend.*

3879
04:11:14,000 --> 04:11:18,000
Kakeru: "You should probably head home, before it gets dark."

3880
04:11:18,000 --> 04:11:19,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

3881
04:11:19,000 --> 04:11:20,000
Kakeru: "..."

3882
04:11:20,000 --> 04:11:21,000
Miyako: "..."

3883
04:11:21,000 --> 04:11:24,000
*I start my day a little earlier than usual.*

3884
04:11:24,000 --> 04:11:29,000
*After meeting up with Miyako and Sora, we wait for Kosaka-senpai to appear.*

3885
04:11:29,000 --> 04:11:32,000
*She should be coming any moment now.*

3886
04:11:32,000 --> 04:11:33,000
Kakeru: "Miyako."

3887
04:11:33,000 --> 04:11:34,000
Miyako: "Yes?"

3888
04:11:34,000 --> 04:11:40,000
Kakeru: "I know you have reservations about using your power. Thanks for doing this."

3889
04:11:40,000 --> 04:11:48,000
Miyako: "It's okay. We have to get as much info on the User as possible. The way I see it, I'm using it in self-defense."

3890
04:11:48,000 --> 04:11:49,000
Kakeru: "Makes sense."

3891
04:11:49,000 --> 04:11:52,000
Sora: "So, hey, yesterday I had this idea."

3892
04:11:52,000 --> 04:11:53,000
Miyako: "What idea?"

3893
04:11:53,000 --> 04:12:02,000
Sora: "If you'd really rather not use your power, why not just ask her about it? Walk up and say, 'So, how was the meetup?' or whatever."

3894
04:12:02,000 --> 04:12:06,000
Kakeru: "That would be fine, if Kosaka-senpai were on our side."

3895
04:12:06,000 --> 04:12:08,000
Sora: "You think she's an enemy?"

3896
04:12:08,000 --> 04:12:14,000
Kakeru: "I'd like to think she's not, but at the very least, she's been a nuisance to us."

3897
04:12:14,000 --> 04:12:19,000
Miyako: "She's tried to use her powers on Kakeru-kun twice already."

3898
04:12:19,000 --> 04:12:26,000
Sora: "Whoa, yeah, she's a total security risk. I didn't know. Cool, then let's do this the sneaky way."

3899
04:12:26,000 --> 04:12:31,000
Kakeru: "How long does it take you to read a person's memories? A second?"

3900
04:12:31,000 --> 04:12:36,000
Miyako: "Around that long, yes. Still, even though it doesn't take much time..."

3901
04:12:36,000 --> 04:12:37,000
Sora: "Yes?"

3902
04:12:37,000 --> 04:12:48,000
Miyako: "Well, I haven't tested it nearly enough times to be certain, but it seems I find it easiest to read the memories that are foremost in the target's mind?"

3903
04:12:48,000 --> 04:12:51,000
Kakeru: "Ahh... You mentioned that yesterday, too."

3904
04:12:51,000 --> 04:12:55,000
*That's how Miyako learned about my feelings for her.*

3905
04:12:55,000 --> 04:13:01,000
*God, that sure was awful. But I suppose I have that to thank for our relationship.*

3906
04:13:01,000 --> 04:13:03,000
*Guess I can't complain.*

3907
04:13:03,000 --> 04:13:09,000
Kakeru: "So if the offline meetup was no big deal for her, you may not be able to read it."

3908
04:13:09,000 --> 04:13:10,000
Miyako: "Maybe, yes."

3909
04:13:10,000 --> 04:13:21,000
Kakeru: "Hmm. So, then, you need to use your power right when she's thinking about it, right? But I guess we'd have to get really lucky for that to happen, huh."

3910
04:13:21,000 --> 04:13:26,000
Sora: "Look, how about we just go for it? We won't know till we try."

3911
04:13:26,000 --> 04:13:28,000
Miyako: "Yeah, I agree."

3912
04:13:28,000 --> 04:13:40,000
Kakeru: "I'm glad we have you on our side, Sora. It would be tough for Miyako to evade detection while using her power in public, without you using yours to mask her presence."

3913
04:13:40,000 --> 04:13:47,000
Sora: "So, uh, while I'm happy you're putting so much faith in me and all, my power is actually pretty shoddy."

3914
04:13:47,000 --> 04:13:54,000
Miyako: "No, I think it's amazing. It was so cool watching you slip her that letter without being noticed."

3915
04:13:54,000 --> 04:14:02,000
Sora: "I mean, it's useful in the right circumstances, but it sure does have its limitations, like I mentioned before."

3916
04:14:02,000 --> 04:14:04,000
Kakeru: "Like what? I forgot."

3917
04:14:04,000 --> 04:14:09,000
Sora: "So like, I've been using my power on both me and Miya this whole time."

3918
04:14:09,000 --> 04:14:10,000
Miyako: "Huh?!"

3919
04:14:10,000 --> 04:14:13,000
Kakeru: "But I can see you both just fine."

3920
04:14:13,000 --> 04:14:22,000
Sora: "And that right there is the limitation. My power just makes things suuuuuper hard to notice. It's not like it turns things invisible."

3921
04:14:22,000 --> 04:14:29,000
Sora: "Basically, using my power during a conversation or when someone is already aware of me won't do squat."

3922
04:14:29,000 --> 04:14:33,000
Kakeru: "What if I looked away from you two for a moment?"

3923
04:14:33,000 --> 04:14:40,000
Sora: "I mean, it's not like you've been staring at us the whole time. It doesn't have much effect on you."

3924
04:14:40,000 --> 04:14:47,000
Sora: "I've used my power around you a few times in the past, too, but you've never lost track of me once."

3925
04:14:47,000 --> 04:14:53,000
Sora: "My guess is, you love me so much that I could never erase my presence from your heart!"

3926
04:14:53,000 --> 04:14:54,000
Kakeru: "Hmm."

3927
04:14:54,000 --> 04:14:58,000
Kakeru: "So, yeah, we should try to divert Senpai just in case."

3928
04:14:58,000 --> 04:15:02,000
Sora: "Yeah, good idea, but don't just ignore me, you jerk."

3929
04:15:02,000 --> 04:15:07,000
Kakeru: "I would never. I'll be counting on you to get the job done, Miss Sora."

3930
04:15:07,000 --> 04:15:09,000
Sora: "Yes, sir! Leave it to me!"

3931
04:15:09,000 --> 04:15:12,000
Miyako: "How are we going to distract her, exactly?"

3932
04:15:12,000 --> 04:15:24,000
Kakeru: "I'll do it. It'll be a bit risky, but I'll try talking to her, and I'll mention the meetup. If I make her think about it, it should be easier for you to read the memory, right?"

3933
04:15:24,000 --> 04:15:28,000
Miyako: "Oh, yeah, I think so, but will you be okay?"

3934
04:15:28,000 --> 04:15:37,000
Kakeru: "I'll be careful of her powers... Well, I say that, but I still don't know exactly what I should do if she does use them on me."

3935
04:15:37,000 --> 04:15:43,000
Kakeru: "Well, I'm the only one without powers here. I've gotta do something to earn my keep."

3936
04:15:43,000 --> 04:15:45,000
Miyako: "Be careful, okay?"

3937
04:15:45,000 --> 04:15:46,000
Kakeru: "Sure will."

3938
04:15:46,000 --> 04:15:49,000
Sora: "Oh, here comes the lovestruck royal guard."

3939
04:15:49,000 --> 04:15:54,000
Kakeru: "I'm going to wait here. You two get some distance from me."

3940
04:15:54,000 --> 04:15:55,000
Miyako: "Okay."

3941
04:15:55,000 --> 04:16:00,000
Sora: "Alright, here we go. I'll keep my power on while we take our positions."

3942
04:16:00,000 --> 04:16:01,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

3943
04:16:01,000 --> 04:16:05,000
*Miyako and Sora split off, heading over by the convenience store.*

3944
04:16:05,000 --> 04:16:13,000
*My eyes flit towards Kosaka-senpai for a moment, and even in just that split second, I lose sight of the two of them.*

3945
04:16:13,000 --> 04:16:15,000
*Huh. Sora's powers are pretty cool.*

3946
04:16:15,000 --> 04:16:23,000
*...Though, if I keep gawking in their direction, there won't be much of a point in them trying to keep out of sight.*

3947
04:16:23,000 --> 04:16:30,000
*I pull out my phone and send them a message saying, "Once I start talking to her, it's go time."*

3948
04:16:30,000 --> 04:16:36,000
*I then pretend like I'm playing with my phone, waiting for Kosaka-senpai to arrive.*

3949
04:16:36,000 --> 04:16:39,000
*Now, if all goes according to plan...*

3950
04:16:39,000 --> 04:16:42,000
Haruka: "Good morning to you, Kakeru-sama."

3951
04:16:42,000 --> 04:16:43,000
*Bingo.*

3952
04:16:43,000 --> 04:16:46,000
*I knew she would make first contact.*

3953
04:16:46,000 --> 04:16:48,000
*I try to play it cool.*

3954
04:16:48,000 --> 04:16:50,000
Kakeru: "Oh, hey there."

3955
04:16:50,000 --> 04:16:53,000
Haruka: "Were you by any chance waiting for me?"

3956
04:16:53,000 --> 04:16:59,000
Kakeru: "Oh, sorry, no. I'm actually waiting for my sister. She and I meet up every morning."

3957
04:16:59,000 --> 04:17:04,000
Haruka: "Ahh, the chirpy girl. We often end up on the same train. Hah hah hah."

3958
04:17:04,000 --> 04:17:06,000
*She delicately covers a giggle.*

3959
04:17:06,000 --> 04:17:08,000
*Behind her stands the Stud Brigade.*

3960
04:17:08,000 --> 04:17:18,000
*They don't seem a bit displeased with me even though I have their queen's attention, and instead all stand around waiting politely, positively beaming.*

3961
04:17:18,000 --> 04:17:21,000
*Man, she really did a number on these guys.*

3962
04:17:21,000 --> 04:17:24,000
*Honestly, seeing this pisses me off.*

3963
04:17:24,000 --> 04:17:31,000
*So it's not surprising when my temper flares up and I let a rather sarcastic quip leave my mouth.*

3964
04:17:31,000 --> 04:17:35,000
Kakeru: "Wooow, just look at all these friends you have."

3965
04:17:35,000 --> 04:17:37,000
Haruka: "Oh, but you're mistaken."

3966
04:17:37,000 --> 04:17:38,000
Kakeru: "Come again?"

3967
04:17:38,000 --> 04:17:40,000
Haruka: "These are my bodyguards."

3968
04:17:40,000 --> 04:17:42,000
Kakeru: "Bodyguards..."

3969
04:17:42,000 --> 04:17:44,000
*Her smile looks strained.*

3970
04:17:44,000 --> 04:17:47,000
*Though she may not even realize that herself.*

3971
04:17:47,000 --> 04:17:59,000
*It would be ridiculous to compare this level of deed to the murderer, but Kosaka-senpai is certainly showing the same lack of restraint in exercising her powers as the Evil Eye's User.*

3972
04:17:59,000 --> 04:18:03,000
*Moreover, what if there's a User among these bodyguards of hers?*

3973
04:18:03,000 --> 04:18:10,000
*What if her goal at the offline meetup was to collect a few guys with powers for her little army?*

3974
04:18:10,000 --> 04:18:18,000
*If she can control even a User, there's a possibility that the Evil Eye's User is standing docilely behind her.*

3975
04:18:18,000 --> 04:18:23,000
*That would be awfully convenient for our information gathering, but...*

3976
04:18:23,000 --> 04:18:25,000
Haruka: "Whatever is the matter?"

3977
04:18:25,000 --> 04:18:34,000
Kakeru: "Oh, nothing big. I was just thinking about how they treat you like a princess, online and offline both. I wish I were so lucky."

3978
04:18:34,000 --> 04:18:41,000
Haruka: "Oh, you. Heh heh heh. Why, you could fulfill that very wish if I were to make you my companion."

3979
04:18:41,000 --> 04:18:49,000
Kakeru: "I'll pass on that. Your fans online would be in uproar. I peek into the Leaves of Agastya forum from time to time."

3980
04:18:49,000 --> 04:18:54,000
Haruka: "Oh, yes. However, I haven't actually met any of those people before."

3981
04:18:54,000 --> 04:18:57,000
Kakeru: "I thought you had an offline meetup?"

3982
04:18:57,000 --> 04:18:59,000
Haruka: "Yes, a few days ago."

3983
04:18:59,000 --> 04:19:02,000
Kakeru: "Were there any genuine Users there?"

3984
04:19:02,000 --> 04:19:05,000
Haruka: "Good question. I wonder that myself."

3985
04:19:05,000 --> 04:19:09,000
*She smiles knowingly, perhaps trying to raise my hopes.*

3986
04:19:09,000 --> 04:19:12,000
*Yeah, no duh she's keeping it secret.*

3987
04:19:12,000 --> 04:19:16,000
Haruka: "Well then, till we meet again, Kakeru-sama."

3988
04:19:16,000 --> 04:19:18,000
Kakeru: "Yes, see you around."

3989
04:19:18,000 --> 04:19:23,000
*Senpai takes the hem of her skirt and gives an overdramatic curtsy.*

3990
04:19:23,000 --> 04:19:32,000
*I breathe a sigh of relief, happy to have escaped her trying to use her powers on me, and watch the queen's procession file by.*

3991
04:19:32,000 --> 04:19:36,000
*Now then, I wonder if they managed to read her memories.*

3992
04:19:36,000 --> 04:19:39,000
*I take a look around and spot the two immediately.*

3993
04:19:39,000 --> 04:19:43,000
*They're walking towards me, so I go to meet them halfway.*

3994
04:19:43,000 --> 04:19:44,000
Kakeru: "Did it work?"

3995
04:19:44,000 --> 04:19:46,000
Sora: "Seems like it did!"

3996
04:19:46,000 --> 04:19:47,000
Miyako: "Yes, but..."

3997
04:19:47,000 --> 04:19:53,000
Kakeru: "We don't know if anyone is listening in, so let's not talk about this here."

3998
04:19:53,000 --> 04:19:55,000
Miyako: "Oh, good point."

3999
04:19:55,000 --> 04:19:59,000
Kakeru: "Let's chat on LING. That should be a bit safer."

4000
04:19:59,000 --> 04:20:01,000
Miyako: "Okay, sounds good."

4001
04:20:01,000 --> 04:20:04,000
Sora: "You better keep me in the loop!"

4002
04:20:04,000 --> 04:20:10,000
Miyako: "Yeah, I'll explain in a group chat. I think I gleaned some useful information."

4003
04:20:10,000 --> 04:20:16,000
Kakeru: "Well, we have to make sure that the culprit doesn't pick up on that. Let's go."

4004
04:20:16,000 --> 04:20:17,000
Miyako: "Right."

4005
04:20:17,000 --> 04:20:22,000
Sora: "Aww, man. Can I just skip today? Using my power sure does make me hungry."

4006
04:20:22,000 --> 04:20:24,000
Kakeru: "Here, take it."

4007
04:20:24,000 --> 04:20:27,000
Sora: "Huh? You're giving me your lunch?"

4008
04:20:27,000 --> 04:20:31,000
Kakeru: "I'll just buy something at the school store."

4009
04:20:31,000 --> 04:20:33,000
Sora: "Yay, I love you, Onii-chan. ☆"

4010
04:20:33,000 --> 04:20:39,000
Miyako: "Haha, Kakeru-kun, you really dote on Sora-chan, don't you? I'm a little jealous."

4011
04:20:39,000 --> 04:20:43,000
Sora: "Oh dear, I never wanted thought I'd end up a homewrecker."

4012
04:20:43,000 --> 04:20:48,000
Miyako: "Unbelievable! To think my boyfriend would cheat on me so brazenly."

4013
04:20:48,000 --> 04:20:49,000
Kakeru: "Hush you."

4014
04:20:49,000 --> 04:20:53,000
*I snap back at them, and for some reason they both grin.*

4015
04:20:53,000 --> 04:21:00,000
*Their personalities aren't very similar, but Sora and Miyako seem to end up on the same wavelength a lot.*

4016
04:21:00,000 --> 04:21:07,000
*I guess it's nice that they get along, but I've about had it up to here with the tag-team teasing.*

4017
04:21:07,000 --> 04:21:09,000
Kakeru: "C'mon, let's go."

4018
04:21:09,000 --> 04:21:11,000
Sora: "Yes, sir. Right away, sir."

4019
04:21:11,000 --> 04:21:12,000
Miyako: "Okaaay."

4020
04:21:12,000 --> 04:21:20,000
*I take the lead as Miyako and Sora share their regular "you can put your bag in the basket" exchange, and we head for school.*

4021
04:21:20,000 --> 04:21:25,000
*I sit impatiently through morning classes, waiting for lunchtime to roll around.*

4022
04:21:25,000 --> 04:21:31,000
*I still haven't gotten a message from Miyako. She's much too strait-laced to text in class.*

4023
04:21:31,000 --> 04:21:37,000
*Probably would be better to save this conversation until after school, all things considered.*

4024
04:21:37,000 --> 04:21:45,000
*As much as I don't want to let the Evil Eye's User get the upper hand on us, rushing things isn't going to help.*

4025
04:21:45,000 --> 04:21:49,000
*Just as I settle my internal debate, my phone vibrates.*

4026
04:21:49,000 --> 04:21:56,000
*To my surprise, though, it's not Miyako, but rather Sora. She's gotten impatient and is demanding a report.*

4027
04:21:56,000 --> 04:22:03,000
*I glance over at Miyako to see her excusing herself from her friends' lunch group so she can send a message.*

4028
04:22:03,000 --> 04:22:06,000
Yoichi: "Hey, Kakeru, are you listening?"

4029
04:22:06,000 --> 04:22:07,000
Kakeru: "Hm? What?"

4030
04:22:07,000 --> 04:22:09,000
Yoichi: "I'm talking about Kujo-san."

4031
04:22:09,000 --> 04:22:10,000
Kakeru: "Oh."

4032
04:22:10,000 --> 04:22:17,000
Yoichi: "I kinda feel like you guys are getting along even better than before she quit talking to you."

4033
04:22:17,000 --> 04:22:19,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, maybe so."

4034
04:22:19,000 --> 04:22:23,000
*I give a noncommittal reply as I fiddle with my phone.*

4035
04:22:23,000 --> 04:22:27,000
*Truth is, I haven't told Yoichi that Miyako and I are going out.*

4036
04:22:27,000 --> 04:22:34,000
*I mean, actually coming out and telling him would just be embarrassing, so why bother, you know?*

4037
04:22:34,000 --> 04:22:41,000
Yoichi: "I sure am glad. I dunno what I would've done if I'd managed to make things awkward between you two."

4038
04:22:41,000 --> 04:22:44,000
*Starting to feel a little guilty here.*

4039
04:22:44,000 --> 04:22:49,000
*If he's this concerned about us, maybe I should just come out and tell him?*

4040
04:22:49,000 --> 04:22:50,000
*...Nah.*

4041
04:22:50,000 --> 04:22:51,000
Yoichi: "More spam?"

4042
04:22:51,000 --> 04:22:53,000
Kakeru: "Naw, my sister."

4043
04:22:53,000 --> 04:22:56,000
Yoichi: "Sora-chan, right? She sure is a cutie."

4044
04:22:56,000 --> 04:22:59,000
Kakeru: "Cute? The hell are you talking about?"

4045
04:22:59,000 --> 04:23:06,000
Yoichi: "She's totally cute. If I were her classmate, I sure as hell wouldn't turn her down, lemme tell you."

4046
04:23:06,000 --> 04:23:12,000
Kakeru: "Might want to wait until you see her personality, before you dig yourself in too deep."

4047
04:23:12,000 --> 04:23:17,000
Yoichi: "Personality can go fuck itself. Tell her I said she's cute."

4048
04:23:17,000 --> 04:23:20,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I'll get right on that."

4049
04:23:20,000 --> 04:23:22,000
Yoichi: "Do it now! Message her!"

4050
04:23:22,000 --> 04:23:24,000
Kakeru: "Alright, alright."

4051
04:23:24,000 --> 04:23:28,000
*With a great show of annoyance, I start typing the message.*

4052
04:23:28,000 --> 04:23:35,000
*This should be good for a laugh, at least, seeing as Sora has a tendency to freak out when you compliment her.*

4053
04:23:35,000 --> 04:23:39,000
*Just when I'm about to hit send, I get a message form Miyako.*

4054
04:23:39,000 --> 04:23:46,000
*It's quite the essay. It would appear she's typed up everything she saw in Kosaka-senpai's memories.*

4055
04:23:46,000 --> 04:23:48,000
*To break it all down...*

4056
04:23:48,000 --> 04:23:50,000
*"An offline meetup took place."*

4057
04:23:50,000 --> 04:23:56,000
*"Boys and girls both, no more than five. No idea who was a User among any of them."*

4058
04:23:56,000 --> 04:24:02,000
*"Two of them, one a boy and one a girl, met up with her again after the offline meetup."*

4059
04:24:02,000 --> 04:24:05,000
*"They can be seen meeting up at the shrine."*

4060
04:24:05,000 --> 04:24:06,000
*...*

4061
04:24:06,000 --> 04:24:07,000
*The shrine, huh?*

4062
04:24:07,000 --> 04:24:08,000
*Interesting.*

4063
04:24:08,000 --> 04:24:13,000
Yoichi: "And? Did she reply, 'I've got such a crush on Yoichi-senpai!'"

4064
04:24:13,000 --> 04:24:16,000
Kakeru: "Hell no. I still haven't sent the message."

4065
04:24:16,000 --> 04:24:18,000
Yoichi: "I bet she will, though!"

4066
04:24:18,000 --> 04:24:22,000
Kakeru: "Even if she does, you're staying away from my sister."

4067
04:24:22,000 --> 04:24:25,000
Yoichi: "Saving her for yourself, eh?"

4068
04:24:25,000 --> 04:24:26,000
Kakeru: "Shut it."

4069
04:24:26,000 --> 04:24:32,000
*While I'm verbally sparring with Yoichi, my mind is working on a completely different problem.*

4070
04:24:32,000 --> 04:24:36,000
*Kosaka-senpai met an unknown boy and girl at the shrine.*

4071
04:24:36,000 --> 04:24:41,000
*And in another branching world, Miyako was murdered at the shrine.*

4072
04:24:41,000 --> 04:24:43,000
*Is this a coincidence?*

4073
04:24:43,000 --> 04:24:45,000
*No. This has to be fate.*

4074
04:24:45,000 --> 04:24:47,000
*The culprit is among those three.*

4075
04:24:47,000 --> 04:24:51,000
*That's exactly why Miyako went to the shrine and got murdered.*

4076
04:24:51,000 --> 04:24:55,000
*She might have seen the culprit, in those memories.*

4077
04:24:55,000 --> 04:25:01,000
Yoichi: "What'd you start looking all serious for? Pretending to be cool for someone?"

4078
04:25:01,000 --> 04:25:03,000
Kakeru: "I'm always serious."

4079
04:25:03,000 --> 04:25:09,000
Yoichi: "Uh-huh, right. You can say whatever you want, as long as you let me at your sister."

4080
04:25:09,000 --> 04:25:11,000
Kakeru: "Pick her up yourself, dude."

4081
04:25:11,000 --> 04:25:15,000
Yoichi: "That's too much of a hassle! Just do it for me!"

4082
04:25:15,000 --> 04:25:22,000
Kakeru: "Christ, you can't even be bothered to try? There's no way I'm letting you date my sister now."

4083
04:25:22,000 --> 04:25:24,000
Yoichi: "You dirty sis-con!"

4084
04:25:24,000 --> 04:25:26,000
Kakeru: "Shut your hole!"

4085
04:25:26,000 --> 04:25:31,000
*Our nonsensical shouting match dissolves into the clamor of the lunchtime break.*

4086
04:25:31,000 --> 04:25:32,000
*...*

4087
04:25:32,000 --> 04:25:35,000
*So they're meeting secretly at the shrine.*

4088
04:25:35,000 --> 04:25:37,000
*Why there of all places?*

4089
04:25:37,000 --> 04:25:42,000
*I doubt she'll know anything, but I do know one person I can ask...*

4090
04:25:42,000 --> 04:25:43,000
Kakeru: "Ms. Naruse!"

4091
04:25:43,000 --> 04:25:44,000
Satsuki: "Yeees?"

4092
04:25:44,000 --> 04:25:53,000
*I exit the classroom as soon as afternoon homeroom ends and call out to Ms. Naruse, already walking towards the faculty office.*

4093
04:25:53,000 --> 04:25:54,000
Satsuki: "What is it?"

4094
04:25:54,000 --> 04:25:57,000
Kakeru: "I have something I'd like to ask."

4095
04:25:57,000 --> 04:26:02,000
Satsuki: "What might that be? Something in class you didn't understand?"

4096
04:26:02,000 --> 04:26:04,000
Kakeru: "Oh, no, nothing like that."

4097
04:26:04,000 --> 04:26:13,000
Satsuki: "Oh, thank God. I was standing here thinking what a pain in the ass it'd be if you were going to ask me something hard."

4098
04:26:13,000 --> 04:26:14,000
Kakeru: "..."

4099
04:26:14,000 --> 04:26:17,000
*I sure do have one hell of a teacher.*

4100
04:26:17,000 --> 04:26:19,000
Satsuki: "So, what is it?"

4101
04:26:19,000 --> 04:26:27,000
Kakeru: "Oh, sorry. Um, not sure how to ask this... Have there been any strange people hanging around the shrine recently?"

4102
04:26:27,000 --> 04:26:33,000
Satsuki: "Hmmm? I mean, there have always been weirdos hanging around there, not just recently."

4103
04:26:33,000 --> 04:26:34,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Really?"

4104
04:26:34,000 --> 04:26:44,000
Satsuki: "Because of the anime, I guess? They just pop up now and then. Some of them have no respect, either. They can be a real hassle to deal with."

4105
04:26:44,000 --> 04:26:47,000
Kakeru: "Ahh, you mentioned that before."

4106
04:26:47,000 --> 04:26:49,000
Satsuki: "So, why are you asking?"

4107
04:26:49,000 --> 04:26:54,000
Kakeru: "Oh, well, I've been passing by on my nightly walks recently."

4108
04:26:54,000 --> 04:27:00,000
Satsuki: "Oh, nighttime specifically? Come to think of it, Dad did say something..."

4109
04:27:00,000 --> 04:27:02,000
Kakeru: "So someone has been there?"

4110
04:27:02,000 --> 04:27:15,000
Satsuki: "He said something like, 'Some youngsters are loitering around.' He was worried, saying that although they weren't causing any real harm, we should keep a close eye on them anyway."

4111
04:27:15,000 --> 04:27:20,000
Kakeru: "Huh. So there actually have been some kids hanging around."

4112
04:27:20,000 --> 04:27:23,000
Satsuki: "Are you in some kind of trouble?"

4113
04:27:23,000 --> 04:27:26,000
Kakeru: "Huh?! Uh, no, nothing like that."

4114
04:27:26,000 --> 04:27:32,000
Satsuki: "You went out of your way to come ask me about this, so I wondered if something was up."

4115
04:27:32,000 --> 04:27:37,000
Kakeru: "I was just curious if they were up to something. Vandalism, or whatever."

4116
04:27:37,000 --> 04:27:43,000
Satsuki: "So, you were concerned for us, I see. Thank you! But, we're fine so far, I think?"

4117
04:27:43,000 --> 04:27:53,000
Satsuki: "Though I must say, as a teacher, I find it a little concerning how late at night they're out. Apparently they're there past nine sometimes."

4118
04:27:53,000 --> 04:27:54,000
Kakeru: "..."

4119
04:27:54,000 --> 04:27:58,000
Satsuki: "'As a teacher? That's rich coming from her.'"

4120
04:27:58,000 --> 04:27:59,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

4121
04:27:59,000 --> 04:28:03,000
Satsuki: "That's what you were thinking just now, right?"

4122
04:28:03,000 --> 04:28:06,000
Kakeru: "No, no. Perish the very thought, ma'am."

4123
04:28:06,000 --> 04:28:14,000
Satsuki: "Niimi-kun, your poker face needs a lot of work. Do remember that, before someone rearranges it for you."

4124
04:28:14,000 --> 04:28:21,000
*Ms. Naruse pats me lightly on the arm with her logbook as she gives a casual goodbye and walks off.*

4125
04:28:21,000 --> 04:28:25,000
*So. They're gathering at the shrine, late at night.*

4126
04:28:25,000 --> 04:28:30,000
*Miyako said there were three people, but there could even be more.*

4127
04:28:30,000 --> 04:28:39,000
*If we assume that the Evil Eye's User is among them, could it be that they're searching for allies, just like how we did at first?*

4128
04:28:39,000 --> 04:28:41,000
*So Kosaka-senpai is an accomplice?*

4129
04:28:41,000 --> 04:28:50,000
*If there are a bunch of Users forming an alliance, all of whom have no qualms about inflicting harm on others, that would spell bad news.*

4130
04:28:50,000 --> 04:29:00,000
*With Sora and Miyako's combined abilities, they can neutralize their opponents while going undetected, but neither of them has mastered their powers.*

4131
04:29:00,000 --> 04:29:06,000
*Nothing is decided yet, but I can't afford to let either of them go to the shrine.*

4132
04:29:06,000 --> 04:29:11,000
*One bad decision could lead to not only Miyako falling victim, but also Sora.*

4133
04:29:11,000 --> 04:29:12,000
*...*

4134
04:29:12,000 --> 04:29:16,000
*My job, as the guy without any powers, is to support them.*

4135
04:29:16,000 --> 04:29:20,000
*It's my responsibility to marshal every resource available.*

4136
04:29:20,000 --> 04:29:23,000
Miyako: "I'll be going in through the back, okay?"

4137
04:29:23,000 --> 04:29:26,000
Kakeru: "Yep. Have a good day at work."

4138
04:29:26,000 --> 04:29:27,000
Miyako: "Thanks."

4139
04:29:27,000 --> 04:29:30,000
Sora: "Laters! Hey, bro, buy me a parfait."

4140
04:29:30,000 --> 04:29:34,000
Kakeru: "You can eat whatever you want, but I ain't paying."

4141
04:29:34,000 --> 04:29:35,000
Sora: "Cheapskate."

4142
04:29:35,000 --> 04:29:40,000
*We part ways with Miyako in front of the cafe and then Sora and I head inside.*

4143
04:29:40,000 --> 04:29:42,000
*We take a seat and order drinks.*

4144
04:29:42,000 --> 04:29:46,000
*I scan the room while putting the glass of water to my lips.*

4145
04:29:46,000 --> 04:29:47,000
*...*

4146
04:29:47,000 --> 04:29:48,000
*Not here yet, huh?*

4147
04:29:48,000 --> 04:29:50,000
Miyako: "Thank you for waiting."

4148
04:29:50,000 --> 04:29:54,000
*Now wearing her work uniform, Miyako brings us our drinks.*

4149
04:29:54,000 --> 04:29:58,000
*She places two cups of coffee side-by-side on the table.*

4150
04:29:58,000 --> 04:30:02,000
Sora: "Damn that's cute. Maybe I should get a job too, huh?"

4151
04:30:02,000 --> 04:30:09,000
Miyako: "Haha, I'll ask my Grandfather if we're accepting part-time applicants. Will there be anything else?"

4152
04:30:09,000 --> 04:30:11,000
Kakeru: "That's it. Appreciate it."

4153
04:30:11,000 --> 04:30:15,000
Miyako: "Please enjoy yourselves, then. Oh, welcome!"

4154
04:30:15,000 --> 04:30:19,000
*Just as Miyako gives us a little nod, the door to the cafe opens.*

4155
04:30:19,000 --> 04:30:20,000
*...*

4156
04:30:20,000 --> 04:30:21,000
*There she is.*

4157
04:30:21,000 --> 04:30:30,000
*Miyako is about to show her to a seat, but I stop her and wave down the girl from across the room, gesturing for her to join us.*

4158
04:30:30,000 --> 04:30:31,000
Noa: "..."

4159
04:30:31,000 --> 04:30:37,000
*She clearly notices ees me, but she ignores me anyway, taking a seat far away from us.*

4160
04:30:37,000 --> 04:30:39,000
*Dammit, still cold as ice.*

4161
04:30:39,000 --> 04:30:41,000
Sora: "So that's the Parfait Queen?"

4162
04:30:41,000 --> 04:30:46,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. You sit tight here, Sora. Miyako, you focus on work."

4163
04:30:46,000 --> 04:30:47,000
Miyako: "R-Right."

4164
04:30:47,000 --> 04:30:51,000
*I get up from my seat and head over to Yuuki's table.*

4165
04:30:51,000 --> 04:30:57,000
*I don't bother with any niceties, instead plopping my rear down in the seat unceremoniously.*

4166
04:30:57,000 --> 04:30:59,000
Noa: "That's not your chair."

4167
04:30:59,000 --> 04:31:01,000
Kakeru: "We need to talk."

4168
04:31:01,000 --> 04:31:02,000
Noa: "Pass."

4169
04:31:02,000 --> 04:31:05,000
Kakeru: "I've got a lead on the Evil Eye's User."

4170
04:31:05,000 --> 04:31:06,000
Noa: "..."

4171
04:31:06,000 --> 04:31:11,000
*After avoiding eye contact this whole time, Yuuki finally looks at me.*

4172
04:31:11,000 --> 04:31:13,000
Kakeru: "Ready to listen?"

4173
04:31:13,000 --> 04:31:14,000
Noa: "Fine."

4174
04:31:14,000 --> 04:31:17,000
Kakeru: "Well, I'm not certain I've got them."

4175
04:31:17,000 --> 04:31:26,000
Noa: "Delaying action until you have certain information is for fools. You have to see the truth of the world with your own eyes."

4176
04:31:26,000 --> 04:31:29,000
Kakeru: "You don't think I'm trying to trap you?"

4177
04:31:29,000 --> 04:31:36,000
Noa: "I don't care either way. I suspect you, regardless, but now I have more things to suspect you of."

4178
04:31:36,000 --> 04:31:37,000
Kakeru: "I see."

4179
04:31:37,000 --> 04:31:42,000
Noa: "...Get to the point already. I come here for relaxation, not annoyance."

4180
04:31:42,000 --> 04:31:46,000
Kakeru: "Before that, I want to confirm your power for myself."

4181
04:31:46,000 --> 04:31:51,000
Noa: "I have no intention of explaining it, which I believe I mentioned already."

4182
04:31:51,000 --> 04:31:59,000
Kakeru: "I wouldn't be able to sleep at night if I gave you intel and you ended up dead because you got in over your head."

4183
04:31:59,000 --> 04:32:06,000
Kakeru: "I'm only telling what I know to someone who would stand a chance against the Evil Eye's User."

4184
04:32:06,000 --> 04:32:07,000
Noa: "..."

4185
04:32:07,000 --> 04:32:08,000
*She glares at me.*

4186
04:32:08,000 --> 04:32:09,000
*I got her this time.*

4187
04:32:09,000 --> 04:32:11,000
*Hook, line, and sinker.*

4188
04:32:11,000 --> 04:32:17,000
Noa: "...I will not reveal any specifics of my ability. However, I will say this much."

4189
04:32:17,000 --> 04:32:22,000
Noa: "The User with petrification powers doesn't stand a chance against me."

4190
04:32:22,000 --> 04:32:24,000
Noa: "The Order is invincible."

4191
04:32:24,000 --> 04:32:26,000
Kakeru: "And why, exactly?"

4192
04:32:26,000 --> 04:32:30,000
Noa: "Because I have a complete understanding of my own powers."

4193
04:32:30,000 --> 04:32:32,000
Kakeru: "You're sure you can win?"

4194
04:32:32,000 --> 04:32:33,000
Noa: "Yes."

4195
04:32:33,000 --> 04:32:36,000
*She answers with a firm, confident smile.*

4196
04:32:36,000 --> 04:32:45,000
*Of course, there's one way she could be so completely certain of her victory. That would be if she is, herself, the Evil Eye's User.*

4197
04:32:45,000 --> 04:32:47,000
*And I can't rule that out.*

4198
04:32:47,000 --> 04:32:55,000
*According to Miyako, the girl she saw in Kosaka's memories was wearing a hood, so she couldn't make out her face.*

4199
04:32:55,000 --> 04:32:58,000
*That hooded girl could very well be Yuuki.*

4200
04:32:58,000 --> 04:33:01,000
*However, I don't think that's likely.*

4201
04:33:01,000 --> 04:33:08,000
*If Yuuki were our Evil Eye User, she would have had a ton of chances to kill both myself and Miyako.*

4202
04:33:08,000 --> 04:33:10,000
Kakeru: "I believe you."

4203
04:33:10,000 --> 04:33:11,000
Noa: "Good for you."

4204
04:33:11,000 --> 04:33:15,000
Kakeru: "And I have a favor to ask, because I trust in your power."

4205
04:33:15,000 --> 04:33:18,000
Noa: "What about the info you promised?"

4206
04:33:18,000 --> 04:33:20,000
Kakeru: "Just hear me out first."

4207
04:33:20,000 --> 04:33:21,000
Noa: "No thanks."

4208
04:33:21,000 --> 04:33:26,000
Kakeru: "I'm not asking you to do something for free. Let's negotiate."

4209
04:33:26,000 --> 04:33:27,000
Noa: "..."

4210
04:33:27,000 --> 04:33:29,000
*Yuuki raises an eyebrow at me.*

4211
04:33:29,000 --> 04:33:35,000
*Hah, I knew it! I had a feeling I could reel her in if I played to her melodramatic side.*

4212
04:33:35,000 --> 04:33:42,000
Kakeru: "I managed to find out where the Evil Eye's User might be meeting up, along with a few associates."

4213
04:33:42,000 --> 04:33:43,000
Noa: "Where?"

4214
04:33:43,000 --> 04:33:46,000
Kakeru: "Afraid I can't tell you that yet."

4215
04:33:46,000 --> 04:33:48,000
Noa: "...What do you want me to do?"

4216
04:33:48,000 --> 04:33:56,000
Kakeru: "Come along with us. There might be more than one of them. The more we can have on our side, the better our chances."

4217
04:33:56,000 --> 04:33:58,000
Noa: "You want a hired gun."

4218
04:33:58,000 --> 04:33:59,000
Kakeru: "Yup."

4219
04:33:59,000 --> 04:34:01,000
Noa: "And what do I get in return?"

4220
04:34:01,000 --> 04:34:05,000
Kakeru: "I thought... the info would be good enough?"

4221
04:34:05,000 --> 04:34:07,000
Noa: "Not a chance in hell."

4222
04:34:07,000 --> 04:34:11,000
Kakeru: "Okay, I'll pay for your parfaits, for a whole week."

4223
04:34:11,000 --> 04:34:12,000
Noa: "Deal!"

4224
04:34:12,000 --> 04:34:14,000
*Wow, talk about enthusiastic.*

4225
04:34:14,000 --> 04:34:17,000
*That was, honestly, the last response I expected.*

4226
04:34:17,000 --> 04:34:20,000
*But whatever. I'm just glad we made a deal.*

4227
04:34:20,000 --> 04:34:23,000
Kakeru: "We couldn't do this without you. Thanks."

4228
04:34:23,000 --> 04:34:25,000
Noa: "When does this all go down?"

4229
04:34:25,000 --> 04:34:35,000
Kakeru: "Tonight. We're either going to neutralize the Evil Eye's User, or we're going to prove that this group of loiterers is unrelated to them."

4230
04:34:35,000 --> 04:34:38,000
Noa: "Understood. You're paying today."

4231
04:34:38,000 --> 04:34:41,000
Kakeru: "Payment up front, huh? Fine."

4232
04:34:41,000 --> 04:34:48,000
*I signal with my hand, calling Miyako, who's been keeping an eye on us the whole time, over to the table.*

4233
04:34:48,000 --> 04:34:50,000
Miyako: "Are you ready to order?"

4234
04:34:50,000 --> 04:34:54,000
Kakeru: "Uh, you always get a chocolate parfait, right?"

4235
04:34:54,000 --> 04:34:57,000
Noa: "Not today. I'll take the fruit parfait."

4236
04:34:57,000 --> 04:34:59,000
Kakeru: "There's a fruit parfait?"

4237
04:34:59,000 --> 04:35:02,000
*I pick up the menu and look it over.*

4238
04:35:02,000 --> 04:35:03,000
*...*

4239
04:35:03,000 --> 04:35:04,000
*Goddammit.*

4240
04:35:04,000 --> 04:35:09,000
Kakeru: "The fruit one... seems rather pricey, compared to the chocolate one."

4241
04:35:09,000 --> 04:35:12,000
Noa: "No duh. It's chock full of fresh fruit."

4242
04:35:12,000 --> 04:35:15,000
Kakeru: "Maybe you could get the chocolate..."

4243
04:35:15,000 --> 04:35:20,000
Noa: "You didn't place any limits on the kind of parfait, when we made our deal."

4244
04:35:20,000 --> 04:35:21,000
Kakeru: "..."

4245
04:35:21,000 --> 04:35:25,000
Noa: "If you'd like to annul our agreement, I don't mind."

4246
04:35:25,000 --> 04:35:26,000
Kakeru: "..."

4247
04:35:26,000 --> 04:35:28,000
Kakeru: "...W-Waitress?"

4248
04:35:28,000 --> 04:35:30,000
Miyako: "Huh? Oh, yes?"

4249
04:35:30,000 --> 04:35:35,000
Kakeru: "Bring us the most ludicrously expensive parfait on the menu...!"

4250
04:35:35,000 --> 04:35:42,000
Miyako: "R-Right. The fruit parfait, right? Please hold tight and I'll be right back with your order."

4251
04:35:42,000 --> 04:35:46,000
*After she gives a little bow, Miyako walks to the kitchen.*

4252
04:35:46,000 --> 04:35:49,000
Noa: "I'm looking forward to this week."

4253
04:35:49,000 --> 04:35:50,000
Kakeru: "...!"

4254
04:35:50,000 --> 04:35:54,000
*Yuuki's merciless dig makes me start grinding my molars.*

4255
04:35:54,000 --> 04:36:00,000
*Well, at this point, I know of at least one thing dying in this branch: my wallet.*

4256
04:36:00,000 --> 04:36:13,000
*Per Ms. Naruse's account, the three are sometimes loitering around until after nine at night. I suspect they'll split up at eight, at the earliest, so I begin staking out the shrine around seven.*

4257
04:36:13,000 --> 04:36:19,000
*Sora and I grab a quick bite for dinner and head to the meetup spot near the shrine.*

4258
04:36:19,000 --> 04:36:25,000
*Miyako, who has wrapped up her shift early, and Yuuki, our mercenary, show up before too long.*

4259
04:36:25,000 --> 04:36:27,000
Noa: "What's the plan?"

4260
04:36:27,000 --> 04:36:37,000
Kakeru: "We'll wait in ambush on the grounds using Sora's power. Once the three of them show up, Miyako will use her power to read their memories."

4261
04:36:37,000 --> 04:36:44,000
Miyako: "If I can identify the culprit, I'll steal their Artifact, thereby neutralizing their powers. Right?"

4262
04:36:44,000 --> 04:36:47,000
Kakeru: "Yep. If they happen to notice us..."

4263
04:36:47,000 --> 04:36:49,000
Noa: "That's when I step in."

4264
04:36:49,000 --> 04:36:57,000
Kakeru: "Right. If and when the time comes, you'll be up. Sora, can you start using your power, so we can start our stakeout?"

4265
04:36:57,000 --> 04:37:03,000
Sora: "So, I do think it'd be a good idea to set up our defenses in advance, but..."

4266
04:37:03,000 --> 04:37:05,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

4267
04:37:05,000 --> 04:37:13,000
Sora: "I just put it all together this morning, but I feel like my power gets less effective the more people I'm using it on."

4268
04:37:13,000 --> 04:37:17,000
Miyako: "There are four of us. Is that going to be too hard?"

4269
04:37:17,000 --> 04:37:27,000
Sora: "I don't think it will have have absolutely no effect, but I do think it will be considerably weaker than when I use it on one or two people."

4270
04:37:27,000 --> 04:37:33,000
Noa: "A support enchantment. The larger the area of effect, the less potent it is."

4271
04:37:33,000 --> 04:37:41,000
Sora: "Right, right, something like that. I'm worried they'll see right through us if we try to coast on my powers."

4272
04:37:41,000 --> 04:37:42,000
Kakeru: "Hmm, I see."

4273
04:37:42,000 --> 04:37:43,000
Kakeru: "..."

4274
04:37:43,000 --> 04:37:49,000
Kakeru: "Okay then. If the worst happens, prioritize protecting yourself and Miyako."

4275
04:37:49,000 --> 04:37:51,000
Sora: "What about you?"

4276
04:37:51,000 --> 04:37:58,000
Kakeru: "Dispel it for me. I'm a guy; I should be covering you all. And Yuuki, you're strong, right?"

4277
04:37:58,000 --> 04:38:00,000
Noa: "Yes. Don't worry about me."

4278
04:38:00,000 --> 04:38:04,000
Kakeru: "Let's go, then. Miyako, I'm counting on you too."

4279
04:38:04,000 --> 04:38:06,000
Miyako: "Yeah. I won't let you down."

4280
04:38:06,000 --> 04:38:09,000
*We start walking, heading for the shrine grounds.*

4281
04:38:09,000 --> 04:38:16,000
*I take a few steps before I realize that Yuuki isn't budging from where she stands, so I turn and look back.*

4282
04:38:16,000 --> 04:38:17,000
Kakeru: "What's up?"

4283
04:38:17,000 --> 04:38:18,000
Noa: "Just one thing."

4284
04:38:18,000 --> 04:38:19,000
Kakeru: "Okay."

4285
04:38:19,000 --> 04:38:23,000
Noa: "Don't think you can use me as a shield for Kujo-san."

4286
04:38:23,000 --> 04:38:24,000
Kakeru: "..."

4287
04:38:24,000 --> 04:38:34,000
Noa: "The only reason you're pretending to trust me with no confirmation of my ability is because you simply want someone to serve as a decoy."

4288
04:38:34,000 --> 04:38:39,000
Noa: "You were never relying on my power in the first place. I'm right, aren't I?"

4289
04:38:39,000 --> 04:38:42,000
Kakeru: "Mind if I just don't answer?"

4290
04:38:42,000 --> 04:38:46,000
Noa: "...I'm still going to earn those fruit parfaits."

4291
04:38:46,000 --> 04:38:48,000
Kakeru: "I'll be counting on you."

4292
04:38:48,000 --> 04:38:49,000
Noa: "..."

4293
04:38:49,000 --> 04:38:51,000
*Yuuki harrumphs at me and walks by.*

4294
04:38:51,000 --> 04:38:53,000
*I breathe out a sigh and catch up.*

4295
04:38:53,000 --> 04:39:05,000
*To be honest, she's wrong. It wasn't my intention at all to use her as a decoy. However, I still opted not to answer, deciding that being coy was the best way to keep a hold on Yuuki.*

4296
04:39:05,000 --> 04:39:13,000
*It goes without saying that if Miyako or Sora were put into harm's way, I'd be stuck making some hard decisions.*

4297
04:39:13,000 --> 04:39:20,000
*But make no mistake. The first person to be used as a decoy—the first person to be sacrificed—would be me.*

4298
04:39:20,000 --> 04:39:24,000
*I have no intention of just being the guy giving orders.*

4299
04:39:24,000 --> 04:39:30,000
*I catch up to Miyako and Sora, who have stopped near the temple gate, and stand next to them.*

4300
04:39:30,000 --> 04:39:35,000
*Because the shrine grounds are barely lit, it's tough to see much of anything.*

4301
04:39:35,000 --> 04:39:44,000
*Where the Naruse family lives is actually a ways away from the shrine itself, so this is pretty much a perfect spot for clandestine meetups.*

4302
04:39:44,000 --> 04:39:46,000
Miyako: "Where should we hide?"

4303
04:39:46,000 --> 04:39:50,000
Kakeru: "Let me see... Sora, how's your power doing?"

4304
04:39:50,000 --> 04:39:56,000
Sora: "I'm already using it. We'll probably get found out in no time if we speak too loudly."

4305
04:39:56,000 --> 04:40:02,000
Kakeru: "Roger that. For the time being, let's move closer to the edge over there..."

4306
04:40:02,000 --> 04:40:03,000
Noa: "...Wait."

4307
04:40:03,000 --> 04:40:05,000
Miyako: "What's the matter?"

4308
04:40:05,000 --> 04:40:06,000
Noa: "..."

4309
04:40:06,000 --> 04:40:08,000
*Yuuki silently points her finger.*

4310
04:40:08,000 --> 04:40:09,000
Kakeru: "...?"

4311
04:40:09,000 --> 04:40:12,000
*It's so dark that I can't make much out.*

4312
04:40:12,000 --> 04:40:15,000
*After straining my vision, I notice.*

4313
04:40:15,000 --> 04:40:19,000
*There's a black shadow in the midst of the dark grounds.*

4314
04:40:19,000 --> 04:40:22,000
*A person? At least, it definitely looks like it.*

4315
04:40:22,000 --> 04:40:25,000
Sora: "Huh? There's someone here already?"

4316
04:40:25,000 --> 04:40:27,000
Miyako: "Wh-What should we do?"

4317
04:40:27,000 --> 04:40:31,000
Noa: "Calm down. They don't seem to have noticed us yet."

4318
04:40:31,000 --> 04:40:35,000
Kakeru: "Let's go around through there and approach slowly."

4319
04:40:35,000 --> 04:40:41,000
*We get some distance from the silhouetted figure, moving into the deeper shadows.*

4320
04:40:41,000 --> 04:40:45,000
*From there, we creep towards them, sticking to the darker areas.*

4321
04:40:45,000 --> 04:40:53,000
*Acting as carefully as if we weren't under the effects of Sora's powers, we close the distance carefully and silently.*

4322
04:40:53,000 --> 04:40:55,000
*Miyako was murdered here.*

4323
04:40:55,000 --> 04:41:00,000
*There's a very real possibility that silhouetted figure is our murderer.*

4324
04:41:00,000 --> 04:41:04,000
*The culprit should be on the lookout for us, especially Miyako.*

4325
04:41:04,000 --> 04:41:06,000
*We can't afford any mistakes.*

4326
04:41:06,000 --> 04:41:12,000
*If possible, I want to settle the score tonight and start leading a peaceful life.*

4327
04:41:12,000 --> 04:41:17,000
*With very step, the silhouette grows closer, and my pulse quickens.*

4328
04:41:17,000 --> 04:41:23,000
*I wish we could get within thirty feet of them, but there's nothing to use as cover.*

4329
04:41:23,000 --> 04:41:26,000
Sora: "We shouldn't get any closer than this."

4330
04:41:26,000 --> 04:41:27,000
Kakeru: "Alright."

4331
04:41:27,000 --> 04:41:30,000
Miyako: "Let's just stay here and keep a lookout."

4332
04:41:30,000 --> 04:41:38,000
Kakeru: "Right. There's already one here, so the odds are good the other two will come. Until all three get here..."

4333
04:41:38,000 --> 04:41:39,000
Noa: "..."

4334
04:41:39,000 --> 04:41:40,000
Kakeru: "Hey, wait!"

4335
04:41:40,000 --> 04:41:47,000
*Yuuki ignores our discussion and tries to step out of cover alone, but I snag her arm before she can.*

4336
04:41:47,000 --> 04:41:49,000
Kakeru: "What are you doing?"

4337
04:41:49,000 --> 04:41:52,000
Noa: "There's no point in just keeping watch."

4338
04:41:52,000 --> 04:41:53,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

4339
04:41:53,000 --> 04:42:00,000
Noa: "I have good night vision, so trust me on this one. There's no way that guy's going to notice us."

4340
04:42:00,000 --> 04:42:02,000
Kakeru: "That guy...? Ah!"

4341
04:42:02,000 --> 04:42:03,000
Miyako: "Y-Yuuki-san!"

4342
04:42:03,000 --> 04:42:04,000
Noa: "..."

4343
04:42:04,000 --> 04:42:11,000
*Yuuki shakes off my hand, ignoring Miyako's plea, and brazenly walks up to the silhouetted figure.*

4344
04:42:11,000 --> 04:42:16,000
Sora: "Uh... My power's not gonna work on her if she gets too far from me."

4345
04:42:16,000 --> 04:42:20,000
Kakeru: "Crap, I guess I have to...! You two, stay here."

4346
04:42:20,000 --> 04:42:21,000
Miyako: "B-But..."

4347
04:42:21,000 --> 04:42:25,000
Kakeru: "Don't worry about me. Sora, take care of Miyako."

4348
04:42:25,000 --> 04:42:26,000
Sora: "Yes, sir."

4349
04:42:26,000 --> 04:42:28,000
*I rush to catch up with Yuuki.*

4350
04:42:28,000 --> 04:42:30,000
*What the hell is she thinking?*

4351
04:42:30,000 --> 04:42:33,000
*Maybe inviting her here was a mistake.*

4352
04:42:33,000 --> 04:42:42,000
*I'm working myself into a frenzy... except that the closer I get to the figure, and the clearer I can make it out, the less agitated I feel.*

4353
04:42:42,000 --> 04:42:44,000
*My legs get heavy. My steps drag.*

4354
04:42:44,000 --> 04:42:47,000
*There's no way that guy's going to notice us.*

4355
04:42:47,000 --> 04:42:48,000
*She was right.*

4356
04:42:48,000 --> 04:42:50,000
*It is, indeed, a guy.*

4357
04:42:50,000 --> 04:42:51,000
Kakeru: "Dammit."

4358
04:42:51,000 --> 04:42:56,000
*More accurately, a stone statue of a boy who will never move again.*

4359
04:42:56,000 --> 04:42:59,000
Kakeru: "That's a Hakusen Academy uniform."

4360
04:42:59,000 --> 04:43:00,000
Noa: "...Know him?"

4361
04:43:00,000 --> 04:43:02,000
Kakeru: "No. Never seen him before."

4362
04:43:02,000 --> 04:43:03,000
Noa: "I see."

4363
04:43:03,000 --> 04:43:09,000
*I can't keep my panic down, but Yuuki is utterly calm as she checks out the statue.*

4364
04:43:09,000 --> 04:43:15,000
*Dammit. I was all set to ambush the culprit, and instead, all we found was the third victim.*

4365
04:43:15,000 --> 04:43:19,000
*Could we have saved him if we had just come quicker?*

4366
04:43:19,000 --> 04:43:22,000
*So, this guy... took Miyako's place, huh?*

4367
04:43:22,000 --> 04:43:24,000
*I'm covered in cold sweat.*

4368
04:43:24,000 --> 04:43:29,000
*There was a time when I would have thought this was a regular statue.*

4369
04:43:29,000 --> 04:43:33,000
*But now I know for a fact that this was once a person.*

4370
04:43:33,000 --> 04:43:35,000
*...I feel like I'm going to puke.*

4371
04:43:35,000 --> 04:43:36,000
Noa: "A note?"

4372
04:43:36,000 --> 04:43:38,000
*Yuuki finds something.*

4373
04:43:38,000 --> 04:43:42,000
*Next to the statue, there's a piece of paper lying on the ground.*

4374
04:43:42,000 --> 04:43:43,000
Noa: "His last words."

4375
04:43:43,000 --> 04:43:46,000
Kakeru: "Did the culprit overlook it?"

4376
04:43:46,000 --> 04:43:48,000
Noa: "...No. It's a suicide note."

4377
04:43:48,000 --> 04:43:49,000
Kakeru: "Huh?"

4378
04:43:49,000 --> 04:43:50,000
Noa: "..."

4379
04:43:50,000 --> 04:43:53,000
*I take the scrap of paper Yuuki hands me.*

4380
04:43:53,000 --> 04:43:54,000
*...*

4381
04:43:54,000 --> 04:43:56,000
*It's too dark to read it.*

4382
04:43:56,000 --> 04:44:00,000
*I light up the note with the flashlight app on my smartphone.*

4383
04:44:00,000 --> 04:44:10,000
*"I feel as though I'm being crushed under the weight of my sins. Before I lose my mind, I'm turning myself to stone and putting an end to it all."*

4384
04:44:10,000 --> 04:44:11,000
Kakeru: "..."

4385
04:44:11,000 --> 04:44:14,000
Kakeru: "Turning... himself... to stone...?"

4386
04:44:14,000 --> 04:44:20,000
Noa: "If you take this at face value, then yes, this person turned himself to stone."

4387
04:44:20,000 --> 04:44:24,000
Kakeru: "Himself...? Then, that means this guy is...?"

4388
04:44:24,000 --> 04:44:27,000
Noa: "The wielder of the petrification powers."

4389
04:44:27,000 --> 04:44:28,000
Kakeru: "No way."

4390
04:44:28,000 --> 04:44:29,000
*I can't believe it.*

4391
04:44:29,000 --> 04:44:32,000
*But it's the only thing that makes sense.*

4392
04:44:32,000 --> 04:44:36,000
*The note reveals that this man is in fact the Evil Eye's User.*

4393
04:44:36,000 --> 04:44:39,000
Kakeru: "The third victim is the culprit himself."

4394
04:44:39,000 --> 04:44:41,000
Miyako: "That can't be..."

4395
04:44:41,000 --> 04:44:44,000
*I turn around at the sound of Miyako's voice.*

4396
04:44:44,000 --> 04:44:47,000
*The other two joined us at some point.*

4397
04:44:47,000 --> 04:44:52,000
*Both Miyako and Sora are looking down at the statue in astonishment.*

4398
04:44:52,000 --> 04:44:55,000
Sora: "Huh? So, wait... What's going on?"

4399
04:44:55,000 --> 04:44:58,000
Kakeru: "Miyako, does this guy look familiar?"

4400
04:44:58,000 --> 04:45:03,000
Miyako: "...I saw him in Kosaka-senpai's memories. She met him at the shrine."

4401
04:45:03,000 --> 04:45:07,000
Noa: "I suppose this does confirm your hypothesis, then."

4402
04:45:07,000 --> 04:45:10,000
*Yuuki crouches down and examines the man's face.*

4403
04:45:10,000 --> 04:45:13,000
*The girl from that one time looked to be in pain.*

4404
04:45:13,000 --> 04:45:15,000
*But this man's face is... tranquil.*

4405
04:45:15,000 --> 04:45:25,000
Noa: "What an anticlimactic resolution. If he were being crushed by the weight of his sins, he should have never committed the crimes in the first place."

4406
04:45:25,000 --> 04:45:32,000
Noa: "This man should have been judged properly. To think he would be the only one to die peacefully."

4407
04:45:32,000 --> 04:45:34,000
*She spits, and then stands up.*

4408
04:45:34,000 --> 04:45:37,000
*Next, she turns around and looks me in the eye.*

4409
04:45:37,000 --> 04:45:39,000
Noa: "My work here is done, correct?"

4410
04:45:39,000 --> 04:45:40,000
Kakeru: "Yeah..."

4411
04:45:40,000 --> 04:45:43,000
Noa: "As agreed, you owe me: one week."

4412
04:45:43,000 --> 04:45:45,000
Kakeru: "As agreed, yes."

4413
04:45:45,000 --> 04:45:47,000
Noa: "...I'll be going, then."

4414
04:45:47,000 --> 04:45:51,000
*Without a hint of hesitation, Yuuki confidently strides away.*

4415
04:45:51,000 --> 04:45:58,000
*We don't watch her walk off, instead turning our attention to the stone statue that was once our culprit.*

4416
04:45:58,000 --> 04:45:59,000
Miyako: "..."

4417
04:45:59,000 --> 04:46:04,000
Miyako: "An anticlimactic resolution, she said. But is it really over?"

4418
04:46:04,000 --> 04:46:08,000
Sora: "I assume you can't, like, read a statue's memories?"

4419
04:46:08,000 --> 04:46:09,000
Miyako: "..."

4420
04:46:09,000 --> 04:46:11,000
Miyako: "No. It seems I cannot."

4421
04:46:11,000 --> 04:46:12,000
Sora: "I see..."

4422
04:46:12,000 --> 04:46:16,000
Kakeru: "This suicide note is the only lead we have left now."

4423
04:46:16,000 --> 04:46:18,000
*The handwriting is all crooked.*

4424
04:46:18,000 --> 04:46:27,000
*I could see it just being regular old, sloppy writing. But I could also see it being shaky due to the guy being forced into writing this.*

4425
04:46:27,000 --> 04:46:30,000
Sora: "Does this mean the murders are over?"

4426
04:46:30,000 --> 04:46:32,000
Miyako: "Yes, it does. However..."

4427
04:46:32,000 --> 04:46:33,000
Miyako: "..."

4428
04:46:33,000 --> 04:46:41,000
Miyako: "Even if it was the culprit himself, yet another person has ended up dead. I can't take any joy in this outcome."

4429
04:46:41,000 --> 04:46:46,000
*Miyako clenches her left hand into a fist, her Stigma glowing faintly.*

4430
04:46:46,000 --> 04:46:49,000
*Yes. It's just like Miyako to see things that way.*

4431
04:46:49,000 --> 04:46:53,000
*If only we could have settled things more peacefully...*

4432
04:46:53,000 --> 04:46:54,000
*But, as for me...*

4433
04:46:54,000 --> 04:46:55,000
Kakeru: "..."

4434
04:46:55,000 --> 04:46:56,000
Kakeru: "Sora."

4435
04:46:56,000 --> 04:47:05,000
Sora: "Huh? Oh, wh-what is it? I've never seen one of these before, so... the fact that this is a person is hitting me really hard."

4436
04:47:05,000 --> 04:47:10,000
Kakeru: "Try not to let it overwhelm you. Can you and Miyako go get Ms. Naruse?"

4437
04:47:10,000 --> 04:47:11,000
Sora: "Satsuki-chan?"

4438
04:47:11,000 --> 04:47:14,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. We can't just leave him like this."

4439
04:47:14,000 --> 04:47:17,000
Miyako: "What are you going to do, Kakeru-kun?"

4440
04:47:17,000 --> 04:47:29,000
Kakeru: "I'll call the police... er, on second thought, maybe I should hold off on that until I get Ms. Naruse's permission. Actually, I think I'll try searching him for clues."

4441
04:47:29,000 --> 04:47:31,000
Miyako: "Oh, let me help you."

4442
04:47:31,000 --> 04:47:37,000
Kakeru: "No, you should stay away from this. Please, try to rest at Ms. Naruse's place."

4443
04:47:37,000 --> 04:47:38,000
Miyako: "..."

4444
04:47:38,000 --> 04:47:40,000
Sora: "Let's go, Miya."

4445
04:47:40,000 --> 04:47:41,000
Miyako: "O-Okay."

4446
04:47:41,000 --> 04:47:48,000
*She doesn't seem happy about my sending her away, but when Sora tugs at her hand, Miyako leaves the scene.*

4447
04:47:48,000 --> 04:47:57,000
*I wait until the two are out of sight, and then I crouch down like Yuuki was doing earlier, investigating the man... I mean, the statue.*

4448
04:47:57,000 --> 04:48:03,000
*There's not a trace of flesh and blood remaining. He's been completely turned to stone.*

4449
04:48:03,000 --> 04:48:07,000
*So he wrote this note, and then he used his power on himself.*

4450
04:48:07,000 --> 04:48:08,000
*...*

4451
04:48:08,000 --> 04:48:10,000
Kakeru: "You here, Sophie?"

4452
04:48:10,000 --> 04:48:12,000
Sophitia: "But of course."

4453
04:48:12,000 --> 04:48:17,000
*Not a moment after I call her name, space distorts and Sophie shows herself.*

4454
04:48:17,000 --> 04:48:22,000
*Since it seems she's been watching the entire time, I can skip the explanation.*

4455
04:48:22,000 --> 04:48:29,000
Sophitia: "I would like to congratulate you on finding them, but I'm afraid I won't be doing that."

4456
04:48:29,000 --> 04:48:30,000
Kakeru: "Yeah..."

4457
04:48:30,000 --> 04:48:31,000
Kakeru: "..."

4458
04:48:31,000 --> 04:48:35,000
Kakeru: "Is it even possible to turn yourself into stone?"

4459
04:48:35,000 --> 04:48:42,000
Sophitia: "I believe you've seen it happen before, where someone's power turned against themself."

4460
04:48:42,000 --> 04:48:45,000
Kakeru: "The guy who started the fire, yeah..."

4461
04:48:45,000 --> 04:48:48,000
Sophitia: "Hm. I don't see the Artifact."

4462
04:48:48,000 --> 04:48:51,000
Kakeru: "Did it get petrified along with him?"

4463
04:48:51,000 --> 04:48:54,000
Sophitia: "No, the Artifact couldn't be petrified."

4464
04:48:54,000 --> 04:48:57,000
Kakeru: "Then it disappeared on its own?"

4465
04:48:57,000 --> 04:49:02,000
Sophitia: "Yes. It has likely already found a new owner. Either that, or..."

4466
04:49:02,000 --> 04:49:05,000
Kakeru: "Or this guy isn't the Evil Eye's User."

4467
04:49:05,000 --> 04:49:08,000
Sophitia: "That is certainly possible, yes."

4468
04:49:08,000 --> 04:49:09,000
Kakeru: "..."

4469
04:49:09,000 --> 04:49:15,000
*We track down a lead, and the very night we go to investigate it, the culprit commits suicide.*

4470
04:49:15,000 --> 04:49:17,000
*This timing is too convenient.*

4471
04:49:17,000 --> 04:49:22,000
*Maybe they really did just give up, feeling they had nowhere else to run.*

4472
04:49:22,000 --> 04:49:26,000
*But could you really say we had them so thoroughly cornered?*

4473
04:49:26,000 --> 04:49:32,000
*Would they choose death so readily, even though they knew about our movements in such detail?*

4474
04:49:32,000 --> 04:49:40,000
*Or perhaps precisely because they had such a firm grasp on our progress, they got tired of trying to hide from us?*

4475
04:49:40,000 --> 04:49:41,000
*Who can say.*

4476
04:49:41,000 --> 04:49:44,000
*There is one thing I'm certain of, though.*

4477
04:49:44,000 --> 04:49:50,000
*If this guy wasn't our culprit, whoever they are, they won't be showing up here again.*

4478
04:49:50,000 --> 04:49:52,000
Kakeru: "We're out of leads."

4479
04:49:52,000 --> 04:50:00,000
Sophitia: "If this person wasn't the culprit, the real one will go into hiding. Assuming they aren't incredibly foolish."

4480
04:50:00,000 --> 04:50:03,000
Kakeru: "Yes. Even if we use Miyako's power..."

4481
04:50:03,000 --> 04:50:09,000
Sophitia: "Seeing as how they're predicting your actions, even that won't help you."

4482
04:50:09,000 --> 04:50:13,000
Kakeru: "Are there any Artifacts that can see into the future?"

4483
04:50:13,000 --> 04:50:22,000
Sophitia: "I cannot deny the possibility. That said, there are none under the supervision of Sephirot, nor have we ever discovered one."

4484
04:50:22,000 --> 04:50:34,000
Sophitia: "Still, if there were such a powerful Artifact, I think it's impossible we would not have discovered it until now. Such a power would have been far out of your league anyway."

4485
04:50:34,000 --> 04:50:36,000
Kakeru: "'Would have been,' huh?"

4486
04:50:36,000 --> 04:50:40,000
*Sure wish I could brush that concern away so easily.*

4487
04:50:40,000 --> 04:50:41,000
*...*

4488
04:50:41,000 --> 04:50:43,000
Kakeru: "So, what do we do now?"

4489
04:50:43,000 --> 04:50:50,000
Sophitia: "I'm going to watch how things unfold from here before giving you your next marching orders."

4490
04:50:50,000 --> 04:50:51,000
Kakeru: "Alright."

4491
04:50:51,000 --> 04:50:57,000
Sophitia: "There's also still the matter of your Artifact to deal with. I'm swamped with work."

4492
04:50:57,000 --> 04:51:03,000
Sophitia: "For the time being, fine job. You did good work, even if it all amounted to nothing."

4493
04:51:03,000 --> 04:51:06,000
Kakeru: "You just HAD to tack on that last comment."

4494
04:51:06,000 --> 04:51:11,000
*Sophitia smiles wryly, sticking out her tongue as she returns to her world.*

4495
04:51:11,000 --> 04:51:15,000
*I hear voices off in the distance. Someone's coming this way.*

4496
04:51:15,000 --> 04:51:18,000
*Looks like Ms. Naruse and the others are here...*

4497
04:51:18,000 --> 04:51:19,000
*...*

4498
04:51:19,000 --> 04:51:20,000
*What a relief.*

4499
04:51:20,000 --> 04:51:26,000
*Miyako may lament there being another victim, but I'm just happy this chapter is over.*

4500
04:51:26,000 --> 04:51:32,000
*Whether this guy was the culprit, or whether there's a new culprit out there in his place...*

4501
04:51:32,000 --> 04:51:41,000
*Either way, the curtain is drawn on this mystery for now. As long as we don't pursue them any longer, Miyako should not be targeted again.*

4502
04:51:41,000 --> 04:51:43,000
*Things have come to a close.*

4503
04:51:43,000 --> 04:51:48,000
*Regardless of the truth of the matter, it's safe to say that this is the end.*

4504
04:51:48,000 --> 04:51:52,000
Kakeru: "User of the Evil Eye, please stay dead. Forever."

4505
04:51:52,000 --> 04:51:56,000
*My words are far too cold to be considered a prayer.*

4506
04:51:56,000 --> 04:51:59,000
*I lay the note atop their cold, hard leg.*

4507
04:51:59,000 --> 04:52:01,000
*And I slowly rise to my feet.*

4508
04:52:01,000 --> 04:52:02,000
*May is almost over.*

4509
04:52:02,000 --> 04:52:07,000
*Outside, it's hot enough that you can break a sweat just walking around.*

4510
04:52:07,000 --> 04:52:09,000
*Summer is on its way.*

4511
04:52:09,000 --> 04:52:14,000
*An ordinary summer, leaving no bad memories, empty of grand mysteries.*

4512
04:52:14,000 --> 04:52:20,000
*The guy at the shrine was never declared to be the culprit behind the series of murders.*

4513
04:52:20,000 --> 04:52:26,000
*Instead, the police announced he had died of a mysterious illness, just like the other victims.*

4514
04:52:26,000 --> 04:52:29,000
*They're just sweeping it under the rug.*

4515
04:52:29,000 --> 04:52:37,000
*The population at large refuses to see this as anything more than a bizarre illness that turns people into stone.*

4516
04:52:37,000 --> 04:52:42,000
*That being the case, it doesn't even make sense to talk about a culprit.*

4517
04:52:42,000 --> 04:52:47,000
*I still don't know how they tried to explain away the suicide note.*

4518
04:52:47,000 --> 04:52:54,000
*They certainly didn't feel a need to tell me; I was just the guy who happened to report the statue.*

4519
04:52:54,000 --> 04:52:58,000
*So that's why I did my own legwork and investigated.*

4520
04:52:58,000 --> 04:53:02,000
*The guy was the owner of the forum The Leaves of Agastya.*

4521
04:53:02,000 --> 04:53:09,000
*Turns out he was on friendly terms with Kosaka-senpai as well, and had met with her several times.*

4522
04:53:09,000 --> 04:53:15,000
*Kosaka-senpai didn't know that he was the culprit behind the petrification incidents, I think.*

4523
04:53:15,000 --> 04:53:25,000
*She was in shock and unable to speak, so it's not like she told me that herself, but you could tell just from the way she reacted to the news.*

4524
04:53:25,000 --> 04:53:32,000
*And so that left one suspect unaccounted for: the hooded girl, whose identity we still didn't know.*

4525
04:53:32,000 --> 04:53:34,000
*That man ended up the last victim.*

4526
04:53:34,000 --> 04:53:41,000
*Nobody else has fallen prey to the Evil Eye since that night, and the petrification incidents have stopped.*

4527
04:53:41,000 --> 04:53:43,000
*Our life is... back to normal.*

4528
04:53:43,000 --> 04:53:45,000
*Nothing out of the ordinary.*

4529
04:53:45,000 --> 04:53:49,000
*I walk to school in the morning and spend my day in class.*

4530
04:53:49,000 --> 04:53:58,000
*Once school is out of session, I make my way home. Sometimes I make a few detours along the way. Sometimes I just head straight there.*

4531
04:53:58,000 --> 04:54:01,000
*I while away my time however I feel like.*

4532
04:54:01,000 --> 04:54:05,000
*And when night rolls around, I go to bed and await tomorrow.*

4533
04:54:05,000 --> 04:54:07,000
*Life is back to being mundane.*

4534
04:54:07,000 --> 04:54:10,000
Miyako: "Come and get it, Kakeru-kun!"

4535
04:54:10,000 --> 04:54:13,000
*She sets out the dishes on the table.*

4536
04:54:13,000 --> 04:54:21,000
*It's my favorite: Salisbury steak, a Caesar salad, and a cup of soup. And, of course, a heaping helping of rice.*

4537
04:54:21,000 --> 04:54:23,000
*Everything made for two.*

4538
04:54:23,000 --> 04:54:29,000
*Lately, perhaps out of consideration for us, Sora has stopped showing up at my apartment.*

4539
04:54:29,000 --> 04:54:40,000
*Miyako says she misses having her around, but personally, seeing as how this means the two of us get to make out as much as we want, I find this to be a welcome change.*

4540
04:54:40,000 --> 04:54:42,000
Kakeru: "Thanks! Looks delicious."

4541
04:54:42,000 --> 04:54:44,000
Miyako: "Yes, let's dig in."

4542
04:54:44,000 --> 04:54:47,000
*After we offer thanks, we pick up our chopsticks.*

4543
04:54:47,000 --> 04:54:51,000
Kakeru: "Something tastes a little Japanese-style today."

4544
04:54:51,000 --> 04:54:56,000
Miyako: "Oh, that's the shiso I used this time. Are you okay with it?"

4545
04:54:56,000 --> 04:54:58,000
Kakeru: "It's my favorite."

4546
04:54:58,000 --> 04:55:03,000
Miyako: "Thank goodness. There's really not much you dislike, huh, Kakeru-kun?"

4547
04:55:03,000 --> 04:55:07,000
Kakeru: "Guess so, yeah. I'll eat just about anything."

4548
04:55:07,000 --> 04:55:09,000
Miyako: "What about cilantro?"

4549
04:55:09,000 --> 04:55:11,000
Kakeru: "Totally fine."

4550
04:55:11,000 --> 04:55:12,000
Miyako: "Oh, wow."

4551
04:55:12,000 --> 04:55:13,000
Kakeru: "Not a fan?"

4552
04:55:13,000 --> 04:55:22,000
Miyako: "Not so much. I think the smell is too strong for me. Since I don't care for it much, I'm not great at cooking with it."

4553
04:55:22,000 --> 04:55:26,000
Miyako: "But if you like it, then I guess I should try using it."

4554
04:55:26,000 --> 04:55:34,000
Kakeru: "I wouldn't really say I'm crazy about it, so save the effort. I'd rather have a meal we can both enjoy."

4555
04:55:34,000 --> 04:55:37,000
Miyako: "How is everything? Enjoying it?"

4556
04:55:37,000 --> 04:55:39,000
Kakeru: "You bet, it's super tasty."

4557
04:55:39,000 --> 04:55:41,000
Miyako: "Haha, that's great."

4558
04:55:41,000 --> 04:55:45,000
*We make idle chatter the rest of the way through dinner.*

4559
04:55:45,000 --> 04:55:49,000
*It's already been almost a month since we started dating.*

4560
04:55:49,000 --> 04:55:56,000
*I'm so used to us being alone together that I've stopped acting awkward over every little thing.*

4561
04:55:56,000 --> 04:56:01,000
*Though that doesn't mean she doesn't make my heart pound, every now and then.*

4562
04:56:01,000 --> 04:56:04,000
*The time I spend with Miyako is bliss.*

4563
04:56:04,000 --> 04:56:07,000
*I honestly hope this relationship lasts forever.*

4564
04:56:07,000 --> 04:56:10,000
*That said, there's still one worry I can't shake.*

4565
04:56:10,000 --> 04:56:12,000
Kakeru: "Are you working tomorrow?"

4566
04:56:12,000 --> 04:56:16,000
Miyako: "Yeah, until a little past noon. But I'm free on Sunday."

4567
04:56:16,000 --> 04:56:22,000
Kakeru: "Well, then, how about we... I mean, boy, I'm asking you out every week, aren't I?"

4568
04:56:22,000 --> 04:56:26,000
Miyako: "Haha, you are, and I love it. Let's go out on Sunday."

4569
04:56:26,000 --> 04:56:31,000
Kakeru: "We went to the movies last time, so this time I was thinking..."

4570
04:56:31,000 --> 04:56:34,000
Sophitia: "Please pardon the interruption."

4571
04:56:34,000 --> 04:56:39,000
*A hole in space tears open, and Sophie emerges onto the dining table.*

4572
04:56:39,000 --> 04:56:42,000
*Christ, it's like she's doing this intentionally.*

4573
04:56:42,000 --> 04:56:45,000
Miyako: "Oh, Sophie-san, long time no see."

4574
04:56:45,000 --> 04:56:51,000
Sophitia: "Yes, it has indeed been a while. I've come to say my goodbyes to you today."

4575
04:56:51,000 --> 04:56:52,000
Kakeru: "Goodbyes...?"

4576
04:56:52,000 --> 04:56:55,000
Sophitia: "Yes. At least for the time being."

4577
04:56:55,000 --> 04:56:59,000
Miyako: "I'm sorry that we couldn't be of more help."

4578
04:56:59,000 --> 04:57:09,000
Sophitia: "So it goes. Because of the Evil Eye's User making such a spectacle of things, the other Users who should still be around will be laying low."

4579
04:57:09,000 --> 04:57:21,000
Sophitia: "The Evil Eye has also gone missing. Even if that man was the owner, since he's killed himself and the Artifact has disappeared, that should give rise to a new Evil Eye User."

4580
04:57:21,000 --> 04:57:29,000
Sophitia: "And we haven't heard so much as a peep since! I tried waiting to see how things turned out, but so far, nothing."

4581
04:57:29,000 --> 04:57:38,000
Sophitia: "It's about time I wash my hands of this branch. I certainly hope the versions of you in other branches have more to offer."

4582
04:57:38,000 --> 04:57:43,000
Kakeru: "So, you've basically got nothing left to do in this branch, huh?"

4583
04:57:43,000 --> 04:57:52,000
Sophitia: "Correct. Though that may change, of course, and if it does, you can expect me to return. Until then, you're on standby."

4584
04:57:52,000 --> 04:58:07,000
Sophitia: "All that said, I'm honestly appalled. I can't tell if the people of this world are incredibly rational, or if they're just plain cowards. To think someone would gain such tremendous power and then not use it."

4585
04:58:07,000 --> 04:58:20,000
Sophitia: "Miyako's ability is far too inefficient for searching. I truly thought collecting some Artifacts with it would be a breeze, too. Thanks to this hiccup, my reputation has suffered."

4586
04:58:20,000 --> 04:58:24,000
Miyako: "Oh, then you can at least have my Artifact."

4587
04:58:24,000 --> 04:58:26,000
Sophitia: "Oh, really? Thank you!"

4588
04:58:26,000 --> 04:58:31,000
Sophitia: "Just kidding. I'll let you hold on to it for a bit longer."

4589
04:58:31,000 --> 04:58:35,000
Miyako: "In case another Evil Eye User makes a move?"

4590
04:58:35,000 --> 04:58:45,000
Sophitia: "Yes. While it is inefficient for a widespread search for Users, your ability is quite handy when it comes to stealing a single Artifact."

4591
04:58:45,000 --> 04:58:51,000
Sophitia: "So I'll leave it in your care for now. Do try not to let anyone steal it."

4592
04:58:51,000 --> 04:58:52,000
Miyako: "Of course."

4593
04:58:52,000 --> 04:58:54,000
Sophitia: "Also, Kakeru?"

4594
04:58:54,000 --> 04:58:55,000
Kakeru: "Yeah?"

4595
04:58:55,000 --> 04:59:02,000
Sophitia: "It's grating that I don't know what your ability does. Have you felt anything out of the ordinary?"

4596
04:59:02,000 --> 04:59:03,000
Kakeru: "Not a thing."

4597
04:59:03,000 --> 04:59:06,000
Sophitia: "Have you had a Stigma appear anywhere?"

4598
04:59:06,000 --> 04:59:07,000
Kakeru: "Nope."

4599
04:59:07,000 --> 04:59:11,000
Sophitia: "It might be somewhere you can't check by yourself."

4600
04:59:11,000 --> 04:59:14,000
Kakeru: "I've had Miyako check. None."

4601
04:59:14,000 --> 04:59:18,000
Sophitia: "Oh my... You're getting naked around each other?"

4602
04:59:18,000 --> 04:59:19,000
Kakeru: "..."

4603
04:59:19,000 --> 04:59:21,000
Miyako: "K-Kakeru-kun..."

4604
04:59:21,000 --> 04:59:22,000
Kakeru: "S-Sorry."

4605
04:59:22,000 --> 04:59:28,000
Sophitia: "Losing your cool over such a trifle shows how immature you both still are."

4606
04:59:28,000 --> 04:59:38,000
Sophitia: "While I deeply regret not being able to find the truth about your powers, I cannot stay here and keep you under surveillance forever."

4607
04:59:38,000 --> 04:59:43,000
Kakeru: "I'm looking forward to you not popping in uninvited anymore."

4608
04:59:43,000 --> 04:59:45,000
Sophitia: "You know you'll miss me."

4609
04:59:45,000 --> 04:59:47,000
*I look away and shrug my shoulders.*

4610
04:59:47,000 --> 04:59:51,000
*Sophie harrumphs and rips a distorted hole in space.*

4611
04:59:51,000 --> 04:59:55,000
Sophitia: "Now, then, I'll leave you two lovebirds alone."

4612
04:59:55,000 --> 04:59:58,000
Miyako: "Um. Will we see each other again?"

4613
04:59:58,000 --> 05:00:06,000
Sophitia: "Of course. I don't plan on letting you hold onto that Artifact forever. I'll return to retrieve it in due time."

4614
05:00:06,000 --> 05:00:08,000
Sophitia: "I'll be back."

4615
05:00:08,000 --> 05:00:12,000
Kakeru: "Well, you know, if you're ever free, come by to hang out."

4616
05:00:12,000 --> 05:00:15,000
Sophitia: "Oh you. I knew you'd miss me."

4617
05:00:15,000 --> 05:00:16,000
Kakeru: "Shaddup."

4618
05:00:16,000 --> 05:00:18,000
Sophitia: "Heh heh. Ta-ta for now."

4619
05:00:18,000 --> 05:00:20,000
Miyako: "S-See you later!"

4620
05:00:20,000 --> 05:00:26,000
*Miyako waves warmly, and Sophie waves back in suit as she disappears into the subspace rift.*

4621
05:00:26,000 --> 05:00:27,000
*...*

4622
05:00:27,000 --> 05:00:28,000
*Ta-ta for now, huh?*

4623
05:00:28,000 --> 05:00:31,000
*But only for now. This isn't over yet.*

4624
05:00:31,000 --> 05:00:35,000
Miyako: "So I'll be keeping this for a bit longer..."

4625
05:00:35,000 --> 05:00:41,000
*She pulls out the hair clip—the Artifact—from her pocket and places it on the table.*

4626
05:00:41,000 --> 05:00:46,000
*As long as Miyako and this accessory are bound together, things aren't over.*

4627
05:00:46,000 --> 05:00:49,000
Miyako: "I wonder when we'll see her again."

4628
05:00:49,000 --> 05:00:56,000
Kakeru: "To be brutally honest, I hope we don't. Honestly, I was hoping she'd take this with her."

4629
05:00:56,000 --> 05:01:01,000
Miyako: "Yes, I agree. It might be too much power for me to handle. Still..."

4630
05:01:01,000 --> 05:01:06,000
Kakeru: "As long as you have it, you can stop the new Evil Eye User if need be."

4631
05:01:06,000 --> 05:01:12,000
Miyako: "Yes. Next time, I don't want to mess up. I don't want anyone else to lose their life."

4632
05:01:12,000 --> 05:01:13,000
Kakeru: "Next time..."

4633
05:01:13,000 --> 05:01:16,000
*I murmur, popping a tomato into my mouth.*

4634
05:01:16,000 --> 05:01:21,000
*Miyako almost says something, but decides against it, returning to her meal.*

4635
05:01:21,000 --> 05:01:26,000
*I don't mean to come across as angry, but that's probably how she's taking it.*

4636
05:01:26,000 --> 05:01:29,000
*Still, I can't force myself to smile.*

4637
05:01:29,000 --> 05:01:31,000
*So we sit and eat in silence.*

4638
05:01:31,000 --> 05:01:33,000
Kakeru: "Thank you for the meal."

4639
05:01:33,000 --> 05:01:35,000
Miyako: "Did you get enough?"

4640
05:01:35,000 --> 05:01:38,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, thanks. It was delicious."

4641
05:01:38,000 --> 05:01:42,000
Miyako: "Oh, no, you can leave the plates. I'll clean up."

4642
05:01:42,000 --> 05:01:45,000
Kakeru: "Thanks. I'm going to get some fresh air."

4643
05:01:45,000 --> 05:01:46,000
Miyako: "Sure."

4644
05:01:46,000 --> 05:01:52,000
*I stack up my dirty dishes, stand up, open the glass door, and step out onto the veranda.*

4645
05:01:52,000 --> 05:01:53,000
Kakeru: "..."

4646
05:01:53,000 --> 05:01:55,000
*The breeze tonight feels great.*

4647
05:01:55,000 --> 05:02:00,000
*It's getting warmer lately, so the early evening air feels nice and cool.*

4648
05:02:00,000 --> 05:02:03,000
*...But inside, I'm anything but cool.*

4649
05:02:03,000 --> 05:02:04,000
*...*

4650
05:02:04,000 --> 05:02:07,000
*I still have that same doubt hanging over me.*

4651
05:02:07,000 --> 05:02:09,000
*The Artifacts remain in this world.*

4652
05:02:09,000 --> 05:02:11,000
*The Evil Eye is out there.*

4653
05:02:11,000 --> 05:02:14,000
*And Miyako is a User. She may be targeted again.*

4654
05:02:14,000 --> 05:02:17,000
*If I at least had a power of my own...*

4655
05:02:17,000 --> 05:02:20,000
*If only my power would reveal itself...*

4656
05:02:20,000 --> 05:02:24,000
*Hell, where even is my Artifact in the first place?*

4657
05:02:24,000 --> 05:02:29,000
*If the Artifacts aren't going away, then I want the power to protect Miyako.*

4658
05:02:29,000 --> 05:02:30,000
Miyako: "Kakeru-kun."

4659
05:02:30,000 --> 05:02:32,000
*I hear Miyako's voice.*

4660
05:02:32,000 --> 05:02:40,000
*I grunt, not turning around. I stare out for a little while longer, before I notice Miyako has come to stand next to me.*

4661
05:02:40,000 --> 05:02:42,000
Miyako: "Are you angry?"

4662
05:02:42,000 --> 05:02:44,000
Kakeru: "Huh? Oh, no, not really."

4663
05:02:44,000 --> 05:02:47,000
Miyako: "Okay then. Are you worried about me?"

4664
05:02:47,000 --> 05:02:48,000
Kakeru: "..."

4665
05:02:48,000 --> 05:02:49,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, I am."

4666
05:02:49,000 --> 05:02:52,000
*When I admit it, Miyako breaks into a smile.*

4667
05:02:52,000 --> 05:02:59,000
Miyako: "You know, I've been puzzling over something for a while. How could you and I have had a falling out?"

4668
05:02:59,000 --> 05:03:03,000
Kakeru: "You mean what happened in that alternate branch?"

4669
05:03:03,000 --> 05:03:06,000
Miyako: "Yeah, exactly. Hear me out for a second."

4670
05:03:06,000 --> 05:03:07,000
Kakeru: "Sure."

4671
05:03:07,000 --> 05:03:12,000
Miyako: "Maybe I was trying too hard to show off for you, or something like that."

4672
05:03:12,000 --> 05:03:13,000
Kakeru: "Hm?"

4673
05:03:13,000 --> 05:03:17,000
Miyako: "What I'm saying is, we didn't really have a falling out."

4674
05:03:17,000 --> 05:03:22,000
*She smiles again, bumping into me and wrapping her arm around mine.*

4675
05:03:22,000 --> 05:03:29,000
Miyako: "What I think is, I found out how you felt about me, but decided I wouldn't be the right fit for you."

4676
05:03:29,000 --> 05:03:30,000
Kakeru: "Why not?"

4677
05:03:30,000 --> 05:03:40,000
Miyako: "You were amazing, in that fire. You fought tooth and nail for Sora-chan, and though I was nothing but a classmate of yours, you protected me."

4678
05:03:40,000 --> 05:03:49,000
Miyako: "I was floored. I didn't realize it at the time, but now, I think that was the moment I fell in love with you, Kakeru-kun."

4679
05:03:49,000 --> 05:03:50,000
Kakeru: "R-Really?"

4680
05:03:50,000 --> 05:03:56,000
Miyako: "Yeah. I mean, isn't that around when I started acting different when I was with you?"

4681
05:03:56,000 --> 05:03:57,000
Kakeru: "Huh..."

4682
05:03:57,000 --> 05:04:04,000
*Come to think of it, that was around when she started cooking for me. She started talking more casually, too.*

4683
05:04:04,000 --> 05:04:09,000
Miyako: "When I learned how you felt about me, I noticed my own feelings for you."

4684
05:04:09,000 --> 05:04:15,000
Miyako: "Maybe, in that other branch, I couldn't accept that. You were just so far above me."

4685
05:04:15,000 --> 05:04:17,000
Kakeru: "Hell of an exaggeration."

4686
05:04:17,000 --> 05:04:26,000
Miyako: "Haha, but it's true. So I must have figured I had to work that much harder. And... I probably went out of control because of it."

4687
05:04:26,000 --> 05:04:31,000
Miyako: "I was trying to impress you by taking care of everything on my own."

4688
05:04:31,000 --> 05:04:36,000
Miyako: "And in the end, I failed. I lost to the Evil Eye's User and died."

4689
05:04:36,000 --> 05:04:37,000
Kakeru: "..."

4690
05:04:37,000 --> 05:04:40,000
Miyako: "Do you see where I'm going with this?"

4691
05:04:40,000 --> 05:04:41,000
Kakeru: "No, I don't."

4692
05:04:41,000 --> 05:04:46,000
Miyako: "I have to be together with you, no matter what, Kakeru-kun."

4693
05:04:46,000 --> 05:04:49,000
*Miyako takes my hand and squeezes it tight.*

4694
05:04:49,000 --> 05:04:56,000
Miyako: "I'm alive because I'm with you, Kakeru-kun. As long as I'm with you, I'll make it through."

4695
05:04:56,000 --> 05:05:01,000
Miyako: "I'll be fine, because you're around. Just like you promised me..."

4696
05:05:01,000 --> 05:05:04,000
Kakeru: "I'm going to keep that promise."

4697
05:05:04,000 --> 05:05:05,000
Miyako: "Good."

4698
05:05:05,000 --> 05:05:06,000
*She smiles sweetly.*

4699
05:05:06,000 --> 05:05:10,000
*As she holds my hand, my own grip naturally gets tighter.*

4700
05:05:10,000 --> 05:05:18,000
Miyako: "I'm even glad that I get to keep this Artifact's power. I think you would rescue me if I were to ever use it wrong."

4701
05:05:18,000 --> 05:05:22,000
Miyako: "You're the one who can teach me how to use it."

4702
05:05:22,000 --> 05:05:26,000
Miyako: "Without you, I'd just mess it all up. Got it?"

4703
05:05:26,000 --> 05:05:27,000
*She smiles kindly.*

4704
05:05:27,000 --> 05:05:32,000
*Almost as if she's assuring me that she needs me. That I don't have to worry.*

4705
05:05:32,000 --> 05:05:33,000
*...*

4706
05:05:33,000 --> 05:05:34,000
*Now I get it.*

4707
05:05:34,000 --> 05:05:38,000
Kakeru: "If we're together, we've got nothing to fear."

4708
05:05:38,000 --> 05:05:39,000
Miyako: "Yeah!"

4709
05:05:39,000 --> 05:05:44,000
Kakeru: "Let me promise, one more time. No matter what, Miyako, I'll protect you."

4710
05:05:44,000 --> 05:05:46,000
Miyako: "Yes. You'll be my guardian."

4711
05:05:46,000 --> 05:05:49,000
Miyako: "From now until forever, I hope."

4712
05:05:49,000 --> 05:05:50,000
Kakeru: "Sure thing."

4713
05:05:50,000 --> 05:05:51,000
Kakeru: "..."

4714
05:05:51,000 --> 05:05:55,000
Kakeru: "Hahah. Makes it sound like we're getting married."

4715
05:05:55,000 --> 05:05:56,000
Miyako: "..."

4716
05:05:56,000 --> 05:05:57,000
Kakeru: "What's up?"

4717
05:05:57,000 --> 05:06:03,000
Miyako: "I'm being serious here. I'd rather you didn't joke around about things like that."

4718
05:06:03,000 --> 05:06:05,000
Kakeru: "I wasn't joking."

4719
05:06:05,000 --> 05:06:06,000
Miyako: "..."

4720
05:06:06,000 --> 05:06:09,000
Kakeru: "But I'm secretly just out for your money."

4721
05:06:09,000 --> 05:06:15,000
Miyako: "Oh no! How could I not have foreseen this?! I'll have to rethink our relationship now."

4722
05:06:15,000 --> 05:06:20,000
Kakeru: "Doesn't matter if you dump me, I ain't leavin'. I DID make a promise."

4723
05:06:20,000 --> 05:06:24,000
Miyako: "Haha, yes you did. You most certainly made me a promise."

4724
05:06:24,000 --> 05:06:27,000
*We stand out there on the veranda, hand in hand.*

4725
05:06:27,000 --> 05:06:32,000
*Our fingers interlaced. Hers warm and soft, mine a little calloused.*

4726
05:06:32,000 --> 05:06:36,000
*Feeling each other's pulse. Confirming each other's love.*

4727
05:06:36,000 --> 05:06:38,000
Miyako: "I'll never leave you."

4728
05:06:38,000 --> 05:06:42,000
Kakeru: "Yeah. I'll never stop holding your hand, Miyako."

4729
05:06:42,000 --> 05:06:43,000
Miyako: "Yeah."

4730
05:06:43,000 --> 05:06:45,000
*A gentle breeze blows.*

4731
05:06:45,000 --> 05:06:49,000
*It swirls around the both of us, ruffling our hair.*

4732
05:06:49,000 --> 05:06:51,000
*My worries have not abated.*

4733
05:06:51,000 --> 05:06:55,000
*My doubts are still lingering in a corner of my mind.*

4734
05:06:55,000 --> 05:07:01,000
*As long as the Artifacts remain in this world, another incident is bound to occur.*

4735
05:07:01,000 --> 05:07:05,000
*And when it does, Miyako will be there to deal with it.*

4736
05:07:05,000 --> 05:07:07,000
*She might even be put into danger.*

4737
05:07:07,000 --> 05:07:09,000
*Even so, we'll face forward.*

4738
05:07:09,000 --> 05:07:11,000
*Not slowing down. Not looking back.*

4739
05:07:11,000 --> 05:07:16,000
*No matter what difficulties may be waiting for us down the road...*

4740
05:07:16,000 --> 05:07:17,000
*We'll overcome them.*

4741
05:07:17,000 --> 05:07:18,000
*Hand-in-hand.*

4742
05:07:18,000 --> 05:07:20,000
*Together, we can do anything.*

4743
05:07:20,000 --> 05:07:25,000
Miyako: "Thanks for waiting! Here you are, one order of teriyaki chicken!"

4744
05:07:25,000 --> 05:07:28,000
*She lays the dishes out on the table.*

4745
05:07:28,000 --> 05:07:30,000
*Everything looks amazing.*

4746
05:07:30,000 --> 05:07:39,000
*This may have something to do with Miyako wearing her work uniform, but even more so than usual, today everything looks perfect.*

4747
05:07:39,000 --> 05:07:43,000
Kakeru: "I sure am glad I waited to eat until you got off work."

4748
05:07:43,000 --> 05:07:48,000
Miyako: "Haha, I'm sorry. I wish I could have wrapped up early today."

4749
05:07:48,000 --> 05:08:00,000
Kakeru: "Nah, you've got nothing to apologize for. If anything, I'm the one who should be apologizing to you for my silly request, asking you to wear your uniform around the apartment."

4750
05:08:00,000 --> 05:08:07,000
Miyako: "No, it's fine. I'd do anything to make you happy. Besides, it's due to go to the cleaners anyway."

4751
05:08:07,000 --> 05:08:11,000
Kakeru: "Begging on my hands and knees was worth it."

4752
05:08:11,000 --> 05:08:19,000
Miyako: "You were oddly intent on this, weren't you, Kakeru-kun? Haha. Now, why don't we eat before it gets cold?"

4753
05:08:19,000 --> 05:08:23,000
Kakeru: "Right, thank you for always cooking for me."

4754
05:08:23,000 --> 05:08:25,000
Miyako: "Why, you're quite welcome."

4755
05:08:25,000 --> 05:08:29,000
*We both offer a prayer and then pick up our chopsticks.*

4756
05:08:29,000 --> 05:08:31,000
Kakeru: "Yeah, great as always."

4757
05:08:31,000 --> 05:08:40,000
Miyako: "You don't think the rice is a little crunchy, do you? I'm worried I put in the wrong amount of water this time around."

4758
05:08:40,000 --> 05:08:42,000
Kakeru: "No way, it's great."

4759
05:08:42,000 --> 05:08:44,000
Miyako: "Thank goodness."

4760
05:08:44,000 --> 05:08:49,000
*It's now an everyday occurrence for the two of us to share a meal.*

4761
05:08:49,000 --> 05:08:51,000
*Just another day in the life.*

4762
05:08:51,000 --> 05:08:57,000
*And yet, I find even the familiarity of it to be a source of amazing and irreplaceable joy.*

4763
05:08:57,000 --> 05:09:02,000
*Sophie has left temporarily and the petrification incidents have come to an end.*

4764
05:09:02,000 --> 05:09:06,000
*We might have our fair share of fights down the road.*

4765
05:09:06,000 --> 05:09:14,000
*But I sincerely hope that the two of us can spend the rest of our lives in peace, together, just like we are now.*

4766
05:09:14,000 --> 05:09:17,000
Miyako: "Oh, should I have put out a spoon?"

4767
05:09:17,000 --> 05:09:21,000
Kakeru: "Hm? Oh, for the soup? I'll manage with chopsticks."

4768
05:09:21,000 --> 05:09:28,000
Miyako: "I'll go fetch one just in case. I diced the onions pretty small, so they might be hard to eat."

4769
05:09:28,000 --> 05:09:32,000
*Miyako rises from her seat and heads back into the kitchen.*

4770
05:09:32,000 --> 05:09:37,000
*Miyako's presence in this apartment has become commonplace now, too.*

4771
05:09:37,000 --> 05:09:41,000
*And it will remain that way. We'll be together from now on.*

4772
05:09:41,000 --> 05:09:48,000
*My sincerest wish is that a day comes where I don't even think about how commonplace this scene has become.*

4773
05:09:48,000 --> 05:09:51,000
Miyako: "Um, let's see, where are the spoons..."

4774
05:09:51,000 --> 05:09:52,000
Miyako: "Ah!"

4775
05:09:52,000 --> 05:09:53,000
Miyako: "Oh no..."

4776
05:09:53,000 --> 05:09:55,000
Kakeru: "What's wrong?"

4777
05:09:55,000 --> 05:09:59,000
Miyako: "Nothing! I just dropped it between a crack!"

4778
05:09:59,000 --> 05:10:02,000
Miyako: "Oh dear... What am I going to do?"

4779
05:10:02,000 --> 05:10:03,000
Miyako: "..."

4780
05:10:03,000 --> 05:10:10,000
Miyako: "This is... somewhat of an abuse of power, but, I'm sorry. Forgive me for using it so lightly."

4781
05:10:10,000 --> 05:10:11,000
Miyako: "..."

4782
05:10:11,000 --> 05:10:16,000
Miyako: "Mm... Okay, perfect, I got it. Now I just have to wash it... off...?"

4783
05:10:16,000 --> 05:10:17,000
Miyako: "...?"

4784
05:10:17,000 --> 05:10:18,000
Miyako: "Wha...?"

4785
05:10:18,000 --> 05:10:19,000
Miyako: "..."

4786
05:10:19,000 --> 05:10:22,000
Miyako: "I'm not... seeing things, am I?"

4787
05:10:22,000 --> 05:10:24,000
Miyako: "The Stigma is expanding...?"
